window.EXAM_DATA=window.EXAM_DATA||{};window.EXAM_DATA["mla_c01"]=[{"id":1,"question_en":"Case Study A company is building a web-based AI application by using Amazon SageMaker. The application will provide the following capabilities and features: ML experimentation, training, a central model registry, model deployment, and model monitoring. The application must ensure secure and isolated use of training data during the ML lifecycle. The training data is stored in Amazon S3. The company needs to use the central model registry to manage different versions of models in the application. Which action will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"案例研究 一位机器学习工程师正在 AWS 上开发一个欺诈检测模型。训练数据集包括交易日志、客户资料以及来 自本地 MySQL 数据库的表。交易日志和客户资料存储在亚马逊 S3 中。 该数据集存在类别不平衡的问题，这影响了模型算法的学习。此外，许多特征之间存在相互依赖关系。 算法未能捕捉到数据中所有期望的潜在模式。 在数据聚合完成后，机器学习工程师必须实现一个解决方案，以自动检测数据中的异常情况，并将结果 可视化。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a separate Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository for each model.","B":"Use Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) and unique tags for each model version.","C":"Use the SageMaker Model Registry and model groups to catalog the models.","D":"Use the SageMaker Model Registry and unique tags for each model version."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用亚马逊 Athena 自动检测异常情况并可视化结果。","B":"使用 Amazon Redshift Spectrum 自动检测异常情况。使用 Amazon QuickSight 可视化结果。","C":"使用 Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler 自动检测异常情况，并可视化结果。","D":"使用 AWS Batch 自动检测异常情况。使用 Amazon QuickSight 可视化结果。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The SageMaker Model Registry is the purpose-built central registry for cataloging and versioning ML models, which is exactly what the requirement asks for. Per AWS docs, the registry is structured as Model (Package) Groups, and 'the version of each model package is a numerical value that starts at 1 and is incremented with each new model package added to a Model Group.' So creating a Model Group and registering each trained model into it gives you native, automatic version management with the least operational overhead. Option D is technically impossible: AWS states explicitly that 'Model packages in the SageMaker Model Registry do not support tags-these are versioned model packages' (only model package groups support tags), so you cannot version model versions via unique tags. Options A and B use Amazon ECR, which is a container image registry rather than a model registry, ignoring the stated requirement to use a central model registry and adding significant operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"SageMaker Model Registry 是專為編目與版本管理 ML 模型而設計的中央登錄機制，正好符合題目要求。根據 AWS 文件，Model Registry 的結構是由多個 Model (Package) Groups 組成，且『每個 model package 的版本是一個從 1 開始、每加入一個新 model package 到 Model Group 就遞增的數值』。因此只要建立一個 Model Group 並將每個訓練好的模型註冊進去，即可獲得原生且自動的版本管理，營運負擔最低。選項 D 在技術上不可行：AWS 明確指出『SageMaker Model Registry 中的 model packages 不支援 tags，它們是版本化的 model packages』（只有 model package group 支援 tagging），因此無法用 unique tags 為模型版本做版本管理。選項 A 與 B 使用 Amazon ECR，那是容器映像登錄處而非模型登錄處，忽略題目要求使用中央模型登錄，並增加大量營運負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon ECR is a Docker container image registry, not a model registry. Creating a separate ECR repo per model does not catalog model versions and ignores the requirement to use a central model registry; it adds high operational overhead with manual per-model repository management.","why_zh":"Amazon ECR 是 Docker 容器映像登錄處，不是模型登錄處。為每個模型建立獨立 ECR repo 無法編目模型版本，且忽略使用中央模型登錄的要求，並需逐一手動管理 repository，營運負擔高。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"ECR with unique tags stores container images, not registered model versions with approval status, lineage, and metadata. It is not the SageMaker central model registry and imposes manual tagging overhead for versioning.","why_zh":"ECR 搭配 unique tags 儲存的是容器映像，而非具核准狀態、譜系與中繼資料的已註冊模型版本。它不是 SageMaker 中央模型登錄，且版本控制需依賴人工 tagging，負擔較高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Technically incorrect: AWS docs state model packages (model versions) in the Model Registry do NOT support tags-only model package groups do. Versioning is automatic via the model group's incrementing numbers, so 'unique tags for each version' is both unsupported and unnecessary, adding overhead.","why_zh":"技術上錯誤：AWS 文件指出 Model Registry 中的 model packages（模型版本）不支援 tags，只有 model package group 支援。版本是透過 model group 自動遞增編號產生，因此『為每個版本用 unique tags』既不被支援也非必要，反而增加負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry-models.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry-tags.html"]}},{"id":2,"question_en":"Case Study A company is building a web-based AI application by using Amazon SageMaker. The application will provide the following capabilities and features: ML experimentation, training, a central model registry, model deployment, and model monitoring. The application must ensure secure and isolated use of training data during the ML lifecycle. The training data is stored in Amazon S3. The company is experimenting with consecutive training jobs. How can the company MINIMIZE infrastructure startup times for these jobs?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师在 us-east-1 区域的账户 A 中有一个 Amazon Comprehend 自定义模型。该机器学习工程 师需要将此模型复制到同一区域的账户 B 中。 哪种解决方案能以最少的开发工作量满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Managed Spot Training.","B":"Use SageMaker managed warm pools.","C":"Use SageMaker Training Compiler.","D":"Use the SageMaker distributed data parallelism (SMDDP) library."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用亚马逊 S3 制作模型的副本。将副本转移到账户 B。","B":"创建一个基于资源的 IAM 策略。使用 Amazon Comprehend ImportModel API 操作将模型复制到账户 B。","C":"使用 AWS DataSync 将模型从账户 A 复制到账户 B。","D":"在账户 A 和账户 B 之间创建一个 AWS 站点到站点 VPN 连接以传输模型。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The qualifier is MINIMIZE infrastructure startup times across consecutive (repetitive) training jobs. SageMaker managed warm pools are purpose-built for this: by setting KeepAlivePeriodInSeconds, SageMaker retains and reuses the provisioned cluster after a job completes, so the next job that matches parameters (instance type/count, etc.) runs on the warm pool and skips the cold-start provisioning phase. The official doc states warm pools 'let you retain and reuse provisioned infrastructure after the completion of a training job to reduce latency for repetitive workloads, such as iterative experimentation or running many jobs consecutively' and that subsequent matching jobs 'speed up start times by reducing the time spent provisioning resources.' This is an almost verbatim match to the scenario of experimenting with consecutive training jobs, so B is correct.","explanation_zh":"本題的限定詞是 MINIMIZE（最小化）連續（反覆性）訓練作業的基礎設施啟動時間。SageMaker managed warm pools 正是為此設計：透過設定 KeepAlivePeriodInSeconds，SageMaker 會在作業完成後保留並重用已佈建的叢集，因此下一個參數相符（執行個體類型/數量等）的作業即可在 warm pool 上執行，跳過冷啟動的資源佈建階段。官方文件指出 warm pools「可在訓練作業完成後保留並重用已佈建的基礎設施，為反覆性工作負載（例如迭代實驗或連續執行多個作業）降低延遲」，且後續相符的作業會「藉由減少佈建資源所花的時間來加快啟動時間」。這幾乎與「連續訓練作業實驗」的情境逐字吻合，因此 B 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Managed Spot Training reduces COST (up to 90%) by using EC2 Spot instances; it does not minimize startup time. Spot capacity can be interrupted or unavailable, which can actually make jobs take longer to start or finish.","why_zh":"Managed Spot Training 透過 EC2 Spot 執行個體降低成本（最高 90%），而非縮短啟動時間。Spot 容量可能被中斷或無法取得，甚至會讓作業需要更長時間才能啟動或完成。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SageMaker Training Compiler accelerates the training computation itself by optimizing deep learning model graphs for GPU, reducing model training/run time. It does not reduce the infrastructure provisioning (cold-start) latency between consecutive jobs.","why_zh":"SageMaker Training Compiler 透過為 GPU 最佳化深度學習模型圖來加速訓練運算本身，縮短的是模型訓練/執行時間，並不會降低連續作業之間的基礎設施佈建（冷啟動）延遲。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The SMDDP library speeds up distributed multi-node/multi-GPU training by optimizing gradient/collective communication across instances. It improves training throughput and scaling, not cluster startup latency for consecutive jobs.","why_zh":"SMDDP 函式庫透過最佳化跨執行個體的梯度/集體通訊來加速分散式多節點/多 GPU 訓練。它改善的是訓練吞吐量與擴展能力，而非連續作業的叢集啟動延遲。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/train-warm-pools.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/train-warm-pools-how-to-use.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-managed-spot-training.html"]}},{"id":3,"question_en":"Case Study A company is building a web-based AI application by using Amazon SageMaker. The application will provide the following capabilities and features: ML experimentation, training, a central model registry, model deployment, and model monitoring. The application must ensure secure and isolated use of training data during the ML lifecycle. The training data is stored in Amazon S3. The company must implement a manual approval-based workflow to ensure that only approved models can be deployed to production endpoints. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司在产品发布后收集了大量的客户互动聊天记录。一位机器学习工程师需要创建一个机器学习模 型来分析这些聊天数据。该工程师需要通过审查客户对产品的态度来确定产品的成功与否。 机器学习工程师应采取哪项行动才能在最短时间内完成评估？","options_en":{"A":"Use SageMaker Experiments to facilitate the approval process during model registration.","B":"Use SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking on the central model registry. Create tracking entities for the approval process.","C":"Use SageMaker Model Monitor to evaluate the performance of the model and to manage the approval.","D":"Use SageMaker Pipelines. When a model version is registered, use the AWS SDK to change the approval status to \"Approved.\""},"options_zh":{"A":"使用亚马逊 Rekognition 分析聊天对话中的情绪。","B":"训练一个朴素贝叶斯分类器来分析聊天对话的情感。","C":"使用亚马逊 comprehend 分析聊天对话中的情感。","D":"使用随机森林对聊天对话的情感进行分类。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Amazon SageMaker Model Registry is the central registry that catalogs model versions and manages each version's approval status. The documented manual-approval workflow is: use SageMaker Pipelines to train and register each model version into the Model Registry, where it is registered with ModelApprovalStatus set to PendingManualApproval. A reviewer then manually changes the status to 'Approved' using the AWS SDK for Python (the update_model_package call) or the Studio console. The official 'Update the Approval Status of a Model' page states that the PendingManualApproval -> Approved transition initiates CI/CD deployment for the approved model version, so only explicitly approved models reach production endpoints. Option D describes exactly this native mechanism, which is why it is correct.","explanation_zh":"Amazon SageMaker Model Registry 是中央登錄，負責編目模型版本並管理每個版本的核准狀態。文件記載的人工核准工作流程為：使用 SageMaker Pipelines 訓練模型並將每個模型版本註冊到 Model Registry，此時 ModelApprovalStatus 設為 PendingManualApproval。接著由審核者透過 AWS SDK for Python（update_model_package 呼叫）或 Studio 主控台手動將狀態改為 'Approved'。官方的 'Update the Approval Status of a Model' 頁面說明 PendingManualApproval -> Approved 的狀態轉換會觸發該核准模型版本的 CI/CD 部署，因此只有明確核准的模型才會進入生產端點。選項 D 正好描述這個原生機制，所以是正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SageMaker Experiments is for tracking, organizing, and comparing ML experiment runs and trials. It has no concept of a model approval status or a deployment approval gate, so it cannot enforce that only approved models are deployed.","why_zh":"SageMaker Experiments 用於追蹤、組織與比較 ML 實驗執行與試驗。它沒有模型核准狀態或部署核准關卡的概念，因此無法強制只有核准的模型才能部署。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking creates and stores information about the steps of an ML workflow for traceability and reproducibility. The Model Registry lists lineage viewing and approval management as separate capabilities; lineage entities document provenance but do not gate or control model deployment approval.","why_zh":"SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking 建立並儲存 ML 工作流程各步驟的資訊以利追溯與重現。Model Registry 將檢視 lineage 與核准管理列為各自獨立的功能；lineage 實體記錄來源資訊，但無法把關或控制模型部署的核准。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SageMaker Model Monitor detects data and model quality drift on already-deployed endpoints. It operates after deployment and provides no pre-deployment approval mechanism in the model registry, so it cannot serve as the manual approval gate before production deployment.","why_zh":"SageMaker Model Monitor 偵測已部署端點上的資料與模型品質漂移。它在部署後運作，且未在模型登錄中提供部署前核准機制，因此無法作為生產部署前的人工核准關卡。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry-approve.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/pipelines-overview.html"]}},{"id":4,"question_en":"Case Study A company is building a web-based AI application by using Amazon SageMaker. The application will provide the following capabilities and features: ML experimentation, training, a central model registry, model deployment, and model monitoring. The application must ensure secure and isolated use of training data during the ML lifecycle. The training data is stored in Amazon S3. The company needs to run an on-demand workflow to monitor bias drift for models that are deployed to real-time endpoints from the application. Which action will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师正在评估几个机器学习模型，并且必须从中选择一个用于生产环境。这些模型出现假 阴性预测的代价远高于出现假阳性预测的代价。 在选择模型时，机器学习工程师应优先考虑哪项指标结果？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the application to invoke an AWS Lambda function that runs a SageMaker Clarify job.","B":"Invoke an AWS Lambda function to pull the sagemaker-model-monitor-analyzer built-in SageMaker image.","C":"Use AWS Glue Data Quality to monitor bias.","D":"Use SageMaker notebooks to compare the bias."},"options_zh":{"A":"低精度","B":"高精度","C":"低召回率","D":"高召回率"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Bias drift monitoring in SageMaker is implemented by SageMaker Clarify: the ModelBiasModelMonitor runs SageMaker Clarify processing jobs that compare live real-time endpoint traffic against the training baseline and emit bias-drift metrics to CloudWatch. SageMaker Model Monitor (and therefore Clarify-based bias monitoring) can run either on a recurring schedule or one time, immediately (on-demand); the scheduling docs state 'you can monitor it one time, immediately' using CronExpressionGenerator.now(). To trigger this from the web application on demand, the application invokes an AWS Lambda function that launches the SageMaker Clarify bias-drift job, which satisfies the on-demand requirement against the real-time endpoint while keeping the S3 training data secure and isolated. Therefore A is the only option that uses the correct, purpose-built service (Clarify) for bias drift and supports event-driven, on-demand invocation.","explanation_zh":"在 SageMaker 中,偏差漂移(bias drift)監控是由 SageMaker Clarify 實作的:ModelBiasModelMonitor 會執行 SageMaker Clarify 的 processing job,將即時端點(real-time endpoint)的流量與訓練基準(baseline)比較,並將偏差漂移指標發送到 CloudWatch。SageMaker Model Monitor(因此包含以 Clarify 為基礎的偏差監控)可以採排程定期執行,也可以一次性立即執行(on-demand);scheduling 文件明確指出「you can monitor it one time, immediately」,方法是使用 CronExpressionGenerator.now()。要從 web 應用程式按需觸發,應用程式可呼叫一個 AWS Lambda 函式來啟動 SageMaker Clarify 偏差漂移 job,正好滿足針對即時端點的「on-demand 工作流程」需求,同時讓存於 S3 的訓練資料維持安全與隔離。因此 A 是唯一使用正確且專為偏差漂移設計的服務(Clarify)、並支援事件驅動按需觸發的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Two problems. First, AWS docs explicitly state you cannot pull the built-in sagemaker-model-monitor-analyzer image directly; it is only used internally when you submit a baseline/monitoring job via the SDK. Second, that Spark/Deequ-based image performs data quality and model quality analysis (statistics generation and constraint validation), not bias drift; bias drift uses the SageMaker Clarify image, so this action would not produce bias-drift analysis.","why_zh":"有兩個問題。第一,AWS 文件明確指出無法直接拉取內建映像 sagemaker-model-monitor-analyzer,它只在你透過 SDK 提交 baseline/監控 job 時於內部使用。第二,該以 Spark/Deequ 為基礎的映像是執行資料品質與模型品質分析(產生統計值與驗證限制),並非偏差漂移;偏差漂移使用的是 SageMaker Clarify 映像,因此此動作無法進行偏差漂移分析。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Glue Data Quality measures the quality of data in tables/datasets (completeness, uniqueness, freshness, etc.) within ETL pipelines; it does not compute ML fairness/bias metrics (such as DPPL) or detect bias drift for models deployed to SageMaker real-time endpoints.","why_zh":"AWS Glue Data Quality 用於在 ETL 流程中衡量資料表/資料集的資料品質(完整性、唯一性、新鮮度等),並不會計算 ML 公平性/偏差指標(例如 DPPL),也無法偵測已部署到 SageMaker 即時端點之模型的偏差漂移。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Manually comparing bias in SageMaker notebooks is an ad hoc, human-driven activity, not an automated, repeatable on-demand monitoring workflow that the application can invoke. It lacks the managed Clarify bias-drift processing job, baseline comparison, and CloudWatch metrics/alerts that the requirement implies.","why_zh":"在 SageMaker notebook 中手動比較偏差屬於臨時、需人工操作的做法,並非可由應用程式觸發、可自動且可重複的按需監控工作流程。它缺少受管理的 Clarify 偏差漂移 processing job、baseline 比較,以及需求所暗示的 CloudWatch 指標/警示整合。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-model-monitor-bias-drift.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-model-monitor-bias-drift-schedule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-scheduling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-pre-built-container.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-configure-processing-jobs.html"]}},{"id":5,"question_en":"HOTSPOT A company stores historical data in .csv files in Amazon S3. Only some of the rows and columns in the .csv files are populated. The columns are not labeled. An ML engineer needs to prepare and store the data so that the company can use the data to train ML models. Select and order the correct steps from the following list to perform this task. Each step should be selected one time or not at all. (Select and order three.) • Create an Amazon SageMaker batch transform job for data cleaning and feature engineering. • Store the resulting data back in Amazon S3. • Use Amazon Athena to infer the schemas and available columns. • Use AWS Glue crawlers to infer the schemas and available columns. • Use AWS Glue DataBrew for data cleaning and feature engineering. Hot Area: Correct Answer: Section: (none) Explanation/Reference: Explanation: The correct steps, in order, are: 1. Use AWS Glue crawlers to infer the schemas and available columns. - AWS Glue crawlers can automatically scan the .csv files in Amazon S3, detect the schema, and catalog the data for further processing. 2. Use AWS Glue DataBrew for data cleaning and feature engineering. - AWS Glue DataBrew provides tools for cleaning, transforming, and preparing the data for ML tasks. 3. Store the resulting data back in Amazon S3. - After cleaning and preparing the data, the resulting dataset can be stored back in Amazon S3 for training ML models.","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一款应用程序，用于向客户推荐产品。该应用程序将调用亚马逊 Q 商业版的 API。公 司必须确保亚马逊 Q 商业版的响应中不包含其主要竞争对手的名称。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{},"options_zh":{"A":"在亚马逊 Q 商务中将竞争对手的名称设置为屏蔽词。","B":"配置 Amazon Q Business 检索器以排除竞争对手的名称。","C":"为 Amazon Q Business 配置 Amazon Kendra 检索器，以构建排除竞争对手名称的索引。","D":"在亚马逊 Q 商业版中配置文档属性提升功能，降低竞争对手名称的优先级。"},"answer":[],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":6,"question_en":"HOTSPOT An ML engineer needs to use Amazon SageMaker Feature Store to create and manage features to train a model. Select and order the steps from the following list to create and use the features in Feature Store. Each step should be selected one time. (Select and order three.) • Access the store to build datasets for training. • Create a feature group. • Ingest the records. Hot Area: Correct Answer: Section: (none) Explanation/Reference: Explanation: The correct steps, in order, are: 4. Create a feature group. A feature group defines the schema and structure for the features, serving as a container for storing and organizing features. 5. Ingest the records. Populate the feature group by ingesting data records, which include the features and their associated values. 6. Access the store to build datasets for training. Retrieve features from the Feature Store to construct datasets for model training.","question_zh":"一家公司已使用亚马逊 SageMaker 将一个预测机器学习模型投入生产。该公司正在该模型上使用 SageMaker 模型监控器。在模型更新后，一位机器学习工程师在模型监控器的检查中发现了数据质量问 题。 机器学习工程师应采取哪些措施来缓解模型监控器所识别出的数据质量问题？","options_en":{},"options_zh":{"A":"调整模型的参数和超参数。","B":"手动启动一个模型监控任务，使用最新的生产数据。","C":"从最新的数据集创建新的基准。更新模型监控以使用新的基准进行评估。","D":"在现有的模型训练集中加入更多数据。重新训练并重新部署模型。"},"answer":[],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":7,"question_en":"HOTSPOT A company wants to host an ML model on Amazon SageMaker. An ML engineer is configuring a continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) pipeline in AWS CodePipeline to deploy the model. The pipeline must run automatically when new training data for the model is uploaded to an Amazon S3 bucket. Select and order the pipeline's correct steps from the following list. Each step should be selected one time or not at all. (Select and order three.) • An S3 event notification invokes the pipeline when new data is uploaded. • S3 Lifecycle rule invokes the pipeline when new data is uploaded. • SageMaker retrains the model by using the data in the S3 bucket. • The pipeline deploys the model to a SageMaker endpoint. • The pipeline deploys the model to SageMaker Model Registry. Hot Area: Correct Answer: Section: (none) Explanation/Reference: Explanation: The correct steps, in order, are: 7. An S3 event notification invokes the pipeline when new data is uploaded. Set up an S3 event notification to trigger the pipeline when new training data is added to the S3 bucket. 8. SageMaker retrains the model by using the data in the S3 bucket. The pipeline should include a step to retrain the ML model using the new data in the S3 bucket. 9. The pipeline deploys the model to a SageMaker endpoint. After retraining, the pipeline deploys the updated model to a SageMaker endpoint for inference.","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师在 AWS Glue DataBrew 中使用最小 - 最大标准化方法对训练数据进行了标准化处理。 在将生产推理数据传递给模型进行预测之前，该机器学习工程师必须以与训练数据相同的方式对生产推 理数据进行标准化处理。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{},"options_zh":{"A":"应用知名数据集中的统计数据对生产样本进行标准化处理。","B":"保留训练集中的最小 - 最大归一化统计数据。使用这些值对生产样本进行归一化处理。","C":"从一批生产样本中计算出一组新的最小 - 最大归一化统计值。使用这些值对所有生产样本进行归一化 处理。","D":"从每个生产样本中计算一组新的最小 - 最大标准化统计值。使用这些值对所有生产样本进行标准化。"},"answer":[],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":8,"question_en":"HOTSPOT An ML engineer is building a generative AI application on Amazon Bedrock by using large language models (LLMs). Select the correct generative AI term from the following list for each description. Each term should be selected one time or not at all. • Embedding • Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) • Temperature • Token Hot Area: Correct Answer: Section: (none) Explanation/Reference: Explanation: The correct terms for each description are: 10.Text representation of basic units of data processed by LLMs - Token Tokens are the basic units of text (such as words or subwords) that LLMs process. 11.High-dimensional vectors that contain the semantic meaning of text - Embedding Embeddings are numerical representations of text in high-dimensional space, capturing semantic meaning. 12.Enrichment of information from additional data sources to improve a generated response - Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) RAG involves retrieving relevant information from external data sources to enhance the quality of generated responses.","question_zh":"一家制造公司使用机器学习模型来判定产品是否达到质量标准。该模型会输出“合格”或“不合格”。机 器人通过使用该模型分析装配线上的照片，将产品分为这两类。 公司应使用哪些指标来评估模型的性能？（选择两项。）","options_en":{},"options_zh":{"A":"精确率和召回率","B":"均方根误差（RMSE）和平均绝对百分比误差（MAPE）","C":"准确率和 F1 值","D":"双语评估参考（BLEU）分数","E":"困惑"},"answer":[],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":9,"question_en":"HOTSPOT An ML engineer is working on an ML model to predict the prices of similarly sized homes. The model will base predictions on several features The ML engineer will use the following feature engineering techniques to estimate the prices of the homes: • Feature splitting • Logarithmic transformation • One-hot encoding • Standardized distribution Select the correct feature engineering techniques for the following list of features. Each feature engineering technique should be selected one time or not at all. Hot Area: Correct Answer: Section: (none) Explanation/Reference: Explanation: The correct feature engineering techniques for each feature are: 13.City (name) - One-hot encoding The city name is a categorical feature, so one-hot encoding is used to convert it into a binary vector representation for the model. 14.Type_year (type of home and year the home was built) - Feature splitting This combined feature can be split into two separate features: \"type of home\" and \"year the home was built,\" for more meaningful analysis. 15.Size of the building (square feet or square meters) - Logarithmic transformation Logarithmic transformation can be applied to normalize the distribution if the size has a skewed distribution.","question_zh":"一家公司正在开展一个机器学习项目，该项目将使用亚马逊 SageMaker 笔记本实例。一位机器学习工程师 必须确保 SageMaker 笔记本实例不允许 root 访问。 哪种解决方案可以防止部署允许 root 访问的笔记本实例？","options_en":{},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 IAM 条件键来阻止部署允许 root 访问的 SageMaker 笔记本实例。","B":"使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥来阻止部署允许 root 访问的 SageMaker 笔记本实例。","C":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 事件监控资源创建情况。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于删除所有允许 root 访问的已部署的 SageMaker 笔记本实例。","D":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 事件监控资源创建。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于删除所有允许 root 访问 的已部署的 SageMaker 笔记本实例。"},"answer":[],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":10,"question_en":"Case study An ML engineer is developing a fraud detection model on AWS. The training dataset includes transaction logs, customer profiles, and tables from an on-premises MySQL database. The transaction logs and customer profiles are stored in Amazon S3. The dataset has a class imbalance that affects the learning of the model's algorithm. Additionally, many of the features have interdependencies. The algorithm is not capturing all the desired underlying patterns in the data. Which AWS service or feature can aggregate the data from the various data sources?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用亚马逊 SageMaker 开发机器学习模型。该公司将敏感的训练数据存储在亚马逊 S3 存 储桶中。模型训练必须与互联网网络隔离。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Amazon EMR Spark jobs","B":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams","C":"Amazon DynamoDB","D":"AWS Lake Formation"},"options_zh":{"A":"在私有子网中运行 SageMaker 训练作业。创建一个 NAT 网关。将训练流量通过 NAT 网关进行路由。","B":"在私有子网中运行 SageMaker 训练作业。创建一个 S3 网关 VPC 终端节点。通过 S3 网关 VPC 终端节点 来路由训练流量。","C":"在具有附加安全组的公共子网中运行 SageMaker 训练作业。在安全组中，使用入站规则限制来自互联网 的流量。使用 AWS KMS 密钥（SSE-KMS）对服务器端加密的 SageMaker 实例存储进行加密。","D":"通过使用包含 aws:SecureTransport 条件键值为 True 的存储桶策略来加密到 Amazon S3 的流量。为 Amazon S3 使用默认的静态数据加密。使用 AWS KMS 密钥的服务器端加密（SSE-KMS）来加密 SageMaker 实例存储。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Database","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Lake Formation is purpose-built to break down data silos and combine structured and unstructured data from disparate sources into a centralized, governed data lake. The official documentation states it helps you 'combine different types of structured and unstructured data into a centralized repository,' importing data from databases already in AWS (MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQL Server, MariaDB, Oracle in Amazon RDS or EC2) and moving data from on-premises databases by connecting via JDBC, while unifying data already stored in Amazon S3. That maps directly to the scenario: aggregating S3-based transaction logs and customer profiles together with tables from an on-premises MySQL database into one catalog. The decisive qualifier is the requirement to AGGREGATE data from multiple, heterogeneous sources (S3 + on-premises MySQL), which is Lake Formation's core function. The other options are single-purpose compute (EMR Spark), real-time streaming ingestion (Kinesis Data Streams), or a NoSQL data store (DynamoDB) rather than a service whose purpose is consolidating heterogeneous sources.","explanation_zh":"AWS Lake Formation 的設計目的就是打破資料孤島，將來自不同來源的結構化與非結構化資料彙整到一個集中、受治理的 data lake。官方文件指出它能協助你「將不同類型的結構化與非結構化資料整合到集中式儲存庫」，可從 AWS 中現有的資料庫匯入資料（Amazon RDS 或 EC2 上的 MySQL、PostgreSQL、SQL Server、MariaDB、Oracle），也可透過 JDBC 連線從地端（on-premises）資料庫搬移資料，同時統一已存放在 Amazon S3 的資料。這正好對應情境：把存在 S3 的交易紀錄與客戶資料，連同地端 MySQL 資料庫的資料表，彙整到單一 catalog 中。決定性的條件是要「彙整（aggregate）」來自多個異質來源（S3 + 地端 MySQL）的資料，這正是 Lake Formation 的核心功能。其他選項分別是單一用途的運算引擎（EMR Spark）、即時串流擷取（Kinesis Data Streams），或 NoSQL 資料儲存（DynamoDB），都不是以整合異質來源為目的的服務。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon EMR Spark is a distributed compute/processing engine. Although Spark can read from multiple sources via connectors during a job, EMR is a processing framework, not a managed service whose purpose is to aggregate and catalog heterogeneous data sources (S3 + on-premises MySQL via JDBC) into a centralized, governed location. The question asks which service can aggregate the data, which is Lake Formation's defined role.","why_zh":"Amazon EMR Spark 是分散式運算/處理引擎。雖然 Spark 在作業中可透過連接器讀取多個來源，但 EMR 是處理框架，並非以將異質資料來源（S3 + 透過 JDBC 的地端 MySQL）彙整並編目到集中、受治理位置為目的的受管服務。題目問的是哪個服務能彙整資料，這是 Lake Formation 的職責。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is for real-time streaming data collection and processing. The scenario involves static batch datasets (transaction logs and customer profiles in S3, tables in an on-premises MySQL database), not streaming ingestion, and Kinesis does not aggregate or catalog disparate stored sources.","why_zh":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 用於即時串流資料的收集與處理。本情境是靜態批次資料（S3 的交易紀錄與客戶資料、地端 MySQL 的資料表），並非串流擷取，且 Kinesis 不會彙整或編目分散的既有儲存來源。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon DynamoDB is a fully managed NoSQL key-value/document database, i.e., a single storage destination. It does not aggregate or unify data from multiple heterogeneous sources such as S3 and an on-premises MySQL database into a centralized catalog.","why_zh":"Amazon DynamoDB 是全代管的 NoSQL 鍵值/文件資料庫，屬於單一儲存目的地。它不會把 S3 與地端 MySQL 等多個異質來源的資料彙整或統一到集中式 catalog。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/what-is-lake-formation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/how-it-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/emr/latest/ReleaseGuide/emr-spark.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/Introduction.html"]}},{"id":11,"question_en":"Case study An ML engineer is developing a fraud detection model on AWS. The training dataset includes transaction logs, customer profiles, and tables from an on-premises MySQL database. The transaction logs and customer profiles are stored in Amazon S3. The dataset has a class imbalance that affects the learning of the model's algorithm. Additionally, many of the features have interdependencies. The algorithm is not capturing all the desired underlying patterns in the data. After the data is aggregated, the ML engineer must implement a solution to automatically detect anomalies in the data and to visualize the result. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"机器学习工程师需要确保数据集符合有关个人身份信息（PII）的规定。该机器学习工程师将使用 这些数据在亚马逊 SageMaker 实例上训练机器学习模型。SageMaker 不得使用任何 PII 信息。 哪种解决方案能以最高效的操作方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Athena to automatically detect the anomalies and to visualize the result.","B":"Use Amazon Redshift Spectrum to automatically detect the anomalies. Use Amazon QuickSight to visualize the result.","C":"Use Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler to automatically detect the anomalies and to visualize the result.","D":"Use AWS Batch to automatically detect the anomalies. Use Amazon QuickSight to visualize the result."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Comprehend 的 DetectPiiEntities API 调用从数据中删除个人身份信息（PII）。将数据存 储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。从 SageMaker 实例访问 S3 存储桶以进行模型训练。","B":"使用 Amazon Comprehend 的 DetectPiiEntities API 调用从数据中删除个人身份信息 （PII）。将数据存 储在 Amazon 弹性文件系统 （Amazon EFS） 中。将 EFS 文件系统挂载到 SageMaker 实例上以进行 模型训练。","C":"使用 AWS Glue DataBrew 清理数据集中的个人身份信息（PII）。将数据存储在 Amazon Elastic File System（Amazon EFS）文件系统中。将 EFS 文件系统挂载到 SageMaker 实例上以进行模型训练。","D":"使用 Amazon Macie 自动发现数据中的个人身份信息（PII）。移除 PII。将数据存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。将 S3 存储桶挂载到 SageMaker 实例上以进行模型训练。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"After the data is aggregated, the ML engineer needs one solution that both automatically detects anomalies in the data and visualizes the result, within the ML data-preparation workflow. Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler is the single tool that does both: its built-in exploratory data analysis (EDA) includes a Data Quality and Insights Report that automatically surfaces outliers and uses the isolation forest algorithm to flag anomalous samples, plus a dedicated 'Detect anomalies in time series data' analysis. Data Wrangler also provides built-in visualizations (histograms, scatter plots, target-column histograms, and custom Altair visualizations), so detection and visualization happen in the same tool with no second service required. The other options either pair a non-detector with a detector or use services that have no native anomaly detection: Athena and Redshift Spectrum are SQL query engines with no built-in anomaly detection, and AWS Batch is a batch job scheduler, not an analytics or ML service. Although QuickSight does offer ML-powered anomaly detection, option B incorrectly assigns the detection job to Redshift Spectrum (which cannot detect anomalies), so it does not satisfy the requirement.","explanation_zh":"資料聚合後，ML 工程師需要一個解決方案，能在 ML 資料準備流程中同時「自動偵測資料中的異常」並「將結果視覺化」。Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler 是唯一同時做到兩件事的工具：其內建的探索性資料分析 (EDA) 包含 Data Quality and Insights Report，會自動呈現離群值並以 isolation forest 演算法標記異常樣本，另外還有專門的『Detect anomalies in time series data』分析。Data Wrangler 同時提供內建視覺化（histogram、scatter plot、target column histogram，以及自訂 Altair 視覺化），因此偵測與視覺化都在同一個工具中完成，無需第二個服務。其他選項要麼把偵測工作交給沒有偵測能力的服務，要麼使用本身就沒有原生異常偵測的服務：Athena 與 Redshift Spectrum 是 SQL 查詢引擎，沒有內建異常偵測；AWS Batch 是批次作業排程器，不是分析或 ML 服務。雖然 QuickSight 確實提供 ML-powered anomaly detection，但選項 B 錯誤地把偵測工作指派給 Redshift Spectrum（無法偵測異常），因此無法滿足需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Athena is an interactive SQL query service for S3 data; it has no built-in automatic anomaly detection and no built-in visualization. You would need additional services (e.g., QuickSight) to visualize, so a single Athena solution cannot meet both requirements.","why_zh":"Amazon Athena 是針對 S3 資料的互動式 SQL 查詢服務，沒有內建的自動異常偵測，也沒有內建視覺化。需要額外服務（例如 QuickSight）才能視覺化，因此僅用 Athena 無法同時滿足兩項需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"QuickSight can do ML-powered anomaly detection and visualization, but this option assigns anomaly detection to Amazon Redshift Spectrum, which is only a query layer that lets Redshift read S3 data via external tables. Redshift Spectrum cannot automatically detect anomalies, so the detection half of this solution is technically wrong.","why_zh":"QuickSight 能進行 ML 驅動的異常偵測與視覺化，但此選項把異常偵測指派給 Amazon Redshift Spectrum，而它只是一個讓 Redshift 透過外部表讀取 S3 資料的查詢層，無法自動偵測異常，因此本方案的偵測部分在技術上是錯誤的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Batch is a managed batch-compute orchestration service that runs containerized jobs; it has no native anomaly-detection capability. You would have to build and code the entire detection logic yourself, which contradicts the requirement to 'automatically detect anomalies.'","why_zh":"AWS Batch 是執行容器化作業的受管批次運算編排服務，沒有原生的異常偵測能力。你必須自行建構並撰寫整個偵測邏輯，這與「自動偵測異常」的需求相牴觸。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-analyses.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/quick/latest/userguide/anomaly-detection.html"]}},{"id":12,"question_en":"Case study An ML engineer is developing a fraud detection model on AWS. The training dataset includes transaction logs, customer profiles, and tables from an on-premises MySQL database. The transaction logs and customer profiles are stored in Amazon S3. The dataset has a class imbalance that affects the learning of the model's algorithm. Additionally, many of the features have interdependencies. The algorithm is not capturing all the desired underlying patterns in the data. The training dataset includes categorical data and numerical data. The ML engineer must prepare the training dataset to maximize the accuracy of the model. Which action will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司想要推出一个新的内部生成式人工智能界面来回答用户的问题。该界面将基于一个流行的开源大 型语言模型（LLM）。 哪两种步骤组合能以最低的操作开销部署该接口？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Glue to transform the categorical data into numerical data.","B":"Use AWS Glue to transform the numerical data into categorical data.","C":"Use Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler to transform the categorical data into numerical data.","D":"Use Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler to transform the numerical data into categorical data."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon SageMaker JumpStart 部署大型语言模型。","B":"将 LLM 下载为 .zip 文件。在基于 GPU 的亚马逊 EC2 实例上部署 LLM。","C":"创建一个前端 HTML 接口，该接口使用亚马逊 API 网关 WebSocket API 以及 AWS Lambda 函数来 处理用户交互。","D":"使用 Amazon QuickSight 创建用户界面来处理用户交互。","E":"使用 Amazon Lex 创建一个用户界面来处理用户交互。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Database","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"ML algorithms such as the fraud-detection classifier require numerical input, so the string categorical features must be encoded into numerical representations; encoding the other direction (numerical to categorical) would discard information the model needs, which eliminates B and D. Between AWS Glue and SageMaker Data Wrangler, Data Wrangler is the purpose-built, no-code ML data-preparation tool. Its built-in 'Encode Categorical' transform converts categorical string data into arrays of integers (one-hot and ordinal encoding), and the same tool directly addresses the other issues in the scenario with no-code transforms: 'Balance Data' (random over/undersampling and SMOTE, which the docs illustrate with a fraud-detection example) for the class imbalance, and 'Reduce Dimensionality' (PCA) for the interdependent features. AWS Glue is a general ETL service whose transforms are driven by PySpark/DynamicFrame scripts, so achieving the same encoding requires writing and maintaining custom code. Because the qualifier is LEAST operational overhead, the no-code Data Wrangler transform wins, so the answer is C.","explanation_zh":"詐欺偵測分類器這類 ML 演算法需要數值輸入，因此字串型的類別 (categorical) 特徵必須編碼成數值表示；反方向 (數值轉類別) 會丟失模型所需的資訊，故可排除 B 和 D。在 AWS Glue 與 SageMaker Data Wrangler 之間，Data Wrangler 是專為 ML 資料準備而設計的免寫程式工具。其內建的 'Encode Categorical' transform 可將類別字串資料轉換為整數陣列 (one-hot 與 ordinal encoding)，而且同一工具還能以免寫程式的 transform 直接處理情境中的其他問題：以 'Balance Data' (random over/undersampling 與 SMOTE，AWS 文件正是用詐欺偵測作為範例) 處理類別不平衡，以 'Reduce Dimensionality' (PCA) 處理彼此相依的特徵。AWS Glue 是一般用途的 ETL 服務，其 transform 透過 PySpark/DynamicFrame 腳本驅動，要達到相同編碼需要撰寫並維護自訂程式碼。由於限定條件是 LEAST operational overhead，免寫程式的 Data Wrangler transform 勝出，因此答案是 C。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Right direction (categorical to numerical) but uses AWS Glue, a general ETL service whose transforms are driven by PySpark/DynamicFrame scripts, so it requires writing and maintaining custom code. That is more operational overhead than Data Wrangler's purpose-built no-code 'Encode Categorical' transform, which also natively covers the class-imbalance and feature-interdependency concerns in the scenario.","why_zh":"方向正確 (類別轉數值)，但使用 AWS Glue，一個一般用途的 ETL 服務，其 transform 透過 PySpark/DynamicFrame 腳本驅動，需撰寫並維護自訂程式碼。相較於 Data Wrangler 專用的免寫程式 'Encode Categorical' transform，營運負擔較高；Data Wrangler 還能原生涵蓋情境中的類別不平衡與特徵相依問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Wrong direction. Converting numerical data into categorical discards the granularity the algorithm needs and does not make the data trainable, because ML algorithms require numerical features. It also leaves the original categorical columns unencoded and uses Glue (higher overhead).","why_zh":"方向錯誤。將數值資料轉成類別會丟失演算法所需的精細度，且無法讓資料可供訓練，因為 ML 演算法需要數值特徵。它也未編碼原本的類別欄位，並使用 Glue (負擔較高)。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same wrong-direction conversion as B (numerical to categorical), which removes information the model needs and does not encode the categorical features the algorithm cannot consume. Using Data Wrangler does not fix the fact that the chosen transform itself is the wrong one.","why_zh":"與 B 相同的錯誤方向 (數值轉類別)，會移除模型所需的資訊，且未編碼演算法無法直接使用的類別特徵。即使使用 Data Wrangler，也改變不了所選 transform 本身就是錯的事實。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler-transform.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/aws-glue-programming-python-transforms.html"]}},{"id":13,"question_en":"Case study An ML engineer is developing a fraud detection model on AWS. The training dataset includes transaction logs, customer profiles, and tables from an on-premises MySQL database. The transaction logs and customer profiles are stored in Amazon S3. The dataset has a class imbalance that affects the learning of the model's algorithm. Additionally, many of the features have interdependencies. The algorithm is not capturing all the desired underlying patterns in the data. Before the ML engineer trains the model, the ML engineer must resolve the issue of the imbalanced data. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用亚马逊 S3 存储桶来收集将用于机器学习工作流的数据。该公司需要使用 AWS Glue DataBrew 来清理和规范化这些数据。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Athena to identify patterns that contribute to the imbalance. Adjust the dataset accordingly.","B":"Use Amazon SageMaker Studio Classic built-in algorithms to process the imbalanced dataset.","C":"Use AWS Glue DataBrew built-in features to oversample the minority class.","D":"Use the Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler balance data operation to oversample the minority class."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 S3 路径创建一个 DataBrew 数据集。通过使用 DataBrew 分析作业来清理和规范化数据。","B":"使用 S3 路径创建一个 DataBrew 数据集。通过使用 DataBrew 配方作业来清理和规范化数据。","C":"使用 Java 数据库连接（JDBC）驱动程序连接到 S3 存储桶，创建一个 DataBrew 数据集。通过使用 DataBrew 分析作业来清理和规范化数据。","D":"使用 Java 数据库连接（JDBC）驱动程序连接到 S3 存储桶，创建一个 DataBrew 数据集。通过使用 DataBrew 配方作业对数据进行清理和规范化。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Database","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler provides a built-in, no-code 'Balance data' operation. Its 'Random oversampling' operator randomly duplicates samples in the minority category, and the AWS documentation uses this exact scenario as its example: detecting fraud when only 10% of cases are fraudulent, duplicating those cases to reach an equal proportion (it also offers Random undersampling and SMOTE). Because the engineer is already using Data Wrangler to import and prepare the S3 transaction logs, customer profiles, and JDBC/on-prem MySQL tables, applying a point-and-click balance transform resolves the imbalance BEFORE training with the LEAST operational effort. The other options require manual analysis and custom remediation (Athena), do not address the pre-training data-preparation step (SageMaker built-in algorithms operate at training time), or rely on a feature that does not exist (DataBrew has no oversampling/balance/SMOTE recipe step).","explanation_zh":"Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler 提供內建、無需撰寫程式碼的 'Balance data' 操作。其 'Random oversampling' 運算子會隨機複製少數類別的樣本，AWS 官方文件正是以此情境為範例：偵測詐欺時僅 10% 為詐欺案例，將這些案例複製以使比例相等（同時也提供 Random undersampling 與 SMOTE）。由於工程師本來就使用 Data Wrangler 來匯入並準備 S3 交易日誌、客戶資料及 JDBC/地端 MySQL 資料表，因此套用點選式的平衡轉換能在訓練前以最少的營運工作量解決資料不平衡。其他選項需要手動分析與自訂補救（Athena）、未處理訓練前的資料準備階段（SageMaker 內建演算法作用於訓練階段），或仰賴並不存在的功能（DataBrew 沒有過採樣/平衡/SMOTE 的配方步驟）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Athena is a SQL query service for analyzing data. It can surface patterns but has no native oversampling or balancing capability. 'Adjust the dataset accordingly' implies manual, custom remediation work, which is the opposite of LEAST operational effort.","why_zh":"Amazon Athena 是用於分析資料的 SQL 查詢服務，可呈現模式但沒有原生的過採樣或平衡功能。'依此調整資料集' 意味著手動、自訂的補救工作，與最少營運工作量背道而馳。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"SageMaker built-in algorithms operate at the training stage, not the data-preparation stage. The requirement is explicitly to resolve imbalanced data BEFORE training; built-in algorithms do not provide a pre-training oversampling/balance operation.","why_zh":"SageMaker 內建演算法作用於訓練階段，而非資料準備階段。需求明確要求在訓練前解決資料不平衡；內建演算法不提供訓練前的過採樣/平衡操作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Glue DataBrew offers 250+ transformations, but its data-science recipe steps are only BINARIZATION, BUCKETIZATION, CATEGORICAL_MAPPING, ONE_HOT_ENCODING, SCALE, SKEWNESS, and TOKENIZATION. There is no built-in feature to oversample a minority class or balance an imbalanced dataset, so a 'built-in oversample feature' does not exist in DataBrew.","why_zh":"AWS Glue DataBrew 提供 250+ 種轉換，但其資料科學配方步驟僅有 BINARIZATION、BUCKETIZATION、CATEGORICAL_MAPPING、ONE_HOT_ENCODING、SCALE、SKEWNESS 與 TOKENIZATION。並無對少數類別過採樣或平衡不平衡資料集的內建功能，因此 DataBrew 並不存在 '內建過採樣功能'。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-transform.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/databrew/latest/dg/recipe-actions.data-science.html"]}},{"id":14,"question_en":"Case study An ML engineer is developing a fraud detection model on AWS. The training dataset includes transaction logs, customer profiles, and tables from an on-premises MySQL database. The transaction logs and customer profiles are stored in Amazon S3. The dataset has a class imbalance that affects the learning of the model's algorithm. Additionally, many of the features have interdependencies. The algorithm is not capturing all the desired underlying patterns in the data. The ML engineer needs to use an Amazon SageMaker built-in algorithm to train the model. Which algorithm should the ML engineer use to meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用亚马逊 SageMaker、AWS 拥有的库以及开源库来构建机器学习模型。该公司必须确保 SageMaker 在训练过程中不会收集有关使用情况和错误的元数据。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"LightGBM","B":"Linear learner","C":"K-means clustering","D":"Neural Topic Model (NTM)"},"options_zh":{"A":"将 SageMaker 域与自定义的 IAM 角色相关联。将该角色附加到拒绝使用 Amazon CloudWatch 服务 使用日志的策略上。","B":"向 SageMaker 域添加一个 IAM 角色，以拒绝 Amazon CloudWatch 报告元数据的权限。","C":"关闭 SageMaker 域中用于共享控制台作业元数据的设置。对于通过 AWS CLI 或 AWS SDK 提交的每个 训练作业，选择退出元数据收集。","D":"通过 AWS CLI、Boto3 或 SageMaker Python SDK 提交的每个训练作业，都设置一个参数以选择不收 集元数据。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario gives three decisive signals: a supervised, labeled tabular task (fraud detection), class imbalance, and features with interdependencies that the current algorithm fails to model. This calls for a high-capacity, non-linear tabular classifier. LightGBM is the SageMaker AI built-in Gradient Boosting Decision Tree (GBDT) supervised algorithm; per AWS docs it 'performs well... because of its robust handling of a variety of data types, relationships, distributions,' and supports binary and multiclass classification. Tree-ensemble GBDT models naturally capture non-linear feature interactions/interdependencies and complex underlying patterns, and LightGBM exposes hyperparameters that help with skewed classes. This makes it the strongest fit. Linear learner only learns a linear/linear-threshold function and would be even worse at capturing the missed patterns, while K-means and NTM are unsupervised algorithms (clustering and text topic modeling) that do not fit a supervised, imbalanced tabular classification problem.","explanation_zh":"情境給出三個決定性線索：這是有標籤的監督式表格型任務 (詐欺偵測)、類別不平衡 (class imbalance)，以及目前演算法無法建模的特徵相互依賴 (feature interdependencies)。因此需要表達能力高、非線性的表格型分類器。LightGBM 是 SageMaker AI 內建的 Gradient Boosting Decision Tree (GBDT) 監督式演算法；根據 AWS 文件，它之所以表現優異，是因為能 robustly 處理多種資料型態、關係與分佈 (robust handling of a variety of data types, relationships, distributions)，並支援 binary 與 multiclass 分類。GBDT 樹的集成天生就能捕捉非線性的特徵交互/相互依賴與複雜的底層模式，且 LightGBM 提供可處理類別偏斜的超參數，因此是最佳選擇。相對地，Linear learner 只學習線性/線性閾值函數，捕捉缺失模式的能力只會更差；而 K-means 與 NTM 都是非監督式演算法 (分群與文本主題建模)，不符合有標籤、不平衡的表格型分類問題。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Linear learner only learns a linear function (or a linear-threshold function for classification), per AWS docs. It cannot model non-linear feature interdependencies or complex patterns, so it would be even worse at capturing the underlying patterns the scenario says are already being missed.","why_zh":"根據 AWS 文件，Linear learner 只學習線性函數 (分類時為線性閾值函數)，無法建模非線性的特徵相互依賴或複雜模式，因此對於情境中已被遺漏的底層模式，表現只會更差。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"K-means is an unsupervised clustering algorithm that finds groupings by similarity. Fraud detection with class imbalance is a labeled, supervised classification problem, so K-means does not fit and has no notion of learning labeled patterns or feature interactions.","why_zh":"K-means 是非監督式分群演算法，依相似度尋找群組。具類別不平衡的詐欺偵測是有標籤的監督式分類問題，K-means 不符合需求，也沒有學習有標籤模式或特徵交互的概念。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Neural Topic Model (NTM) is an unsupervised text topic-modeling algorithm that organizes a document corpus into topics. It is designed for documents, not for tabular fraud classification with imbalanced labels and feature interdependencies.","why_zh":"Neural Topic Model (NTM) 是非監督式的文本主題建模演算法，將文件語料組織成主題。它用於文件，而非具不平衡標籤與特徵相互依賴的表格型詐欺分類。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/lightgbm.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/lightgbm-HowItWorks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/linear-learner.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/k-means.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/ntm.html"]}},{"id":15,"question_en":"A company has deployed an XGBoost prediction model in production to predict if a customer is likely to cancel a subscription. The company uses Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor to detect deviations in the F1 score. During a baseline analysis of model quality, the company recorded a threshold for the F1 score. After several months of no change, the model's F1 score decreases significantly. What could be the reason for the reduced F1 score?","question_zh":"一家公司已在生产环境中部署了一个 XGBoost 预测模型，用于预测客户是否可能取消订阅。该公司使用 亚马逊 SageMaker 模型监控器来检测 F1 分数的偏差。 在对模型质量进行基线分析时，该公司记录了 F1 分数的阈值。几个月来一直未发生变化，但之后模型 的 F1 分数显著下降。 F1 分数降低的原因可能是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Concept drift occurred in the underlying customer data that was used for predictions.","B":"The model was not sufficiently complex to capture all the patterns in the original baseline data.","C":"The original baseline data had a data quality issue of missing values.","D":"Incorrect ground truth labels were provided to Model Monitor during the calculation of the baseline."},"options_zh":{"A":"用于预测的底层客户数据发生了概念漂移。","B":"该模型不够复杂，无法涵盖原始基线数据中的所有模式。","C":"原始基线数据存在缺失值的数据质量问题。","D":"在计算基准值期间，提供给模型监控器的正确答案标签有误。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive clue is the temporal pattern: the model's F1 score was stable for several months and then dropped significantly. AWS Machine Learning Lens (MLPERF06-BP04) states that 'model performance could degrade over time' because 'as real-world data changes over time, models can experience data drift (changes in the distribution of input data) or concept drift (changes in the relationship between inputs and target variables).' For a subscription-cancellation classifier, the relationship between customer features and churn behavior evolves over time (new competitors, pricing changes, economic shifts), so a model that performs well for months and then declines is the textbook signature of drift in the production customer data. SageMaker Model Monitor's model-quality job detects this by merging live predictions with Ground Truth labels and comparing them against the recorded F1 baseline threshold. Options describing baseline defects (C, D) or model under-complexity (B) would have produced a poor or skewed F1 from the very start, not a stable period followed by a sudden decrease, so they are inconsistent with the described timeline; A is the only choice that introduces a change occurring after deployment.","explanation_zh":"決定性線索在於時間模式：模型的 F1 score 穩定維持數個月後才顯著下降。AWS Machine Learning Lens（MLPERF06-BP04）指出「模型效能會隨時間退化」，因為「當真實世界資料隨時間變化，模型會遭遇 data drift（輸入資料分佈改變）或 concept drift（輸入與目標變數之間關係的改變）」。對於訂閱取消預測分類器而言，客戶特徵與流失行為之間的關係會隨時間演變（新競爭者、定價、經濟變動），因此模型在數月間表現良好後才退化，正是生產環境客戶資料發生 drift 的典型徵兆。SageMaker Model Monitor 的 model quality 工作會將即時預測與 Ground Truth 標籤合併，並比對記錄的 F1 baseline 門檻來偵測此情況。描述 baseline 缺陷（C、D）或模型複雜度不足（B）的選項，會導致一開始 F1 就偏低或偏差，而非先穩定後驟降，因此與題目描述的時間軸不符；A 是唯一描述部署後才發生變化的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Insufficient model complexity (underfitting) would cause a low F1 score from the start, not stable performance for several months followed by a sudden significant drop.","why_zh":"模型複雜度不足（underfitting）會導致 F1 一開始就偏低，而非穩定數月後才突然大幅下降。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Missing values in the baseline data would have skewed the recorded baseline threshold from day one, so monitoring would have been off from the beginning rather than degrading only after several months of normal operation.","why_zh":"baseline 資料中的缺失值會從一開始就扭曲記錄的門檻，使監控自始就失準，而非在數月正常運作後才退化。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Incorrect Ground Truth labels during baseline calculation would corrupt the threshold immediately and produce wrong results from the start; it cannot explain months of stable F1 followed by a decline.","why_zh":"baseline 計算時使用錯誤的 Ground Truth 標籤會立即污染門檻，自始即產生錯誤結果，無法解釋 F1 先穩定數月後才下降。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/machine-learning-lens/mlperf06-bp04.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/gen-ai-lifecycle-operational-excellence/prod-monitoring-drift.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-model-quality.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor.html"]}},{"id":16,"question_en":"A company has a team of data scientists who use Amazon SageMaker notebook instances to test ML models. When the data scientists need new permissions, the company attaches the permissions to each individual role that was created during the creation of the SageMaker notebook instance. The company needs to centralize management of the team's permissions. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一支数据科学家团队，他们使用亚马逊 SageMaker 笔记本实例来测试机器学习模型。当数据 科学家需要新的权限时，公司会将这些权限附加到在创建 SageMaker 笔记本实例期间创建的每个单独角色 上。 公司需要集中管理团队的权限。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a single IAM role that has the necessary permissions. Attach the role to each notebook instance that the team uses.","B":"Create a single IAM group. Add the data scientists to the group. Associate the group with each notebook instance that the team uses.","C":"Create a single IAM user. Attach the AdministratorAccess AWS managed IAM policy to the user. Configure each notebook instance to use the IAM user.","D":"Create a single IAM group. Add the data scientists to the group. Create an IAM role. Attach the AdministratorAccess AWS managed IAM policy to the role. Associate the role with the group. Associate the group with each notebook instance that the team uses."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个具有必要权限的单一 IAM 角色。将该角色附加到团队使用的每个笔记本实例上。","B":"创建一个单一的 IAM 组。将数据科学家添加到该组中。将该组与团队使用的每个笔记本实例相 关联。","C":"创建一个单一的 IAM 用户。将 AWS 管理的 AdministratorAccess IAM 策略附加到该用户。将每个 笔记本实例配置为使用该 IAM 用户。","D":"创建一个 IAM 组。将数据科学家添加到该组。创建一个 IAM 角色。将 AdministratorAccess AWS 管理的 IAM 策略附加到该角色。将该角色与组关联。将该组与团队使用的每个笔记本实例相关联。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"An Amazon SageMaker notebook instance receives its AWS permissions through a single IAM execution role that the SageMaker service assumes on the user's behalf. When you create a notebook instance, the configuration field is 'IAM role' and it accepts only an IAM role (a role ARN) -- never an IAM group or an IAM user. The company's current pain is that every notebook was created with its own individual role, so each permission change must be repeated across many roles. Creating one shared IAM role that holds only the necessary permissions and attaching it to every notebook instance centralizes management: a single edit to that one role instantly applies to all notebooks, and granting only the permissions the team needs preserves least privilege. This is exactly the supported association model documented for notebook instance execution roles.","explanation_zh":"Amazon SageMaker notebook instance 透過單一的 IAM execution role 取得 AWS 權限,該 role 由 SageMaker 服務代為承擔 (assume)。建立 notebook instance 時,設定欄位是 'IAM role',只接受 IAM role(role ARN),絕對不接受 IAM group 或 IAM user。公司目前的痛點在於每個 notebook 建立時都帶有各自獨立的 role,因此每次調整權限都得在多個 role 上重複操作。建立一個只含必要權限的共用 IAM role,並將它附加到每一個 notebook instance,即可集中管理:只要修改這一個 role 的權限,就會立即套用到所有 notebook,同時只授予團隊實際需要的權限,維持最小權限原則。這正是官方文件中針對 notebook instance execution role 所記載的關聯方式。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"You cannot associate an IAM group with a SageMaker notebook instance. A notebook instance is granted permissions exclusively through an IAM execution role, not a group. IAM groups exist only to organize IAM users for console/API access and are not an execution principal for AWS services, so this configuration is technically impossible.","why_zh":"無法將 IAM group 關聯到 SageMaker notebook instance。Notebook instance 只能透過 IAM execution role 取得權限,而非 group。IAM group 只是用來組織 IAM users 以管理主控台/API 存取,並非 AWS 服務的執行主體(execution principal),因此這個設定在技術上無法成立。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A notebook instance is configured with an IAM execution role, not an IAM user, so 'configure each notebook instance to use the IAM user' is not a valid option. It also attaches AdministratorAccess, which grossly violates least privilege by granting far more than a data science team needs.","why_zh":"Notebook instance 是用 IAM execution role 來設定,而非 IAM user,所以「讓每個 notebook instance 使用該 IAM user」並非有效選項。此外它附加了 AdministratorAccess,授予遠超過資料科學團隊所需的權限,嚴重違反最小權限原則。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is invalid on multiple counts: you cannot 'associate a role with a group', and you cannot associate a group with a notebook instance -- a notebook instance only takes an execution role. It also attaches AdministratorAccess, far more privilege than the team needs. The convoluted group-plus-role wiring described here does not exist in IAM.","why_zh":"這個選項有多處不成立:無法「把 role 關聯到 group」,也無法把 group 關聯到 notebook instance——notebook instance 只接受 execution role。它同樣附加 AdministratorAccess,遠超出團隊所需的權限範圍。文中所述這種 group 加 role 的繞圈接法在 IAM 中根本不存在。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/sagemaker-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/gs-setup-working-env.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/security_iam_service-with-iam.html"]}},{"id":17,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to use an ML model to predict the price of apartments in a specific location. Which metric should the ML engineer use to evaluate the model's performance?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师需要使用一个机器学习模型来预测特定地点的公寓价格。 机器学习工程师应该使用哪个指标来评估模型的性能？","options_en":{"A":"Accuracy","B":"Area Under the ROC Curve (AUC)","C":"F1 score","D":"Mean absolute error (MAE)"},"options_zh":{"A":"准确性","B":"受试者工作特征曲线下的面积（AUC）","C":"F1 值","D":"平均绝对误差（MAE）"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Predicting the price of apartments is predicting a continuous numeric target value, which makes this a regression problem (not classification). Mean absolute error (MAE) is a regression metric: it averages the absolute differences between predicted and actual values, with values ranging from 0 to infinity (smaller is better). The Amazon SageMaker Canvas metrics reference explicitly lists MAE under 'Metrics for numeric prediction' (along with MAPE, MSE, R2, and RMSE). By contrast, Accuracy, AUC, and F1 are all listed under 'Metrics for categorical prediction' (classification), where the target is a discrete class label rather than a continuous number. Therefore MAE is the only appropriate metric among the options for evaluating an apartment-price regression model.","explanation_zh":"預測公寓價格是預測一個連續的數值目標，因此這是一個迴歸（regression）問題，而非分類（classification）問題。Mean absolute error (MAE) 是一個迴歸指標：它計算預測值與實際值之間絕對差異的平均值，數值範圍從 0 到無限大（越小越好）。Amazon SageMaker Canvas 的指標參考文件明確將 MAE 列在「Metrics for numeric prediction」之下（同時還有 MAPE、MSE、R2 和 RMSE）。相對地，Accuracy、AUC 和 F1 都被列在「Metrics for categorical prediction」（分類）之下，其目標是離散的類別標籤，而非連續數值。因此在這些選項中，MAE 是評估公寓價格迴歸模型唯一合適的指標。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Accuracy is a classification metric — the percentage of correct discrete-class predictions. It is meaningless for a continuous price prediction, since predicted prices will almost never exactly equal actual prices. AWS lists Accuracy under 'Metrics for categorical prediction'.","why_zh":"Accuracy 是分類指標，代表離散類別預測正確的百分比。對於連續的價格預測毫無意義，因為預測的價格幾乎不會完全等於實際價格。AWS 將 Accuracy 列在「Metrics for categorical prediction」之下。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Area Under the ROC Curve (AUC) measures how well a binary classifier separates categories (value 0 to 1). It does not apply to a continuous regression target like price. AWS lists AUC under 'Metrics for categorical prediction'.","why_zh":"Area Under the ROC Curve (AUC) 衡量二元分類器區分類別的能力（數值 0 到 1）。它不適用於像價格這樣的連續迴歸目標。AWS 將 AUC 列在「Metrics for categorical prediction」之下。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"F1 score is the harmonic mean of precision and recall — a classification metric that balances class accuracy. It requires discrete class labels and cannot evaluate a continuous numeric prediction. AWS lists F1 under 'Metrics for categorical prediction'.","why_zh":"F1 score 是 precision 與 recall 的調和平均數，屬於平衡類別準確度的分類指標。它需要離散的類別標籤，無法評估連續的數值預測。AWS 將 F1 列在「Metrics for categorical prediction」之下。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/latest/dg/regression-model-insights.html"]}},{"id":18,"question_en":"An ML engineer has trained a neural network by using stochastic gradient descent (SGD). The neural network performs poorly on the test set. The values for training loss and validation loss remain high and show an oscillating pattern. The values decrease for a few epochs and then increase for a few epochs before repeating the same cycle. What should the ML engineer do to improve the training process?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师使用随机梯度下降（SGD）训练了一个神经网络。该神经网络在测试集上的表现不 佳。训练损失和验证损失的值一直较高，并呈现出波动的模式。这些值会在几个周期内下降，然后又在 几个周期内上升，如此循环往复。 机器学习工程师应该采取什么措施来改进训练过程？","options_en":{"A":"Introduce early stopping.","B":"Increase the size of the test set.","C":"Increase the learning rate.","D":"Decrease the learning rate."},"options_zh":{"A":"引入提前停止机制。","B":"增大测试集的规模。","C":"提高学习率。","D":"降低学习率。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The symptom is an optimization (convergence) problem, not overfitting: BOTH training loss and validation loss stay high and oscillate, decreasing for a few epochs then increasing in a repeating cycle. (Overfitting instead shows training loss falling while validation loss rises - a widening gap, which is not the case here.) This bouncing, non-converging pattern is the classic signature of a learning rate that is too large in Stochastic Gradient Descent. AWS's Amazon Machine Learning documentation states that in SGD 'Too large a learning rate might prevent the weights from approaching the optimal solution' because the update steps controlled by the learning rate overshoot the minimum on each pass, sending the loss up and down instead of settling. Decreasing the learning rate makes the weight updates smaller so the optimizer can descend into and stay near the minimum, removing the oscillation and lowering loss. Therefore the engineer should decrease the learning rate.","explanation_zh":"此症狀是優化（收斂）問題，而非過度擬合：training loss 與 validation loss 兩者都維持偏高且呈震盪，先下降幾個 epoch 再上升，循環往復。（過度擬合的特徵是 training loss 下降但 validation loss 上升、兩者差距擴大，與此處不符。）這種來回跳動、無法收斂的模式正是 Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD) 中 learning rate 過大的典型特徵。AWS 的 Amazon Machine Learning 文件指出，在 SGD 中『learning rate 過大可能使權重無法接近最佳解』，因為由 learning rate 控制的更新步幅每次都越過最小值，導致 loss 上下震盪而無法穩定下來。降低 learning rate 可縮小權重更新幅度，使優化器能下降並停留在最小值附近，消除震盪並降低 loss。因此工程師應降低 learning rate。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Early stopping is a remedy for overfitting (training loss low and falling while validation loss rises). Here both losses are high and oscillate together, so there is no clean point to stop at and stopping does not fix the underlying non-convergence caused by the too-large learning rate.","why_zh":"Early stopping 是用來解決過度擬合（training loss 低且持續下降，但 validation loss 上升）。此處兩種 loss 都偏高且一起震盪，沒有適當的停止點，且停止也無法修正由 learning rate 過大造成的不收斂根因。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Test set size affects only how reliably you evaluate the final model; it has zero effect on training dynamics or the oscillating training/validation loss. It does not address the optimization problem.","why_zh":"test set 大小只影響最終模型評估的可靠度，對訓練動態或震盪的 training/validation loss 毫無作用，無法解決此優化問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Increasing the learning rate makes the overshoot and oscillation worse, pushing the optimizer further from the minimum. It is the opposite of the correct fix.","why_zh":"增加 learning rate 會使越過最小值與震盪更嚴重，讓優化器離最小值更遠，與正確修正方向完全相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/latest/dg/training-parameters1.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/latest/dg/learning-algorithm.html"]}},{"id":19,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to process thousands of existing CSV objects and new CSV objects that are uploaded. The CSV objects are stored in a central Amazon S3 bucket and have the same number of columns. One of the columns is a transaction date. The ML engineer must query the data based on the transaction date. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师需要处理数千个现有的 CSV 对象以及新上传的 CSV 对象。这些 CSV 对象存储在中 央的亚马逊 S3 存储桶中，并且具有相同数量的列。其中一列是交易日期。该机器学习工程师必须根据 交易日期查询数据。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an Amazon Athena CREATE TABLE AS SELECT (CTAS) statement to create a table based on the transaction date from data in the central S3 bucket. Query the objects from the table.","B":"Create a new S3 bucket for processed data. Set up S3 replication from the central S3 bucket to the new S3 bucket. Use S3 Object Lambda to query the objects based on transaction date.","C":"Create a new S3 bucket for processed data. Use AWS Glue for Apache Spark to create a job to query the CSV objects based on transaction date. Configure the job to store the results in the new S3 bucket. Query the objects from the new S3 bucket.","D":"Create a new S3 bucket for processed data. Use Amazon Data Firehose to transfer the data from the central S3 bucket to the new S3 bucket. Configure Firehose to run an AWS Lambda function to query the data based on transaction date."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Athena 的 CREATE TABLE AS SELECT（CTAS）语句，根据中央 S3 存储桶中的数据中 的交易日期创建一个表。从该表中查询对象。","B":"为处理后的数据创建一个新的 S3 存储桶。设置从中央 S3 存储桶到新 S3 存储桶的 S3 复制。使用 S3 对象 Lambda 根据交易日期查询对象。","C":"为处理后的数据创建一个新的 S3 存储桶。使用 AWS Glue 配合 Apache Spark 创建一个作业，根据交易日 期查询 CSV 对象。配置该作业将结果存储在新的 S3 存储桶中。从新的 S3 存储桶中查询对象。","D":"创建一个用于处理后数据的新 S3 存储桶。使用 Amazon Data Firehose 将数据从中央 S3 存储桶传输到新 S3 存储桶。配置 Firehose 运行一个 AWS Lambda 函数，根据交易日期查询数据。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Athena is a serverless, schema-on-read query service. As the Athena docs state, creating a table 'simply describes the schema and the location where the table data are located in Amazon S3 for read-time querying,' and this schema-on-read approach 'eliminates the need for data loading or transformation.' That means you can run SQL directly against the CSV objects already in the central S3 bucket and filter by the transaction-date column with no new infrastructure and no custom code. Option A (a CTAS statement) is the only presented choice that uses this low-overhead serverless pattern, so it is the LEAST operational overhead. Option C (Glue for Apache Spark) works technically but requires writing/maintaining Spark ETL code, managing a job, and an extra bucket. Options B and D are architecturally wrong: S3 Object Lambda only transforms the output of individual S3 GET/LIST/HEAD requests per object (and is no longer broadly available for new customers as of Nov 2025), and Amazon Data Firehose is a streaming-delivery service whose only auto-read source is a Kinesis data stream, not an existing S3 bucket, and it does not query data. The one imperfection of CTAS is that it materializes a one-time snapshot to a new S3 location, so newly uploaded objects do not auto-appear (a plain CREATE EXTERNAL TABLE on the bucket LOCATION would be cleaner); but since no plain external table is offered, A remains the best, lowest-overhead, and most architecturally valid choice.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Athena 是無伺服器、schema-on-read 的查詢服務。如 Athena 文件所述，建立資料表只是「描述結構描述以及資料在 Amazon S3 中的位置以供讀取時查詢」，而這種 schema-on-read 方式「不需要載入或轉換資料」。因此可直接對中央 S3 bucket 中既有的 CSV 物件執行 SQL，並依交易日期欄位篩選，無需新增基礎設施或自訂程式碼。選項 A（CTAS 陳述式）是四個選項中唯一採用此低負擔無伺服器模式的方案，因此運維負擔最低。選項 C（Glue for Apache Spark）技術上可行，但須撰寫與維護 Spark ETL 程式碼、管理作業並建立額外 bucket。選項 B 與 D 架構錯誤：S3 Object Lambda 只會以單一物件為單位轉換 S3 GET/LIST/HEAD 請求的輸出（且自 2025 年 11 月起已不再對新客戶廣泛開放），而 Amazon Data Firehose 是串流傳遞服務，其唯一可自動讀取的來源是 Kinesis data stream，而非既有 S3 bucket，且本身不做查詢。CTAS 的一個瑕疵是它會將一次性快照具體化（materialize）到新的 S3 位置，因此之後新上傳的物件不會自動出現（若用單純的 CREATE EXTERNAL TABLE 指向 bucket LOCATION 會更乾淨）；但由於沒有提供單純的 external table 選項，A 仍是最佳、負擔最低且架構最正確的選擇。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 Object Lambda only transforms the bytes of individual objects on S3 GET/LIST/HEAD requests for the requesting client; it cannot perform SQL-style filtering across thousands of objects by a column value. Adding S3 replication to a second bucket also increases overhead, and the feature is no longer generally available to new customers as of Nov 2025.","why_zh":"S3 Object Lambda 只會在 S3 GET/LIST/HEAD 請求時為呼叫端轉換「單一物件」的位元組，無法跨數千個物件依欄位值做 SQL 式篩選。再加上設定 S3 replication 到第二個 bucket 也增加運維負擔，且該功能自 2025 年 11 月起已不再對新客戶開放。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An AWS Glue for Apache Spark ETL job requires writing/maintaining Spark code, managing a job, provisioning a new output bucket, and re-running the job to capture newly uploaded objects, which is significantly more operational overhead than a serverless Athena SQL query.","why_zh":"AWS Glue for Apache Spark 的 ETL 作業需要撰寫/維護 Spark 程式碼、管理作業、配置新的輸出 bucket，並重新執行作業才能納入新上傳的物件，比起無伺服器的 Athena SQL 查詢運維負擔高出許多。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Data Firehose is a streaming-delivery service; its only auto-read source is a Kinesis data stream, not an existing S3 bucket, so it cannot transfer objects between buckets, and it cannot 'query' data by column value. Using a Lambda function to query by date here is an architectural mismatch and adds heavy pipeline overhead.","why_zh":"Amazon Data Firehose 是串流傳遞服務；其唯一可自動讀取的來源是 Kinesis data stream，而非既有 S3 bucket，因此無法在 bucket 間搬移物件，也無法依欄位值「查詢」資料。此處用 Lambda 函式依日期查詢在架構上不相符，且增加大量管線負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/creating-tables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/create-table-as.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/transforming-objects.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html"]}},{"id":20,"question_en":"A company has a large, unstructured dataset. The dataset includes many duplicate records across several key attributes. Which solution on AWS will detect duplicates in the dataset with the LEAST code development?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个庞大的非结构化数据集。该数据集在多个关键属性上包含许多重复记录。 在 AWS 上，哪种解决方案能以最少的代码开发量检测数据集中的重复项？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Mechanical Turk jobs to detect duplicates.","B":"Use Amazon QuickSight ML Insights to build a custom deduplication model.","C":"Use Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler to pre-process and detect duplicates.","D":"Use the AWS Glue FindMatches transform to detect duplicates."},"options_zh":{"A":"利用亚马逊机械土耳其人平台的任务来检测重复项。","B":"使用 Amazon QuickSight ML Insights 构建自定义去重模型。","C":"使用 Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler 进行预处理并检测重复项。","D":"使用 AWS Glue 的 FindMatches 转换来检测重复项。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The question asks for the solution that detects duplicate records spanning several key attributes in a large, unstructured (messy) dataset with the LEAST code development. AWS Glue's FindMatches ML transform (a Lake Formation record-matching transform) is purpose-built for this. The official AWS documentation states verbatim that FindMatches 'enables you to identify duplicate or matching records in your dataset, even when the records do not have a common unique identifier and no fields match exactly. This will not require writing any code or knowing how machine learning works.' You teach the transform by labeling example match/non-match pairs in the console, so it handles fuzzy, non-exact duplicates across multiple attributes with essentially no code. This directly matches both qualifiers ('duplicates across several key attributes' and 'LEAST code development'). The other options either require heavy manual/custom effort (Mechanical Turk, a non-existent custom QuickSight model) or only handle exact, value-for-value matches (Data Wrangler Drop Duplicates uses Spark dropDuplicates and is case sensitive), so D is the clear best fit.","explanation_zh":"本題要求在大型、非結構化（雜亂）資料集中偵測橫跨多個關鍵屬性的重複記錄，且需「最少的程式開發」(LEAST code)。AWS Glue 的 FindMatches ML transform（屬於 Lake Formation 的 record-matching 轉換）正是為此而生。官方 AWS 文件原文指出，FindMatches『可讓您識別資料集中的重複或相符記錄，即使這些記錄沒有共同的唯一識別碼、且沒有欄位完全相符。這不需要撰寫任何程式碼，也不需要了解機器學習如何運作。』您只需在主控台中標記範例的相符／不相符配對來「教導」此轉換，因此能在幾乎不寫程式的情況下處理橫跨多屬性的模糊（非完全相符）重複。這直接吻合兩個關鍵詞（「橫跨多個關鍵屬性的重複」與「最少程式開發」）。其他選項要嘛需要大量人工／自訂開發（Mechanical Turk、不存在的 QuickSight 自訂模型），要嘛只能處理逐值完全相符的重複（Data Wrangler 的 Drop Duplicates 使用 Spark dropDuplicates 且區分大小寫），因此 D 是明確的最佳解。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Mechanical Turk is a human-in-the-loop crowdsourcing marketplace, not an automated de-duplication service. Building MTurk HIT workflows and aggregating results requires significant custom code and orchestration, and does not scale economically to a large dataset, so it is the opposite of 'least code'.","why_zh":"Amazon Mechanical Turk 是人力眾包平台，並非自動去重複服務。建立 MTurk HIT 工作流程並彙整結果需要大量自訂程式與協調，且對大型資料集既不經濟也不易擴展，與『最少程式碼』背道而馳。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"QuickSight ML Insights provides built-in anomaly detection, forecasting, and auto-narratives for BI dashboards. It does NOT let you 'build a custom deduplication model'; the option describes a capability that does not exist, and any custom model would imply substantial development effort anyway.","why_zh":"QuickSight ML Insights 提供 BI 儀表板的內建異常偵測、預測與自動敘述功能，並不能讓你『建立自訂去重複模型』；此選項描述了不存在的功能，且任何自訂模型本來就意味著大量開發工作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SageMaker Data Wrangler can drop duplicates, but its Drop Duplicates transform only removes rows that match EXACTLY (case-sensitive, value-for-value via Spark dropDuplicates) on entire rows or specified keys. It cannot detect fuzzy/non-exact duplicates 'across several key attributes' in an unstructured dataset, which is precisely what FindMatches handles with no code.","why_zh":"SageMaker Data Wrangler 可去除重複，但其 Drop Duplicates transform 只能移除「完全相符」(區分大小寫、透過 Spark dropDuplicates 逐值相符) 的整列或指定鍵的列，無法偵測非結構化資料中跨多個關鍵屬性的模糊／非精確重複，而那正是 FindMatches 無需程式即可處理的情境。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/machine-learning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/machine-learning-transform-tutorial.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/console-machine-learning-transforms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker-unified-studio/latest/userguide/drop-duplicates-transform.html"]}},{"id":21,"question_en":"A company needs to run a batch data-processing job on Amazon EC2 instances. The job will run during the weekend and will take 90 minutes to finish running. The processing can handle interruptions. The company will run the job every weekend for the next 6 months. Which EC2 instance purchasing option will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司需要在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行一个批处理数据处理任务。该任务将在周末运行，完成需要 90 分 钟。处理过程可以中断。该公司将在接下来的 6 个月内每个周末都运行此任务。 哪种 EC2 实例购买选项能以最具成本效益的方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Spot Instances","B":"Reserved Instances","C":"On-Demand Instances","D":"Dedicated Instances"},"options_zh":{"A":"按需实例","B":"预留实例","C":"按需实例","D":"专用实例"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The workload is explicitly interruption-tolerant, short (90 minutes), and runs only on weekends for 6 months. EC2 Spot Instances are purpose-built for exactly this profile: the Spot product page describes them as a way to 'run fault-tolerant workloads for up to 90% off' On-Demand pricing, and the AWS Batch best-practices guidance says to use Spot when 'you can tolerate potential interruptions and job rescheduling.' Because the job 'can handle interruptions,' the steep Spot discount is available, making Spot the MOST cost-effective option. Reserved Instances apply a billing discount only in exchange for a 1- or 3-year commitment to a specific instance configuration, which is wasteful for a job that runs ~90 minutes once per week. On-Demand has no commitment but charges the highest per-hour rate and ignores the workload's interruption tolerance, and Dedicated Instances add a single-tenant hardware premium meant for compliance/licensing isolation rather than cost savings. Therefore A is correct.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載明確可容忍中斷、執行時間短（90 分鐘），且只在週末執行、為期 6 個月。EC2 Spot Instances 正是為這種情境設計：Spot 產品頁將其描述為「以最高省 90% 的價格執行可容錯（fault-tolerant）工作負載」，而 AWS Batch 最佳實務指引也指出，當「可以容忍潛在中斷與工作重新排程」時應使用 Spot。由於此工作「可處理中斷」，便能取得 Spot 的大幅折扣，使其成為最具成本效益的選項。Reserved Instances 只有在承諾 1 年或 3 年、且綁定特定執行個體組態時才提供折扣，對於每週僅執行約 90 分鐘的工作而言極為浪費。On-Demand 雖無承諾，但每小時費率最高，且未利用此工作的可中斷特性；Dedicated Instances 則因單一租戶硬體而有額外溢價，用途在於合規/授權隔離而非節省成本。因此正確答案為 A。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Reserved Instances require a 1- or 3-year commitment to a specific instance configuration for a billing discount; paying for continuous reserved capacity to cover a ~90-minute weekly job is highly wasteful and not cost-effective.","why_zh":"Reserved Instances 需承諾 1 年或 3 年並綁定特定執行個體組態才能取得折扣；為了僅每週約 90 分鐘的工作支付持續性的預留容量極為浪費，並不具成本效益。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"On-Demand has no commitment but charges the highest per-hour rate and does not leverage the workload's interruption tolerance, so it is not the MOST cost-effective choice.","why_zh":"On-Demand 無需承諾但每小時費率最高，且未利用此工作可容忍中斷的特性，因此並非最具成本效益的選擇。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Dedicated Instances run on single-tenant hardware at a premium intended for compliance or licensing isolation, which increases cost rather than optimizing it.","why_zh":"Dedicated Instances 在單一租戶硬體上執行並有額外溢價，用途為合規或授權隔離，會增加成本而非優化成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/cost-optimization-leveraging-ec2-spot-instances/when-to-use-spot-instances.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/batch/latest/userguide/bestpractice5.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/batch/latest/userguide/bestpractice6.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/cost-optimization-reservation-models/reserved-instances-payment-options.html"]}},{"id":22,"question_en":"An ML engineer has an Amazon Comprehend custom model in Account A in the us-east-1 Region. The ML engineer needs to copy the model to Account B in the same Region. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST development effort?","question_zh":"","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon S3 to make a copy of the model. Transfer the copy to Account B.","B":"Create a resource-based IAM policy. Use the Amazon Comprehend ImportModel API operation to copy the model to Account B.","C":"Use AWS DataSync to replicate the model from Account A to Account B.","D":"Create an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection between Account A and Account B to transfer the model."},"options_zh":{},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Comprehend provides a purpose-built, fully managed capability to copy a trained custom model (custom classifier or custom entity recognizer) between AWS accounts in the same Region, which is exactly the scenario here (Account A to Account B, both in us-east-1). The process has two steps: in Account A the owner attaches a resource-based IAM policy to the model version (using comprehend:PutResourcePolicy) authorizing an entity in Account B, and in Account B the user calls the Amazon Comprehend ImportModel API to create a fully-trained duplicate model. The importer does not need to access or copy the original training data, and the model must be imported into the same Region as the original. This matches option B precisely and requires the least development effort because it is native managed functionality. The other options fail because a Comprehend custom model is not an object or file the customer can directly access; it lives inside the managed service, so generic data-transfer mechanisms (S3 copy, DataSync, VPN) cannot move it.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Comprehend 提供專門設計的全代管功能，可在同一個 Region 內的不同 AWS 帳戶之間複製已訓練的 custom model（custom classifier 或 custom entity recognizer），這正是本題的情境（Account A 複製到 Account B，皆位於 us-east-1）。流程分為兩步：在 Account A，擁有者對 model version 附加 resource-based IAM policy（使用 comprehend:PutResourcePolicy）授權 Account B 的實體；在 Account B，使用者呼叫 Amazon Comprehend 的 ImportModel API，建立一份完整訓練好的複製模型。匯入者不需要存取或複製原始訓練資料，且必須在與原始模型相同的 Region 匯入。這完全對應選項 B，且因為是原生代管功能，開發工作量最少。其他選項不可行，因為 Comprehend custom model 並非客戶可直接存取的物件或檔案，它存在於代管服務內部，因此一般的資料傳輸機制（S3 複製、DataSync、VPN）都無法移動它。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A Comprehend custom model is a managed resource inside the service, not a file the customer can download and place in S3. There is no supported way to export the trained model artifact to S3 and re-import it as a usable Comprehend model; the native ImportModel flow is the intended mechanism. Copying training data and retraining would require far more effort.","why_zh":"Comprehend custom model 是服務內部的代管資源，並非客戶可下載並放入 S3 的檔案。並無支援將已訓練模型匯出到 S3 再匯入為可用 Comprehend 模型的方式；原生 ImportModel 流程才是設計的機制。若改為複製訓練資料再重新訓練，工作量更大。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS DataSync transfers files/objects between storage systems (NFS, SMB, HDFS, S3, EFS, FSx). A Comprehend custom model is not an accessible file or object in storage, so DataSync cannot replicate it between accounts.","why_zh":"AWS DataSync 用於在儲存系統（NFS、SMB、HDFS、S3、EFS、FSx）之間傳輸檔案或物件。Comprehend custom model 並非儲存中可存取的檔案或物件，因此 DataSync 無法在帳戶之間複製它。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Site-to-Site VPN establishes encrypted network connectivity (typically on-premises to a VPC); it is not a mechanism for copying a managed Comprehend model between two AWS accounts and would add significant, irrelevant setup effort.","why_zh":"Site-to-Site VPN 建立的是加密網路連線（通常是地端到 VPC），並非在兩個 AWS 帳戶之間複製代管 Comprehend 模型的機制，且會增加大量無關的設定工作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/custom-copy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/custom-copy-sharing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/custom-copy-importing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/APIReference/API_ImportModel.html"]}},{"id":23,"question_en":"An ML engineer is training a simple neural network model. The ML engineer tracks the performance of the model over time on a validation dataset. The model's performance improves substantially at first and then degrades after a specific number of epochs. Which solutions will mitigate this problem? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师正在训练一个简单的神经网络模型。该工程师通过验证数据集跟踪模型随时间推移的 表现。起初模型的表现大幅提高，但在经过特定数量的训练周期后开始下降。 哪些解决方案可以缓解这个问题？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable early stopping on the model.","B":"Increase dropout in the layers.","C":"Increase the number of layers.","D":"Increase the number of neurons.","E":"Investigate and reduce the sources of model bias."},"options_zh":{"A":"在模型上启用提前停止功能。","B":"增加各层的丢弃率。","C":"增加层数。","D":"增加神经元的数量。","E":"调查并减少模型偏差的来源。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The pattern described -- validation performance improves substantially, then degrades after a specific number of epochs while training continues -- is the textbook signature of overfitting. The SageMaker training/validation curve page states this explicitly: 'if training accuracy continues to increase over time, but, at some point, validation accuracy starts to decrease, you are likely overfitting your model. To address this, you can make adjustments to your model, such as increasing regularization.' Early stopping (A) directly mitigates this: AWS documents that 'stopping training jobs early ... helps you avoid overfitting your model,' because it halts training at the point of best validation performance before degradation sets in. Increasing dropout (B) is a regularization technique that reduces overfitting by preventing co-adaptation of neurons; the Amazon ML overfitting guidance prescribes 'increase the amount of regularization used,' and SageMaker deep-learning algorithms expose dropout/dropout_rate hyperparameters for exactly this purpose. Options C and D (more layers/neurons) increase model capacity and flexibility, which worsens overfitting -- the opposite of what AWS recommends (reduce flexibility / increase regularization); option E targets model bias (an underfitting / fairness axis), which is unrelated to this high-variance problem.","explanation_zh":"題目描述的現象 -- 驗證集表現先大幅提升、訓練持續進行到某個 epoch 後卻開始劣化 -- 正是 overfitting（過度擬合）的典型徵兆。SageMaker 的 training/validation curve 文件明確指出：當訓練準確度持續上升、但驗證準確度在某個時間點開始下降時，模型很可能在過度擬合，可透過增加 regularization 來改善。Early stopping（A）直接緩解此問題：AWS 文件說明 early stopping「有助於避免模型過度擬合」，因為它會在驗證表現最佳的時點停止訓練，避免後續劣化。增加 dropout（B）是一種 regularization 技術，藉由防止神經元共適應來降低過度擬合；Amazon ML 對抗 overfitting 的建議即為「增加 regularization 的使用量」，而 SageMaker 的深度學習演算法也正是為此提供 dropout/dropout_rate 超參數。C 與 D（增加層數／神經元）會提高模型容量與彈性，反而加劇過度擬合，與 AWS 建議的修正方向（降低彈性／增加 regularization）相反；E 針對 model bias（屬於欠擬合／公平性面向），與此高變異問題無關。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Increasing the number of layers raises model capacity and flexibility, which makes overfitting worse, not better -- the opposite of the corrective action AWS recommends (reduce flexibility / increase regularization).","why_zh":"增加層數會提高模型容量與彈性，使過度擬合更嚴重，與 AWS 建議的修正方向（降低彈性／增加 regularization）相反。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Increasing the number of neurons also increases model capacity and flexibility, amplifying overfitting rather than mitigating it.","why_zh":"增加神經元數量同樣提高模型容量與彈性，會放大過度擬合而非緩解。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Reducing sources of model bias addresses underfitting or fairness concerns. The scenario is a high-variance overfitting problem (good then degrading validation performance), so bias reduction does not target the actual cause.","why_zh":"降低模型 bias 來源是針對欠擬合或公平性問題。本題是高變異的過度擬合問題（驗證表現先好後劣），降低 bias 並未對應真正的成因。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/train-valid-curve.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/automatic-model-tuning-early-stopping.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/latest/dg/model-fit-underfitting-vs-overfitting.html"]}},{"id":24,"question_en":"A company has a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) application that uses a vector database to store embeddings of documents. The company must migrate the application to AWS and must implement a solution that provides semantic search of text files. The company has already migrated the text repository to an Amazon S3 bucket. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款检索增强生成（RAG）应用程序，该程序使用向量数据库来存储文档的嵌入。该公司 必须将此应用程序迁移到 AWS，并且必须实现一种能够对文本文件进行语义搜索的解决方案。该公司已 经将文本库迁移到了一个 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an AWS Batch job to process the files and generate embeddings. Use AWS Glue to store the embeddings. Use SQL queries to perform the semantic searches.","B":"Use a custom Amazon SageMaker notebook to run a custom script to generate embeddings. Use SageMaker Feature Store to store the embeddings. Use SQL queries to perform the semantic searches.","C":"Use the Amazon Kendra S3 connector to ingest the documents from the S3 bucket into Amazon Kendra. Query Amazon Kendra to perform the semantic searches.","D":"Use an Amazon Textract asynchronous job to ingest the documents from the S3 bucket. Query Amazon Textract to perform the semantic searches."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Batch 作业处理文件并生成嵌入向量。使用 AWS Glue 存储嵌入向量。使用 SQL 查询 执行语义搜索。","B":"使用自定义的 Amazon SageMaker 笔记本运行自定义脚本以生成嵌入向量。使用 SageMaker 特征 存储来存储嵌入向量。使用 SQL 查询执行语义搜索。","C":"使用 Amazon Kendra 的 S3 连接器将文档从 S3 存储桶导入到 Amazon Kendra 中。查询 Amazon Kendra 以执行语义搜索。","D":"使用 Amazon Textract 异步作业从 S3 存储桶中导入文档。查询 Amazon Textract 以执行语义搜 索。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Amazon Kendra is a managed intelligent search and retrieval service that, unlike traditional keyword-based search, uses semantic and contextual similarity to decide whether a document or text chunk is relevant to a query; the Basic Enterprise Edition explicitly provides semantic search capabilities and the GenAI Enterprise Edition is purpose-built for RAG. Kendra also offers a native Amazon S3 connector that ingests and indexes documents directly from an S3 bucket, so for a text repository already in S3 you simply point the S3 connector at the bucket and then query Kendra to get semantically ranked results. This makes Option C the fully managed, lowest-operational-overhead fit for semantic search of text files already in S3. The other options either misuse a service that cannot run semantic queries (Textract is OCR/text extraction) or stitch together storage and SQL that cannot perform vector/semantic similarity search through the stated query mechanism.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Kendra 是一個受管的智慧搜尋與檢索服務，與傳統的關鍵字搜尋不同，它利用語意與上下文相似度來判斷某份文件或文字片段是否與查詢相關；Basic Enterprise Edition 明確提供 semantic search 能力，而 GenAI Enterprise Edition 更是專為 RAG 設計。Kendra 也提供原生的 Amazon S3 connector，可直接從 S3 bucket 擷取並建立文件索引，因此對於已存放在 S3 的文字資料庫，只需將 S3 connector 指向該 bucket，再向 Kendra 送出查詢即可取得依語意排序的結果。這使得選項 C 成為對「已在 S3 的文字檔進行語意搜尋」最受管化、最低營運負擔的方案。其他選項不是誤用無法執行語意查詢的服務（Textract 只是 OCR/文字擷取），就是拼湊了無法透過所述查詢機制進行向量/語意相似度搜尋的儲存與 SQL。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Glue is an ETL/data-catalog service and is not a vector store; SQL queries over a Glue catalog cannot perform vector similarity (semantic) search, so this pipeline does not deliver semantic search.","why_zh":"AWS Glue 是 ETL/資料目錄服務，並非向量儲存；對 Glue 目錄執行 SQL 查詢無法進行向量相似度（語意）搜尋，因此此流程無法實現語意搜尋。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"SageMaker Feature Store stores ML features for training/inference, not as a vector database for similarity search, and standard SQL queries cannot perform nearest-neighbor semantic search over embeddings; it is also high operational overhead with a custom script.","why_zh":"SageMaker Feature Store 用於儲存訓練/推論的 ML 特徵，並非用於相似度搜尋的向量資料庫，且標準 SQL 查詢無法對嵌入向量做最近鄰語意搜尋；自訂腳本也帶來較高營運負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Textract is an OCR/text-detection and document-analysis service; its asynchronous jobs and Queries feature extract text or specific fields from individual documents, but Textract has no search index and cannot be queried to perform semantic search across a document repository.","why_zh":"Amazon Textract 是 OCR/文字偵測與文件分析服務；其非同步作業與 Queries 功能用於從個別文件擷取文字或特定欄位，但 Textract 並無搜尋索引，無法被查詢以對文件庫執行語意搜尋。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kendra/latest/dg/what-is-kendra.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kendra/latest/dg/data-source-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/textract/latest/dg/what-is.html"]}},{"id":25,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon Athena to query a dataset in Amazon S3. The dataset has a target variable that the company wants to predict. The company needs to use the dataset in a solution to determine if a model can predict the target variable. Which solution will provide this information with the LEAST development effort?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 Athena 查询存储在亚马逊 S3 中的数据集。该数据集包含一个目标变量，该公司希 望对其进行预测。 该公司需要在解决方案中使用该数据集来确定模型是否能够预测目标变量。 哪种解决方案能以最少的开发工作量提供这些信息？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new model by using Amazon SageMaker Autopilot. Report the model's achieved performance.","B":"Implement custom scripts to perform data pre-processing, multiple linear regression, and performance evaluation. Run the scripts on Amazon EC2 instances.","C":"Configure Amazon Macie to analyze the dataset and to create a model. Report the model's achieved performance.","D":"Select a model from Amazon Bedrock. Tune the model with the data. Report the model's achieved performance."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon SageMaker Autopilot 创建一个新模型。报告该模型所达到的性能。","B":"实现自定义脚本以执行数据预处理、多元线性回归和性能评估。 评估。在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行脚本。","C":"配置 Amazon Macie 对数据集进行分析并创建模型。报告模型所达到的性能。","D":"从亚马逊 Bedrock 中选择一个模型。使用数据对模型进行调优。报告模型所达到的性能。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The goal is to determine whether a model can predict a target variable from a tabular dataset (in S3, queried via Athena) with the LEAST development effort. Amazon SageMaker Autopilot is an AutoML capability for regression and classification on tabular data: you point it at the input/output data locations and name the target column, and it automatically performs data preprocessing, candidate algorithm selection, training, and hyperparameter optimization, then produces a leaderboard plus performance and explainability reports. This lets the company report the best model's achieved performance with essentially no custom code, so it is the lowest-effort option. Option B is the highest-effort path and directly contradicts the qualifier. Option C is invalid because Amazon Macie is a data security service that discovers sensitive data in S3 and cannot build a predictive model. Option D is the wrong tool and more effort, because Amazon Bedrock provides foundation/generative models (text, image) rather than a turnkey path for supervised tabular regression or classification.","explanation_zh":"目標是以最少的開發投入，判斷模型能否從表格資料集（存於 S3、透過 Athena 查詢）預測目標變數。Amazon SageMaker Autopilot 是針對表格資料的迴歸與分類 AutoML 功能：只要指定輸入/輸出資料位置與目標欄位，它會自動執行資料前處理、候選演算法選擇、訓練與超參數最佳化，並產出排行榜以及效能與可解釋性報告。如此公司幾乎不需撰寫自訂程式即可回報最佳模型的達成效能，因此是投入最少的選項。選項 B 是投入最高的做法，直接違反題目限制。選項 C 不成立，因為 Amazon Macie 是資料安全服務，用於探索 S3 中的敏感資料，無法建立預測模型。選項 D 工具錯誤且更費工，因為 Amazon Bedrock 提供的是基礎/生成式模型（文字、影像），並非用於監督式表格迴歸或分類的開箱即用途徑。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Writing custom preprocessing, multiple linear regression, and evaluation scripts to run on EC2 is the highest-effort option and directly contradicts the LEAST development effort requirement.","why_zh":"自行撰寫資料前處理、多元線性迴歸與評估腳本並於 EC2 執行，是投入最高的選項，直接違反「最少開發投入」的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Macie is a data security service that discovers sensitive data (e.g., PII) in S3 using ML and pattern matching; it does not train or create predictive models, so it cannot determine whether the target variable can be predicted.","why_zh":"Amazon Macie 是資料安全服務，利用機器學習與模式比對在 S3 中探索敏感資料（如 PII），並不會訓練或建立預測模型，因此無法判斷目標變數是否可被預測。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Bedrock provides foundation/generative models for text and images; it is not a turnkey path for supervised tabular regression/classification, and fine-tuning a foundation model on the data is both the wrong tool and far more effort than AutoML.","why_zh":"Amazon Bedrock 提供的是文字與影像的基礎/生成式模型，並非監督式表格迴歸/分類的開箱即用途徑；以該資料微調基礎模型不僅工具錯誤，投入也遠高於 AutoML。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/autopilot-automate-model-development-create-experiment-ui.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/autopilot-model-insights.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/decision-guides/latest/bedrock-or-sagemaker/bedrock-or-sagemaker.html"]}},{"id":26,"question_en":"A company wants to predict the success of advertising campaigns by considering the color scheme of each advertisement. An ML engineer is preparing data for a neural network model. The dataset includes color information as categorical data. Which technique for feature engineering should the ML engineer use for the model?","question_zh":"一家公司希望通过考虑每则广告的配色方案来预测广告活动的成功率。一位机器学习工程师正在为 神经网络模型准备数据。数据集中包含的颜色信息以分类数据的形式呈现。 机器学习工程师应该为模型使用哪种特征工程技术？","options_en":{"A":"Apply label encoding to the color categories. Automatically assign each color a unique integer.","B":"Implement padding to ensure that all color feature vectors have the same length.","C":"Perform dimensionality reduction on the color categories.","D":"One-hot encode the color categories to transform the color scheme feature into a binary matrix."},"options_zh":{"A":"对颜色类别应用标签编码。自动为每种颜色分配一个唯一的整数。","B":"实施填充以确保所有颜色特征向量具有相同的长度。","C":"对颜色类别进行降维处理。","D":"对颜色类别进行独热编码，将颜色方案特征转换为二进制矩阵。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Color scheme is nominal categorical data: colors have no inherent rank or order. The AWS SageMaker Data Wrangler 'Encode Categorical' documentation explicitly distinguishes nominal categories (no inherent order) from ordinal categories (e.g., degree levels High school < Bachelors < Masters) and gives the exact one-hot example: Dog -> [1,0] and Cat -> [0,1]. One-hot encoding turns each color into a binary indicator vector, producing a binary matrix that lets a neural network treat each color independently without implying any false ordinal relationship. This is the correct technique for nominal categories. Label/integer encoding (A) would inject a spurious magnitude/ordering that misleads gradient-based neural-network learning, which AWS reserves only for ordinal data with a true inherent order.","explanation_zh":"色彩配色屬於名目 (nominal) 類別資料：各種顏色之間沒有內在的順序或大小關係。AWS SageMaker Data Wrangler 的 'Encode Categorical' 文件明確區分名目類別 (無內在順序) 與序數 (ordinal) 類別 (如學歷 High school < Bachelors < Masters)，並給出 one-hot 的範例：Dog -> [1,0]、Cat -> [0,1]。One-hot encoding 將每個顏色轉換成二元指示向量，形成一個二元矩陣，讓神經網路把每個顏色視為彼此獨立，不會引入錯誤的順序關係，因此是名目類別正確的技術。Label/整數編碼 (A) 會替顏色注入虛假的大小與順序，誤導以梯度為基礎的神經網路學習；AWS 僅將 ordinal 編碼保留給真正具有內在順序的資料。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Label/integer encoding (Data Wrangler 'Ordinal encode') assigns each color a unique integer, imposing an artificial ordinal ranking and magnitude (e.g., red=1, blue=2, green=3). For nominal data like colors this misleads the neural network into inferring false numeric relationships; AWS reserves ordinal encoding for categories with a true inherent order.","why_zh":"Label/整數編碼 (Data Wrangler 的 'Ordinal encode') 給每個顏色指定唯一整數，會強加人為的順序與大小 (如 red=1、blue=2、green=3)。對顏色這類名目資料，這會誤導神經網路推斷出不存在的數值關係；AWS 將 ordinal 編碼保留給真正具有內在順序的類別。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Padding makes variable-length sequences (such as text token sequences or time series) the same length so they fit fixed-size tensors. A single categorical color attribute is not a variable-length sequence, so padding does not address converting the categorical value into a usable numeric feature.","why_zh":"Padding 是把長度不一的序列 (如文字 token 序列或時間序列) 補齊成相同長度以符合固定大小張量。單一的顏色類別屬性不是變動長度序列，因此 padding 無法解決把類別值轉成可用數值特徵的問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Dimensionality reduction (e.g., PCA in Data Wrangler 'Reduce Dimensionality within a Dataset') compresses many numeric features into fewer principal components to reduce dataset size or collinearity. It operates on numeric inputs and does not transform raw categorical strings into numeric features; an encoding step is needed first, so PCA alone does not solve the stated problem.","why_zh":"降維 (如 Data Wrangler 的 'Reduce Dimensionality within a Dataset' PCA) 是把眾多數值特徵壓縮成較少的主成分以縮小資料規模或消除共線性。它作用於數值輸入，無法把原始的類別字串轉成數值特徵；必須先做編碼步驟，所以單靠 PCA 無法解決題目所述問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler-transform.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/latest/dg/data-transformations-for-machine-learning.html"]}},{"id":27,"question_en":"A company uses a hybrid cloud environment. A model that is deployed on premises uses data in Amazon S3 to provide customers with a live conversational engine. The model is using sensitive data. An ML engineer needs to implement a solution to identify and remove the sensitive data. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司采用混合云环境。部署在本地的一个模型使用亚马逊 S3 中的数据为客户提供实时对话引 擎。 该模型正在使用敏感数据。一位机器学习工程师需要实施解决方案来识别并移除这些敏感数据。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the model on Amazon SageMaker. Create a set of AWS Lambda functions to identify and remove the sensitive data.","B":"Deploy the model on an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster that uses AWS Fargate. Create an AWS Batch job to identify and remove the sensitive data.","C":"Use Amazon Macie to identify the sensitive data. Create a set of AWS Lambda functions to remove the sensitive data.","D":"Use Amazon Comprehend to identify the sensitive data. Launch Amazon EC2 instances to remove the sensitive data."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon SageMaker 上部署模型。创建一组 AWS Lambda 函数来识别并移除敏感数据。","B":"在使用 AWS Fargate 的 Amazon Elastic Container Service （Amazon ECS） 集群上部署模型。 创建一个 AWS Batch 作业来识别并移除敏感数据。","C":"使用 Amazon Macie 来识别敏感数据。创建一组 AWS Lambda 函数来移除敏感数据。","D":"使用 Amazon Comprehend 来识别敏感数据。启动 Amazon EC2 实例以移除敏感数据。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The deciding factors are the LEAST operational overhead qualifier and the fact that the sensitive data lives in Amazon S3. Amazon Macie is the fully managed, purpose-built AWS service for discovering/identifying sensitive data (PII, financial data, credentials) in S3 buckets using managed data identifiers, requiring essentially no custom detection code. For the removal step, AWS Lambda is serverless and fully managed, and Macie integrates natively with EventBridge to trigger Lambda for automated remediation, so option C combines a managed identification service with a serverless removal mechanism, the lowest-overhead pairing offered. Option D is wrong despite Comprehend being capable at PII: as written, D performs the removal on self-managed Amazon EC2 instances (which you must launch, patch, scale, and secure), and EC2 is the highest operational-overhead compute choice in the list; Comprehend also operates on text passed to its API rather than natively scanning the S3 estate the way Macie does. The dump suggested answer (C) is therefore correct, and the first analyst's correction to D is wrong because it traded a serverless removal path (Lambda) for a server-managed one (EC2), increasing operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"決定性因素是「LEAST operational overhead」這個限定條件，以及敏感資料存放在 Amazon S3 這個事實。Amazon Macie 是 AWS 專為在 S3 bucket 中發現/識別敏感資料（PII、金融資料、憑證）而打造的全受管服務，透過 managed data identifiers 幾乎不需要自訂偵測程式碼。在移除步驟方面，AWS Lambda 為無伺服器且全受管，且 Macie 原生整合 EventBridge 以觸發 Lambda 進行自動化修補，因此選項 C 結合了受管識別服務與無伺服器移除機制，是各選項中運維負擔最低的組合。選項 D 不正確，儘管 Comprehend 對 PII 很有能力：按題目所述，D 的移除是在自管的 Amazon EC2 執行個體上進行（需自行啟動、修補、擴展與保護），而 EC2 是清單中運維負擔最高的運算選擇；此外 Comprehend 是針對傳入其 API 的文字運作，並非像 Macie 那樣原生掃描整個 S3 資料環境。因此題庫建議答案 C 正確，而第一位分析師改成 D 是錯的，因為它把無伺服器的移除路徑（Lambda）換成需自管伺服器的路徑（EC2），反而增加了運維負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Redeploying the on-premises model onto Amazon SageMaker does not address identifying or removing sensitive data, and a full custom set of Lambda functions that both detect and remove PII means building and maintaining your own detection logic from scratch, far more overhead than using the managed Macie service.","why_zh":"把地端模型重新部署到 Amazon SageMaker 並不能解決識別或移除敏感資料的問題，而要寫一整套同時負責偵測與移除 PII 的自訂 Lambda，等於從零打造並維護自己的偵測邏輯，運維負擔遠高於使用受管的 Macie 服務。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An Amazon ECS on Fargate cluster plus an AWS Batch job is a fully self-built data-processing pipeline with no managed sensitive-data detection at all; you would implement and operate all detection and removal logic yourself, the highest operational overhead of the options.","why_zh":"Amazon ECS on Fargate 叢集加上 AWS Batch 作業是完全自建的資料處理管線，完全沒有受管的敏感資料偵測；所有偵測與移除邏輯都得自行實作並運維，是各選項中運維負擔最高的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Although Amazon Comprehend can detect (and even redact) PII in text, this option assigns the removal to self-managed Amazon EC2 instances, which you must launch, patch, scale, and secure. EC2 is the heaviest operational-overhead compute choice here, so D loses to C on the LEAST operational overhead requirement; Comprehend also targets text sent to its API rather than natively discovering sensitive data across the S3 estate the way Macie does.","why_zh":"雖然 Amazon Comprehend 能偵測（甚至遮罩）文字中的 PII，但此選項把移除工作交給自管的 Amazon EC2 執行個體，需自行啟動、修補、擴展與保護。EC2 是此處運維負擔最重的運算選擇，因此就「LEAST operational overhead」需求而言 D 輸給 C；此外 Comprehend 是針對傳入其 API 的文字，而非像 Macie 那樣原生掃描整個 S3 資料環境來發現敏感資料。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/discovery-jobs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/how-pii.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/redact-api-pii.html"]}},{"id":28,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to create data ingestion pipelines and ML model deployment pipelines on AWS. All the raw data is stored in Amazon S3 buckets. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师需要在 AWS 上创建数据摄取管道和机器学习模型部署管道。所有原始数据都存储 在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Data Firehose to create the data ingestion pipelines. Use Amazon SageMaker Studio Classic to create the model deployment pipelines.","B":"Use AWS Glue to create the data ingestion pipelines. Use Amazon SageMaker Studio Classic to create the model deployment pipelines.","C":"Use Amazon Redshift ML to create the data ingestion pipelines. Use Amazon SageMaker Studio Classic to create the model deployment pipelines.","D":"Use Amazon Athena to create the data ingestion pipelines. Use an Amazon SageMaker notebook to create the model deployment pipelines."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Data Firehose 创建数据摄取管道。使用 Amazon SageMaker Studio Classic 创建模型 部署管道。","B":"使用 AWS Glue 创建数据摄取管道。使用 Amazon SageMaker Studio Classic 创建模型部署管道。","C":"使用 Amazon Redshift ML 创建数据摄取管道。使用 Amazon SageMaker Studio Classic 创建模型 部署管道。","D":"使用 Amazon Athena 创建数据摄取管道。使用 Amazon SageMaker 笔记本创建模型部署管道。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Database","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The question needs ONE solution that builds both data ingestion pipelines (from raw data already stored in S3) and ML model deployment pipelines. AWS Glue is AWS's serverless data integration service: the official docs state you can 'visually create, run, and monitor extract, transform, and load (ETL) pipelines to load data into your data lakes' from 70+ sources, and it 'integrates with AWS analytics services and Amazon S3 data lakes.' That makes Glue the canonical choice for the ingestion-pipeline half. Amazon SageMaker Studio (Classic) is the integrated ML IDE that authors and runs SageMaker Pipelines and drives model-registry approval that initiates CI/CD model deployment, so it covers the model-deployment-pipeline half. Only option B pairs a true ingestion-pipeline service with a true model-deployment-pipeline tool, so B is correct.","explanation_zh":"題目需要一個方案同時建立資料擷取管線 (raw data 已存於 S3) 與 ML 模型部署管線。AWS Glue 是 AWS 的 serverless 資料整合服務，官方文件明確指出可「以視覺化方式建立、執行與監控 ETL 管線，將資料載入 data lake」，可連接 70 多種來源，並「整合 AWS 分析服務與 Amazon S3 data lake」，因此是擷取管線部分的標準選擇。Amazon SageMaker Studio (Classic) 是整合式 ML IDE，可撰寫並執行 SageMaker Pipelines，並透過 model registry 的核准動作觸發 CI/CD 模型部署，涵蓋模型部署管線部分。只有選項 B 同時搭配了正確的擷取管線服務與正確的模型部署管線工具，故 B 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The deployment half (SageMaker Studio Classic) is fine, but Amazon Data Firehose is a near-real-time streaming delivery service that loads streaming data INTO destinations such as S3, Redshift, and OpenSearch. The raw data here already sits at rest in S3, so Firehose is the wrong tool to build ingestion pipelines over it. This makes A weaker than B.","why_zh":"部署部分 (SageMaker Studio Classic) 正確，但 Amazon Data Firehose 是近即時串流傳送服務，將串流資料載入 S3、Redshift、OpenSearch 等目的地。本題 raw data 已靜態存於 S3，Firehose 並不適合對其建立擷取管線，故 A 弱於 B。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Redshift ML lets you create, train, and run predictions on ML models using SQL inside Redshift (integrating with SageMaker Autopilot). It is a machine-learning feature, not a data ingestion pipeline service, so it cannot satisfy the ingestion-pipeline requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon Redshift ML 是在 Redshift 內以 SQL 建立、訓練與執行 ML 模型預測 (整合 SageMaker Autopilot) 的功能，屬於機器學習能力，並非資料擷取管線服務，無法滿足建立擷取管線的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Athena is an interactive serverless SQL query service over data in S3, not a tool for building data ingestion pipelines. In addition, an ad-hoc SageMaker notebook is for experimentation, not a purpose-built, repeatable model deployment pipeline. Both halves are weaker than B.","why_zh":"Amazon Athena 是針對 S3 資料的互動式 serverless SQL 查詢服務，並非用來建立資料擷取管線的工具。此外，臨時性的 SageMaker notebook 偏向實驗用途，而非可重複、專為模型部署而設計的管線。兩部分皆弱於 B。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/what-is-glue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry-details-studio-deploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/pipelines-build.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/redshift/latest/gsg/machine-learning.html"]}},{"id":29,"question_en":"A company that has hundreds of data scientists is using Amazon SageMaker to create ML models. The models are in model groups in the SageMaker Model Registry. The data scientists are grouped into three categories: computer vision, natural language processing (NLP), and speech recognition. An ML engineer needs to implement a solution to organize the existing models into these groups to improve model discoverability at scale. The solution must not affect the integrity of the model artifacts and their existing groupings. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家拥有数百名数据科学家的公司正在使用亚马逊 SageMaker 来创建机器学习模型。这些模型被分 组存放在 SageMaker 模型注册表中。 数据科学家被分为三类：计算机视觉、自然语言处理（NLP）和语音识别。机器学习工程师需要实现一 个解决方案，将现有的模型按这些类别进行组织，以大规模提高模型的可发现性。该解决方案不得影响 模型资产的完整性及其现有的分组。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a custom tag for each of the three categories. Add the tags to the model packages in the SageMaker Model Registry.","B":"Create a model group for each category. Move the existing models into these category model groups.","C":"Use SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking to automatically identify and tag which model groups should contain the models.","D":"Create a Model Registry collection for each of the three categories. Move the existing model groups into the collections."},"options_zh":{"A":"为这三个类别中的每一个创建一个自定义标签。将这些标签添加到 SageMaker 模型注册表中 的模型包中。","B":"为每个类别创建一个模型组。将现有的模型移入这些类别模型组中。","C":"使用 SageMaker ML 血统跟踪功能自动识别并标记哪些模型组应包含这些模型。","D":"为这三个类别分别创建一个模型注册中心集合。将现有的模型组移入这些集合中。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"SageMaker Model Registry Collections are purpose-built to group related registered models into hierarchies to improve model discoverability at scale. The official Collections documentation gives the exact example in this question: categorizing models by the domain of the problem they solve into Collections titled NLP-models, CV-models, and Speech-recognition-models. The docs explicitly state that 'Any operation you perform on your Collections does not affect the integrity of the individual Model Groups they contain—the underlying Model Group artifacts in Amazon S3 and Amazon ECR are not modified,' which directly satisfies the requirement to preserve artifact integrity and existing groupings. The supported workflow is to create a Collection per category and add/move the existing Model Groups into the Collections; the Add Model Groups operation works on whole model groups, so the groups themselves are preserved. This is the only option that organizes the existing groups into a discoverability hierarchy at scale while leaving artifacts and groupings intact.","explanation_zh":"SageMaker Model Registry Collections 專為將相關的已註冊模型分組成階層、以在大規模下提升模型可發現性而設計。官方 Collections 文件給出的範例與本題完全相同：依問題領域將模型分類為名為 NLP-models、CV-models 與 Speech-recognition-models 的 Collections。文件明確指出『對 Collections 執行的任何操作都不會影響其所包含個別 Model Groups 的完整性——底層 Model Group 在 Amazon S3 與 Amazon ECR 中的成品不會被修改』，這直接滿足了保留成品完整性與既有分組的需求。受支援的做法是為每個類別建立一個 Collection，並將既有的 Model Groups 加入／移動到 Collections 中；Add Model Groups 操作是針對整個 model group 進行，因此群組本身得以保留。這是唯一能在大規模下將既有群組組織成可發現性階層、同時保持成品與分組不變的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Tagging the model packages with custom category tags improves search/filtering but does not provide the hierarchical organization that Collections offer for discoverability at scale. Tags also operate at the model package/version level rather than organizing the existing model groups, and AWS positions Collections (not ad-hoc tags) as the purpose-built discoverability-at-scale solution.","why_zh":"對 model packages 加上自訂類別標籤可改善搜尋／篩選，但無法提供 Collections 為大規模可發現性所提供的階層式組織。標籤是在 model package／版本層級運作，而非組織既有的 model groups；AWS 將 Collections（而非臨時標籤）定位為專為大規模可發現性設計的解決方案。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Creating new model groups per category and moving the existing models into them would alter the existing groupings (each model group already represents a versioned model lineage). Moving model versions between groups breaks the requirement to preserve existing groupings and risks artifact/lineage integrity. Model groups are not designed to act as nested category buckets; Collections are.","why_zh":"為每個類別建立新的 model groups 並把現有模型移入，會更動既有分組（每個 model group 已代表一個有版本的模型譜系）。在群組間移動模型版本違反保留既有分組的需求，並可能影響成品／譜系完整性。Model groups 並非設計成可巢狀的類別容器，Collections 才是。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking records the provenance of ML workflow steps (data, training jobs, models) for traceability and auditing; it does not automatically classify models into computer vision/NLP/speech categories nor auto-tag model groups into category collections. No such automatic identification-and-tagging capability exists, so this option describes functionality that does not work as stated.","why_zh":"SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking 記錄 ML 工作流程步驟（資料、訓練作業、模型）的來源譜系以供追溯與稽核；它不會自動將模型分類為電腦視覺／NLP／語音類別，也不會自動把 model groups 標記到類別 collections。並不存在這種自動識別並標記的功能，因此此選項描述的能力與實際不符。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/modelcollections.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/modelcollections-add-models.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/modelcollections-move-models.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry-models.html"]}},{"id":30,"question_en":"A company runs an Amazon SageMaker domain in a public subnet of a newly created VPC. The network is configured properly, and ML engineers can access the SageMaker domain. Recently, the company discovered suspicious traffic to the domain from a specific IP address. The company needs to block traffic from the specific IP address. Which update to the network configuration will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司在新创建的 VPC 的公共子网中运行着一个 Amazon SageMaker 域。网络配置正确，机器学习工程 师可以访问该 SageMaker 域。 最近，公司发现有可疑流量从特定 IP 地址访问该域名。公司需要封锁来自该特定 IP 地址的流量。 哪种网络配置更新能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a security group inbound rule to deny traffic from the specific IP address. Assign the security group to the domain.","B":"Create a network ACL inbound rule to deny traffic from the specific IP address. Assign the rule to the default network Ad for the subnet where the domain is located.","C":"Create a shadow variant for the domain. Configure SageMaker Inference Recommender to send traffic from the specific IP address to the shadow endpoint.","D":"Create a VPC route table to deny inbound traffic from the specific IP address. Assign the route table to the domain."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个安全组入站规则，拒绝来自特定 IP 地址的流量。将该安全组分配给域。","B":"创建一条网络访问控制列表（ACL）入站规则，拒绝来自特定 IP 地址的流量。将该规则分配给该域所 在子网的默认网络 ACL。","C":"为该域创建一个影子变体。配置 SageMaker 推理推荐器，将来自特定 IP 地址的流量发送到影子端点。","D":"创建一个 VPC 路由表以拒绝来自特定 IP 地址的入站流量。将该路由表分配给域。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to block inbound traffic from one specific IP address that reaches a SageMaker domain living in a public subnet of the VPC. A network ACL (NACL) operates at the subnet level, is stateless, and supports both ALLOW and DENY rules. Because the domain sits in a subnet, all inbound traffic destined for it is evaluated by that subnet's NACL, so adding an inbound DENY rule with the offending IP as the Source CIDR (for example x.x.x.x/32) blocks it. AWS documentation makes the deciding distinction explicit in its comparison table: a network ACL has 'Allow and deny rules,' while a security group has 'Allow rules only.' That single fact eliminates option A, because a security group cannot express a deny rule and therefore cannot block a specific source IP. Option B is the only choice that can actually deny traffic from a specific IP, so it is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是封鎖來自某個特定 IP 位址、進入位於 VPC public subnet 的 SageMaker domain 的 inbound 流量。network ACL (NACL) 作用於 subnet 層級、屬於 stateless，且同時支援 ALLOW 與 DENY 規則。由於 domain 位於 subnet 中，所有進入它的 inbound 流量都會被該 subnet 的 NACL 評估，因此新增一條以該惡意 IP 作為 Source CIDR（例如 x.x.x.x/32）的 inbound DENY 規則即可封鎖它。AWS 文件在比較表中明確指出關鍵差異：network ACL 支援「Allow and deny rules」，而 security group 只支援「Allow rules only」。這項事實直接排除選項 A，因為 security group 無法設定 deny 規則，也就無法封鎖特定來源 IP。選項 B 是唯一能真正拒絕特定 IP 流量的方案，因此正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Security groups support allow rules only, not deny rules. The AWS comparison table lists the security group rule type as 'Allow rules only,' so you cannot create a security group rule that denies traffic from a specific IP, making this option technically impossible.","why_zh":"Security group 只支援 allow 規則，不支援 deny 規則。AWS 比較表將 security group 的 rule type 列為「Allow rules only」，因此無法建立 deny 特定 IP 的 security group 規則，此選項在技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Shadow variants and SageMaker Inference Recommender are ML model evaluation and benchmarking features used to compare model versions and test inference performance, not network security controls. They cannot inspect source IPs or block network traffic, and Inference Recommender does not route traffic based on client IP.","why_zh":"Shadow variant 與 SageMaker Inference Recommender 是用於比較模型版本與測試推論效能的 ML 模型評估/基準功能，並非網路安全控制。它們無法檢查來源 IP 或封鎖網路流量，Inference Recommender 也不會依用戶端 IP 來導流。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"VPC route tables direct traffic to targets based on the DESTINATION CIDR; they have no allow/deny semantics and no concept of inbound source-IP filtering. Route tables are associated with subnets or gateways, not with a SageMaker domain, and cannot block inbound traffic from a specific source IP.","why_zh":"VPC route table 依據「目的地 CIDR」將流量導向 target，沒有 allow/deny 概念，也無法依 inbound 來源 IP 過濾。Route table 是與 subnet 或 gateway 關聯，而非與 SageMaker domain 關聯，且無法封鎖來自特定來源 IP 的 inbound 流量。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nacl-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-network-acls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nacl-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/security-group-rules.html"]}},{"id":31,"question_en":"A company is gathering audio, video, and text data in various languages. The company needs to use a large language model (LLM) to summarize the gathered data that is in Spanish. Which solution will meet these requirements in the LEAST amount of time?","question_zh":"一家公司正在收集多种语言的音频、视频和文本数据。该公司需要使用一个大型语言模型（LLM）来总 结所收集的西班牙语数据。 哪种解决方案能在最短的时间内满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Train and deploy a model in Amazon SageMaker to convert the data into English text. Train and deploy an LLM in SageMaker to summarize the text.","B":"Use Amazon Transcribe and Amazon Translate to convert the data into English text. Use Amazon Bedrock with the Jurassic model to summarize the text.","C":"Use Amazon Rekognition and Amazon Translate to convert the data into English text. Use Amazon Bedrock with the Anthropic Claude model to summarize the text.","D":"Use Amazon Comprehend and Amazon Translate to convert the data into English text. Use Amazon Bedrock with the Stable Diffusion model to summarize the text."},"options_zh":{"A":"在亚马逊 SageMaker 中训练并部署一个模型，将数据转换为英文文本。在 SageMaker 中训练并部署一个 大型语言模型来对文本进行总结。","B":"使用亚马逊 Transcribe 和亚马逊 Translate 将数据转换为英文文本。使用亚马逊 Bedrock 和 Jurassic 模 型对文本进行总结。","C":"使用亚马逊 Rekognition 和亚马逊 Translate 将数据转换为英文文本。使用亚马逊 Bedrock 和 Anthropic Claude 模型对文本进行总结。","D":"使用亚马逊 Comprehend 和亚马逊 Translate 将数据转换为英文文本。使用亚马逊 Bedrock 和 Stable Diffusion 模型对文本进行总结。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The pipeline must (1) convert audio, video, and text in Spanish into English text, then (2) summarize it with an LLM, in the LEAST amount of time, which favors fully managed AI services over custom training. Amazon Transcribe is the automatic speech recognition (ASR) service that converts spoken audio (including the audio in video) to text, and Amazon Translate converts the Spanish text to English. For summarization, Amazon Bedrock offers the AI21 Labs Jurassic model, a text-generation LLM whose inference parameters (temperature, max tokens, stop sequences) make it suitable for summarizing text. Option B is the only choice that pairs the correct service with each task while using only fully managed services (no custom model training/deployment), so it meets the 'least time' qualifier. The other options either use a non-speech service for the audio/video conversion (Rekognition is visual image/video analysis; Comprehend is NLP over existing text), pick a non-text model for summarization (Stable Diffusion is a text-to-image model), or require building/training custom SageMaker models, which takes far longer.","explanation_zh":"此流程必須(1)將西班牙語的音訊、影片與文字轉換為英文文字,然後(2)用 LLM 進行摘要,且要花最少時間,因此偏好使用完全受管的 AI 服務,而非自訓模型。Amazon Transcribe 是自動語音辨識(ASR)服務,可將語音音訊(含影片中的音訊)轉為文字;Amazon Translate 則將西班牙語文字翻譯成英文。摘要方面,Amazon Bedrock 提供 AI21 Labs Jurassic 這個文字生成 LLM,其推論參數(temperature、最大 token、停止序列)適合用於文字摘要。選項 B 是唯一為每項任務搭配正確服務、且僅使用完全受管服務(無須自訓或部署模型)的選擇,因此符合「最少時間」的條件。其他選項不是用了錯誤的轉換服務(Amazon Rekognition 做的是影像/影片的視覺分析;Amazon Comprehend 是針對既有文字的 NLP,皆不做語音轉文字),就是選了非文字模型來摘要(Stable Diffusion 是文字轉影像模型),或是需要自建並訓練 SageMaker 自訂模型,耗時遠長於受管服務。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Training and deploying custom models in SageMaker (both a conversion model and a summarization LLM) takes far longer than using managed services, violating the 'LEAST amount of time' qualifier.","why_zh":"在 SageMaker 自行訓練並部署自訂模型(包含轉換模型與摘要 LLM)所花時間遠多於使用受管服務,違反「最少時間」的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Rekognition performs visual image/video analysis (labels, faces, objects), not speech-to-text, so it cannot convert the spoken audio of audio/video into text. Claude would summarize fine, but the conversion step is wrong.","why_zh":"Amazon Rekognition 做的是影像/影片的視覺分析(標籤、人臉、物件),並非語音轉文字,無法將音訊/影片中的語音轉成文字。雖然 Claude 能勝任摘要,但轉換步驟錯誤。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Two errors: Amazon Comprehend does NLP on existing text (entities, sentiment, key phrases) and cannot do speech-to-text on audio/video, and Stable Diffusion is a text-to-image generation model, not a text-summarization LLM.","why_zh":"有兩處錯誤:Amazon Comprehend 針對既有文字做 NLP(實體、情緒、關鍵字),無法對音訊/影片做語音轉文字;且 Stable Diffusion 是文字轉影像的生成模型,並非文字摘要 LLM。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ai/responsible-ai/transcribe-speech-recognition/overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transcribe/latest/dg/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-parameters-jurassic2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-parameters-stability-diffusion.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/what-is.html"]}},{"id":32,"question_en":"A financial company receives a high volume of real-time market data streams from an external provider. The streams consist of thousands of JSON records every second. The company needs to implement a scalable solution on AWS to identify anomalous data points. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家金融公司从外部供应商那里每秒接收大量实时市场数据流。这些数据流包含数千条 JSON 记录。 该公司需要在 AWS 上实施一个可扩展的解决方案来识别异常数据点。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Ingest real-time data into Amazon Kinesis data streams. Use the built-in RANDOM_CUT_FOREST function in Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink to process the data streams and to detect data anomalies.","B":"Ingest real-time data into Amazon Kinesis data streams. Deploy an Amazon SageMaker endpoint for real-time outlier detection. Create an AWS Lambda function to detect anomalies. Use the data streams to invoke the Lambda function.","C":"Ingest real-time data into Apache Kafka on Amazon EC2 instances. Deploy an Amazon SageMaker endpoint for real-time outlier detection. Create an AWS Lambda function to detect anomalies. Use the data streams to invoke the Lambda function.","D":"Send real-time data to an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) FIFO queue. Create an AWS Lambda function to consume the queue messages. Program the Lambda function to start an AWS Glue extract, transform, and load (ETL) job for batch processing and anomaly detection."},"options_zh":{"A":"将实时数据摄入到亚马逊 Kinesis 数据流中。使用亚马逊托管的 Apache Flink 服务中的内置 RANDOM_CUT_FOREST 函数处理数据流并检测数据异常。","B":"将实时数据摄入到 Amazon Kinesis 数据流中。部署一个 Amazon SageMaker 端点以进行实时异常检测。 创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来检测异常。使用数据流调用 Lambda 函数。","C":"将实时数据摄入到亚马逊 EC2 实例上的 Apache Kafka 中。部署一个用于实时异常检测的 Amazon SageMaker 端点。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来检测异常。使用数据流调用 Lambda 函数。","D":"将实时数据发送到 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）FIFO 队列。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来处理队列消息。编写 Lambda 函数以启动 AWS Glue 提取、转换和加载（ETL）作业，用于批 处理和异常检测。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifiers are real-time and LEAST operational overhead. Option A ingests the JSON streams into Amazon Kinesis Data Streams and uses the built-in RANDOM_CUT_FOREST function to score anomalies in-stream. RANDOM_CUT_FOREST is a built-in, fully managed streaming SQL function that assigns an anomaly score to each record based on its numeric columns; AWS documents it in the Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink SQL Reference (the rebranded Kinesis Data Analytics SQL reference), and the official example wires Kinesis Data Streams -> in-application stream -> RANDOM_CUT_FOREST with no model training, no endpoint to host, and no custom anomaly-detection code. This serverless, managed pipeline therefore has the least operational overhead. Options B and C require building, training, hosting, scaling, and patching a SageMaker outlier-detection endpoint plus custom Lambda glue, and C additionally adds a self-managed Apache Kafka cluster on EC2 (broker provisioning, patching, scaling). Option D is a batch architecture (SQS FIFO -> Lambda -> Glue ETL) that routes records into a batch ETL job rather than scoring them in-stream, so it does not satisfy real-time anomaly detection, and FIFO queues require enabling high-throughput mode and careful message-group partitioning to approach thousands of records per second.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定條件是「即時 (real-time)」與「最少維運負擔 (LEAST operational overhead)」。選項 A 將 JSON 串流擷取到 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams，並使用內建的 RANDOM_CUT_FOREST 函式在串流中直接計算異常分數。RANDOM_CUT_FOREST 是一個內建、全託管的串流 SQL 函式，可依據數值欄位為每筆記錄指派異常分數；AWS 將其文件歸入 Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink SQL Reference（即改名後的 Kinesis Data Analytics SQL 參考），官方範例的流程為 Kinesis Data Streams -> in-application stream -> RANDOM_CUT_FOREST，無需訓練模型、無需託管端點、也不需自行撰寫異常偵測程式碼，因此維運負擔最低。選項 B 與 C 需要建置、訓練、託管、擴展並修補 SageMaker 離群偵測端點及自訂 Lambda，C 還額外要在 EC2 上自行管理 Apache Kafka 叢集（broker 佈建、修補、擴展）。選項 D 是批次架構（SQS FIFO -> Lambda -> Glue ETL），它把記錄送進批次 ETL 作業而非在串流中即時評分，無法滿足即時異常偵測；而且 FIFO 佇列需啟用 high-throughput 模式並仔細規劃 message group 分區，才可能接近每秒數千筆。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Deploying and operating a SageMaker real-time endpoint (model training, hosting, autoscaling, patching) plus a custom anomaly-detection Lambda is far more operational overhead than calling the built-in, fully managed RANDOM_CUT_FOREST streaming SQL function.","why_zh":"部署並維運 SageMaker 即時端點（模型訓練、託管、自動擴展、修補）再加上自訂異常偵測 Lambda，維運負擔遠高於直接呼叫內建、全託管的 RANDOM_CUT_FOREST 串流 SQL 函式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Self-managed Apache Kafka on EC2 adds the most operational overhead (cluster provisioning, patching, scaling, broker management) on top of a SageMaker endpoint and Lambda, directly contradicting the LEAST overhead requirement.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上自行管理 Apache Kafka 帶來最高的維運負擔（叢集佈建、修補、擴展、broker 管理），再加上 SageMaker 端點與 Lambda，直接違反「最少維運負擔」的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SQS FIFO -> Lambda -> Glue ETL is a batch pipeline: it hands records to a batch ETL job instead of scoring them in-stream, so it does not provide real-time anomaly detection, and FIFO throughput needs high-throughput mode plus message-group partitioning to reach thousands of records per second.","why_zh":"SQS FIFO -> Lambda -> Glue ETL 是批次管線：它把記錄交給批次 ETL 作業而非在串流中即時評分，因此不提供即時異常偵測；且 FIFO 吞吐量需啟用 high-throughput 模式並搭配 message group 分區才可能達到每秒數千筆。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/app-anomaly-detection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/sqlref/analytics-sql-reference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/randomcutforest.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/high-throughput-fifo.html"]}},{"id":33,"question_en":"A company has a large collection of chat recordings from customer interactions after a product release. An ML engineer needs to create an ML model to analyze the chat data. The ML engineer needs to determine the success of the product by reviewing customer sentiments about the product. Which action should the ML engineer take to complete the evaluation in the LEAST amount of time?","question_zh":"","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Rekognition to analyze sentiments of the chat conversations.","B":"Train a Naive Bayes classifier to analyze sentiments of the chat conversations.","C":"Use Amazon Comprehend to analyze sentiments of the chat conversations.","D":"Use random forests to classify sentiments of the chat conversations."},"options_zh":{},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is LEAST amount of time. Amazon Comprehend is a fully managed NLP service that provides sentiment analysis (Positive, Negative, Neutral, Mixed) as a built-in insight using pre-trained models. The ML engineer can call DetectSentiment, BatchDetectSentiment, or StartSentimentDetectionJob directly on the chat text and get results immediately, with no data labeling, feature engineering, model training, or tuning. This is the fastest path to evaluate customer sentiment. Options B (Naive Bayes) and D (random forests) are custom ML approaches that require collecting and labeling training data, building features, and training/tuning a model, which takes far longer. Option A (Rekognition) is a computer vision service for image and video analysis, not text sentiment.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定條件是 LEAST amount of time（花最少時間）。Amazon Comprehend 是完全託管的 NLP 服務，使用預先訓練好的模型提供內建的情感分析功能（Positive、Negative、Neutral、Mixed）。ML 工程師可直接對聊天文字呼叫 DetectSentiment、BatchDetectSentiment 或 StartSentimentDetectionJob，立即取得結果，完全不需要標註資料、特徵工程、模型訓練或調校，因此是評估客戶情感最快的途徑。選項 B（Naive Bayes）與 D（random forests）皆屬自建 ML 方法，需要收集與標註訓練資料、建立特徵並訓練/調校模型，耗時遠多於此。選項 A（Rekognition）是用於影像與影片分析的電腦視覺服務，並非文字情感分析。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Rekognition is a computer vision service for analyzing images and video (faces, objects, text in images, content moderation). It does not perform NLP sentiment analysis on chat text, so it does not fit the use case.","why_zh":"Amazon Rekognition 是用於分析影像與影片的電腦視覺服務（臉部、物件、影像中的文字、內容審核），無法對聊天文字執行 NLP 情感分析，因此不符合此情境。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Training a Naive Bayes classifier requires collecting and labeling a sentiment dataset, feature engineering, and model training/evaluation, which takes far more time than using a pre-trained managed service.","why_zh":"訓練 Naive Bayes 分類器需收集與標註情感資料集、進行特徵工程及模型訓練/評估，比使用預先訓練的託管服務耗時許多。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using random forests is a custom ML approach that requires labeled training data, feature engineering, and model training/tuning, making it much slower than Amazon Comprehend's ready-to-use sentiment API.","why_zh":"使用 random forests 屬自建 ML 方法，需要標註訓練資料、特徵工程及模型訓練/調校，遠比 Amazon Comprehend 即用型情感分析 API 來得慢。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/how-sentiment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/what-is.html"]}},{"id":34,"question_en":"A company has a conversational AI assistant that sends requests through Amazon Bedrock to an Anthropic Claude large language model (LLM). Users report that when they ask similar questions multiple times, they sometimes receive different answers. An ML engineer needs to improve the responses to be more consistent and less random. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款通过亚马逊 Bedrock 向 Anthropic Claude 大型语言模型（LLM）发送请求的对话式人 工智能助手。用户反映，当他们多次提出类似问题时，有时会得到不同的答案。一位机器学习工程师 需要改进这些回答，使其更具一致性，减少随机性。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Increase the temperature parameter and the top_k parameter.","B":"Increase the temperature parameter. Decrease the top_k parameter.","C":"Decrease the temperature parameter. Increase the top_k parameter.","D":"Decrease the temperature parameter and the top_k parameter."},"options_zh":{"A":"提高温度参数和 top_k 参数。","B":"提高温度参数。降低 top_k 参数。","C":"降低温度参数。提高 top_k 参数。","D":"降低温度参数和 top_k 参数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The goal is more consistent, less random Claude responses on Amazon Bedrock, which means narrowing the pool of next-token candidates and steepening the probability distribution. Per the AWS Bedrock 'Influence response generation with inference parameters' page, a LOWER temperature steepens the probability mass function and leads to more deterministic responses (it increases the likelihood of higher-probability tokens and decreases the likelihood of lower-probability tokens), while a higher temperature flattens the distribution and increases randomness. The same page's summary table states that a LOWER Top K removes lower-probability tokens (limiting the candidate pool to the most likely outputs), whereas a higher Top K allows lower-probability tokens and increases diversity. Therefore decreasing BOTH temperature and top_k produces the most deterministic, least random, most consistent output, which is exactly Option D. Any option that increases temperature or increases top_k would add randomness and contradict the requirement.","explanation_zh":"目標是讓 Claude 在 Amazon Bedrock 上的回應更一致、更不隨機，也就是要縮小下一個 token 的候選池並使機率分布更陡峭。根據 AWS Bedrock「Influence response generation with inference parameters」文件，較「低」的 temperature 會使機率質量函數更陡峭、產生更具決定性 (deterministic) 的回應（提高高機率 token 的機率、降低低機率 token 的機率），而較高的 temperature 會使分布變平並增加隨機性。同一頁的彙總表也指出，較「低」的 Top K 會移除低機率 token（將候選池限制在最可能的輸出），較高的 Top K 則允許低機率 token 並增加多樣性。因此「同時降低」temperature 與 top_k 會產生最具決定性、最不隨機、最一致的輸出，正好是選項 D。任何提高 temperature 或提高 top_k 的選項都會增加隨機性，與需求相牴觸。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Increasing temperature flattens the probability distribution and increasing top_k enlarges the candidate pool to include lower-probability tokens. Both changes increase randomness and diversity, the opposite of the goal.","why_zh":"提高 temperature 會使機率分布變平，提高 top_k 會擴大候選池並納入低機率 token；兩者都會增加隨機性與多樣性，與目標相反。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Increasing temperature makes responses MORE random by flattening the distribution. Even though decreasing top_k helps, the temperature increase works against consistency, so this option is contradictory and wrong.","why_zh":"提高 temperature 會使分布變平、回應更隨機；即便降低 top_k 有幫助，提高 temperature 仍與一致性背道而馳，故此選項自相矛盾且錯誤。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Decreasing temperature is correct, but increasing top_k enlarges the candidate pool to allow lower-probability tokens, which increases diversity and randomness. The wrong top_k direction makes this option incorrect.","why_zh":"降低 temperature 正確，但提高 top_k 會擴大候選池、允許低機率 token，增加多樣性與隨機性；top_k 方向錯誤使此選項不正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/inference-parameters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-parameters-anthropic-claude-messages.html"]}},{"id":35,"question_en":"A company is using ML to predict the presence of a specific weed in a farmer's field. The company is using the Amazon SageMaker linear learner built-in algorithm with a value of multiclass_dassifier for the predictorjype hyperparameter. What should the company do to MINIMIZE false positives?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用机器学习来预测农民田地里是否存在某种特定的杂草。该公司使用的是亚马逊 SageMaker 的线性学习器内置算法，并将 predictorjype 超参数的值设为 multiclass_dassifier。 公司应采取什么措施来最大限度地减少误报？","options_en":{"A":"Set the value of the weight decay hyperparameter to zero.","B":"Increase the number of training epochs.","C":"Increase the value of the target_precision hyperparameter.","D":"Change the value of the predictorjype hyperparameter to regressor."},"options_zh":{"A":"将权重衰减超参数的值设为零。","B":"增加训练轮数。","C":"提高 target_precision 超参数的值。","D":"将预测器类型超参数的值更改为回归器。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Minimizing false positives is fundamentally a precision objective: Precision = TP / (TP + FP), so requiring the model to hold a higher precision forces it to produce fewer false positives. In the SageMaker linear learner, the only hyperparameter among the options tied to precision is target_precision. The official docs state: 'The target precision. If binary_classifier_model_selection_criteria is recall_at_target_precision, then precision is held at this value while recall is maximized.' Raising target_precision therefore pushes the chosen model toward higher precision and fewer false positives, which is exactly what the company wants. The other three options are clearly off-target: setting wd (weight decay) to zero only disables L2 regularization and controls overfitting; increasing epochs only changes how long the model trains/converges; and switching predictor_type to regressor abandons classification entirely, so the notion of a false positive no longer applies. One honest caveat the question glosses over: target_precision and binary_classifier_model_selection_criteria are documented as applying to binary_classifier, while the scenario uses multiclass_classifier, so strictly the parameter is ignored there. Even so, C is the only option that conceptually addresses precision and false positives, and the other three are unambiguously wrong, making C the intended best answer.","explanation_zh":"降低 false positives 本質上是 precision 的目標：Precision = TP / (TP + FP)，要求模型維持更高的 precision 就會迫使它產生更少的 false positives。在 SageMaker linear learner 的這些選項中，唯一與 precision 相關的超參數是 target_precision。官方文件指出：'The target precision. If binary_classifier_model_selection_criteria is recall_at_target_precision, then precision is held at this value while recall is maximized.'（目標精確度；當 binary_classifier_model_selection_criteria 為 recall_at_target_precision 時，precision 固定於此值並最大化 recall。）因此提高 target_precision 會使所選模型朝向更高 precision 與更少 false positives，正是公司所需。其餘三個選項明顯偏離目標：將 wd（weight decay）設為零只是停用 L2 regularization，控制的是過擬合；增加 epochs 只改變訓練時間/收斂；而把 predictor_type 改為 regressor 則完全放棄分類，false positive 的概念便不再適用。需誠實指出題目忽略的一點：target_precision 與 binary_classifier_model_selection_criteria 在文件中僅適用於 binary_classifier，而情境使用的是 multiclass_classifier，故嚴格而言此參數會被忽略。即便如此，C 仍是唯一在概念上針對 precision 與 false positives 的選項，其餘三項明確錯誤，故 C 為題目意圖的最佳答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Setting wd (weight decay) to zero only disables L2 regularization, which governs overfitting and model complexity, not the precision/recall tradeoff that determines false positives. It does nothing to reduce false positives.","why_zh":"將 wd（weight decay）設為零只是停用 L2 regularization，那控制的是過擬合與模型複雜度，而非決定 false positives 的 precision/recall 取捨，對降低 false positives 毫無作用。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Increasing the number of training epochs only changes how many passes the model makes over the data (convergence, and potentially more overfitting). It does not adjust the decision threshold or optimize for precision, so it does not specifically reduce false positives.","why_zh":"增加訓練 epochs 只是改變模型掃過資料的次數（收斂，甚至可能更過擬合），並不會調整決策門檻或針對 precision 最佳化，因此無法特別降低 false positives。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Changing predictor_type to regressor abandons classification altogether; a regressor outputs a continuous numeric prediction with no class label, so concepts like false positives and precision do not even apply and the business goal cannot be met.","why_zh":"將 predictor_type 改為 regressor 完全放棄分類；regressor 輸出連續數值預測而無類別標籤，因此 false positives 與 precision 等概念根本不適用，也無法達成業務目標。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/ll_hyperparameters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/linear-learner.html"]}},{"id":36,"question_en":"A company has implemented a data ingestion pipeline for sales transactions from its ecommerce website. The company uses Amazon Data Firehose to ingest data into Amazon OpenSearch Service. The buffer interval of the Firehose stream is set for 60 seconds. An OpenSearch linear model generates real-time sales forecasts based on the data and presents the data in an OpenSearch dashboard. The company needs to optimize the data ingestion pipeline to support sub-second latency for the real-time dashboard. Which change to the architecture will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司已为其电子商务网站的销售交易实施了数据摄取管道。该公司使用亚马逊数据火线将数据摄取到 亚马逊 OpenSearch 服务中。火线流的缓冲间隔设置为 60 秒。OpenSearch 线性模型基于数据生成实时销 售预测，并在 OpenSearch 仪表板中展示数据。 该公司需要优化数据摄取管道，以支持实时仪表板实现亚秒级延迟。 哪种架构变更能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use zero buffering in the Firehose stream. Tune the batch size that is used in the PutRecordBatch operation.","B":"Replace the Firehose stream with an AWS DataSync task. Configure the task with enhanced fan-out consumers.","C":"Increase the buffer interval of the Firehose stream from 60 seconds to 120 seconds.","D":"Replace the Firehose stream with an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Firehose 流中使用零缓冲区。调整 PutRecordBatch 操作中使用的批处理大小。","B":"用 AWS DataSync 任务替换 Firehose 流。为该任务配置增强型扇出消费者。","C":"将 Firehose 流的缓冲间隔从 60 秒增加到 120 秒。","D":"用 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列替换 Firehose 流。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The pipeline is ecommerce site -> Amazon Data Firehose -> Amazon OpenSearch Service, and the sole latency bottleneck is the 60-second Firehose buffer interval. AWS documentation explicitly states: 'To meet lower latencies of real-time use cases, you can use zero buffering interval hint. When you configure buffering interval as zero seconds, Firehose will not buffer data and will deliver data within a few seconds.' The destination buffering-hint table confirms the OpenSearch destination accepts a buffering interval of 0-900 seconds, so a zero-second value is valid, and zero buffering is available for application destinations such as OpenSearch. Using zero buffering removes the buffering delay while keeping the existing Firehose-to-OpenSearch dashboard architecture intact, and tuning the PutRecordBatch batch size optimizes the producer write path for high-throughput, low-latency ingestion. Therefore Option A is the only change that drives latency toward sub-second without replacing the pipeline.","explanation_zh":"管線為電商網站 -> Amazon Data Firehose -> Amazon OpenSearch Service，唯一的延遲瓶頸是 Firehose 的 60 秒 buffer interval。AWS 官方文件明確指出：「為滿足即時使用情境的較低延遲，可使用 zero buffering interval hint。當你將 buffering interval 設為 0 秒時，Firehose 不會緩衝資料，會在幾秒內傳遞資料。」destination 的 buffering hint 對照表確認 OpenSearch destination 的 buffering interval 範圍為 0-900 秒，因此 0 秒為合法值，且 zero buffering 適用於 OpenSearch 等 application destinations。使用 zero buffering 可移除緩衝延遲，同時保留現有的 Firehose 到 OpenSearch 儀表板架構；而調整 PutRecordBatch 的 batch size 則可在生產者寫入端最佳化高吞吐、低延遲的擷取。因此選項 A 是唯一能將延遲降至接近 sub-second 又無須替換管線的變更。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS DataSync is a file/object data-transfer (migration) service for storage locations such as NFS, SMB, HDFS, S3, EFS, and FSx; it does not perform real-time streaming and cannot deliver to Amazon OpenSearch Service. 'Enhanced fan-out consumers' is an Amazon Kinesis Data Streams feature, not a DataSync feature, so this option is technically incoherent and would break the pipeline.","why_zh":"AWS DataSync 是針對 NFS、SMB、HDFS、S3、EFS、FSx 等儲存位置的檔案/物件資料傳輸（遷移）服務，不執行即時串流，也無法傳遞資料至 Amazon OpenSearch Service。「Enhanced fan-out consumers」是 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 的功能，而非 DataSync 的功能，因此此選項在技術上不合理且會破壞管線。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Increasing the buffer interval from 60 to 120 seconds makes latency worse, not better. A larger buffering interval means Firehose waits longer before delivering, which is the opposite of the sub-second latency requirement.","why_zh":"將 buffer interval 從 60 秒增加到 120 秒會使延遲更糟而非更好。較大的 buffering interval 代表 Firehose 在傳遞前等待更久，與 sub-second 延遲需求完全相反。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon SQS does not natively deliver to Amazon OpenSearch Service; replacing Firehose with SQS would require additional consumers (such as AWS Lambda) to poll messages and index them, adding operational overhead and latency while removing the built-in Firehose-to-OpenSearch integration. It does not achieve sub-second delivery to the dashboard.","why_zh":"Amazon SQS 無法原生傳遞資料至 Amazon OpenSearch Service；以 SQS 取代 Firehose 將需要額外的消費者（例如 AWS Lambda）輪詢訊息並建立索引，增加營運負擔與延遲，同時失去 Firehose 對 OpenSearch 的內建整合，無法達成對儀表板的 sub-second 傳遞。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/create-configure-backup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/APIReference/API_PutRecordBatch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/what-is-datasync.html"]}},{"id":37,"question_en":"A company has trained an ML model in Amazon SageMaker. The company needs to host the model to provide inferences in a production environment. The model must be highly available and must respond with minimum latency. The size of each request will be between 1 KB and 3 MB. The model will receive unpredictable bursts of requests during the day. The inferences must adapt proportionally to the changes in demand. How should the company deploy the model into production to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已在亚马逊 SageMaker 中训练了一个机器学习模型。该公司需要将模型部署起来，在生产 环境中提供推理服务。 该模型必须具备高可用性，并且响应延迟要尽可能小。每个请求的大小将在 1KB 到 3MB 之间。模型在 白天会收到不可预测的请求高峰。推理能力必须与需求变化成比例地进行调整。 公司应如何将模型部署到生产环境中以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a SageMaker real-time inference endpoint. Configure auto scaling. Configure the endpoint to present the existing model.","B":"Deploy the model on an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. Use ECS scheduled scaling that is based on the CPU of the ECS cluster.","C":"Install SageMaker Operator on an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. Deploy the model in Amazon EKS. Set horizontal pod auto scaling to scale replicas based on the memory metric.","D":"Use Spot Instances with a Spot Fleet behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) for inferences. Use the ALBRequestCountPerTarget metric as the metric for auto scaling."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 SageMaker 实时推理端点。配置自动缩放。将端点配置为呈现现有模型。","B":"在 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）集群上部署模型。使用基于 ECS 集群 CPU 的 ECS 计划扩展功能。","C":"在 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service （Amazon EKS） 集群上安装 SageMaker Operator。在 Amazon EKS 中部署模型。设置水平 Pod 自动扩展，根据内存指标来扩展副本。","D":"使用应用负载均衡器（ALB）后面的按需实例队列中的竞价实例进行推理。使用 ALBRequestCount PerTarget 指标作为自动扩展的指标。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"SageMaker Real-Time Inference is purpose-built for online, interactive workloads that require low latency and high availability, which directly matches 'minimum latency' and 'highly available.' The endpoint is a persistent, fully managed REST API backed by instances spread across multiple Availability Zones, and AWS docs state it supports payload sizes up to 25 MB, which comfortably covers the 1 KB to 3 MB request range. To make the inferences 'adapt proportionally to changes in demand' during 'unpredictable bursts,' you attach Application Auto Scaling to the endpoint; AWS docs state auto scaling 'dynamically adjusts the number of instances provisioned for a model in response to changes in your workload,' adding instances as traffic rises and removing them as it falls (typically target-tracking on SageMakerVariantInvocationsPerInstance). This is exactly what Option A describes: a real-time endpoint serving the existing model with auto scaling configured. (Note: SageMaker Serverless Inference also handles unpredictable traffic, but it caps payloads at 4 MB and incurs cold-start latency that conflicts with 'minimum latency,' and it is not offered as an answer choice here.)","explanation_zh":"SageMaker Real-Time Inference 專為需要低延遲與高可用性的線上互動式工作負載而設計，正好對應題目的「minimum latency」與「highly available」。該端點是一個持久、全託管的 REST API，由分散於多個 Availability Zone 的執行個體支援；AWS 文件指出它支援最大 25 MB 的 payload，足以涵蓋 1 KB 到 3 MB 的請求範圍。為了讓推論在「unpredictable bursts」期間能「按需求變化成比例調整」，可對端點附加 Application Auto Scaling；AWS 文件指出 auto scaling 會「依工作負載的變化動態調整為模型佈建的執行個體數量」，流量上升時增加執行個體、下降時移除執行個體（通常以 SageMakerVariantInvocationsPerInstance 做 target-tracking）。這正是選項 A 所述：以設定了 auto scaling 的 real-time endpoint 來服務既有模型。（補充：SageMaker Serverless Inference 同樣能處理不可預測流量，但其 payload 上限為 4 MB 且有 cold start 延遲，與「minimum latency」相衝突，且本題並未提供此選項。）","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Deploying on ECS with scheduled scaling based on cluster CPU does not adapt proportionally to unpredictable bursts. Scheduled scaling reacts to a calendar/time pattern, not to real-time demand, so it fails the 'unpredictable bursts' and 'adapt proportionally to demand' requirements, and it adds significant operational overhead versus a managed SageMaker endpoint.","why_zh":"在 ECS 上以叢集 CPU 的 scheduled scaling 部署，無法針對無法預測的突發流量成比例調整。Scheduled scaling 依時間排程觸發而非依即時需求，因此不符合「unpredictable bursts」與「按需求成比例調整」的要求，且相較全託管的 SageMaker 端點還增加大量維運負擔。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Running SageMaker Operator on EKS with horizontal pod autoscaling on a memory metric is far more operationally complex (you manage the EKS cluster, operator, and pods), and scaling on memory does not track request-volume demand for inference, so capacity will not adapt proportionally to traffic. It is overkill versus the lowest-latency, simplest highly available path the model already supports natively via a real-time endpoint.","why_zh":"在 EKS 上執行 SageMaker Operator 並以記憶體指標做 horizontal pod autoscaling，維運上複雜許多（需自管 EKS 叢集、operator 與 pod），且以記憶體做擴縮無法反映推論的請求量需求，容量無法按流量成比例調整。相對於模型可原生使用的 real-time 端點，這是過度設計，並非最低延遲、最簡單的高可用方案。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Spot Instances can be reclaimed with two minutes' notice, which undermines the high-availability and minimum-latency requirements for a production endpoint. While ALBRequestCountPerTarget could scale on demand, building a Spot Fleet behind an ALB with custom auto scaling is heavy self-managed infrastructure and is not the recommended way to host a SageMaker-trained model for low-latency production inference.","why_zh":"Spot Instances 可能在兩分鐘通知後被回收，會破壞正式環境端點的高可用與最低延遲要求。雖然 ALBRequestCountPerTarget 可依需求擴縮，但在 ALB 後方建置 Spot Fleet 並自訂 auto scaling 屬於繁重的自管基礎設施，並非託管 SageMaker 訓練模型以提供低延遲正式推論的建議做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/realtime-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/deploy-model-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/endpoint-auto-scaling.html"]}},{"id":38,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to use an Amazon EMR cluster to process large volumes of data in batches. Any data loss is unacceptable. Which instance purchasing option will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师需要使用亚马逊 EMR 集群以批处理的方式处理大量数据。任何数据丢失都是不 可接受的。 哪种实例购买选项能以最具成本效益的方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Run the primary node, core nodes, and task nodes on On-Demand Instances.","B":"Run the primary node, core nodes, and task nodes on Spot Instances.","C":"Run the primary node on an On-Demand Instance. Run the core nodes and task nodes on Spot Instances.","D":"Run the primary node and core nodes on On-Demand Instances. Run the task nodes on Spot Instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"在按需实例上运行主节点、核心节点和任务节点。","B":"在按需实例上运行主节点、核心节点和任务节点。","C":"在按需实例上运行主节点。在竞价实例上运行核心节点和任务节点。","D":"将主节点和核心节点部署在按需实例上。将任务节点部署在竞价实例上。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the textbook AWS EMR 'Data-critical workloads' scenario: lower cost is more important than time to completion, but losing partial work (data) is NOT acceptable. The official EMR best-practices table maps this scenario exactly to Primary=On-Demand, Core=On-Demand, Task=Spot. AWS explains that core nodes process data and store information in HDFS, so terminating a core node 'risks data loss' and core nodes should run on Spot only 'when partial HDFS data loss is tolerable'; the primary node controls the cluster and its termination ends the cluster. Running primary and core on On-Demand guarantees data persistence in HDFS and protects the cluster from Spot market fluctuations, while task nodes (which 'do not hold persistent data in HDFS' so that when reclaimed 'no data is lost and the effect on your cluster is minimal') run on Spot for the lowest cost. Therefore option D meets the no-data-loss requirement at the lowest cost.","explanation_zh":"這正是 AWS EMR 教科書級的 'Data-critical workloads' 情境：成本比完成時間重要，但絕對不能遺失任何工作 (資料)。官方 EMR 最佳實務表格將此情境精確對應到 Primary=On-Demand、Core=On-Demand、Task=Spot。AWS 說明 core 節點處理資料並以 HDFS 儲存資訊，因此終止 core 節點『會有資料遺失風險』，只有在『可容忍部分 HDFS 資料遺失時』才應在 core 節點使用 Spot；primary 節點控制叢集，其終止會結束整個叢集。將 primary 與 core 使用 On-Demand 可保證資料在 HDFS 中持久化，並避免叢集因 Spot 市場波動而終止；task 節點（『不儲存持久性 HDFS 資料』，被回收時『不會遺失資料且對叢集影響極小』）使用 Spot 以達到最低成本。因此選項 D 在不遺失任何資料的前提下達到最低成本。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Running all three node types on On-Demand prevents data loss but is the most expensive option, so it is not the MOST cost-effective. Task nodes hold no HDFS data and can safely use Spot for large savings with zero data-loss risk.","why_zh":"三種節點全部使用 On-Demand 雖可避免資料遺失，但成本最高，並非最具成本效益。Task 節點不存放 HDFS 資料，可安全使用 Spot 大幅省錢且無任何資料遺失風險。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Running everything on Spot is the AWS 'Cost-driven workloads' scenario, which AWS says applies only when 'losing partial work is acceptable.' Spot reclamation of core nodes causes HDFS data loss and reclamation of the primary node terminates the cluster, violating the 'any data loss is unacceptable' requirement.","why_zh":"全部使用 Spot 屬於 AWS 的 'Cost-driven workloads' 情境，AWS 明確指出此情境僅適用於『可接受部分工作遺失』時。Spot 回收 core 節點會造成 HDFS 資料遺失、回收 primary 節點會終止整個叢集，違反『任何資料遺失都不可接受』的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Putting core nodes on Spot risks HDFS data loss when those Spot Instances are reclaimed. AWS explicitly states to run core nodes on Spot only 'when partial HDFS data loss is tolerable,' which directly contradicts the requirement that any data loss is unacceptable.","why_zh":"將 core 節點放在 Spot，在這些 Spot Instance 被回收時會有 HDFS 資料遺失風險。AWS 明確指出只有在『可容忍部分 HDFS 資料遺失時』才在 core 節點使用 Spot，與『任何資料遺失都不可接受』的要求直接矛盾。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/emr/latest/ManagementGuide/emr-plan-instances-guidelines.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/emr/latest/ManagementGuide/emr-master-core-task-nodes.html"]}},{"id":39,"question_en":"A company wants to improve the sustainability of its ML operations. Which actions will reduce the energy usage and computational resources that are associated with the company's training jobs? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司希望提高其机器学习业务的可持续性。 哪些措施可以减少与公司培训任务相关的能源使用和计算资源？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon SageMaker Debugger to stop training jobs when non-converging conditions are detected.","B":"Use Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth for data labeling.","C":"Deploy models by using AWS Lambda functions.","D":"Use AWS Trainium instances for training.","E":"Use PyTorch or TensorFlow with the distributed training option."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon SageMaker Debugger 在检测到训练未收敛的情况时停止训练任务。","B":"使用 Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth 进行数据标注。","C":"使用 AWS Lambda 函数部署模型。","D":"使用 AWS Trainium 实例进行训练。","E":"使用 PyTorch 或 TensorFlow 并启用分布式训练选项。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The question maps to the AWS Well-Architected Machine Learning Lens sustainability pillar (MLSUS), which targets reduced energy and computational resources for ML workloads. Option A is correct: MLSUS04-BP01 (Define sustainable performance criteria) explicitly says to 'Use SageMaker AI Debugger to automatically stop training when specific conditions are met. Add rules like LossNotDecreasing... avoiding wasted computation' (early stopping for non-converging jobs). Option D is correct: MLSUS05-BP02 (Use efficient silicon) states that purpose-built ML accelerators reduce energy consumption by up to 60%, and that a Trainium-based cluster uses approximately 25% lower total energy to train BERT Large from scratch versus comparable accelerated EC2 instances. The other options are not sustainability/energy-reduction actions for training: Ground Truth (B) is data labeling, Lambda (C) is deployment/inference. Critically, distributed training (E) lives under the COST pillar (MLCOST04-BP07 'Use distributed training'), whose stated benefits are reduced training time and cost optimization; spreading work across more GPUs parallelizes compute to finish faster but does not inherently reduce total energy or computational resources, so it is not the energy-reduction answer.","explanation_zh":"本題對應 AWS Well-Architected Machine Learning Lens 的永續性支柱(MLSUS),目標是降低 ML 工作負載的能源與運算資源。選項 A 正確:MLSUS04-BP01(定義永續效能準則)明確指出要「使用 SageMaker AI Debugger,在符合特定條件時自動停止訓練;加入如 LossNotDecreasing 之類的規則……避免浪費運算」(對不收斂工作提早停止)。選項 D 正確:MLSUS05-BP02(使用高效晶片)指出專用 ML 加速器最多可降低 60% 能耗,且以 Trainium 叢集從頭訓練 BERT Large,總能耗約比相當的加速型 EC2 執行個體叢集低 25%。其餘選項並非針對訓練的永續/節能做法:Ground Truth(B)屬資料標註;Lambda(C)屬部署/推論。關鍵在於分散式訓練(E)歸屬於成本支柱(MLCOST04-BP07「使用分散式訓練」),其列出的效益是縮短訓練時間與成本最佳化;將工作分散到更多 GPU 是把運算平行化以更快完成,本質上並不會降低總能源或運算資源,因此不是節能的正解。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth is a data labeling service. Labeling is a data-preparation activity and does not reduce the energy or compute consumed by training jobs.","why_zh":"Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth 是資料標註服務,屬於資料準備活動,並不會降低訓練工作所耗用的能源或運算資源。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Deploying models with AWS Lambda concerns inference/deployment, not training. The question specifically asks about reducing resources associated with training jobs.","why_zh":"以 AWS Lambda 部署模型屬於推論/部署階段,與訓練無關。本題明確針對降低訓練工作相關的資源。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Distributed training (PyTorch/TensorFlow) is documented in the ML Lens COST pillar (MLCOST04-BP07), whose benefits are reduced training TIME and cost optimization, plus the ability to train models too large for one GPU. Parallelizing across more instances/GPUs finishes faster but does not inherently lower total energy or computational resources; it is not framed as a sustainability/energy-reduction action, unlike early stopping (MLSUS04-BP01) and efficient silicon/Trainium (MLSUS05-BP02).","why_zh":"分散式訓練(PyTorch/TensorFlow)記載於 ML Lens 的成本支柱(MLCOST04-BP07),其效益是縮短訓練時間與成本最佳化,並能訓練單一 GPU 容納不下的模型。將工作分散到更多執行個體/GPU 雖能更快完成,但本質上不會降低總能源或運算資源;它並未被定位為永續/節能做法,與提早停止(MLSUS04-BP01)及高效晶片/Trainium(MLSUS05-BP02)不同。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/machine-learning-lens/mlsus04-bp01.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/machine-learning-lens/mlsus05-bp02.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/machine-learning-lens/mlcost04-bp07.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/debugger-stop-training.html"]}},{"id":40,"question_en":"A company is planning to create several ML prediction models. The training data is stored in Amazon S3. The entire dataset is more than 5 TB in size and consists of CSV, JSON, Apache Parquet, and simple text files. The data must be processed in several consecutive steps. The steps include complex manipulations that can take hours to finish running. Some of the processing involves natural language processing (NLP) transformations. The entire process must be automated. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司计划创建多个机器学习预测模型。训练数据存储在亚马逊 S3 中。整个数据集大小超过 5 TB，包含 CSV、JSON、Apache Parquet 和简单的文本文件。 这些数据必须经过几个连续的步骤进行处理。这些步骤包含复杂的操作，可能需要数小时才能完成。其中 一些处理涉及自然语言处理（NLP）的转换。整个过程必须实现自动化。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Process data at each step by using Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler. Automate the process by using Data Wrangler jobs.","B":"Use Amazon SageMaker notebooks for each data processing step. Automate the process by using Amazon EventBridge.","C":"Process data at each step by using AWS Lambda functions. Automate the process by using AWS Step Functions and Amazon EventBridge.","D":"Use Amazon SageMaker Pipelines to create a pipeline of data processing steps. Automate the pipeline by using Amazon EventBridge."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个步骤中使用 Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler 处理数据。通过使用 Data Wrangler 作业来实现 流程自动化。","B":"对于每个数据处理步骤，使用 Amazon SageMaker 笔记本。通过使用 Amazon EventBridge 实现流程自 动化。","C":"在每个步骤中使用 AWS Lambda 函数处理数据。通过使用 AWS Step Functions 和 Amazon EventBridge 实 现流程自动化。","D":"使用 Amazon SageMaker Pipelines 创建数据处理步骤的流水线。通过使用 Amazon EventBridge 实现流水线 的自动化。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement is to automate several consecutive, complex data-processing steps (including NLP) on a 5+ TB mixed-format dataset (CSV, JSON, Parquet, text) where individual steps can run for hours. Amazon SageMaker Pipelines is the purpose-built orchestrator: a pipeline is a directed acyclic graph (DAG) of interconnected steps, and the ProcessingStep type runs SageMaker Processing jobs on fully managed infrastructure. SageMaker Processing reads multi-TB data directly from Amazon S3 and lets you bring your own container, so you can package custom NLP libraries, and processing jobs have no short execution-time limit, so hours-long steps are fine. The pipeline can be triggered automatically with Amazon EventBridge, satisfying full automation. This makes option D the complete fit.","explanation_zh":"需求是自動化編排數個連續且複雜的資料處理步驟（包含 NLP），資料集超過 5 TB、格式混合（CSV、JSON、Parquet、文字），且單一步驟可能執行數小時。Amazon SageMaker Pipelines 正是專為此設計的編排服務：一個 pipeline 是由互相連接的步驟構成的有向無環圖 (DAG)，其中 ProcessingStep 步驟類型會在全代管基礎設施上執行 SageMaker Processing 作業。SageMaker Processing 可直接從 Amazon S3 讀取多 TB 資料，並支援自帶容器 (bring your own container)，因此可打包自訂 NLP 函式庫；且 processing 作業沒有短時的執行時間限制，數小時的步驟完全可行。Pipeline 還可透過 Amazon EventBridge 自動觸發，滿足完全自動化的需求。因此選項 D 是最完整的解答。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SageMaker Data Wrangler is a low-/no-code visual data-prep feature of SageMaker Studio Classic (now in Canvas) aimed at interactive featurization and analysis. It is not designed to orchestrate a robust, multi-step, hours-long, multi-TB custom NLP processing workflow; in fact it exports data flows TO SageMaker Pipelines for automation rather than being the orchestration engine itself.","why_zh":"SageMaker Data Wrangler 是 SageMaker Studio Classic（現整合於 Canvas）中低程式碼/無程式碼的視覺化資料準備功能，著重互動式特徵化與分析。它並非用來編排穩健、多步驟、長達數小時、多 TB 的自訂 NLP 處理流程；事實上它是將 data flow 匯出至 SageMaker Pipelines 來自動化，本身並非編排引擎。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Driving each processing step from SageMaker notebooks and stitching them with EventBridge is operationally fragile and is not a managed pipeline pattern. Notebooks are interactive environments that require running instances and provide no built-in DAG, step dependency, retry, or caching orchestration for an automated multi-step ML workflow.","why_zh":"用 SageMaker notebook 執行各處理步驟、再以 EventBridge 串接，運維脆弱且非託管 pipeline 模式。Notebook 是互動式環境，需常駐執行個體，且缺乏內建 DAG、步驟相依、重試或快取等自動化多步驟 ML 工作流程的編排能力。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Lambda has a hard maximum timeout of 900 seconds (15 minutes), but the question states steps can take hours to finish. Lambda therefore cannot run these long, complex processing/NLP steps, so this option is technically disqualified regardless of Step Functions/EventBridge orchestration.","why_zh":"AWS Lambda 最長逾時為 900 秒 (15 分鐘)，但題目明示步驟可能執行數小時。Lambda 無法執行這些長時間、複雜的處理/NLP 步驟，因此不論用 Step Functions/EventBridge 編排，此選項在技術上都被排除。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/pipelines-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/build-and-manage-steps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/processing-job.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-timeout.html"]}},{"id":41,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to use AWS CloudFormation to create an ML model that an Amazon SageMaker endpoint will host. Which resource should the ML engineer declare in the CloudFormation template to meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师需要使用 AWS CloudFormation 来创建一个由 Amazon SageMaker 端点托管的机器学 习模型。 ML 工程师应在 CloudFormation 模板中声明哪种资源才能满足此要求？","options_en":{"A":"AWS::SageMaker::Model","B":"AWS::SageMaker::Endpoint","C":"AWS::SageMaker::NotebookInstance","D":"AWS::SageMaker::Pipeline"},"options_zh":{"A":"AWS::SageMaker:：模型","B":"AWS::SageMaker:：终端节点","C":"AWS::SageMaker:：笔记本实例","D":"AWS::SageMaker::Pipeline"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The question asks which CloudFormation resource declares the ML model that a SageMaker endpoint will host. The AWS CloudFormation Template Reference for AWS::SageMaker::Model states verbatim: 'The AWS::SageMaker::Model resource to create a model to host at an Amazon SageMaker endpoint.' This resource defines the model artifacts and inference container(s) via PrimaryContainer/Containers plus the ExecutionRoleArn, which together constitute the deployable model object. The hosting flow then references this model through an EndpointConfig (AWS::SageMaker::EndpointConfig) and an AWS::SageMaker::Endpoint, but those resources provision and deploy the hosting infrastructure rather than create the model itself. Therefore the resource that actually creates the ML model is AWS::SageMaker::Model.","explanation_zh":"本題詢問要用哪一個 CloudFormation 資源來宣告由 SageMaker endpoint 託管的 ML model。AWS CloudFormation Template Reference 對 AWS::SageMaker::Model 的描述逐字寫道:'The AWS::SageMaker::Model resource to create a model to host at an Amazon SageMaker endpoint.' 此資源透過 PrimaryContainer/Containers 以及 ExecutionRoleArn 定義 model 的 artifacts 與 inference container,這些共同構成可部署的 model 物件。後續的託管流程會透過 EndpointConfig(AWS::SageMaker::EndpointConfig)與 AWS::SageMaker::Endpoint 來參照此 model,但那些資源是用來佈建並部署託管基礎設施,而非建立 model 本身。因此真正建立 ML model 的資源是 AWS::SageMaker::Model。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS::SageMaker::Endpoint creates the hosting endpoint that provisions resources and deploys a model via an EndpointConfig; it does not create the model itself, which must already exist as an AWS::SageMaker::Model.","why_zh":"AWS::SageMaker::Endpoint 建立的是託管 endpoint,透過 EndpointConfig 佈建資源並部署 model;它本身不會建立 model,model 必須已先以 AWS::SageMaker::Model 存在。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS::SageMaker::NotebookInstance provisions a managed Jupyter notebook development environment for authoring code, not a deployable ML model hosted by an endpoint.","why_zh":"AWS::SageMaker::NotebookInstance 佈建的是託管式 Jupyter notebook 開發環境用於撰寫程式,而不是由 endpoint 託管的可部署 ML model。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS::SageMaker::Pipeline defines a SageMaker Pipelines workflow (DAG of ML steps) for orchestration, not the model object that an endpoint hosts.","why_zh":"AWS::SageMaker::Pipeline 定義的是 SageMaker Pipelines 工作流程(ML 步驟的 DAG)用於編排,而非 endpoint 託管的 model 物件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-sagemaker-model.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-sagemaker-endpoint.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/how-it-works-hosting.html"]}},{"id":42,"question_en":"An advertising company uses AWS Lake Formation to manage a data lake. The data lake contains structured data and unstructured data. The company's ML engineers are assigned to specific advertisement campaigns. The ML engineers must interact with the data through Amazon Athena and by browsing the data directly in an Amazon S3 bucket. The ML engineers must have access to only the resources that are specific to their assigned advertisement campaigns. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way?","question_zh":"一家广告公司使用 AWS Lake Formation 来管理数据湖。该数据湖包含结构化数据和非结构化数据。 公司的机器学习工程师被分配到特定的广告活动中。 机器学习工程师必须通过亚马逊 Athena 与数据进行交互，并直接在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中浏览数据。机器学习 工程师只能访问与其所负责的广告活动相关的特定资源。 哪种解决方案 将以最高效的操作方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure IAM policies on an AWS Glue Data Catalog to restrict access to Athena based on the ML engineers' campaigns.","B":"Store users and campaign information in an Amazon DynamoDB table. Configure DynamoDB Streams to invoke an AWS Lambda function to update S3 bucket policies.","C":"Use Lake Formation to authorize AWS Glue to access the S3 bucket. Configure Lake Formation tags to map ML engineers to their campaigns.","D":"Configure S3 bucket policies to restrict access to the S3 bucket based on the ML engineers' campaigns."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Glue 数据目录上配置 IAM 策略，以根据机器学习工程师的活动限制对 Athena 的访问。","B":"将用户和活动信息存储在 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。配置 DynamoDB 流以调用 AWS Lambda 函数来更新 S3 存储桶策略。","C":"使用 Lake Formation 授权 AWS Glue 访问 S3 存储桶。配置 Lake Formation 标签以将机器学习工程师与 其活动关联起来。","D":"配置 S3 存储桶策略，根据机器学习工程师的活动限制对 S3 存储桶的访问。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The data lake is already governed by AWS Lake Formation, which provides a centralized, fine-grained (RDBMS-style) permissions model that AWS docs say explicitly 'replaces the complex Amazon S3 bucket policies and corresponding IAM policies.' Option C uses the native pattern: register the S3 location so Lake Formation authorizes the AWS Glue/Lake Formation service role to access the bucket (credential vending), then use Lake Formation tag-based access control (LF-Tags) to map each ML engineer to their campaign. AWS documents LF-TBAC as the recommended, lowest-maintenance method when there are a large number of Data Catalog objects, because you grant on tag expressions instead of making per-resource grants. This works for Athena, a trusted integrated engine that checks Lake Formation permissions and receives vended, scoped S3 credentials, and it centralizes governance over the underlying registered S3 data. The qualifier 'MOST operationally efficient' decides in favor of LF-Tags over hand-maintained IAM/Glue policies, hand-maintained S3 bucket policies, or a custom DynamoDB/Streams/Lambda pipeline, all of which scale poorly and duplicate the governance the lake already has.","explanation_zh":"此 data lake 已由 AWS Lake Formation 集中治理，它提供集中式、細粒度（類 RDBMS）的權限模型，AWS 文件明確指出可『取代複雜的 Amazon S3 bucket policies 與對應的 IAM policies』。選項 C 採用原生模式：註冊 S3 location，讓 Lake Formation 授權 AWS Glue/Lake Formation 服務角色存取該 bucket（credential vending），再使用 Lake Formation tag-based access control（LF-Tags）將每位 ML engineer 對應到其廣告活動。AWS 文件指出，當 Data Catalog 物件數量龐大時，LF-TBAC 是建議且維運成本最低的授權方法，因為是針對 tag 運算式授權，而非逐一資源授權。這對 Athena 有效，因為 Athena 是受信任的整合引擎，會檢查 Lake Formation 權限並取得被限縮範圍的 S3 暫時憑證，同時對底層已註冊的 S3 資料集中治理。題目限定『MOST operationally efficient』使得 LF-Tags 優於手動維護的 IAM/Glue policies、手動維護的 S3 bucket policies，或自建的 DynamoDB/Streams/Lambda 流程，後三者擴充性差且重複建置 data lake 已具備的治理機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"IAM policies on the Glue Data Catalog only govern the Athena/metadata layer and do not address browsing the underlying S3 data; they also bypass the existing Lake Formation governance. AWS explicitly states Lake Formation replaces such complex IAM/Glue policies, and per-campaign catalog IAM policies scale poorly and are harder to manage, so this is not the most operationally efficient choice.","why_zh":"在 Glue Data Catalog 上設定 IAM policies 只治理 Athena/metadata 層，無法涵蓋瀏覽底層 S3 資料，且繞過既有的 Lake Formation 治理。AWS 明確指出 Lake Formation 取代此類複雜的 IAM/Glue policies，且逐活動的 catalog IAM policies 擴充性差、難以管理，故非最具維運效率的選項。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Building a DynamoDB table plus DynamoDB Streams plus a Lambda function to rewrite S3 bucket policies is a brittle, custom, high-maintenance pipeline that reinvents access control the lake already has via Lake Formation. S3 bucket policies also have size limits and do not scale to many campaigns/principals, and it ignores the Athena/Glue Data Catalog integration, making it the least operationally efficient option.","why_zh":"建置 DynamoDB 表加 DynamoDB Streams 再加 Lambda 來改寫 S3 bucket policies，是脆弱、自建且維運成本高的流程，重做 data lake 已透過 Lake Formation 提供的存取控制。S3 bucket policies 亦有大小限制，無法擴展至大量活動/主體，且忽略 Athena/Glue Data Catalog 整合，故為最不具維運效率的選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Hand-maintained per-campaign S3 bucket policies are exactly what Lake Formation is designed to replace; they do not integrate with the Glue Data Catalog metadata-level controls Athena uses, and they scale poorly because of bucket policy size limits and per-prefix rule sprawl. This is the opposite of operationally efficient for campaign-scoped access.","why_zh":"手動維護逐活動的 S3 bucket policies 正是 Lake Formation 設計要取代的對象；它無法與 Athena 所用的 Glue Data Catalog metadata 層級控制整合，且因 bucket policy 大小限制與逐 prefix 規則膨脹而擴充性差。對於以活動為範圍的存取而言，這與最具維運效率背道而馳。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/how-it-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/tag-based-access-control.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/register-data-lake.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/storage-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/security-athena-lake-formation.html"]}},{"id":43,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to use data with Amazon SageMaker Canvas to train an ML model. The data is stored in Amazon S3 and is complex in structure. The ML engineer must use a file format that minimizes processing time for the data. Which file format will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师需要使用亚马逊 S3 中存储的数据通过亚马逊 SageMaker Canvas 来训练机器学习模型。 这些数据结构复杂，工程师必须选用一种能最大程度减少处理步骤的文件格式。 数据处理时间。 哪种文件格式能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"CSV files compressed with Snappy","B":"JSON objects in JSONL format","C":"JSON files compressed with gzip","D":"Apache Parquet files"},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Snappy 压缩的 CSV 文件","B":"JSONL 格式的 JSON 对象","C":"用 gzip 压缩的 JSON 文件","D":"Apache Parquet 文件"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Apache Parquet is correct. The Amazon SageMaker Canvas 'Create a dataset' documentation lists the supported file types for tabular models (categorical, numeric, time series, and text) as 'CSV and Parquet (local upload, Amazon S3, or databases); JSON (databases)'. JSON is therefore only an option when importing from a database, never from Amazon S3, which eliminates both JSON choices for an S3-stored dataset. The same page restricts S3 and local tabular imports to files with the extensions .csv, .parquet, .parq, and .pqt, and states that only Parquet files may use compression (gzip or snappy) — CSV files cannot be Snappy-compressed in Canvas. Between the only two valid S3 formats (CSV and Parquet), Parquet is a columnar, compressed, splittable format that stores data column-by-column with built-in statistics, so it minimizes the data scanned and the processing time when ingesting large, complex/structured datasets from S3. The first analyst's verdict (D) is fully supported by the AWS documentation.","explanation_zh":"正確答案是 Apache Parquet。Amazon SageMaker Canvas 的「Create a dataset」文件列出 tabular 模型（categorical、numeric、time series 與 text）支援的檔案類型為 'CSV 與 Parquet（local upload、Amazon S3 或 databases）；JSON（僅 databases）'。因此 JSON 只有在從資料庫匯入時才支援，無法從 Amazon S3 匯入，對於存放在 S3 的資料集即可排除兩個 JSON 選項。同一頁面亦限制 S3 與本機的 tabular 匯入只允許副檔名為 .csv、.parquet、.parq、.pqt 的檔案，並說明只有 Parquet 檔案可使用壓縮（gzip 或 snappy）—CSV 在 Canvas 中無法使用 Snappy 壓縮。在僅有的兩種有效 S3 格式（CSV 與 Parquet）中，Parquet 是 columnar、壓縮、可切分的格式，逐欄儲存並內建統計資訊，因此在從 S3 匯入大型且結構複雜的資料時能最小化掃描資料量與處理時間。第一位分析師的判定（D）完全獲得 AWS 官方文件支持。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Canvas does not support Snappy-compressed CSV. The docs limit compression (gzip/snappy) to Parquet files only, and CSV is a row-based text format that is far less efficient than columnar Parquet for large, complex/structured data, so it does not minimize processing time.","why_zh":"Canvas 不支援 Snappy 壓縮的 CSV。文件僅允許 Parquet 檔案使用壓縮（gzip/snappy），而 CSV 是 row-based 文字格式，對大型且結構複雜的資料遠不如 columnar 的 Parquet 有效率，無法最小化處理時間。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"JSON (including JSONL) is only supported when importing from databases, not from Amazon S3. Canvas restricts S3 and local tabular imports to .csv, .parquet, .parq, and .pqt extensions, so a JSONL file in S3 cannot be imported.","why_zh":"JSON（含 JSONL）僅在從 databases 匯入時支援，無法從 Amazon S3 匯入。Canvas 將 S3 與本機的 tabular 匯入限制為 .csv、.parquet、.parq、.pqt 副檔名，因此 S3 中的 JSONL 檔案無法匯入。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same limitation as B: JSON is supported only from databases, not S3, and gzip-compressed JSON is not among the accepted S3 extensions (.csv, .parquet, .parq, .pqt). It is not a valid Canvas S3 import format and JSON text is slower to scan than columnar Parquet.","why_zh":"與 B 相同的限制：JSON 僅支援從 databases 匯入而非 S3，且 gzip 壓縮的 JSON 不在可接受的 S3 副檔名（.csv、.parquet、.parq、.pqt）之列，並非有效的 Canvas S3 匯入格式，且 JSON 文字掃描速度比 columnar 的 Parquet 慢。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-import-dataset.html"]}},{"id":44,"question_en":"An ML engineer is evaluating several ML models and must choose one model to use in production. The cost of false negative predictions by the models is much higher than the cost of false positive predictions. Which metric finding should the ML engineer prioritize the MOST when choosing the model?","question_zh":"","options_en":{"A":"Low precision","B":"High precision","C":"Low recall","D":"High recall"},"options_zh":{},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Recall = TP / (TP + FN), so it is the metric that directly penalizes false negatives. AWS defines recall as the fraction of actual positives that the model correctly predicts as positive, and states that a larger value indicates better predictive accuracy. A false negative is a case where the true value is positive (1) but the model predicts negative (0) - exactly the missed positive that recall captures. Because the question says false negatives are far more costly than false positives, the engineer wants to minimize missed positives, which means maximizing recall. AWS explicitly describes this scenario: an application that 'needs to correctly predict as many positive examples as possible' should target high recall (accepting some false positives / moderate precision). Therefore High recall (D) is the metric to prioritize.","explanation_zh":"Recall = TP / (TP + FN)，因此它正是直接懲罰 false negative 的指標。AWS 將 recall 定義為模型正確預測為正類的實際正類比例，且數值越大代表預測準確度越好。False negative 指實際值為正類 (1) 但模型預測為負類 (0) 的情況，也就是被漏掉的正類，正是 recall 所衡量的對象。由於題目說 false negative 的成本遠高於 false positive，工程師希望盡量減少被漏掉的正類，也就是要最大化 recall。AWS 文件明確描述此情境：當應用程式『需要盡可能正確預測出最多的正類範例』時應追求 high recall（並接受部分 false positive / 中等的 precision）。因此應優先選擇 High recall (D)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Low precision is never a goal; precision relates to false positives (TP/(TP+FP)), not false negatives, and you would never deliberately prioritize a 'low' quality metric.","why_zh":"Low precision 從來不是目標；precision 與 false positive 相關 (TP/(TP+FP))，與 false negative 無關，且不會刻意追求『低』的品質指標。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"High precision optimizes against false positives; AWS notes precision is the metric that matters 'when the cost of a false positive is high' - the opposite of this question, where false negatives are the costly errors.","why_zh":"High precision 是針對 false positive 的優化；AWS 指出 precision 在『false positive 成本高』時才是重要指標，與本題相反，本題的高成本錯誤是 false negative。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Low recall means MORE false negatives go uncaught (Recall = TP/(TP+FN), more missed positives) - the exact failure mode that must be avoided when false negatives are costly.","why_zh":"Low recall 代表更多 false negative 未被捕捉（Recall = TP/(TP+FN)，漏掉更多正類），正是 false negative 成本高時必須避免的失敗模式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/latest/dg/binary-model-insights.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-metrics.html"]}},{"id":45,"question_en":"A company has trained and deployed an ML model by using Amazon SageMaker. The company needs to implement a solution to record and monitor all the API call events for the SageMaker endpoint. The solution also must provide a notification when the number of API call events breaches a threshold. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 SageMaker 训练并部署了一个机器学习模型。该公司需要实施一个解决方案来记录和 监控 SageMaker 端点的所有 API 调用事件。该解决方案还必须在 API 调用事件数量超过阈值时提供通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use SageMaker Debugger to track the inferences and to report metrics. Create a custom rule to provide a notification when the threshold is breached.","B":"Use SageMaker Debugger to track the inferences and to report metrics. Use the tensor_variance built- in rule to provide a notification when the threshold is breached.","C":"Log all the endpoint invocation API events by using AWS CloudTrail. Use an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard for monitoring. Set up a CloudWatch alarm to provide notification when the threshold is breached.","D":"Add the Invocations metric to an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard for monitoring. Set up a CloudWatch alarm to provide notification when the threshold is breached."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 SageMaker Debugger 来跟踪推理过程并报告指标。创建自定义规则，在阈值被突破时提供通 知。","B":"使用 SageMaker Debugger 来跟踪推理过程并报告指标。使用内置的 tensor_variance 规则在阈值被突破时 提供通知。","C":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 记录所有端点调用 API 事件。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板进行监控。设 置 CloudWatch 警报，在阈值被突破时提供通知。","D":"将调用次数指标添加到 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板中以进行监控。设置 CloudWatch 警报，以便在阈值 被突破时提供通知。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The SageMaker 'Invocations' CloudWatch metric is officially defined as 'The number of InvokeEndpoint requests sent to a model endpoint' and is published automatically to the AWS/SageMaker namespace as an endpoint invocation metric at 1-minute frequency, with a 15-month retention. This metric IS the count of API call events to the endpoint. Adding it to a CloudWatch dashboard satisfies the record-and-monitor requirement, and a CloudWatch alarm on the Invocations Sum statistic sends an SNS notification the moment the request count breaches a threshold. This is the AWS-native, lowest-overhead pattern and directly fulfills all three requirements (record, monitor, and notify on a count threshold). Option C (the dump's suggested answer) is wrong because InvokeEndpoint is a CloudTrail data event that is NOT logged by default and is never kept in Event history; more importantly, a CloudWatch alarm cannot watch raw CloudTrail logs - you would need CloudTrail to deliver to CloudWatch Logs plus a metric filter before an alarm could fire on a count, a step Option C omits. CloudTrail is an audit/governance tool, not a count-and-threshold alarming mechanism for inference traffic.","explanation_zh":"SageMaker 的 CloudWatch 'Invocations' 指標官方定義為「傳送到模型端點的 InvokeEndpoint 請求數量」，會自動以 1 分鐘頻率發佈到 AWS/SageMaker 命名空間（endpoint invocation 指標），並保留 15 個月。此指標本身即為端點 API 呼叫事件的計數。將其加入 CloudWatch dashboard 可滿足記錄與監控需求，並在 Invocations 的 Sum 統計上設定 CloudWatch alarm，即可在請求數量超過閾值時透過 SNS 立即發出通知。這是 AWS 原生、營運開銷最低的做法，直接滿足三項需求（記錄、監控、以及在計數閾值上通知）。選項 C（dump 建議答案）錯誤，因為 InvokeEndpoint 屬於 CloudTrail data event，預設不會記錄且不會保留在 Event history；更關鍵的是 CloudWatch alarm 無法直接監看原始 CloudTrail 日誌——需先將 CloudTrail 送到 CloudWatch Logs 並建立 metric filter，alarm 才能對計數告警，C 省略了此步驟。CloudTrail 是稽核/治理工具，並非針對推論流量做計數與閾值告警的機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SageMaker Debugger monitors and debugs training jobs (tensors, gradients, system resources), not endpoint inference API call counts. It does not track InvokeEndpoint events nor alarm on invocation volume, so it cannot meet the requirement.","why_zh":"SageMaker Debugger 用於監控與除錯訓練作業（張量、梯度、系統資源），而非端點推論的 API 呼叫計數，無法追蹤 InvokeEndpoint 事件或對呼叫量告警，故無法滿足需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same Debugger limitation as A (it targets training, not endpoint API calls); additionally the tensor_variance built-in rule inspects the variance of tensor values during training, which is entirely unrelated to counting endpoint API call events.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的 Debugger 限制（針對訓練而非端點 API 呼叫）；此外 tensor_variance 內建規則檢查訓練期間張量值的變異數，與計數端點 API 呼叫事件完全無關。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"InvokeEndpoint is a CloudTrail data event - by default CloudTrail does not log data events and they never appear in Event history, so logging them requires explicit data-event selectors. Critically, a CloudWatch alarm watches CloudWatch metrics, not raw CloudTrail logs; alarming on a count would need CloudTrail to CloudWatch Logs plus a metric filter first, which this option omits. CloudTrail is for audit/governance, not native count-threshold alarming, so it is incomplete and not the best fit.","why_zh":"InvokeEndpoint 屬於 CloudTrail data event——預設 CloudTrail 不記錄 data event，且永遠不會出現在 Event history，因此需明確設定 data-event selector 才能記錄。關鍵在於 CloudWatch alarm 監看的是 CloudWatch 指標而非原始 CloudTrail 日誌；要對計數告警需先將 CloudTrail 送至 CloudWatch Logs 並建立 metric filter，本選項省略此步驟。CloudTrail 用於稽核/治理而非原生的計數閾值告警，故不完整且非最佳解。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/monitoring-cloudwatch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/logging-using-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/AlarmThatSendsEmail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/logging-data-events-with-cloudtrail.html"]}},{"id":46,"question_en":"A company has AWS Glue data processing jobs that are orchestrated by an AWS Glue workflow. The AWS Glue jobs can run on a schedule or can be launched manually. The company is developing pipelines in Amazon SageMaker Pipelines for ML model development. The pipelines will use the output of the AWS Glue jobs during the data processing phase of model development. An ML engineer needs to implement a solution that integrates the AWS Glue jobs with the pipelines. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有由 AWS Glue 工作流编排的 AWS Glue 数据处理作业。这些 AWS Glue 作业可以按照 计划运行，也可以手动启动。 该公司正在亚马逊的 SageMaker Pipelines 中开发用于机器学习模型开发的管道。这些管道在模型开发 的数据处理阶段将使用 AWS Glue 作业的输出。一位机器学习工程师需要实现一个将 AWS Glue 作业 与管道集成的解决方案。 哪种解决方案能在运营开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Step Functions for orchestration of the pipelines and the AWS Glue jobs.","B":"Use processing steps in SageMaker Pipelines. Configure inputs that point to the Amazon Resource Names (ARNs) of the AWS Glue jobs.","C":"Use Callback steps in SageMaker Pipelines to start the AWS Glue workflow and to stop the pipelines until the AWS Glue jobs finish running.","D":"Use Amazon EventBridge to invoke the pipelines and the AWS Glue jobs in the desired order."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Step Functions 对管道和 AWS Glue 作业进行编排。","B":"在 SageMaker 管道中使用处理步骤。配置指向 AWS Glue 作业的 Amazon 资源名称（ARN）的输 入。","C":"在 SageMaker 管道中使用回调步骤来启动 AWS Glue 工作流，并在 AWS Glue 作业完成运行之前停 止管道。","D":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 按照期望的顺序调用管道和 AWS Glue 作业。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The Callback step is purpose-built for exactly this scenario. AWS docs state: 'Use a Callback step to add additional processes and AWS services into your workflow that aren't directly provided by Amazon SageMaker Pipelines.' When the Callback step runs, Pipelines sends a message containing a generated token to a customer-specified Amazon SQS queue and then waits; a consumer retrieves the message and starts the custom process (here, the existing AWS Glue workflow that already orchestrates the Glue jobs), and on completion calls SendPipelineExecutionStepSuccess (or SendPipelineExecutionStepFailure) with the token to resume or fail the pipeline. This reuses the already-built Glue workflow inside the SageMaker pipeline with the least operational overhead: the only new pieces are an SQS queue and a small consumer to start the workflow and signal completion. No Glue logic is re-implemented and no separate external orchestrator is introduced.","explanation_zh":"Callback step 正是為此情境設計。AWS 官方文件明確指出：'Use a Callback step to add additional processes and AWS services into your workflow that aren't directly provided by Amazon SageMaker Pipelines.' 當 Callback step 執行時，Pipelines 會把含有產生之 token 的訊息送到客戶指定的 Amazon SQS queue，然後等待；消費端取得訊息並啟動自訂流程（此處即已存在、且已負責編排各 Glue jobs 的 AWS Glue workflow），完成後再以該 token 呼叫 SendPipelineExecutionStepSuccess（或 SendPipelineExecutionStepFailure）讓 pipeline 繼續或失敗。如此可直接在 SageMaker pipeline 內重複使用既有的 Glue workflow，營運負擔最低：唯一新增的只有一個 SQS queue 與一個小型消費端來啟動 workflow 並回報完成，不需重寫 Glue 邏輯，也不需另建外部編排器。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Using Step Functions to orchestrate both the SageMaker pipeline and the Glue jobs adds a whole new orchestration layer outside both existing systems, and would require rebuilding/replicating the existing Glue workflow orchestration in Step Functions. That is significantly more operational overhead than embedding a native Callback step in the existing pipeline to invoke the existing Glue workflow.","why_zh":"用 Step Functions 同時編排 SageMaker pipeline 與 Glue jobs，等於在兩個既有系統之外新增一整層編排，且需在 Step Functions 中重建/複製既有的 Glue workflow 邏輯，相較於在既有 pipeline 內嵌入原生 Callback step 來呼叫既有 Glue workflow，營運負擔明顯較高。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"There is no SageMaker ProcessingStep input that points to a Glue job ARN to run it. A ProcessingStep launches a SageMaker Processing job (a container on SageMaker-managed compute); its inputs are ProcessingInput objects (S3 data sources/destinations), not Glue job ARNs. It cannot trigger or wait on the existing Glue workflow, so this would mean re-implementing the Glue logic as a Processing job—high overhead and contrary to reusing the existing jobs.","why_zh":"SageMaker ProcessingStep 並沒有可指向 Glue job ARN 來執行它的輸入。ProcessingStep 啟動的是 SageMaker Processing job（在 SageMaker 管理的運算上跑容器），其 inputs 是 ProcessingInput 物件（S3 資料來源/目的地），而非 Glue job ARN，無法觸發或等待既有的 Glue workflow；此選項等於要把 Glue 邏輯重寫成 Processing job，負擔高且違背重複使用既有作業的目標。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EventBridge can trigger jobs on events/schedules but it is not a sequential orchestrator that runs the Glue jobs first and then starts the pipeline 'in the desired order' with completion dependencies. Coordinating ordering and waiting for Glue completion via EventBridge requires extra plumbing (multiple rules, completion events, possibly Lambda) and does not give the pipeline an in-line wait, resulting in more overhead and fragility than a Callback step.","why_zh":"EventBridge 能依事件/排程觸發作業，但它不是能先跑 Glue jobs、再依完成相依性『按期望順序』啟動 pipeline 的循序編排器。要用 EventBridge 協調順序並等待 Glue 完成需額外串接（多條 rule、完成事件、可能還要 Lambda），且無法在 pipeline 內提供同步等待，較 Callback step 更繁瑣且脆弱。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/build-and-manage-steps-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/APIReference/API_SendPipelineExecutionStepSuccess.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/APIReference/API_SendPipelineExecutionStepFailure.html"]}},{"id":47,"question_en":"A company is using an Amazon Redshift database as its single data source. Some of the data is sensitive. A data scientist needs to use some of the sensitive data from the database. An ML engineer must give the data scientist access to the data without transforming the source data and without storing anonymized data in the database. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST implementation effort?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用亚马逊 Redshift 数据库作为其唯一的数据源。其中部分数据是敏感的。 数据科学家需要使用数据库中的一些敏感数据。机器学习工程师必须让数据科学家能够访问这些数据， 同时既不能对源数据进行转换，也不能在数据库中存储匿名化数据。 哪种解决方案能以最少的实施工作量满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure dynamic data masking policies to control how sensitive data is shared with the data scientist at query time.","B":"Create a materialized view with masking logic on top of the database. Grant the necessary read permissions to the data scientist.","C":"Unload the Amazon Redshift data to Amazon S3. Use Amazon Athena to create schema-on-read with masking logic. Share the view with the data scientist.","D":"Unload the Amazon Redshift data to Amazon S3. Create an AWS Glue job to anonymize the data. Share the dataset with the data scientist."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置动态数据屏蔽策略，以控制在查询时如何与数据科学家共享敏感数据。","B":"在数据库之上创建一个带有屏蔽逻辑的物化视图。向数据科学家授予必要的读取权限。","C":"将 Amazon Redshift 中的数据卸载到 Amazon S3。使用 Amazon Athena 创建读取时模式并应用掩码逻 辑。与数据科学家共享视图。","D":"将 Amazon Redshift 中的数据卸载到 Amazon S3。创建一个 AWS Glue 作业来对数据进行匿名化处 理。与数据科学家共享该数据集。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Database","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Redshift dynamic data masking (DDM) is purpose-built for this exact requirement. The official Redshift docs state you can 'manipulate how Amazon Redshift shows sensitive data to the user at query time, without transforming it in the database' by attaching masking policies (custom obfuscation rules) to a user or role via RBAC. This satisfies every constraint: the source data is never transformed, no anonymized/derived copy is persisted in the database (masking is applied dynamically at query time), and it is the lowest-effort approach because the ML engineer simply creates a masking policy and attaches it to the data scientist's role/columns. The other options all require building masking/anonymization logic and either persist a derived dataset (materialized view, Glue-anonymized dataset) or move the data out of the single Redshift source (S3 + Athena, S3 + Glue), adding effort and storing anonymized data, which violates the requirements.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Redshift dynamic data masking (DDM) 正是為此需求量身打造的功能。官方 Redshift 文件明確指出，透過 RBAC 將 masking policy (自訂混淆規則) 附加到使用者或 role，即可『在查詢時 (at query time) 控制 Amazon Redshift 如何向使用者顯示敏感資料，而不需在資料庫中轉換資料』。這完全符合所有限制：來源資料不會被轉換、資料庫中不會持久化任何匿名化/衍生副本 (遮罩是在查詢時動態套用)，而且這是工作量最少的方式，ML engineer 只需建立一個 masking policy 並附加到 data scientist 的 role 或欄位即可。其他選項都需要自行建構 masking/匿名化邏輯，且不是持久化一份衍生資料集 (materialized view、Glue 匿名化後的資料集)，就是把資料搬出單一的 Redshift 來源 (S3 + Athena、S3 + Glue)，既增加工作量又會儲存匿名化資料，違反需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A materialized view stores precomputed results, so the masked/anonymized output is physically persisted in the database, violating the 'without storing anonymized data in the database' requirement. It also requires authoring masking logic and managing refreshes, so it is more effort than DDM.","why_zh":"Materialized view 會儲存預先計算的結果，因此遮罩/匿名化後的輸出會實際持久化在資料庫中，違反『不在資料庫中儲存匿名化資料』的要求；它還需要撰寫 masking 邏輯並管理 refresh，工作量比 DDM 更大。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Unloading to Amazon S3 and using Athena schema-on-read with masking logic moves data out of the single Redshift source and is a much larger re-architecture and implementation effort than a built-in DDM policy.","why_zh":"把資料 unload 到 Amazon S3 再用 Athena schema-on-read 加上遮罩邏輯，會把資料搬出單一的 Redshift 來源，且比內建的 DDM 政策需要更大規模的重新架構與實作工作量。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An AWS Glue job to anonymize the data creates and stores a separate anonymized dataset (in S3) outside the source, and is the heaviest implementation effort, contradicting both the no-stored-anonymized-data and least-effort requirements.","why_zh":"用 AWS Glue job 匿名化資料會在來源之外建立並儲存一份獨立的匿名化資料集 (於 S3)，是最重的實作工作量，同時違反『不儲存匿名化資料』與『最少工作量』兩項要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/redshift/latest/dg/t_ddm.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/redshift/latest/dg/t_ddm-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/redshift/latest/dg/materialized-view-overview.html"]}},{"id":48,"question_en":"An ML engineer is using a training job to fine-tune a deep learning model in Amazon SageMaker Studio. The ML engineer previously used the same pre-trained model with a similar dataset. The ML engineer expects vanishing gradient, underutilized GPU, and overfitting problems. The ML engineer needs to implement a solution to detect these issues and to react in predefined ways when the issues occur. The solution also must provide comprehensive real-time metrics during the training. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师正在使用训练任务在亚马逊 SageMaker Studio 中对深度学习模型进行微调。该工程师 此前曾使用相同的预训练模型处理过类似的训练数据集。这位工程师预计会出现梯度消失、GPU 利用率 低以及过拟合等问题。 机器学习工程师需要实现一种解决方案，以检测这些问题，并在问题出现时以预定义的方式做出反应。 该解决方案还必须在训练期间提供全面的实时指标。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use TensorBoard to monitor the training job. Publish the findings to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Create an AWS Lambda function to consume the findings and to initiate the predefined actions.","B":"Use Amazon CloudWatch default metrics to gain insights about the training job. Use the metrics to invoke an AWS Lambda function to initiate the predefined actions.","C":"Expand the metrics in Amazon CloudWatch to include the gradients in each training step. Use the metrics to invoke an AWS Lambda function to initiate the predefined actions.","D":"Use SageMaker Debugger built-in rules to monitor the training job. Configure the rules to initiate the predefined actions."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 TensorBoard 监控训练任务。将发现结果发布到 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。创建 一个 AWS Lambda 函数来获取这些发现结果并启动预定义的操作。","B":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 的默认指标来深入了解训练作业。利用这些指标调用 AWS Lambda 函数以 启动预定义的操作。","C":"在 Amazon CloudWatch 中扩展指标，以包含每个训练步骤中的梯度。使用这些指标调用 AWS Lambda 函数来启动预定义的操作。","D":"使用 SageMaker Debugger 内置规则来监控训练任务。配置规则以启动预定义的操作。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Amazon SageMaker Debugger is purpose-built for this scenario. Its built-in rules natively detect all three named issues: the vanishing_gradient rule (for deep learning frameworks), the LowGPUUtilization profiler rule (for GPU underutilization), and the overfit/overtraining rules. Debugger evaluates output tensors and system metrics in real time during training, delivering the comprehensive real-time metrics the question requires. To react in predefined ways with no custom code, Debugger provides built-in actions (StopTraining, Email, and SMS via Amazon SNS) that are attached directly to the rules, and it is a fully managed capability of SageMaker, giving the LEAST operational overhead. Options A, B, and C each require building and maintaining custom plumbing (TensorBoard analysis plus SNS plus Lambda, default CloudWatch metrics plus Lambda, or custom per-step gradient metrics plus Lambda), and none of them natively detect vanishing gradients or GPU underutilization, so they are both higher overhead and technically incomplete.","explanation_zh":"Amazon SageMaker Debugger 正是為此情境設計的工具。其 built-in rules 可原生偵測題目所列的三種問題：vanishing_gradient rule（適用於深度學習框架）、LowGPUUtilization profiler rule（偵測 GPU 使用率過低），以及 overfit/overtraining rules。Debugger 在訓練過程中即時評估 output tensors 與系統指標，提供題目要求的全面即時指標。要以預先定義的方式反應且無需自訂程式碼，Debugger 提供 built-in actions（StopTraining、Email、以及透過 Amazon SNS 的 SMS），可直接掛在 rules 上；而且 Debugger 是 SageMaker 的全託管功能，因此維運負擔最低。選項 A、B、C 都需要自行建置與維護額外的串接（TensorBoard 分析加 SNS 加 Lambda、預設 CloudWatch 指標加 Lambda、或自訂逐步梯度指標加 Lambda），且都無法原生偵測 vanishing gradient 或 GPU 使用率過低，因此維運負擔更高且技術上不完整。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"TensorBoard only visualizes metrics; it does not auto-detect vanishing gradients, GPU underutilization, or overfitting, nor does it natively publish findings to SNS. Wiring TensorBoard to SNS to Lambda is custom integration with high operational overhead and is not how TensorBoard works.","why_zh":"TensorBoard 僅用於視覺化指標，無法自動偵測 vanishing gradient、GPU 使用率不足或 overfitting，也無法原生將發現發布到 SNS。串接 TensorBoard 至 SNS 至 Lambda 屬於高維運負擔的自訂整合，且不符合 TensorBoard 的運作方式。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudWatch default metrics for SageMaker training (CPU/GPU/memory utilization) cannot detect vanishing gradients or overfitting, which require analysis of model output tensors. They provide coarse system metrics only and still require custom Lambda logic, so they neither meet the detection requirements nor minimize overhead.","why_zh":"SageMaker 訓練的 CloudWatch 預設指標（CPU/GPU/記憶體使用率）無法偵測 vanishing gradient 或 overfitting，因為這些需要分析模型 output tensors。它們僅提供粗略的系統指標且仍需自訂 Lambda 邏輯，既不滿足偵測需求也未將負擔降到最低。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Manually publishing per-step gradients as custom CloudWatch metrics requires instrumenting the training script and building detection/threshold logic plus Lambda actions yourself. This is significantly more engineering effort than Debugger's managed built-in rules, and it still does not cover GPU underutilization or overfitting out of the box.","why_zh":"手動將逐步梯度作為自訂 CloudWatch 指標發布，需要在訓練腳本中加入埋點並自行建立偵測/閾值邏輯與 Lambda 動作。這比 Debugger 受管的 built-in rules 多出大量工程投入，且仍無法開箱即用地涵蓋 GPU 使用率不足或 overfitting。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/train-debug-and-improve-model-performance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/debugger-built-in-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/debugger-built-in-profiler-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/debugger-built-in-actions.html"]}},{"id":49,"question_en":"A credit card company has a fraud detection model in production on an Amazon SageMaker endpoint. The company develops a new version of the model. The company needs to assess the new model's performance by using live data and without affecting production end users. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家信用卡公司正在亚马逊 SageMaker 端点上运行一个欺诈检测模型。该公司开发了该模型的新版本。公司 需要使用实时数据评估新模型的性能，同时又不影响生产端用户。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up SageMaker Debugger and create a custom rule.","B":"Set up blue/green deployments with all-at-once traffic shifting.","C":"Set up blue/green deployments with canary traffic shifting.","D":"Set up shadow testing with a shadow variant of the new model."},"options_zh":{"A":"设置 SageMaker Debugger 并创建自定义规则。","B":"设置蓝/绿部署，并一次性完成流量切换。","C":"设置蓝/绿部署并进行金丝雀流量切换。","D":"使用新模型的影子版本设置影子测试。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Shadow testing is purpose-built for this exact scenario. With a shadow variant, SageMaker deploys the new model in shadow mode within the same endpoint and routes a real-time copy of live inference requests to it, while only the production variant's responses are returned to the calling application. The AWS docs state this validates changes to the model 'without any end user impact' and explicitly list the matching use case: 'You are considering promoting a new model that has been validated offline to production, but want to evaluate operational performance metrics such as latency and error rate before making this decision.' This satisfies both requirements: assessment with live data, and no impact on production end users. Blue/green canary or all-at-once shifting route real traffic to the new model and return those responses to users, so they DO affect end users; SageMaker Debugger is a training-time diagnostic tool, not a production inference comparison mechanism.","explanation_zh":"Shadow testing（影子測試）正是為這個情境設計的。使用 shadow variant 時，SageMaker 會在同一個 endpoint 內以 shadow 模式部署新模型，並將即時的推論請求複本路由到該模型，但只有 production variant 的回應會回傳給呼叫端應用程式。AWS 文件明確指出這可在「不影響任何最終使用者（without any end user impact）」的情況下驗證模型變更，並列出相符的使用情境：「你考慮把已離線驗證的新模型推上 production，但想在決策前先評估如延遲、錯誤率等運作效能指標。」這同時滿足兩項需求：用 live data 評估，且不影響 production 最終使用者。Blue/green canary 或 all-at-once 流量切換會把實際流量導向新模型並把回應回傳給使用者，因此會影響最終使用者；SageMaker Debugger 則是訓練階段的診斷工具，並非用於 production 推論比較。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SageMaker Debugger inspects and debugs model state during training (tensors, gradients, vanishing/exploding values). It is not a mechanism for evaluating a deployed model's performance on live production inference traffic.","why_zh":"SageMaker Debugger 用於在訓練階段檢查與除錯模型狀態（張量、梯度、消失/爆炸數值），並非評估已部署模型在線上正式推論流量上效能的機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"All-at-once blue/green shifting moves 100% of production traffic to the new model immediately, so the new model directly serves all end users. This affects production users and cannot pre-assess performance risk-free.","why_zh":"All-at-once 的 blue/green 切換會立即把 100% 正式流量導向新模型，新模型直接服務所有使用者，會影響正式使用者，無法在無風險下事先評估效能。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Canary traffic shifting routes a real portion (up to 50%) of production traffic to the new green fleet and returns those responses to end users during the baking period. Although it limits blast radius, those canary users ARE affected, violating the 'without affecting production end users' requirement.","why_zh":"Canary 流量切換會在 baking period 期間把一部分（最多 50%）實際正式流量導向新的 green fleet，並把這些回應回傳給使用者。雖然能限制影響範圍，但這些 canary 使用者仍會受影響，違反『不影響正式使用者』的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/shadow-tests.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/shadow-tests-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/deployment-guardrails-blue-green-canary.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/how-it-works-model-validation.html"]}},{"id":50,"question_en":"A company stores time-series data about user clicks in an Amazon S3 bucket. The raw data consists of millions of rows of user activity every day. ML engineers access the data to develop their ML models. The ML engineers need to generate daily reports and analyze click trends over the past 3 days by using Amazon Athena. The company must retain the data for 30 days before archiving the data. Which solution will provide the HIGHEST performance for data retrieval?","question_zh":"一家公司将有关用户点击的时间序列数据存储在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中。原始数据每天包含数百万行用户活 动记录。机器学习工程师访问这些数据以开发他们的机器学习模型。 机器学习工程师需要利用相关数据生成每日报告，并分析过去 3 天的点击趋势。 亚马逊阿特纳。该公司必须将数据保留 30 天，然后才能将数据归档。 哪种解决方案能为数据检索提供最高的性能？","options_en":{"A":"Keep all the time-series data without partitioning in the S3 bucket. Manually move data that is older than 30 days to separate S3 buckets.","B":"Create AWS Lambda functions to copy the time-series data into separate S3 buckets. Apply S3 Lifecycle policies to archive data that is older than 30 days to S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval.","C":"Organize the time-series data into partitions by date prefix in the S3 bucket. Apply S3 Lifecycle policies to archive partitions that are older than 30 days to S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval.","D":"Put each day's time-series data into its own S3 bucket. Use S3 Lifecycle policies to archive S3 buckets that hold data that is older than 30 days to S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval."},"options_zh":{"A":"将所有的时间序列数据完整保留在 S3 存储桶中，不进行分区。手动将超过 30 天的数据移至单独 的 S3 存储桶。","B":"创建 AWS Lambda 函数，将时间序列数据复制到单独的 S3 存储桶中。应用 S3 生命周期策略， 将超过 30 天的数据归档到 S3 Glacier 柔性检索中。","C":"按日期前缀将时间序列数据在 S3 存储桶中组织成分区。对超过 30 天的分区应用 S3 生命周期策略，将 其归档到 S3 Glacier 柔性检索中。","D":"将每天的时间序列数据放入各自的 S3 存储桶。使用 S3 生命周期策略将保存有超过 30 天数据的 S3 存 储桶归档至 S3 Glacier 柔性检索。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The deciding qualifier is HIGHEST performance for data retrieval with Amazon Athena. Athena performance is driven by how much data each query scans, and the AWS partitions documentation states that partitioning restricts the amount of data scanned per query (improving performance and reducing cost), that time-based (date) partitioning is the recommended common practice, and that when a query specifies the partition in the WHERE clause Athena scans data only from that partition. Organizing click data by date prefix means the 'past 3 days' query reads only 3 partitions instead of scanning millions of rows across the whole bucket, giving the fastest retrieval; it also avoids the S3 GET throttling that the docs explicitly warn about for large unpartitioned buckets. The retain-30-days-then-archive requirement is met natively because S3 Lifecycle rules support key-prefix filters and can automatically transition matching objects (older date partitions) to S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval, with no custom code. C is the only option that actually partitions the data, so it is correct.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定詞是使用 Amazon Athena 達到最高的資料擷取效能。Athena 的效能取決於每次查詢掃描的資料量。AWS partitions 文件指出，partitioning 可限制每次查詢掃描的資料量（提升效能並降低成本）、以時間（日期）分割是建議的常見做法，且當查詢在 WHERE 子句中指定分割時，Athena 只會掃描該分割的資料。將點擊資料以日期前綴 (date prefix) 組織後，「過去 3 天」的查詢只需讀取 3 個分割，而非掃描整個 bucket 中數百萬列，因此擷取速度最快；同時也避免了文件明確警告的大型未分割 bucket 之 S3 GET 節流問題。保留 30 天後封存的需求可原生達成，因為 S3 Lifecycle 規則支援 key-prefix 篩選，可自動將符合的物件（較舊的日期分割）轉換到 S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval，且無需自訂程式碼。C 是唯一真正對資料做分割的選項，故為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Keeping all data unpartitioned forces Athena to scan the entire bucket (millions of rows) on every query, the worst retrieval performance, and it risks the S3 GET rate-limit exceptions the partitions docs warn about. Manually moving old data is high operational overhead and not automated archiving.","why_zh":"未分割地保存所有資料會迫使 Athena 每次查詢都掃描整個 bucket（數百萬列），擷取效能最差，並可能觸發 partitions 文件警告的 S3 GET 速率限制例外。手動搬移舊資料營運負擔高，也非自動化封存。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Lambda copying data into separate buckets adds custom code and does not partition the data for Athena, so query scan volume and retrieval performance are not improved. The archiving piece can work, but the question asks for highest retrieval performance, which this does not provide.","why_zh":"用 Lambda 將資料複製到其他 bucket 增加自訂程式碼，且未為 Athena 分割資料，因此查詢掃描量與擷取效能並未改善。封存部分雖可行，但題目要求最高擷取效能，此方案無法提供。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"One bucket per day is an anti-pattern: an Athena table points to a single S3 location, so fragmenting data across daily buckets complicates the table definition and prevents efficient single-table partition pruning. S3 Lifecycle rules also act on objects/prefixes within a bucket, not on whole buckets, so the described 'archiving buckets' is imprecise.","why_zh":"每天一個 bucket 是反模式：Athena 資料表指向單一 S3 位置，將資料分散到每日 bucket 會使資料表定義複雜化，並妨礙有效的單一資料表分割修剪 (partition pruning)。S3 Lifecycle 規則作用於 bucket 內的物件/前綴，而非整個 bucket，因此所述「封存整個 bucket」並不精確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/partitions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/ctas-partitioning-and-bucketing-what-is-partitioning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/intro-lifecycle-filters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/lifecycle-transition-general-considerations.html"]}},{"id":51,"question_en":"A company has deployed an ML model that detects fraudulent credit card transactions in real time in a banking application. The model uses Amazon SageMaker Asynchronous Inference. Consumers are reporting delays in receiving the inference results. An ML engineer needs to implement a solution to improve the inference performance. The solution also must provide a notification when a deviation in model quality occurs. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在其银行应用程序中部署了一个实时检测信用卡欺诈交易的机器学习模型，该模型使用了 亚马逊 SageMaker 异步推理功能。消费者反映收到推理结果存在延迟。 一位机器学习工程师需要实现一个解决方案来提升推理性能。该方案还必须在模型质量出现偏差时提 供通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use SageMaker real-time inference for inference. Use SageMaker Model Monitor for notifications about model quality.","B":"Use SageMaker batch transform for inference. Use SageMaker Model Monitor for notifications about model quality.","C":"Use SageMaker Serverless Inference for inference. Use SageMaker Inference Recommender for notifications about model quality.","D":"Keep using SageMaker Asynchronous Inference for inference. Use SageMaker Inference Recommender for notifications about model quality."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 SageMaker 实时推理进行推理。使用 SageMaker 模型监控器获取有关模型质量的通知。","B":"使用 SageMaker 批量转换进行推理。使用 SageMaker 模型监控器获取有关模型质量的通知。","C":"使用 SageMaker 无服务器推理进行推理。使用 SageMaker 推理推荐器获取有关模型质量的通知。","D":"继续使用 SageMaker 异步推理进行推理。使用 SageMaker 推理推荐器获取有关模型质量 的通知。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The fraud-detection model needs low-latency, real-time predictions, but it runs on SageMaker Asynchronous Inference. AWS docs state Async Inference 'queues incoming requests and processes them asynchronously' and is meant for large payloads (up to 1 GB), long processing times (up to one hour), and only near real-time latency. That internal queuing is exactly why consumers experience delays. Switching to SageMaker real-time inference, which the docs describe as 'ideal for inference workloads where you have real-time, interactive, low latency requirements,' directly fixes the performance problem. For the model-quality notification requirement, SageMaker Model Monitor monitors models in production, detects drift in model-quality metrics such as accuracy, and 'set[s] alerts that notify you when there are deviations in the model quality.' Inference Recommender (in C and D) only automates load testing to pick the best instance type/endpoint configuration for performance and cost; it does not detect model-quality drift or send quality notifications, so it cannot satisfy the second requirement.","explanation_zh":"此詐欺偵測模型需要低延遲的即時預測，但目前部署在 SageMaker Asynchronous Inference 上。AWS 文件指出 Async Inference 會「將傳入的請求排入佇列並以非同步方式處理」，其設計目的是處理大型負載（最高 1 GB）、長處理時間（最長一小時），且僅提供「近即時」(near real-time) 延遲；此內部佇列正是消費者遇到延遲的原因。改用 SageMaker real-time inference（文件描述為「適用於具有即時、互動、低延遲需求的推論工作負載」）可直接解決效能問題。至於模型品質通知需求，SageMaker Model Monitor 會監控生產環境中的模型、偵測模型品質指標（如 accuracy）的漂移，並「設定警示，在模型品質出現偏差時通知您」。選項 C 與 D 使用的 SageMaker Inference Recommender 只透過自動化負載測試來挑選最佳執行個體類型/端點組態（效能與成本），無法偵測模型品質漂移或發送品質通知，因此無法滿足第二項需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Batch transform processes an entire dataset offline in batches; it is the opposite of real-time and would worsen latency, not improve it, for a real-time fraud application. Model Monitor is appropriate, but the inference choice is wrong.","why_zh":"Batch transform 以離線批次方式處理整個資料集，與即時相反，對即時詐欺應用會讓延遲更糟而非改善。Model Monitor 部分合適，但推論方式選錯。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Serverless Inference can serve real-time requests but targets intermittent/spiky traffic with idle periods and tolerates cold starts, which is risky for always-on fraud detection. More decisively, SageMaker Inference Recommender only benchmarks instance/endpoint configurations for performance and cost; it does NOT detect model-quality drift or send quality notifications.","why_zh":"Serverless Inference 可服務即時請求，但適用於有閒置期的間歇性/突發流量且會有冷啟動，對需持續運作的詐欺偵測有風險。更關鍵的是，SageMaker Inference Recommender 僅針對執行個體/端點組態做效能與成本基準測試，並不會偵測模型品質漂移或發送品質通知。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Keeping Asynchronous Inference does nothing to fix the reported delays, because the async internal queue is the root cause. Inference Recommender also does not provide model-quality deviation notifications, so neither requirement is met.","why_zh":"繼續使用 Asynchronous Inference 無法解決所回報的延遲，因為非同步內部佇列正是延遲的根本原因。Inference Recommender 也無法提供模型品質偏差通知，因此兩項需求皆未滿足。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/async-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/realtime-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-model-quality.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/inference-recommender.html"]}},{"id":52,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to implement a solution to host a trained ML model. The rate of requests to the model will be inconsistent throughout the day. The ML engineer needs a scalable solution that minimizes costs when the model is not in use. The solution also must maintain the model's capacity to respond to requests during times of peak usage. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师需要实现一个解决方案来部署一个训练好的机器学习模型。该模型全天收到的 请求频率会不均衡。 机器学习工程师需要一种可扩展的解决方案，在模型未使用时能将成本降至最低。该方案还必须确保模型 在使用高峰期能够响应请求。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create AWS Lambda functions that have fixed concurrency to host the model. Configure the Lambda functions to automatically scale based on the number of requests to the model.","B":"Deploy the model on an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster that uses AWS Fargate. Set a static number of tasks to handle requests during times of peak usage.","C":"Deploy the model to an Amazon SageMaker endpoint. Deploy multiple copies of the model to the endpoint. Create an Application Load Balancer to route traffic between the different copies of the model at the endpoint.","D":"Deploy the model to an Amazon SageMaker endpoint. Create SageMaker endpoint auto scaling policies that are based on Amazon CloudWatch metrics to adjust the number of instances dynamically."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建具有固定并发量的 AWS Lambda 函数来托管模型。配置 Lambda 函数，使其根据对模型的请求 数量自动扩展。","B":"在使用 AWS Fargate 的 Amazon Elastic Container Service （Amazon ECS） 集群上部署模型。在高 峰使用时段设置固定数量的任务来处理请求。","C":"将模型部署到 Amazon SageMaker 端点。在该端点部署模型的多个副本。创建一个应用负载均衡器，用 于在端点的不同模型副本之间分配流量。","D":"将模型部署到 Amazon SageMaker 端点。创建基于 Amazon CloudWatch 指标的 SageMaker 端点自动扩 展策略，以动态调整实例数量。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The workload has an inconsistent request rate and needs a scalable host that minimizes cost during idle periods while preserving capacity at peak. Deploying the model to an Amazon SageMaker real-time endpoint and attaching auto scaling policies driven by Amazon CloudWatch metrics (for example target tracking on InvocationsPerInstance) lets SageMaker dynamically add instances during peak demand and remove them when traffic drops. This is the AWS-recommended pattern in the Well-Architected Machine Learning Lens MLREL05-BP01, which explicitly lists fixed/over-provisioned infrastructure as an anti-pattern and states that auto scaling 'optimizes costs through dynamic resource allocation' while strengthening the ability to handle traffic spikes. SageMaker auto scaling creates and manages CloudWatch alarms to decide when to add or remove instances, exactly matching option D. (SageMaker Serverless Inference, which scales to zero, would also fit, but it is not an answer choice; among the four options D is the only one that is both technically correct and provides true dynamic scaling.)","explanation_zh":"此工作負載的請求量整天不一致，需要一個可擴展的託管方案，在閒置時降低成本，同時在尖峰時維持回應能力。將模型部署到 Amazon SageMaker 即時 (real-time) endpoint，並附加由 Amazon CloudWatch 指標驅動的 auto scaling 政策（例如以 target tracking 追蹤 InvocationsPerInstance），可讓 SageMaker 在需求尖峰時動態增加執行個體，並在流量下降時移除執行個體。這正是 Well-Architected Machine Learning Lens MLREL05-BP01 所建議的模式，該文件明確將固定／過度配置的基礎設施列為反模式，並指出 auto scaling 能「透過動態資源配置最佳化成本」，同時增強處理流量尖峰的能力。SageMaker auto scaling 會建立並管理 CloudWatch 警示以判斷何時增減執行個體，完全符合選項 D。（SageMaker Serverless Inference 可縮放至零也很適合，但它不是選項之一；在四個選項中，D 是唯一在技術上正確且能提供真正動態擴展的方案。）","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The option is self-contradictory: it specifies AWS Lambda with 'fixed concurrency' yet then asks it to 'automatically scale' based on requests, and fixed (provisioned) concurrency keeps capacity reserved and billed even when idle, so it does not minimize cost when the model is not in use. Lambda is also not a standard ML model host given its package-size, memory, and 15-minute timeout limits.","why_zh":"此選項自相矛盾：先指定 AWS Lambda 採用「固定併發 (fixed concurrency)」，卻又要求依請求量「自動擴展」；而固定（佈建）併發會保留並持續計費，即使閒置也是如此，因此無法在模型未使用時降低成本。考量 Lambda 的套件大小、記憶體與 15 分鐘逾時限制，它也不是標準的 ML 模型託管選擇。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A 'static number of tasks' on ECS Fargate means no scaling at all. To survive peak it must be sized for peak permanently and run 24/7, so it cannot minimize cost during idle periods. This is precisely the MLREL05-BP01 anti-pattern of over-provisioning fixed infrastructure for peak load at non-peak times.","why_zh":"ECS Fargate 上設定「靜態任務數量 (static number of tasks)」代表完全沒有擴展。要撐過尖峰就必須永久依尖峰量配置並 24/7 運行，因此無法在閒置期間降低成本。這正是 MLREL05-BP01 所述的反模式：為了尖峰負載而在離峰時段過度配置固定基礎設施。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Putting an Application Load Balancer in front of a SageMaker endpoint to route between model copies is architecturally incorrect: a SageMaker endpoint already manages and load-balances its own instance fleet behind a single invocation URL, so you do not front it with an ALB. The option also adds no auto scaling, so it neither scales dynamically nor minimizes cost when idle.","why_zh":"在 SageMaker endpoint 前面放置 Application Load Balancer 以在多個模型副本間路由，在架構上是錯誤的：SageMaker endpoint 已在單一呼叫 URL 後方自行管理並負載平衡其執行個體叢集，因此並不需要前置 ALB。此選項也未加入任何 auto scaling，因此既無法動態擴展，也無法在閒置時降低成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/endpoint-auto-scaling-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/endpoint-auto-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/machine-learning-lens/mlrel05-bp01.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/serverless-endpoints.html"]}},{"id":53,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon SageMaker Studio to develop an ML model. The company has a single SageMaker Studio domain. An ML engineer needs to implement a solution that provides an automated alert when SageMaker compute costs reach a specific threshold. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 SageMaker Studio 来开发机器学习模型。该公司拥有一个 SageMaker Studio 域。 一位机器学习工程师需要实现一个解决方案，当 SageMaker 计算成本达到特定阈值时自动发出警报。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add resource tagging by editing the SageMaker user profile in the SageMaker domain. Configure AWS Cost Explorer to send an alert when the threshold is reached.","B":"Add resource tagging by editing the SageMaker user profile in the SageMaker domain. Configure AWS Budgets to send an alert when the threshold is reached.","C":"Add resource tagging by editing each user's IAM profile. Configure AWS Cost Explorer to send an alert when the threshold is reached.","D":"Add resource tagging by editing each user's IAM profile. Configure AWS Budgets to send an alert when the threshold is reached."},"options_zh":{"A":"通过编辑 SageMaker 域中的 SageMaker 用户配置文件添加资源标签。配置 AWS 成本管理器在达到阈 值时发送警报。","B":"通过编辑 SageMaker 域中的 SageMaker 用户配置文件来添加资源标签。配置 AWS 预算，以便在达到 阈值时发送警报。","C":"通过编辑每个用户的 IAM 配置文件添加资源标签。配置 AWS 成本管理器，在达到阈值时发送警报。","D":"通过编辑每个用户的 IAM 配置文件添加资源标签。配置 AWS 预算，以便在达到阈值时发送警报。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Two independent decisions resolve this. (1) Alerting service: AWS Budgets cost budgets 'set spending limits for services and receive alerts when costs approach or exceed your defined threshold,' delivered via email and/or Amazon SNS. AWS Cost Explorer is only an analysis/visualization/forecasting tool and does not itself fire threshold alerts, so options using Cost Explorer for alerting (A, C) are wrong. (2) Tagging level: SageMaker Studio cost tracking relies on SageMaker tags such as sagemaker:domain-arn and sagemaker:user-profile-arn, which SageMaker applies/propagates at the SageMaker domain and user-profile level (then activated as cost allocation tags in the Billing console and consumed by Budgets/Cost Explorer). Tagging is done on the SageMaker user profile within the domain, not by editing each user's IAM profile, which governs permissions rather than cost-allocation tags. The only combination pairing the correct tagging construct (SageMaker user profile in the domain) with the correct alerting service (AWS Budgets) is option B, which confirms both the dump's suggested answer and the first analyst.","explanation_zh":"此題由兩個獨立判斷決定。(1) 告警服務:AWS Budgets 的 cost budget 可為服務設定支出上限,並在成本接近或超過所設門檻時發出告警(透過 email 與/或 Amazon SNS)。AWS Cost Explorer 僅是分析、視覺化與預測工具,本身不會觸發門檻告警,因此任何用 Cost Explorer 做告警的選項(A、C)皆錯誤。(2) 標記層級:SageMaker Studio 的成本追蹤依賴 sagemaker:domain-arn、sagemaker:user-profile-arn 等 SageMaker tag,這些 tag 由 SageMaker 在 SageMaker domain 與 user profile 層級套用/傳播(再於 Billing console 啟用為 cost allocation tags,供 Budgets/Cost Explorer 使用)。標記是在 domain 內的 SageMaker user profile 上完成,而非編輯每位使用者的 IAM profile(IAM 管理權限,非成本分攤標記)。唯一同時搭配正確標記方式(domain 內的 SageMaker user profile)與正確告警服務(AWS Budgets)的選項即為 B,此結論同時確認了題庫建議答案與第一位分析師的判斷。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The tagging half (SageMaker user profile in the domain) is correct, but Cost Explorer only analyzes, visualizes, and forecasts spend; it does not send automated threshold alerts. Cost-threshold alerting is the role of AWS Budgets.","why_zh":"標記方式(domain 內的 SageMaker user profile)正確,但 Cost Explorer 僅用於分析、視覺化與預測支出,不會自動發送門檻告警。成本門檻告警是 AWS Budgets 的職責。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Both halves are wrong: Cost Explorer does not send threshold alerts, and SageMaker cost-allocation tags are applied at the SageMaker domain/user-profile level, not by editing each user's IAM profile (IAM controls permissions, not resource cost tags).","why_zh":"兩部分皆錯:Cost Explorer 不會發送門檻告警,且 SageMaker 成本分攤標記是在 SageMaker domain/user profile 層級設定,而非編輯各使用者的 IAM profile(IAM 管理權限,非資源成本標記)。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Budgets is the correct alerting service, but tagging by editing each user's IAM profile is wrong. IAM profiles manage permissions, not SageMaker resource cost-allocation tags; those tags (sagemaker:user-profile-arn, sagemaker:domain-arn) are applied at the SageMaker domain/user-profile level.","why_zh":"AWS Budgets 是正確的告警服務,但透過編輯各使用者的 IAM profile 來標記是錯的。IAM profile 管理權限,而非 SageMaker 資源的成本分攤標記;那些 tag(sagemaker:user-profile-arn、sagemaker:domain-arn)是在 SageMaker domain/user profile 層級套用。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-managing-costs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/sagemaker-studio-admin-best-practices/cost-attribution.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/custom-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/cost-alloc-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-what-is.html"]}},{"id":54,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon SageMaker for its ML workloads. The company's ML engineer receives a 50 MB Apache Parquet data file to build a fraud detection model. The file includes several correlated columns that are not required. What should the ML engineer do to drop the unnecessary columns in the file with the LEAST effort?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 SageMaker 来处理其机器学习工作负载。该公司的机器学习工程师收到了一个 50MB 的 Apache Parquet 数据文件，用于构建欺诈检测模型。该文件包含几个相关联但不需要的列。 机器学习工程师应如何以最小的努力从文件中删除不必要的列？","options_en":{"A":"Download the file to a local workstation. Perform one-hot encoding by using a custom Python script.","B":"Create an Apache Spark job that uses a custom processing script on Amazon EMR.","C":"Create a SageMaker processing job by calling the SageMaker Python SDK.","D":"Create a data flow in SageMaker Data Wrangler. Configure a transform step."},"options_zh":{"A":"将文件下载到本地工作站。使用自定义的 Python 脚本执行独热编码。","B":"在 Amazon EMR 上创建一个使用自定义处理脚本的 Apache Spark 作业。","C":"通过调用 SageMaker Python SDK 创建一个 SageMaker 处理作业。","D":"在 SageMaker Data Wrangler 中创建一个数据流。配置一个转换步骤。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The qualifier is LEAST effort, meaning the lowest operational and coding overhead. Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler is a visual, low/no-code data preparation feature that natively imports Apache Parquet (and other formats) from Amazon S3. You create a data flow and add transform steps from the built-in transform library. Dropping unneeded columns is the built-in 'Manage Columns' transform (Drop column); AWS docs explicitly state Data Wrangler built-in transforms let you transform columns 'without any code' and that you can 'delete multiple columns in a single step.' For a small 50 MB file, this requires no script authoring and no separate cluster or job to manage, so D is the least-effort option. Every other option requires writing custom code or provisioning/orchestrating compute, so they are all higher effort.","explanation_zh":"題目的關鍵限定詞是 LEAST effort（最少的操作與程式負擔）。Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler 是視覺化、低/無程式碼的資料準備功能，可直接從 Amazon S3 原生匯入 Apache Parquet（及其他格式）。你建立一個 data flow，再從內建轉換清單中加入 transform step。刪除不需要的欄位正是內建的 'Manage Columns' 轉換（Drop column）；AWS 文件明確指出 Data Wrangler 內建轉換可讓你 'without any code'（不需任何程式碼）處理欄位，並且可以 'delete multiple columns in a single step'（在單一步驟中刪除多個欄位）。對於僅 50 MB 的小檔案，這不需撰寫任何腳本，也不需管理額外的叢集或作業，因此 D 是最省力的選項。其他每個選項都需撰寫自訂程式碼或佈建／編排運算資源，工作量都更高。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Downloading to a local workstation and writing a custom Python script is manual, off-platform, code-heavy work, and one-hot encoding is categorical feature encoding, not dropping columns. It neither performs the requested task nor minimizes effort.","why_zh":"下載到本機並撰寫自訂 Python 腳本屬於平台外、手動且大量寫程式的作業，而且 one-hot encoding 是類別特徵編碼，並非刪除欄位。它既未完成題目要求的工作，也非最省力的做法。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Building a custom Spark job on Amazon EMR means writing code, plus provisioning and managing a cluster, which is massive overkill for dropping columns from a 50 MB file and far more effort.","why_zh":"在 Amazon EMR 上建立自訂 Spark 作業需要撰寫程式，並佈建與管理叢集，對於從 50 MB 檔案刪除欄位而言過度龐大，工作量遠高得多。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A SageMaker processing job called via the Python SDK still requires writing a processing script (e.g., pandas/Spark) and configuring/orchestrating the job and container, which is more coding and setup effort than Data Wrangler's no-code 'Manage Columns' transform.","why_zh":"透過 Python SDK 呼叫 SageMaker processing job 仍需撰寫處理腳本（例如 pandas/Spark），並設定與編排作業及容器，比起 Data Wrangler 無需程式碼的 'Manage Columns' 轉換需要更多撰寫程式與設定的工作量。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-transform.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler-data-flow.html"]}},{"id":55,"question_en":"A company is creating an application that will recommend products for customers to purchase. The application will make API calls to Amazon Q Business. The company must ensure that responses from Amazon Q Business do not include the name of the company's main competitor. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"","options_en":{"A":"Configure the competitor's name as a blocked phrase in Amazon Q Business.","B":"Configure an Amazon Q Business retriever to exclude the competitor’s name.","C":"Configure an Amazon Kendra retriever for Amazon Q Business to build indexes that exclude the competitor's name.","D":"Configure document attribute boosting in Amazon Q Business to deprioritize the competitor's name."},"options_zh":{},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Q Business provides a 'Blocked phrases' (labeled 'Blocked words' in the console) setting within its guardrail global controls. The AWS documentation states that you define blocked words/phrases for the application environment and that 'The application environment will not respond to questions that contain these words or mention them in any responses.' This is an output-level guardrail that directly guarantees the competitor's name will not appear in generated chat responses, which is exactly what the requirement asks for. You can also configure a custom message shown to end users when a blocked phrase is encountered. The retrieval/ranking options (B, C, D) only affect which source documents are fetched or how they are ranked; they cannot guarantee a specific word is absent from the LLM-generated response, so configuring the competitor's name as a blocked phrase is the only solution that meets the requirement.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Q Business 在其 guardrail global controls 中提供「Blocked phrases」（在主控台標示為「Blocked words」）設定。AWS 官方文件指出：你可為應用環境定義 blocked words/phrases，且『The application environment will not respond to questions that contain these words or mention them in any responses.』這是一種輸出層級的 guardrail，可直接保證競爭對手的名稱不會出現在生成的聊天回應中，正符合題目需求。你還可以設定當觸發 blocked phrase 時向使用者顯示的自訂訊息。檢索/排序類選項（B、C、D）只影響擷取哪些來源文件或如何排序，無法保證生成回應中不出現特定字詞，因此將競爭對手名稱設為 blocked phrase 是唯一符合需求的解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"There is no Amazon Q Business retriever option to 'exclude a name.' A retriever connects and fetches enterprise data for RAG; it controls which data sources/documents are searched and retrievable, not whether the LLM's generated output mentions a word, so it cannot guarantee the competitor's name is absent from responses.","why_zh":"Amazon Q Business 的 retriever 並沒有「排除某個名稱」的設定。Retriever 負責連接並擷取企業資料供 RAG 使用，控制的是要搜尋與可擷取的資料來源/文件，而非 LLM 生成輸出是否提及某字詞，因此無法保證回應中不出現競爭對手名稱。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An Amazon Kendra retriever builds search indexes over enterprise data; you cannot build indexes that filter out an arbitrary word like a competitor's name. Indexing governs what content is searchable/retrievable, not what words appear in the LLM-generated answer, so even with curated indexes the model could still produce the name. This is also far heavier operationally than the built-in blocked phrases control.","why_zh":"Amazon Kendra retriever 為企業資料建立搜尋索引；無法建立可過濾掉如競爭對手名稱這類任意字詞的索引。索引決定哪些內容可被搜尋/擷取，而非 LLM 生成答案中會出現哪些字詞，因此即使索引經過篩選，模型仍可能產生該名稱。這在維運上也比內建的 blocked phrases 控制繁重許多。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Document attribute boosting only tunes relevance ranking based on attributes (recency, source, rank order). AWS docs explicitly state that 'Choosing to boost document attributes doesn't by itself cause Amazon Q Business to include or exclude a document in the chat response.' Deprioritizing merely lowers ranking and cannot guarantee the competitor's name is excluded from responses.","why_zh":"Document attribute boosting 只依據屬性（recency、source、rank order）調整相關性排序。AWS 文件明確指出：『Choosing to boost document attributes doesn't by itself cause Amazon Q Business to include or exclude a document in the chat response.』降低優先順序只是降低排名，無法保證回應中排除競爭對手名稱。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonq/latest/qbusiness-ug/guardrails-global-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonq/latest/qbusiness-ug/guardrails-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonq/latest/qbusiness-ug/relevancy-tuning.html"]}},{"id":56,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to use Amazon SageMaker to fine-tune a large language model (LLM) for text summarization. The ML engineer must follow a low-code no-code (LCNC) approach. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师需要使用亚马逊 Sagemaker 对大型语言模型（LLM）进行微调以实现文本摘要功 能。该机器学习工程师必须采用低代码无代码（LCNC）的方法。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use SageMaker Studio to fine-tune an LLM that is deployed on Amazon EC2 instances.","B":"Use SageMaker Autopilot to fine-tune an LLM that is deployed by a custom API endpoint.","C":"Use SageMaker Autopilot to fine-tune an LLM that is deployed on Amazon EC2 instances.","D":"Use SageMaker Autopilot to fine-tune an LLM that is deployed by SageMaker JumpStart."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 SageMaker Studio 对部署在 Amazon EC2 实例上的大型语言模型进行微调。","B":"使用 SageMaker Autopilot 对通过自定义 API 端点部署的大型语言模型进行微调。","C":"使用 SageMaker Autopilot 对部署在 Amazon EC2 实例上的大型语言模型进行微调。","D":"使用 SageMaker Autopilot 对由 SageMaker JumpStart 部署的大型语言模型进行微调。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The low-code/no-code (LCNC) AutoML capability in SageMaker for fine-tuning LLMs is Amazon SageMaker Autopilot. AWS documentation states explicitly that 'Using Autopilot API, users can fine-tune large language models (LLMs) that are powered by Amazon SageMaker JumpStart,' and that 'Autopilot supports the instruction-based fine-tuning of a selection of general-purpose large language models (LLMs) powered by JumpStart.' The supported models (e.g., Dolly 3B/7B/12B, Falcon) are documented as able to 'perform tasks including... summarization,' which satisfies the text summarization requirement. Therefore the correct pairing is Autopilot fine-tuning an LLM that is deployed/powered by SageMaker JumpStart (D). The other Autopilot options are wrong because the fine-tunable LLMs come from the JumpStart model catalog, not from a self-managed EC2 deployment (C) or a custom API endpoint (B), and option A uses Studio (a development IDE) rather than the LCNC AutoML service.","explanation_zh":"在 SageMaker 中用於微調 LLM 的低程式碼/無程式碼 (LCNC) AutoML 功能是 Amazon SageMaker Autopilot。AWS 文件明確指出：『使用 Autopilot API，使用者可以微調由 Amazon SageMaker JumpStart 提供支援的大型語言模型 (LLM)』，並且『Autopilot 支援對一系列由 JumpStart 提供支援的通用型 LLM 進行基於指令的微調 (instruction-based fine-tuning)』。文件中所列的支援模型（例如 Dolly 3B/7B/12B、Falcon）可『執行包括 summarization 在內的任務』，符合文字摘要的需求。因此正確配對為：Autopilot 微調由 SageMaker JumpStart 部署/提供支援的 LLM（選項 D）。其他 Autopilot 選項錯誤，因為可微調的 LLM 來自 JumpStart 模型目錄，而非自行管理的 EC2 部署（C）或自訂 API endpoint（B）；選項 A 使用的是 Studio（開發 IDE），而非 LCNC AutoML 服務。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SageMaker Studio is an integrated development environment for building, training, and deploying models with code; it is not the LCNC/AutoML capability the question asks for. It is also paired with an LLM self-deployed on EC2, which is a manual, code-heavy deployment rather than a low-code no-code workflow.","why_zh":"SageMaker Studio 是用於以程式碼建構、訓練及部署模型的整合開發環境，並非題目要求的 LCNC/AutoML 功能。它還配對了自行部署於 EC2 的 LLM，屬於需大量程式碼的手動部署，而非低程式碼無程式碼工作流程。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Autopilot fine-tunes LLMs sourced from the SageMaker JumpStart model catalog, not LLMs exposed through a self-built 'custom API endpoint.' The deployment-by-custom-API pairing does not match how Autopilot LLM fine-tuning works.","why_zh":"Autopilot 微調的 LLM 來自 SageMaker JumpStart 模型目錄，而非透過自建『自訂 API endpoint』所提供的 LLM。自訂 API 部署的配對不符合 Autopilot LLM 微調的運作方式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Although Autopilot is the correct LCNC service, the fine-tunable LLMs are JumpStart-powered models, not models the engineer self-deploys on Amazon EC2. The Autopilot + EC2-deployed-LLM pairing is incorrect.","why_zh":"雖然 Autopilot 是正確的 LCNC 服務，但可微調的 LLM 是由 JumpStart 提供支援的模型，而非工程師自行部署於 Amazon EC2 的模型。Autopilot 搭配 EC2 部署 LLM 的配對並不正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/autopilot-llms-finetuning-models.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/autopilot-create-experiment-finetune-llms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/use-auto-ml.html"]}},{"id":57,"question_en":"A company has an ML model that needs to run one time each night to predict stock values. The model input is 3 MB of data that is collected during the current day. The model produces the predictions for the next day. The prediction process takes less than 1 minute to finish running. How should the company deploy the model on Amazon SageMaker to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个机器学习模型，需要每晚运行一次来预测股票价值。该模型 输入的是当天收集的 3MB 数据。该模型会生成次日的预测结果。预测过程在不到 1 分钟内即可完成 运行。 公司应如何在亚马逊 SageMaker 上部署模型以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use a multi-model serverless endpoint. Enable caching.","B":"Use an asynchronous inference endpoint. Set the InitialInstanceCount parameter to 0.","C":"Use a real-time endpoint. Configure an auto scaling policy to scale the model to 0 when the model is not in use.","D":"Use a serverless inference endpoint. Set the MaxConcurrency parameter to 1."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用多模型无服务器端点。启用缓存。","B":"使用异步推理端点。将 InitialInstanceCount 参数设置为 0。","C":"使用实时端点。配置自动扩展策略，在模型未使用时将其扩展至 0。","D":"使用无服务器推理端点。将 MaxConcurrency 参数设置为 1。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The workload runs once per night, has a tiny 3 MB payload, finishes in under a minute, and is idle the rest of the day. Amazon SageMaker Serverless Inference is purpose-built for this: AWS docs state it is 'ideal for workloads which have idle periods between traffic spurts and can tolerate cold starts' and is 'a cost-effective option if you have an infrequent or unpredictable traffic pattern,' automatically scaling the endpoint down to 0 when there are no requests so you pay only per use. MaxConcurrency=1 is a valid setting (the allowed range for a serverless endpoint is 1-200) and is appropriate for a single nightly request, giving the lowest cost and least operational overhead. Option B is technically impossible because the ProductionVariant InitialInstanceCount parameter has a minimum valid value of 1 (it cannot be 0), and async scale-to-zero is achieved through Application Auto Scaling (MinCapacity=0), not InitialInstanceCount. Therefore D is correct.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載每晚僅執行一次，輸入只有 3 MB、處理時間不到一分鐘，其餘時間端點完全閒置。Amazon SageMaker Serverless Inference 正是為此設計：AWS 文件指出它「適合在流量爆發之間有閒置期且能容忍 cold start 的工作負載」，並且是「流量不頻繁或不可預測時具成本效益的選項」，當沒有請求時會自動將端點縮減至 0，只按使用量計費。MaxConcurrency=1 是合法設定（serverless 端點允許範圍為 1 到 200），對單一每晚請求十分恰當，既最省成本也最省維運。選項 B 在技術上不可行，因為 ProductionVariant 的 InitialInstanceCount 參數最小合法值為 1（不可設為 0），且非同步端點縮減至 0 是透過 Application Auto Scaling（MinCapacity=0）達成，而非 InitialInstanceCount。因此 D 為正解。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no 'multi-model serverless endpoint'; multi-model endpoints are a real-time hosting feature, and Serverless Inference does not support multi-model endpoints. There is also only one model, so caching is meaningless for a single nightly invocation.","why_zh":"並不存在「multi-model serverless endpoint」；multi-model endpoints 是 real-time 託管功能，且 Serverless Inference 並不支援 multi-model endpoints。此外此處只有一個模型，對每晚僅一次的呼叫啟用 caching 毫無意義。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"InitialInstanceCount cannot be set to 0: the ProductionVariant API defines its minimum valid value as 1. Async scale-to-zero is configured via Application Auto Scaling with MinCapacity=0, not an InitialInstanceCount=0 parameter, so the described configuration is invalid. Async inference is also designed for large payloads (up to 1 GB) and long processing (up to 1 hour), which is overkill for a 3 MB, sub-minute job.","why_zh":"InitialInstanceCount 無法設為 0：ProductionVariant API 定義其最小合法值為 1。非同步端點縮減至零是透過 Application Auto Scaling 設定 MinCapacity=0，而非 InitialInstanceCount=0 參數，因此此選項描述的設定無效。此外 async inference 是為大型負載（最高 1 GB）與長處理時間（最長 1 小時）設計，對 3 MB、不到一分鐘的工作而言過度。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Standard real-time endpoints provisioned via InitialInstanceCount have a minimum of 1 instance and cannot natively auto scale down to 0, so an instance stays always-on and you keep paying standby cost all day. This is more operational overhead and a worse fit than serverless, which is purpose-built to scale to 0 for infrequent traffic.","why_zh":"以 InitialInstanceCount 佈建的標準 real-time 端點最少需 1 個執行個體，無法原生自動縮減至 0，因此執行個體會持續在線，整天都要付待機成本。比 serverless 維運負擔更高且較不適配；serverless 本就是為不頻繁流量自動縮減至 0 而設計。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/serverless-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/serverless-endpoints-create-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/async-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/async-inference-autoscale.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/APIReference/API_ProductionVariant.html"]}},{"id":58,"question_en":"An ML engineer trained an ML model on Amazon SageMaker to detect automobile accidents from dosed- circuit TV footage. The ML engineer used SageMaker Data Wrangler to create a training dataset of images of accidents and non-accidents. The model performed well during training and validation. However, the model is underperforming in production because of variations in the quality of the images from various cameras. Which solution will improve the model's accuracy in the LEAST amount of time?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师在亚马逊的 SageMaker 上训练了一个机器学习模型，用于从闭路电视录像中检测 汽车事故。该工程师使用 SageMaker Data Wrangler 创建了一个包含事故和非事故图像的训练数据集。 该模型在训练和验证阶段表现良好。然而，由于来自不同相机的图像质量存在差异，该模型在 实际应用中的表现不佳。 哪种解决方案能在最短时间内提高模型的准确性？","options_en":{"A":"Collect more images from all the cameras. Use Data Wrangler to prepare a new training dataset.","B":"Recreate the training dataset by using the Data Wrangler corrupt image transform. Specify the impulse noise option.","C":"Recreate the training dataset by using the Data Wrangler enhance image contrast transform. Specify the Gamma contrast option.","D":"Recreate the training dataset by using the Data Wrangler resize image transform. Crop all images to the same size."},"options_zh":{"A":"从所有摄像头收集更多图像。使用数据整理工具准备一个新的训练数据集。","B":"使用“数据整理器”中的“损坏图像”转换来重新创建训练数据集。指定脉冲噪声选项。","C":"使用“数据编织器”中的增强图像对比度转换来重新创建训练数据集。指定伽马对比度选项。","D":"使用 Data Wrangler 的调整图像大小转换来重新创建训练数据集。将所有图像裁剪为相同的尺寸。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The model trains/validates well but fails in production because of variations in image quality across cameras (sensor noise, low-quality footage). The fastest fix is data augmentation on the EXISTING dataset rather than gathering new data. SageMaker Data Wrangler's built-in image transforms come from the open-source imgaug library and include a CorruptImage transform; specifying the impulse-noise option (salt-and-pepper noise) injects realistic quality degradation into the training images so the model learns to be robust to the noisy, varied-quality footage it sees in production. imgaug documents this corruption module as a way 'to train neural networks that are more robust to these types of degradations in real-world scenarios.' AWS's Well-Architected Responsible AI Lens (RAISP02-BP09) prescribes the same approach: 'Include robustness techniques during training by adding controlled noise (small random changes) to your data... to learn to ignore minor input differences,' using 'data augmentation that creates variations of your training examples.' Because it reuses the current dataset and requires only re-running the Data Wrangler flow, it improves accuracy in the LEAST amount of time. The 'LEAST amount of time' qualifier eliminates Option A (collecting and labeling new images is the slowest path).","explanation_zh":"模型在訓練/驗證表現良好，但在生產環境因各攝影機影像品質差異（感測器雜訊、低品質畫面）而表現不佳。最快的修正方式是對「既有」資料集做 data augmentation，而非重新收集資料。SageMaker Data Wrangler 內建影像轉換來自開源 imgaug 函式庫，包含 CorruptImage 轉換；指定 impulse noise（椒鹽雜訊）選項可將真實的品質劣化注入訓練影像，使模型學會對生產環境中雜訊多、品質參差的畫面更具韌性。imgaug 將此 corruption 模組記載為可「訓練出對真實世界這類劣化更具韌性的神經網路」。AWS Well-Architected Responsible AI Lens（RAISP02-BP09）也提出相同做法：在訓練時加入受控雜訊（小幅隨機變化）以讓模型學會忽略次要的輸入差異，並使用 data augmentation 產生訓練樣本的變體。由於此法重用現有資料集、只需重新執行 Data Wrangler flow，能在最短時間內提升準確度。題目「LEAST amount of time」此一限定詞直接排除選項 A（重新收集並標註影像是最慢的路徑）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Collecting more images from all cameras and building a new dataset requires data gathering, labeling, and re-preparation — by far the slowest option, directly contradicting the 'LEAST amount of time' qualifier even though it could eventually help.","why_zh":"從所有攝影機收集更多影像並建立新資料集需要蒐集、標註與重新準備，是最慢的選項，直接違反「LEAST amount of time」限定詞，即使長期可能有幫助。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EnhanceImage with the Gamma contrast option only adjusts/normalizes contrast and brightness; it does not make the model robust to the general quality degradation (sensor noise) described, and at inference the model still receives raw varied-quality footage. It targets a narrower lighting/contrast issue rather than the noisy-quality variation problem.","why_zh":"EnhanceImage 的 Gamma contrast 選項僅調整/正規化對比與亮度，無法讓模型對題目所述的一般品質劣化（感測器雜訊）具韌性，且推論時模型仍接收原始品質參差的畫面。它針對的是較窄的光線/對比問題，而非雜訊品質變化問題。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"ResizeImage / cropping to a uniform size addresses resolution and dimension differences, but the problem is image QUALITY variation (noise), not size. Models already require uniform input dimensions, so this does nothing to improve robustness to noisy, low-quality footage.","why_zh":"ResizeImage／裁切成統一尺寸處理的是解析度與尺寸差異，但問題是影像「品質」變化（雜訊），而非尺寸。模型本就需要統一輸入尺寸，因此這無法提升對雜訊、低品質畫面的韌性。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-transform.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/responsible-ai-lens/raisp02-bp09.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/responsible-ai-lens/rairc03-bp04.html"]}},{"id":59,"question_en":"A company has an application that uses different APIs to generate embeddings for input text. The company needs to implement a solution to automatically rotate the API tokens every 3 months. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个应用程序，该程序使用不同的 API 为输入文本生成嵌入。该公司需要实现一 个解决方案，每 3 个月自动轮换 API 令牌。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Store the tokens in AWS Secrets Manager. Create an AWS Lambda function to perform the rotation.","B":"Store the tokens in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Create an AWS Lambda function to perform the rotation.","C":"Store the tokens in AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). Use an AWS managed key to perform the rotation.","D":"Store the tokens in AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). Use an AWS owned key to perform the rotation."},"options_zh":{"A":"将令牌存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来执行轮换操作。","B":"将令牌存储在 AWS 系统管理器参数存储中。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来执行轮换操作。","C":"将令牌存储在 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）中。使用 AWS 管理的密钥执行轮换操作。","D":"将令牌存储在 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）中。使用 AWS 所拥有的密钥执行轮换操作。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Secrets Manager natively supports automatic rotation of secrets, including non-database secrets such as API tokens and OAuth keys, by attaching a Lambda rotation function to the secret. You configure a rotation schedule (for example, every 90 days / 3 months) and Secrets Manager automatically invokes the Lambda function to update the token in both Secrets Manager and the external service. This exactly matches option A: store the tokens in Secrets Manager and create a Lambda function to perform the rotation. Parameter Store (B) has no built-in rotation engine or scheduler, so you would have to build and operate the entire EventBridge + Lambda orchestration yourself, meaning it does not natively meet the automatic-rotation requirement. AWS KMS (C and D) rotates cryptographic key material for encryption keys, not arbitrary application API tokens; AWS managed and AWS owned keys cannot store or rotate third-party API tokens, and AWS owned keys are not even customer-configurable.","explanation_zh":"AWS Secrets Manager 原生支援密鑰的自動輪替，包括非資料庫類型的密鑰，例如 API tokens 與 OAuth keys，做法是將一個 Lambda rotation function 附加到該密鑰上。你可以設定輪替排程（例如每 90 天 / 3 個月），Secrets Manager 便會自動呼叫該 Lambda function，同時更新 Secrets Manager 內與外部服務端的 token。這正好對應選項 A：將 tokens 存放於 Secrets Manager 並建立 Lambda function 來執行輪替。Parameter Store（B）沒有內建的輪替引擎或排程器，你必須自行建置並維運整套 EventBridge + Lambda 流程，因此它無法原生滿足自動輪替的需求。AWS KMS（C 與 D）輪替的是加密金鑰的密碼學金鑰材料，而非任意的應用程式 API tokens；AWS managed key 與 AWS owned key 無法存放或輪替第三方 API tokens，而且 AWS owned key 甚至無法由客戶設定。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Parameter Store has no native, built-in secret rotation feature; it does not include a rotation scheduler or managed Lambda rotation integration, so achieving automatic 90-day rotation would require building custom EventBridge + Lambda orchestration yourself rather than using a native capability.","why_zh":"Parameter Store 沒有原生內建的密鑰輪替功能，不提供輪替排程器或受管的 Lambda 輪替整合，因此要達成每 90 天自動輪替需自行建置 EventBridge + Lambda 的客製化流程，而非使用原生能力。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS KMS rotates cryptographic key material of encryption keys, not application API tokens. An AWS managed key cannot store an external API token, and KMS rotation does not update credentials on a third-party service, so it cannot meet the token-rotation requirement.","why_zh":"AWS KMS 輪替的是加密金鑰的密碼學金鑰材料，而非應用程式 API tokens。AWS managed key 無法存放外部 API token，且 KMS 輪替不會更新第三方服務端的憑證，因此無法滿足 token 輪替需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fundamental mismatch as C: KMS rotates key material, not API tokens. AWS owned keys are managed entirely by AWS, are not visible or configurable by customers, cannot store third-party tokens, and cannot rotate application API tokens.","why_zh":"與 C 相同的根本性不符：KMS 輪替的是金鑰材料而非 API tokens。AWS owned key 完全由 AWS 管理，客戶無法檢視或設定，無法存放第三方 token，也無法輪替應用程式 API tokens。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/rotating-secrets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/rotate-secrets_turn-on-for-other.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/rotate-secrets_lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-parameter-store.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/rotate-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html"]}},{"id":60,"question_en":"An ML engineer receives datasets that contain missing values, duplicates, and extreme outliers. The ML engineer must consolidate these datasets into a single data frame and must prepare the data for ML. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师收到的资料集中包含缺失值、重复值和极端异常值。该工程师必须将这些数据集整合 到一个数据框中，并对数据进行处理以用于机器学习。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler to import the datasets and to consolidate them into a single data frame. Use the cleansing and enrichment functionalities to prepare the data.","B":"Use Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth to import the datasets and to consolidate them into a single data frame. Use the human-in-the-loop capability to prepare the data.","C":"Manually import and merge the datasets. Consolidate the datasets into a single data frame. Use Amazon Q Developer to generate code snippets that will prepare the data.","D":"Manually import and merge the datasets. Consolidate the datasets into a single data frame. Use Amazon SageMaker data labeling to prepare the data."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler 导入数据集，并将其整合到一个数据框中。利用数据清理和丰 富功能来准备数据。","B":"使用 Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth 导入数据集，并将其整合到一个数据框中。利用人机交互功能 来准备数据。","C":"手动导入并合并数据集。将数据集整合到一个数据框中。使用 Amazon Q Developer 生成代码片段 以准备数据。","D":"手动导入并合并数据集。将数据集整合为一个数据框。使用亚马逊 SageMaker 数据标注功能来准 备数据。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler is purpose-built for this end-to-end task. It imports data from 40+ sources (Amazon S3, Athena, Amazon Redshift, Snowflake, Databricks, etc.) and lets you consolidate multiple datasets into a single data frame within a data flow using the built-in Join Datasets and Concatenate Datasets transforms; the AWS docs state that each transform 'modifies your dataset and produces a new dataframe.' Its catalog of code-free ML transforms directly covers the three problems described: Handle Missing Values (impute or drop), Handle Outliers (clip/standard-deviation/quantile methods), and Manage Rows (sort, shuffle, and drop duplicate rows). This delivers import, consolidation, and cleansing in one low-code/no-code tool, making it the most fit-for-purpose and lowest-overhead solution.","explanation_zh":"Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler 正是為這類端到端任務而設計。它可從 40 多種來源（Amazon S3、Athena、Amazon Redshift、Snowflake、Databricks 等）匯入資料，並在 data flow 中透過內建的 Join Datasets 與 Concatenate Datasets 轉換，將多個資料集整合成單一 data frame；AWS 文件指出每個 transform 都會『modifies your dataset and produces a new dataframe』。其免程式碼的 ML transform 目錄直接涵蓋題目所述三大問題：Handle Missing Values（補值或刪除）、Handle Outliers（clip／標準差／分位數方法）以及 Manage Rows（排序、洗牌與刪除重複列）。它在單一低程式碼／無程式碼工具中完成匯入、整合與清理，是最契合且作業負擔最低的解決方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"SageMaker Ground Truth is a data labeling service that uses human-in-the-loop workers to assign labels to data for training. It does not import or consolidate datasets into a data frame, and it has no functionality to handle missing values, duplicates, or outliers.","why_zh":"SageMaker Ground Truth 是資料標註服務，透過 human-in-the-loop 人力為訓練資料指派標籤。它無法匯入或整合資料集成 data frame，也沒有處理缺失值、重複值或離群值的功能。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Q Developer is a coding assistant that only generates code snippets; the engineer must still manually import/merge the data and run and debug the generated code. This adds significant manual effort and operational overhead compared to the purpose-built Data Wrangler, which performs the cleansing itself with no code.","why_zh":"Amazon Q Developer 只是程式碼助理，僅生成程式碼片段；工程師仍須手動匯入／合併資料並執行與除錯所生成的程式碼。相較於本身即可無程式碼完成清理的 Data Wrangler，這增加大量手動工作與作業負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SageMaker data labeling (Ground Truth) assigns labels to data for supervised training; it is not a tool for handling missing values, duplicates, or outliers. It also still requires manual import and merge, making it both the wrong tool and higher effort.","why_zh":"SageMaker data labeling（Ground Truth）是為監督式訓練的資料指派標籤，並非處理缺失值、重複值或離群值的工具。且仍需手動匯入與合併，既選錯工具又增加負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-transform.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler-data-flow.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-label.html"]}},{"id":61,"question_en":"A company has historical data that shows whether customers needed long-term support from company staff. The company needs to develop an ML model to predict whether new customers will require long-term support. Which modeling approach should the company use to meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有历史数据，这些数据表明客户是否需要公司员工提供长期支持。该公司需要开发一个机器学习 模型来预测新客户是否需要长期支持。 公司应采用哪种建模方法来满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Anomaly detection","B":"Linear regression","C":"Logistic regression","D":"Semantic segmentation"},"options_zh":{"A":"异常检测","B":"线性回归","C":"逻辑回归","D":"语义分割"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The task is to predict a binary (yes/no) outcome from labeled historical data: whether a new customer will require long-term support. Predicting one of two possible classes is a binary classification problem, and the AWS 'Types of ML Models' page explicitly states that for binary classification Amazon ML 'uses the industry-standard learning algorithm known as logistic regression.' That same page lists the directly analogous example 'Will the customer buy this product?' as a binary classification problem. Logistic regression outputs a prediction score in [0,1] that is thresholded into one of two classes, which is exactly what is needed here. Because the company has labeled historical outcomes, this is a supervised classification task, making logistic regression (C) the correct modeling approach.","explanation_zh":"此題要從有標註的歷史資料預測一個二元（是/否）結果：新客戶是否會需要長期支援。預測兩種可能類別之一屬於 binary classification（二元分類）問題，而 AWS 的 'Types of ML Models' 頁面明確指出 binary classification 在 Amazon ML 中『使用業界標準演算法 logistic regression』。同一頁面甚至列出直接類比的範例『Will the customer buy this product?』作為 binary classification 問題。Logistic regression 會輸出 [0,1] 範圍的預測分數，再以門檻值對應到兩種類別之一，正符合此處需求。由於公司已有標註的歷史結果，這是監督式分類任務，因此 logistic regression（C）為正確的建模方法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Anomaly detection (e.g., SageMaker Random Cut Forest) is an unsupervised technique that flags rare/outlier observations. It is not used when you have labeled historical data and want to predict a known yes/no class, so it does not fit a supervised binary prediction task.","why_zh":"Anomaly detection（如 SageMaker Random Cut Forest）是非監督式技術，用於標記罕見或離群觀測值。當你已有標註的歷史資料並要預測已知的是/否類別時並不適用，故不符合此監督式二元預測任務。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Linear regression predicts a continuous numeric value (e.g., a price or temperature). AWS docs assign linear regression to regression problems, not to predicting a two-class yes/no outcome, so it is the wrong model type for this binary target.","why_zh":"Linear regression 預測連續數值（例如價格或溫度）。AWS 文件將 linear regression 對應到 regression 問題，而非預測兩類別的是/否結果，因此對此二元目標而言是錯誤的模型類型。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Semantic segmentation is a computer-vision task that classifies each pixel of an image into a category. It is irrelevant to predicting a yes/no support outcome from historical tabular customer data.","why_zh":"Semantic segmentation 是電腦視覺任務，將影像中每個像素分類到某個類別，與從歷史表格客戶資料預測是/否支援結果毫無關聯。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/latest/dg/types-of-ml-models.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/latest/dg/binary-classification.html"]}},{"id":62,"question_en":"An ML engineer has developed a binary classification model outside of Amazon SageMaker. The ML engineer needs to make the model accessible to a SageMaker Canvas user for additional tuning. The model artifacts are stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. The ML engineer and the Canvas user are part of the same SageMaker domain. Which combination of requirements must be met so that the ML engineer can share the model with the Canvas user? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师在亚马逊 SageMaker 之外开发了一个二分类模型。该工程师需要让 SageMaker Canvas 用户能够访问此模型，以便进行进一步的调优。 模型工件存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。机器学习工程师和 Canvas 用户属于同一个 SageMaker 域。 为了使机器学习工程师能够与 Canvas 用户共享模型，必须满足哪两个要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"The ML engineer and the Canvas user must be in separate SageMaker domains.","B":"The Canvas user must have permissions to access the S3 bucket where the model artifacts are stored.","C":"The model must be registered in the SageMaker Model Registry.","D":"The ML engineer must host the model on AWS Marketplace.","E":"The ML engineer must deploy the model to a SageMaker endpoint."},"options_zh":{"A":"机器学习工程师和画布用户必须处于不同的 SageMaker 域中。","B":"Canvas 用户必须拥有访问存储模型构件的 S3 存储桶的权限。","C":"该模型必须在 SageMaker 模型注册表中注册。","D":"机器学习工程师必须在 AWS 市场托管该模型。","E":"机器学习工程师必须将模型部署到 SageMaker 端点。"},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The documented way to make a model that was built outside SageMaker available to a SageMaker Canvas user is the bring-your-own-model pattern that relies on the SageMaker Model Registry. Because the model was created externally, it is not yet a SageMaker object, so it must first be registered as a model version (a model package that points to the S3 artifacts and an inference container) in the SageMaker Model Registry; the Model Registry overview lists 'Share models with other users' as a core capability, making it the catalog and sharing mechanism within the shared domain (C). The model artifacts physically live in S3, so the Canvas user's execution role must have IAM permissions to read that bucket; the AmazonSageMakerModelRegistryFullAccess managed policy explicitly grants s3:GetObject 'to retrieve objects from the Amazon S3 buckets where model versions are stored,' confirming that without S3 access the Canvas user cannot consume the model (B). The remaining options are wrong: separate domains contradict the premise and are not needed, AWS Marketplace is for external commercial distribution, and deploying to a real-time endpoint is an inference-hosting step that is not the documented sharing-for-tuning path into Canvas.","explanation_zh":"要把在 SageMaker 之外建立的模型提供給 SageMaker Canvas 使用者，官方記載的作法是以 SageMaker Model Registry 為基礎的 bring-your-own-model 流程。由於該模型是在外部建立、尚不是 SageMaker 物件，必須先將它註冊為一個 model version（一個指向 S3 artifacts 與 inference container 的 model package）到 SageMaker Model Registry；Model Registry 概述明確將「Share models with other users」列為核心能力，因此它就是同一個 domain 內的編目與分享機制（C）。模型 artifacts 實際存放在 S3，因此 Canvas 使用者的 execution role 必須具備讀取該 bucket 的 IAM 權限；AmazonSageMakerModelRegistryFullAccess 受管政策明確授予 s3:GetObject 以「從存放 model versions 的 Amazon S3 buckets 取得物件」，這確認了若沒有 S3 存取權限，Canvas 使用者就無法使用該模型（B）。其餘選項皆錯誤：分開的 domain 與題目前提矛盾且非必要、AWS Marketplace 用於對外的商業散布、而部署到即時 endpoint 是推論託管步驟，並非官方記載把模型分享給 Canvas 進行調整的路徑。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The premise explicitly states both users are in the same SageMaker domain, and same-domain/same-account access is exactly what enables Canvas to consume the registered model. Forcing them into separate domains is neither required nor helpful and contradicts the scenario.","why_zh":"題目明確指出兩位使用者位於同一個 SageMaker domain，而同一 domain／帳戶的存取正是讓 Canvas 能使用已註冊模型的關鍵。強制將他們分到不同 domain 既非必要也無幫助，且與情境矛盾。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Marketplace is for publicly listing and selling models to external customers, not for internal sharing between two users in the same SageMaker domain. It is irrelevant to making a model available for Canvas tuning.","why_zh":"AWS Marketplace 用於公開上架並對外部客戶銷售模型，並非用於同一 SageMaker domain 內兩位使用者之間的內部分享，與讓模型可供 Canvas 調整無關。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Deploying the model to a SageMaker endpoint provides real-time inference hosting; it is not how a model is shared into Canvas for further tuning. The documented bring-your-own-model path into Canvas uses the Model Registry, not a live endpoint, and an endpoint would add unnecessary cost.","why_zh":"將模型部署到 SageMaker endpoint 是提供即時推論託管，並非把模型分享進 Canvas 以做進一步調整的方式。官方記載進入 Canvas 的 bring-your-own-model 路徑使用的是 Model Registry，而非執行中的 endpoint，且 endpoint 會帶來不必要的成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-register-model.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/security-iam-awsmanpol-model-registry.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-custom-models.html"]}},{"id":63,"question_en":"A company is building a deep learning model on Amazon SageMaker. The company uses a large amount of data as the training dataset. The company needs to optimize the model's hyperparameters to minimize the loss function on the validation dataset. Which hyperparameter tuning strategy will accomplish this goal with the LEAST computation time?","question_zh":"一家公司正在亚马逊的 SageMaker 平台上构建深度学习模型。该公司使用大量数据作为训练数据集。公司 需要优化模型的超参数，以使验证数据集上的损失函数最小化。 哪种超参数调整策略能在最短的计算时间内实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Hyperband","B":"Grid search","C":"Bayesian optimization","D":"Random search"},"options_zh":{"A":"Hyperband 算法","B":"网格搜索","C":"贝叶斯优化","D":"随机搜索"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Hyperband is a multi-fidelity tuning strategy designed exactly for large, iterative deep learning jobs. AWS docs state that Hyperband 'uses both intermediate and final results of training jobs to re-allocate epochs to well-utilized hyperparameter configurations and automatically stops those that underperform,' and that these features 'can significantly speed up hyperparameter tuning over random search and Bayesian optimization strategies.' The Best Practices guide is explicit: 'For large jobs, using the Hyperband tuning strategy can reduce computation time.' Because the scenario is a deep learning model (an iterative algorithm that publishes metrics per epoch) with a large dataset and the goal of minimizing validation loss in the LEAST computation time, Hyperband's early stopping plus parallel execution wins decisively over the other three strategies.","explanation_zh":"Hyperband 是一種 multi-fidelity 調校策略，正是為大型、迭代式的 deep learning 工作而設計。AWS 文件指出 Hyperband 會「同時使用訓練工作的中間與最終結果，將 epoch 重新分配給表現良好的 hyperparameter 組合，並自動停止表現不佳者」，且這些特性「相較於 random search 與 Bayesian optimization，可顯著加快 hyperparameter 調校速度」。Best Practices 指南更明確指出：「對於大型工作，使用 Hyperband 調校策略可減少運算時間。」因為本情境是一個 deep learning 模型（會逐 epoch 發布指標的迭代式演算法），搭配大型資料集，且目標是在最少運算時間內最小化 validation loss，Hyperband 的 early stopping 加上平行執行，明顯勝過其他三種策略。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Grid search exhaustively evaluates every hyperparameter combination (categorical only), so its compute cost grows combinatorially; AWS recommends it only for reproducibility/transparency or evenly exploring the full space, not for minimizing computation time.","why_zh":"Grid search 會窮舉每一種 hyperparameter 組合（且僅支援 categorical），運算成本以組合方式暴增；AWS 僅建議在需要可重現性/透明度或均勻探索整個空間時使用，而非為了最小化運算時間。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Bayesian optimization is sequential (each run depends on prior runs) so it 'cannot massively scale' and has no early stopping; AWS positions it for smaller jobs, and the Hyperband doc explicitly says Hyperband significantly speeds up tuning over Bayesian optimization.","why_zh":"Bayesian optimization 是序列式（每次運行依賴先前結果），因此「無法大規模擴展」且無 early stopping；AWS 將其定位於較小型工作，且 Hyperband 文件明確表示 Hyperband 相較 Bayesian optimization 可顯著加快調校速度。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Random search runs the most parallel trials but has no early stopping and no resource reallocation, so for a large deep learning model it wastes compute finishing under-performing trials; AWS recommends it for smaller jobs and the Hyperband doc states Hyperband significantly speeds up tuning over random search.","why_zh":"Random search 可平行執行最多試驗，但沒有 early stopping 也不會重新分配資源，因此對大型深度學習模型會浪費運算去完成表現不佳的試驗；AWS 建議用於較小型工作，且 Hyperband 文件指出 Hyperband 相較 random search 可顯著加快調校速度。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/automatic-model-tuning-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/automatic-model-tuning-how-it-works.html"]}},{"id":64,"question_en":"A company is planning to use Amazon Redshift ML in its primary AWS account. The source data is in an Amazon S3 bucket in a secondary account. An ML engineer needs to set up an ML pipeline in the primary account to access the S3 bucket in the secondary account. The solution must not require public IPv4 addresses. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司计划在其主要的 AWS 账户中使用 Amazon Redshift ML。源数据位于另一个辅助账户中的 Amazon S3 存储桶内。 一位机器学习工程师需要在主账户中设置一个机器学习管道，以访问次账户中的 S3 存储桶。解决方案 不得使用公共 IPv4 地址。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Provision a Redshift cluster and Amazon SageMaker Studio in a VPC with no public access enabled in the primary account. Create a VPC peering connection between the accounts. Update the VPC route tables to remove the route to 0.0.0.0/0.","B":"Provision a Redshift cluster and Amazon SageMaker Studio in a VPC with no public access enabled in the primary account. Create an AWS Direct Connect connection and a transit gateway. Associate the VPCs from both accounts with the transit gateway. Update the VPC route tables to remove the route to 0.0.0.0/0.","C":"Provision a Redshift cluster and Amazon SageMaker Studio in a VPC in the primary account. Create an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection with two encrypted IPsec tunnels between the accounts. Set up interface VPC endpoints for Amazon S3.","D":"Provision a Redshift cluster and Amazon SageMaker Studio in a VPC in the primary account. Create an S3 gateway endpoint. Update the S3 bucket policy to allow IAM principals from the primary account. Set up interface VPC endpoints for SageMaker and Amazon Redshift."},"options_zh":{"A":"在主账户中配置一个没有启用公共访问权限的 Redshift 集群和 Amazon SageMaker Studio 的 VPC。在 账户之间创建 VPC 对等连接。更新 VPC 路由表以移除到 0.0.0.0/0 的路由。","B":"在主账户的 VPC 中配置一个 Redshift 集群和 Amazon SageMaker Studio，且不启用公共访问。创建一 个 AWS Direct Connect 连接和一个中转网关。将两个账户的 VPC 与中转网关关联。更新 VPC 路由 表以移除到 0.0.0.0/0 的路由。","C":"在主账户的 VPC 中配置 Redshift 集群和 Amazon SageMaker Studio。在两个账户之间创建具有两条 加密 IPsec 隧道的 AWS 站点到站点 VPN 连接。为 Amazon S3 设置接口 VPC 终端节点。","D":"在主账户的 VPC 中配置 Redshift 集群和 Amazon SageMaker Studio。创建 S3 网关端点。更新 S3 存储 桶策略以允许来自主账户的 IAM 实体。为 SageMaker 和 Amazon Redshift 设置接口 VPC 端点。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Redshift ML internally calls Amazon SageMaker and reads/writes training data in Amazon S3, so the primary-account VPC needs private connectivity to (1) the S3 service that hosts the bucket and (2) the SageMaker and Amazon Redshift control-plane APIs, all without public IPv4 addresses. An S3 gateway VPC endpoint provides exactly this: it lets the VPC reach Amazon S3 in the same Region with no internet gateway, NAT device, or public IP, at no extra cost. The bucket living in a secondary account does not change the network path, because a gateway endpoint targets the regional S3 service and can reach any bucket in that Region; cross-account access is authorized purely at the IAM/bucket-policy layer, which is why the secondary account adds a bucket policy allowing the primary account's IAM principals (the standard cross-account S3 pattern, AWS Example 2). Interface VPC endpoints (PrivateLink) for SageMaker and Amazon Redshift then give the no-public-access VPC private API access. Option D is the only choice whose mechanisms actually map to the resources involved (an S3 bucket plus the Redshift/SageMaker APIs).","explanation_zh":"Amazon Redshift ML 在背後會呼叫 Amazon SageMaker，並在 Amazon S3 讀寫訓練資料，因此 primary 帳號的 VPC 必須在不使用 public IPv4 位址的前提下，私密地連到 (1) 存放該 bucket 的 S3 服務，以及 (2) SageMaker 與 Amazon Redshift 的控制平面 API。S3 gateway VPC endpoint 正好滿足此需求：它讓 VPC 在同一個 Region 內無需 internet gateway、NAT device 或 public IP 即可存取 Amazon S3，且不額外收費。該 bucket 位於 secondary 帳號並不會改變網路路徑，因為 gateway endpoint 指向的是 Region 級的 S3 服務，能存取該 Region 內任何 bucket；跨帳號授權純粹在 IAM/bucket policy 層處理，因此由 secondary 帳號加上允許 primary 帳號 IAM principal 的 bucket policy（即標準跨帳號 S3 模式，AWS Example 2）。接著為 SageMaker 與 Amazon Redshift 建立 interface VPC endpoint（PrivateLink），讓無公開存取的 VPC 取得私密 API 連線。D 是唯一機制能對應到實際資源（S3 bucket 加上 Redshift/SageMaker API）的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"VPC peering connects VPC-to-VPC, but the source data is in an S3 bucket, not inside the secondary account's VPC. S3 is a regional service reached via its service endpoint or a gateway/interface endpoint, so peering provides no path to the bucket; AWS even states resources on the other side of a peering connection cannot use a gateway endpoint to reach S3, and removing the 0.0.0.0/0 route just kills internet access while leaving S3 unreachable.","why_zh":"VPC peering 連接的是 VPC 對 VPC，但來源資料在 S3 bucket，而非 secondary 帳號的 VPC 內。S3 是透過服務端點或 gateway/interface endpoint 存取的 Region 級服務，peering 無法提供到 bucket 的路徑；AWS 甚至明確指出 peering 另一端的資源無法使用 gateway endpoint 連到 S3，移除 0.0.0.0/0 路由也只是切斷對外網路，仍無法存取 S3。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Direct Connect is for on-premises-to-AWS connectivity and is irrelevant between two AWS accounts; a transit gateway connects VPCs, not S3 buckets. Neither addresses reaching an S3 bucket, gateway endpoints cannot even be reached through a transit gateway, and the whole design is grossly over-engineered for this requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Direct Connect 用於 on-premises 與 AWS 間的連線，在兩個 AWS 帳號之間並不適用；transit gateway 連接的是 VPC，而非 S3 bucket。兩者都無法解決存取 S3 bucket 的問題，gateway endpoint 也無法經由 transit gateway 連線，整體設計對此需求嚴重過度設計。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Site-to-Site VPN with IPsec tunnels is designed to connect remote/on-premises networks to a VPC, not to link two AWS accounts; the design is nonsensical for cross-account S3 access and adds needless complexity. It also omits the SageMaker and Redshift interface endpoints that Redshift ML needs for private API calls.","why_zh":"AWS Site-to-Site VPN 搭配 IPsec 通道是用來把遠端或 on-premises 網路連到 VPC，並非用於連接兩個 AWS 帳號；以此做跨帳號 S3 存取並不合理且徒增複雜度。此外它也缺少 Redshift ML 進行私密 API 呼叫所需的 SageMaker 與 Redshift interface endpoint。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/gateway-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-walkthroughs-managing-access-example2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/create-interface-endpoint.html"]}},{"id":65,"question_en":"A company is using an AWS Lambda function to monitor the metrics from an ML model. An ML engineer needs to implement a solution to send an email message when the metrics breach a threshold. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS Lambda 函数来监控一个机器学习模型的指标。一位机器学习工程师需要实现 一个解决方案，以便在指标超出阈值时发送电子邮件通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Log the metrics from the Lambda function to AWS CloudTrail. Configure a CloudTrail trail to send the email message.","B":"Log the metrics from the Lambda function to Amazon CloudFront. Configure an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to send the email message.","C":"Log the metrics from the Lambda function to Amazon CloudWatch. Configure a CloudWatch alarm to send the email message.","D":"Log the metrics from the Lambda function to Amazon CloudWatch. Configure an Amazon CloudFront rule to send the email message."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Lambda 函数的指标记录到 AWS CloudTrail 中。配置 CloudTrail 跟踪以发送电子邮件消息。","B":"将 Lambda 函数的指标记录到 Amazon CloudFront 中。配置 Amazon CloudWatch 警报以发送电子邮 件消息。","C":"将 Lambda 函数的指标记录到 Amazon CloudWatch 中。配置 CloudWatch 警报以发送电子邮件消息。","D":"将 Lambda 函数的指标记录到 Amazon CloudWatch 中。配置 Amazon CloudFront 规则以发送电子邮 件消息。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The canonical AWS pattern for threshold-based email is: a Lambda function publishes custom metrics to Amazon CloudWatch via the PutMetricData API, a CloudWatch metric alarm watches that metric against a threshold, and when the threshold is breached (ALARM state) the alarm performs an action. AWS docs explicitly state a CloudWatch alarm watches metrics and sends notifications when a threshold is breached, and that the action can be sending a notification to an Amazon SNS topic. An SNS topic with an email subscription then delivers the message to subscribers. Option C is the only choice that pairs the correct metric store (CloudWatch) with the correct threshold-notification mechanism (CloudWatch alarm), so it is correct.","explanation_zh":"AWS 用於門檻 email 通知的標準模式是：Lambda 函式透過 PutMetricData API 將自訂指標發布到 Amazon CloudWatch，CloudWatch metric alarm 根據門檻監控該指標，當突破門檻（進入 ALARM 狀態）時執行 alarm action。AWS 文件明確指出 CloudWatch alarm 監控指標並在突破門檻時送出通知，而該 action 可以是發送通知到 Amazon SNS topic。具有 email 訂閱的 SNS topic 隨即將訊息送達訂閱者。選項 C 是唯一同時搭配正確指標儲存（CloudWatch）與正確門檻通知機制（CloudWatch alarm）的選項，因此正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS CloudTrail records AWS API/management and data events for governance and auditing, not custom ML application metrics, and a CloudTrail trail cannot evaluate a threshold or send email itself. The threshold-to-email step requires a CloudWatch alarm plus SNS, which this option omits.","why_zh":"AWS CloudTrail 記錄 AWS API/管理與資料事件以供治理與稽核，而非自訂 ML 應用指標，且 CloudTrail trail 本身無法評估門檻或發送 email。門檻到 email 的步驟需要 CloudWatch alarm 加 SNS，此選項缺少這部分。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon CloudFront is a content delivery network (CDN); you cannot publish arbitrary custom application metrics to it, so a CloudWatch alarm has nothing to read from CloudFront. Although it correctly names a CloudWatch alarm for email, the metric destination is wrong.","why_zh":"Amazon CloudFront 是內容傳遞網路（CDN）；無法將任意自訂應用指標發布到它，因此 CloudWatch alarm 無從 CloudFront 讀取指標。雖然它正確使用 CloudWatch alarm 發送 email，但指標目的地錯誤。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Logging metrics to CloudWatch is correct, but there is no 'Amazon CloudFront rule' that sends email; CloudFront is a CDN with no threshold-notification feature. Email on a breached threshold is delivered by a CloudWatch alarm publishing to an SNS topic, not by any CloudFront rule.","why_zh":"將指標記錄到 CloudWatch 是正確的，但並不存在會發送 email 的「Amazon CloudFront rule」；CloudFront 是 CDN，沒有門檻通知功能。突破門檻的 email 是由 CloudWatch alarm 發布到 SNS topic 完成，而非任何 CloudFront 規則。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/AlarmThatSendsEmail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/publishingMetrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/alarm-actions.html"]}},{"id":66,"question_en":"A company has used Amazon SageMaker to deploy a predictive ML model in production. The company is using SageMaker Model Monitor on the model. After a model update, an ML engineer notices data quality issues in the Model Monitor checks. What should the ML engineer do to mitigate the data quality issues that Model Monitor has identified?","question_zh":"","options_en":{"A":"Adjust the model's parameters and hyperparameters.","B":"Initiate a manual Model Monitor job that uses the most recent production data.","C":"Create a new baseline from the latest dataset. Update Model Monitor to use the new baseline for evaluations.","D":"Include additional data in the existing training set for the model. Retrain and redeploy the model."},"options_zh":{},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"SageMaker Model Monitor data quality monitoring compares the statistics and constraints of captured production inference data against a baseline (statistics.json and constraints.json) that is computed from the dataset used to train the model. AWS docs state the baseline 'calculations of statistics and constraints are needed as a standard against which data drift and other data quality issues can be detected,' and that 'the training dataset that you used to train the model is usually a good baseline dataset.' After a model update (retrain on a new/updated dataset), the original baseline becomes stale and no longer represents the data the new model expects, so Model Monitor flags data quality violations that are really a baseline-vs-new-model mismatch. The documented mitigation is to generate a new baseline from the latest dataset (DefaultModelMonitor.suggest_baseline) and update the monitoring schedule to evaluate against the new baseline, which re-establishes the correct standard and resolves the findings tied to the model update.","explanation_zh":"SageMaker Model Monitor 的 data quality 監控會將擷取到的生產推論資料的統計與約束，與一個 baseline（statistics.json 與 constraints.json）進行比較，而該 baseline 是由訓練模型所用的資料集計算而來。AWS 文件指出 baseline 的「statistics 與 constraints 計算是作為偵測 data drift 與其他 data quality 問題的標準」，且「用來訓練模型的訓練資料集通常就是良好的 baseline 資料集」。在模型更新（以新的或更新後的資料集重新訓練）之後，原本的 baseline 已過時，不再代表新模型所預期的資料，因此 Model Monitor 會標記出 data quality 違規，而這其實是 baseline 與新模型之間的不匹配。文件記載的緩解方式是用最新資料集產生新的 baseline（DefaultModelMonitor.suggest_baseline），並更新 monitoring schedule 以針對新的 baseline 進行評估，藉此重新建立正確的標準並解決因模型更新所產生的問題。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Adjusting model parameters and hyperparameters changes model predictive accuracy, not the input data's statistical/schema properties. Data quality monitoring evaluates input data against a baseline, so retuning the model does nothing to resolve the data quality violations Model Monitor flagged.","why_zh":"調整模型參數與超參數改變的是模型預測準確度，而非輸入資料的統計／結構特性。Data quality 監控是把輸入資料與 baseline 比較，重新調參無法解決 Model Monitor 回報的資料品質違規。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Running another (manual) monitoring job re-evaluates production data against the same stale baseline, so it would simply re-detect the same violations. It re-evaluates rather than mitigates, and does not fix the root cause (an outdated baseline after the model update).","why_zh":"再執行一次（手動）監控工作只是用相同且過時的 baseline 重新評估生產資料，仍會偵測到相同的違規。它只是重新評估而非緩解，無法解決根本原因（模型更新後過時的 baseline）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Adding data, retraining, and redeploying is the remedy for genuine model-quality degradation/real-world data drift and is heavyweight. Here the issue is data quality checks failing right after a model update due to a mismatched/stale baseline; retraining and redeploying again does not update the baseline standard, so the stale baseline would still trigger the same violations, and is disproportionate to the identified problem.","why_zh":"加入資料、重新訓練並重新部署是針對真正的模型品質退化／真實世界 data drift 的補救措施，且成本高。此情境是模型更新後因 baseline 過時不匹配而導致 data quality 檢查失敗；再次重新訓練與部署並不會更新 baseline 標準，過時的 baseline 仍會觸發相同違規，且對於所識別的問題而言過度。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-data-quality.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-create-baseline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-interpreting-results.html"]}},{"id":67,"question_en":"A company has an ML model that generates text descriptions based on images that customers upload to the company's website. The images can be up to 50 MB in total size. An ML engineer decides to store the images in an Amazon S3 bucket. The ML engineer must implement a processing solution that can scale to accommodate changes in demand. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款机器学习模型，能够根据客户上传至公司网站的图片生成文字描述。这些图片的总大 小最多可达 50MB。 一位机器学习工程师决定将图像存储在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中。该机器学习工程师必须实现一种能够扩展以 适应需求变化的处理方案。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon SageMaker batch transform job to process all the images in the S3 bucket.","B":"Create an Amazon SageMaker Asynchronous Inference endpoint and a scaling policy. Run a script to make an inference request for each image.","C":"Create an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster that uses Karpenter for auto scaling. Host the model on the EKS cluster. Run a script to make an inference request for each image.","D":"Create an AWS Batch job that uses an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. Specify a list of images to process for each AWS Batch job."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon SageMaker 批量转换作业来处理 S3 存储桶中的所有图像。","B":"创建一个 Amazon SageMaker 异步推理端点和一个扩展策略。运行一个脚本，针对每张图片发出一次 推理请求。","C":"创建一个使用 Karpenter 进行自动扩展的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service（Amazon EKS）集群。在 EKS 集群上托管模型。运行一个脚本，针对每张图片发出一次推理请求。","D":"创建一个使用 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）集群的 AWS Batch 作业。为每个 AWS Batch 作业指定要处理的镜像列表。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The workload is an ongoing stream of customer-uploaded images that already land in S3 and must be processed with auto scaling at the LEAST operational overhead. SageMaker Asynchronous Inference is purpose-built for this: per AWS docs it queues requests, natively reads the request payload from an S3 location and writes the inference result back to S3, supports large payloads up to 1 GB (so 50 MB is well within limits), targets near-real-time latency for individual requests, and supports automatic scaling via a scaling policy (including scale-to-zero when idle). Because it is a fully managed SageMaker endpoint, there is no cluster, container orchestration, or instance fleet to operate. Batch Transform (A) is for offline processing of data available upfront and is not a continuous, demand-scaled online service; EKS+Karpenter (C) and AWS Batch on ECS (D) require you to build and operate the hosting/scaling infrastructure yourself, which is far more operational overhead. Therefore B meets the requirements with the least operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載是客戶持續上傳影像、已落在 S3、並需要隨需求自動擴展且維運負擔最低的處理方案。SageMaker Asynchronous Inference 正是為此設計：依 AWS 文件，它會將請求排入佇列，原生地從 S3 位置讀取請求負載、再將推論結果寫回 S3，支援高達 1 GB 的大型負載（因此 50 MB 完全在範圍內），針對單一請求提供近即時延遲，並透過 scaling policy 支援自動擴展（包含閒置時縮減至零）。由於它是全代管的 SageMaker endpoint，沒有叢集、容器調度或執行個體機群需要維運。Batch Transform（A）用於離線處理事先備齊的資料，並非持續、隨需求擴展的線上服務；EKS+Karpenter（C）與 AWS Batch on ECS（D）都需要自行建置與維運託管/擴展基礎設施，維運負擔遠高得多。因此 B 以最低維運負擔滿足需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Batch Transform is for offline processing of datasets available upfront with no persistent endpoint. The website continuously receives new images, so you would have to repeatedly trigger and orchestrate batch jobs as images arrive; it does not auto-scale to live per-request demand and adds orchestration overhead.","why_zh":"Batch Transform 適用於事先備齊資料的離線處理，且不需要持久端點。網站持續接收新影像，必須隨影像到達反覆觸發與協調批次工作；它不會依即時逐一請求需求自動擴展，並增加協調負擔。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Hosting the model on a self-managed EKS cluster with Karpenter means operating Kubernetes, node groups, model serving, and scaling configuration yourself. This is the highest operational overhead, the opposite of what the question asks.","why_zh":"在自管的 EKS 叢集上以 Karpenter 託管模型，代表你要自行維運 Kubernetes、節點群組、模型服務與擴展設定。這是最高的維運負擔，與題目要求相反。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Batch on an ECS cluster requires building container images, job definitions, job queues, and compute environments, and is designed for batch jobs rather than a continuous, demand-scaled inference workload. It carries far more operational overhead than a fully managed SageMaker async endpoint.","why_zh":"AWS Batch 搭配 ECS 叢集需自行建立容器映像、job definitions、job queues 與運算環境，且是為批次工作而非持續、隨需求擴展的推論工作負載設計。維運負擔遠高於全代管的 SageMaker 非同步端點。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/async-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/async-inference-autoscale.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/deploy-model-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/batch-transform.html"]}},{"id":68,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to use AWS services to identify and extract meaningful unique keywords from documents. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师需要使用 AWS 服务从文档中识别并提取有意义的独特关键词。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use the Natural Language Toolkit (NLTK) library on Amazon EC2 instances for text pre-processing. Use the Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) algorithm to identify and extract relevant keywords.","B":"Use Amazon SageMaker and the BlazingText algorithm. Apply custom pre-processing steps for stemming and removal of stop words. Calculate term frequency-inverse document frequency (TF-IDF) scores to identify and extract relevant keywords.","C":"Store the documents in an Amazon S3 bucket. Create AWS Lambda functions to process the documents and to run Python scripts for stemming and removal of stop words. Use bigram and trigram techniques to identify and extract relevant keywords.","D":"Use Amazon Comprehend custom entity recognition and key phrase extraction to identify and extract relevant keywords."},"options_zh":{"A":"在亚马逊 EC2 实例上使用自然语言工具包（NLTK）库进行文本预处理。使用潜在狄利克雷分配 （LDA）算法来识别并提取相关关键词。","B":"使用亚马逊 SageMaker 和 BlazingText 算法。应用自定义的预处理步骤进行词干提取和停用词去除。 计算词频 - 逆文档频率（TF-IDF）得分以识别并提取相关关键词。","C":"将文档存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。创建 AWS Lambda 函数来处理文档，并运行 Python 脚本以进行 词干提取和停用词去除。使用二元语法和三元语法技术来识别和提取相关关键词。","D":"使用亚马逊 comprehend 自定义实体识别和关键短语提取功能来识别并提取相关关键词。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to identify and extract meaningful unique keywords from documents with the LEAST operational overhead. Amazon Comprehend is a fully managed NLP service whose pre-trained key phrase extraction (DetectKeyPhrases / BatchDetectKeyPhrases / StartKeyPhrasesDetectionJob) returns noun phrases (keywords) directly, using a continuously trained pre-trained model so you supply no training data, manage no infrastructure, and write no custom pre-processing. AWS explicitly lists scanning an entire document repository for key phrases as a Comprehend use case. Options A (NLTK on EC2 + LDA), B (SageMaker BlazingText + custom stemming/stop-word removal + TF-IDF), and C (S3 + Lambda + Python stemming/stop-word scripts + bigram/trigram) all require self-managed compute and hand-written NLP pipelines, which is far higher operational overhead. Within option D, custom entity recognition by itself does add overhead because it needs manually annotated training data plus model training and targets specific business entity types rather than general keywords; however, taken as a whole D is still by far the lowest-overhead option because the managed key phrase extraction feature alone meets the requirement with no infrastructure or code to maintain.","explanation_zh":"需求是以「最少維運負擔」從文件中辨識並擷取有意義且唯一的關鍵字。Amazon Comprehend 是全託管的 NLP 服務，其預先訓練的 key phrase extraction（DetectKeyPhrases / BatchDetectKeyPhrases / StartKeyPhrasesDetectionJob）會直接回傳名詞片語（即關鍵字），且使用持續訓練的 pre-trained 模型，因此不需提供訓練資料、不需管理任何基礎設施、也不需自行撰寫前處理。AWS 文件明確將「掃描整個文件庫以找出 key phrases」列為 Comprehend 用途。選項 A（EC2 上的 NLTK + LDA）、B（SageMaker BlazingText + 自訂 stemming/去停用詞 + TF-IDF）、C（S3 + Lambda + Python stemming/去停用詞腳本 + bigram/trigram）都需要自行管理運算資源並手刻 NLP 流程，維運負擔遠高。註：D 選項中的 custom entity recognition 本身確實會增加負擔（需要人工標註訓練資料與模型訓練，且針對特定商業實體類型而非一般關鍵字）；但整體而言，D 仍是維運負擔最低的選項，因為單靠全託管的 key phrase extraction 功能即可滿足需求，且無須維護任何基礎設施或程式碼。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Running NLTK on Amazon EC2 instances and applying LDA requires provisioning, patching, and scaling EC2, plus writing and maintaining custom text pre-processing and topic-modeling code. LDA produces topics/clusters, not a clean list of keywords, and this is high operational overhead.","why_zh":"在 Amazon EC2 上跑 NLTK 並套用 LDA，需自行佈建、修補、擴充 EC2，並撰寫與維護自訂文字前處理與主題模型程式碼。LDA 產生的是主題/分群而非乾淨的關鍵字清單，維運負擔高。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"SageMaker BlazingText is a word-embedding / text-classification algorithm, not a keyword extractor; you would also build custom stemming, stop-word removal, and TF-IDF logic and manage SageMaker training jobs and endpoints. This is significant operational overhead and not the intended tool for direct keyword extraction.","why_zh":"SageMaker BlazingText 是字詞嵌入/文字分類演算法，並非關鍵字擷取器；還需自行建立 stemming、去停用詞與 TF-IDF 邏輯並管理 SageMaker 訓練工作與端點，維運負擔大且非直接擷取關鍵字的工具。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"S3 plus Lambda functions running custom Python stemming/stop-word scripts with bigram/trigram extraction means writing, testing, and maintaining the entire NLP pipeline yourself. Although serverless, the custom-code burden makes operational overhead much higher than a managed Comprehend API call.","why_zh":"S3 加上執行自訂 Python stemming/去停用詞腳本並做 bigram/trigram 擷取的 Lambda，等於要自行撰寫、測試與維護整條 NLP 流程。雖為無伺服器，但自訂程式碼負擔使維運成本遠高於直接呼叫託管的 Comprehend API。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/how-key-phrases.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/custom-entity-recognition.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/APIReference/API_DetectKeyPhrases.html"]}},{"id":69,"question_en":"A company needs to give its ML engineers appropriate access to training data. The ML engineers must access training data from only their own business group. The ML engineers must not be allowed to access training data from other business groups. The company uses a single AWS account and stores all the training data in Amazon S3 buckets. All ML model training occurs in Amazon SageMaker. Which solution will provide the ML engineers with the appropriate access?","question_zh":"一家公司需要为其机器学习工程师提供适当的训练数据访问权限。机器学习工程师只能访问其所在业务 部门的训练数据，不得访问其他业务部门的训练数据。 该公司使用一个 AWS 账户，并将所有训练数据存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。所有机器学习模型的训 练都在 Amazon SageMaker 中进行。 哪种解决方案能为机器学习工程师提供适当的访问权限？","options_en":{"A":"Enable S3 bucket versioning.","B":"Configure S3 Object Lock settings for each user.","C":"Add cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) policies to the S3 buckets.","D":"Create IAM policies. Attach the policies to IAM users or IAM roles."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 S3 存储桶版本控制。","B":"为每个用户配置 S3 对象锁定设置。","C":"为 S3 存储桶添加跨源资源共享（CORS）策略。","D":"创建 IAM 策略。将策略附加到 IAM 用户或 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Within a single AWS account, the correct way to restrict which ML engineers can read which training data in Amazon S3 is to author IAM identity-based policies that scope S3 actions (such as s3:ListBucket and s3:GetObject) to specific bucket ARNs and key prefixes, then attach those policies to the relevant IAM users or roles, including the SageMaker execution roles used for training. By default IAM users and roles have no S3 permissions, so an administrator must explicitly grant least-privilege access. The AWS 'Controlling access to a bucket with user policies' walkthrough demonstrates this exact pattern: create IAM users/groups, verify they start with no permissions, then grant each principal access only to its own folder/prefix and explicitly deny access to others. This per-business-group, prefix-scoped authorization is precisely what option D delivers. The other options address durability (versioning), immutability/retention (Object Lock), or browser cross-origin behavior (CORS), none of which control which principal may read which data.","explanation_zh":"在單一 AWS 帳戶內,要限制不同 ML engineers 只能讀取各自業務群組在 Amazon S3 的訓練資料,正確做法是撰寫 IAM identity-based policies,將 S3 動作(例如 s3:ListBucket、s3:GetObject)限定到特定 bucket ARN 與 key prefix,再把這些 policy 附加到對應的 IAM users 或 IAM roles(包含用於訓練的 SageMaker execution role)。預設情況下 IAM users 與 roles 對 S3 沒有任何權限,因此管理員必須明確以最小權限原則授權。AWS 的「Controlling access to a bucket with user policies」教學正示範此模式:建立 IAM users/groups、確認其一開始沒有任何權限,再分別授予每個 principal 只能存取自己的資料夾/prefix 並明確拒絕其他。這種依業務群組、以 prefix 為界的授權正是選項 D 所提供的。其餘選項分別處理耐久性(versioning)、不可變/保留(Object Lock)、或瀏覽器跨來源行為(CORS),皆無法控制哪個 principal 能讀取哪份資料。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 bucket versioning preserves and recovers prior object versions to protect against overwrites/deletes. It is a data-protection/durability feature and provides no per-user authorization, so it cannot restrict engineers to their own group's data.","why_zh":"S3 bucket versioning 是保留並還原舊版物件以防覆寫/刪除的資料保護/耐久性功能,完全不提供依使用者授權,無法限制工程師只能存取自己群組的資料。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 Object Lock enforces WORM retention/legal-hold to make objects immutable for a period; it is configured per object/bucket (not 'for each user') and does not control which principal may read data. It addresses retention/immutability, not access authorization.","why_zh":"S3 Object Lock 透過 WORM 保留期/legal hold 使物件在一段時間內不可變;其設定是針對物件/bucket(而非『為每個使用者』),也不控制哪個 principal 能讀取資料;它處理的是保留期/不可變性而非存取授權。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CORS controls whether a web browser on one origin may make client-side requests to S3 resources on another origin. It governs cross-origin browser behavior, not IAM authorization, and does nothing to segregate business-group access.","why_zh":"CORS 控制某個 origin 的網頁瀏覽器是否可向另一 origin 的 S3 資源發出用戶端請求,規範的是跨來源瀏覽器行為而非 IAM 授權,完全無法區隔不同業務群組的存取。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/walkthrough1.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/security_iam_id-based-policy-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_controlling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_examples_s3_rw-bucket.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-access-training-data.html"]}},{"id":70,"question_en":"A company needs to host a custom ML model to perform forecast analysis. The forecast analysis will occur with predictable and sustained load during the same 2-hour period every day. Multiple invocations during the analysis period will require quick responses. The company needs AWS to manage the underlying infrastructure and any auto scaling activities. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要托管一个自定义的机器学习模型来执行预测分析。预测分析将在每天相同的 2 小时内以可预 测且持续的负载进行。 在分析期间，多次调用将需要快速响应。该公司需要 AWS 来管理底层基础设施以及任何自动扩展活动。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Schedule an Amazon SageMaker batch transform job by using AWS Lambda.","B":"Configure an Auto Scaling group of Amazon EC2 instances to use scheduled scaling.","C":"Use Amazon SageMaker Serverless Inference with provisioned concurrency.","D":"Run the model on an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster on Amazon EC2 with pod auto scaling."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Lambda 安排 Amazon SageMaker 批量转换作业。","B":"配置一个使用计划缩放功能的 Amazon EC2 实例自动扩展组。","C":"使用具有预配置并发量的 Amazon SageMaker 无服务器推理。","D":"在配备自动伸缩功能的 Amazon EC2 上的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service （Amazon EKS） 集群上 运行模型。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements decompose into four constraints: (1) AWS must manage the underlying infrastructure, (2) AWS must manage auto scaling, (3) the load is predictable and sustained during a fixed 2-hour daily window, and (4) multiple invocations need quick (low-latency) responses. Amazon SageMaker Serverless Inference 'enables you to deploy and scale ML models without configuring or managing any of the underlying infrastructure,' satisfying the fully managed requirement. Adding Provisioned Concurrency keeps the endpoint warm so 'the compute resources are initialized and ready to respond within milliseconds,' which eliminates cold starts and delivers the quick responses needed during the busy window. AWS docs explicitly state Serverless Inference with Provisioned Concurrency 'is a cost-effective option when you have predictable bursts in your traffic,' and it integrates with Application Auto Scaling so Provisioned Concurrency can be managed 'based on a target metric or on a schedule' to cover exactly the daily 2-hour period. This is the only option where AWS manages both the infrastructure and the scaling while guaranteeing low-latency responses.","explanation_zh":"需求可拆解為四個條件：(1) AWS 必須管理底層基礎設施，(2) AWS 必須管理 auto scaling，(3) 負載在每天固定的 2 小時時段內可預測且持續，(4) 多次呼叫需要快速（低延遲）回應。Amazon SageMaker Serverless Inference 讓你『在不設定或管理任何底層基礎設施的情況下部署並擴展 ML 模型』，滿足全託管需求。加上 Provisioned Concurrency 可讓端點保持暖機，使『運算資源已初始化並能在數毫秒內回應』，消除冷啟動，在繁忙時段提供所需的快速回應。AWS 文件明確指出，具備 Provisioned Concurrency 的 Serverless Inference『在流量具有可預測突發時是符合成本效益的選項』，且它與 Application Auto Scaling 整合，可『依據目標指標或排程』管理 Provisioned Concurrency，正好涵蓋每天的 2 小時時段。此為唯一同時由 AWS 管理基礎設施與擴展、又保證低延遲回應的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Batch transform is for asynchronous, offline batch scoring of datasets; it does not provide a low-latency endpoint for 'multiple invocations requiring quick responses,' and orchestrating it with Lambda adds operational overhead rather than letting AWS manage scaling for synchronous requests.","why_zh":"Batch transform 用於非同步、離線的批次資料評分，無法為『需要快速回應的多次呼叫』提供低延遲端點；用 Lambda 排程反而增加維運負擔，並非交由 AWS 管理同步請求的擴展。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An EC2 Auto Scaling group with scheduled scaling requires you to manage instances, AMIs, the model serving stack, patching, and the scaling configuration yourself; the question explicitly requires AWS to manage the underlying infrastructure, which EC2 does not satisfy.","why_zh":"EC2 Auto Scaling group 搭配排程擴展需自行管理執行個體、AMI、模型服務堆疊、修補與擴展設定；題目明確要求由 AWS 管理底層基礎設施，EC2 無法滿足此點。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Running the model on EKS on EC2 with pod autoscaling means you manage the cluster, worker nodes, container orchestration, and scaling logic. This is high operational overhead and AWS does not manage the underlying infrastructure for you, contradicting the requirement.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上的 EKS 執行模型並使用 pod 自動擴展，代表你需自行管理叢集、工作節點、容器編排與擴展邏輯。此為高維運負擔，且 AWS 不會替你管理底層基礎設施，與需求相牴觸。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/serverless-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/serverless-endpoints-autoscale.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/deploy-model-options.html"]}},{"id":71,"question_en":"A company's ML engineer has deployed an ML model for sentiment analysis to an Amazon SageMaker endpoint. The ML engineer needs to explain to company stakeholders how the model makes predictions. Which solution will provide an explanation for the model's predictions?","question_zh":"一家公司的机器学习工程师已将一个用于情感分析的机器学习模型部署到了亚马逊 SageMaker 端点。 该机器学习工程师需要向公司相关利益方解释模型是如何进行预测的。 哪种解决方案能为模型的预测提供解释？","options_en":{"A":"Use SageMaker Model Monitor on the deployed model.","B":"Use SageMaker Clarify on the deployed model.","C":"Show the distribution of inferences from A/B testing in Amazon CloudWatch.","D":"Add a shadow endpoint. Analyze prediction differences on samples."},"options_zh":{"A":"在已部署的模型上使用 SageMaker 模型监控器。","B":"在已部署的模型上使用 SageMaker Clarify。","C":"在亚马逊 CloudWatch 中展示 A/B 测试推断结果的分布情况。","D":"添加一个影子端点。分析样本上的预测差异。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to explain HOW the model makes predictions (model explainability/interpretability). Amazon SageMaker Clarify is purpose-built for this: AWS docs state it 'can help you understand why your ML model made a specific prediction' and 'helps explain how your models make predictions using feature attributions.' Clarify computes feature attributions based on Shapley values (SHAP), quantifying how much each input feature contributed to a prediction, both globally and for individual inferences. It can run as a processing job to generate an explainability report, or be enabled as online explainability on a real-time endpoint, returning explanations alongside predictions. AWS even cites the exact use case of providing 'explanations about how ML models made certain predictions' to stakeholders. None of the other options produce per-feature explanations of model reasoning.","explanation_zh":"需求是解釋模型「如何」做出預測（即模型可解釋性 / interpretability）。Amazon SageMaker Clarify 正是為此打造：AWS 文件明確指出它「能幫助你理解模型為何做出某個特定預測」，且「使用 feature attributions 解釋模型如何做出預測」。Clarify 透過 Shapley values（SHAP）計算 feature attributions，量化每個輸入特徵對某次預測的貢獻程度，既可針對整體模型，也可針對個別推論。它可作為 processing job 產生可解釋性報告，或作為 online explainability 掛在 real-time endpoint 上，與預測一起回傳解釋。AWS 文件甚至直接舉出向利害關係人提供「模型如何做出某些預測的解釋」這個使用情境。其他選項都無法產生針對模型推理的逐特徵解釋。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SageMaker Model Monitor detects data quality, model quality, bias, and feature-attribution drift in production. It tells you WHEN behavior degrades, not HOW the model reaches a given prediction, so it does not explain predictions to stakeholders.","why_zh":"SageMaker Model Monitor 偵測生產環境中的資料品質、模型品質、偏差與特徵歸因漂移。它告訴你「何時」行為退化，而非「如何」做出某次預測，因此無法向利害關係人解釋預測。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Showing the distribution of A/B test inferences in CloudWatch surfaces aggregate metrics and operational behavior. It compares variants and traffic but provides no feature-level reasoning for how predictions are made.","why_zh":"在 CloudWatch 顯示 A/B 測試推論的分佈只呈現彙總指標與運維行為。它比較變體與流量，但完全不提供預測如何產生的特徵層級推理。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A shadow endpoint mirrors live traffic to a candidate variant to compare predictions/performance before promotion (validation). Analyzing prediction differences shows where versions disagree, not why the model decides as it does.","why_zh":"Shadow endpoint 將即時流量鏡像到候選變體，以在升級前比較預測/效能（驗證用途）。分析預測差異只顯示版本何處不一致，而非模型為何如此決策。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-configure-processing-jobs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-shapley-values.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-online-explainability.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor.html"]}},{"id":72,"question_en":"An ML engineer is using Amazon SageMaker to train a deep learning model that requires distributed training. After some training attempts, the ML engineer observes that the instances are not performing as expected. The ML engineer identifies communication overhead between the training instances. What should the ML engineer do to MINIMIZE the communication overhead between the instances?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师正在使用亚马逊 SageMaker 训练一个需要分布式训练的深度学习模型。经过几次 训练尝试后，该工程师发现实例的运行情况未达预期。工程师发现训练实例之间存在通信开销。 机器学习工程师应采取什么措施来最小化实例之间的通信开销？","options_en":{"A":"Place the instances in the same VPC subnet. Store the data in a different AWS Region from where the instances are deployed.","B":"Place the instances in the same VPC subnet but in different Availability Zones. Store the data in a different AWS Region from where the instances are deployed.","C":"Place the instances in the same VPC subnet. Store the data in the same AWS Region and Availability Zone where the instances are deployed.","D":"Place the instances in the same VPC subnet. Store the data in the same AWS Region but in a different Availability Zone from where the instances are deployed."},"options_zh":{"A":"将实例置于同一 VPC 子网中。将数据存储在与实例部署所在区域不同的 AWS 区域。","B":"将实例置于同一 VPC 子网但位于不同的可用区。将数据存储在与实例部署位置不同的 AWS 区 域。","C":"将实例置于同一 VPC 子网中。将数据存储在实例部署的同一 AWS 区域和可用区中。","D":"将实例置于同一 VPC 子网中。将数据存储在与实例部署位置不同的可用区，但位于同一 AWS 区域。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS's SageMaker distributed training guidance is explicit. Under 'Availability zones and network backplane' in the Get started with distributed training page, it states verbatim: 'To reduce communication overhead, make sure that you configure instances, VPC subnet, and data storage in the same AWS Region and Availability Zone.' Distributed data-parallel training runs collective operations such as AllReduce between the nodes of the compute cluster and transfers training data between the nodes and storage (Amazon S3 or Amazon FSx for Lustre), so colocating the compute instances, the VPC subnet, and the data in one Region and one AZ minimizes both inter-node and node-to-storage network latency. Option C is the only choice that aligns all three (instances, subnet, data) in the same Region and the same Availability Zone. EC2 cluster placement groups follow the same principle of packing tightly coupled instances within a single AZ for low-latency communication, reinforcing that spreading across AZs or Regions increases overhead.","explanation_zh":"AWS SageMaker 分散式訓練文件明確指出，在「Get started with distributed training」頁面的「Availability zones and network backplane」一節中逐字說明：「To reduce communication overhead, make sure that you configure instances, VPC subnet, and data storage in the same AWS Region and Availability Zone.」分散式 data-parallel 訓練會在 compute cluster 的節點之間執行 AllReduce 等 collective 運算，並在節點與儲存體（Amazon S3 或 Amazon FSx for Lustre）之間傳輸訓練資料，因此將運算 instances、VPC subnet 與資料同置於同一個 Region 與同一個 Availability Zone，可將節點之間以及節點到儲存體的網路延遲降到最低。選項 C 是唯一將三者（instances、subnet、data）全部對齊在相同 Region 與相同 AZ 的選項。EC2 cluster placement group 也遵循相同原則，將緊密耦合的 instances 集中在單一 AZ 內以達成低延遲通訊，這也佐證跨 AZ 或跨 Region 會增加 overhead。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Storing the data in a different AWS Region from the instances forces cross-Region data transfer, which adds significant latency and increases (not minimizes) communication overhead. It also leaves the AZ of the data unaligned with the instances, directly contradicting the AWS guidance to keep data in the same Region and AZ.","why_zh":"將資料存放在與 instances 不同的 AWS Region，會強制進行跨 Region 資料傳輸，造成顯著延遲並增加（而非減少）通訊 overhead；同時資料的 AZ 也未與 instances 對齊，直接違反 AWS 將資料保留在相同 Region 與 AZ 的指引。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This is the worst option: it tries to spread instances across different Availability Zones (which adds cross-AZ latency, and a single subnet lives in only one AZ anyway), and it stores data in a different Region (adding cross-Region latency). Both choices increase communication overhead, the opposite of the goal.","why_zh":"這是最差的選項：它嘗試將 instances 分散到不同的 Availability Zone（會增加跨 AZ 延遲，且單一 subnet 本來就只存在於一個 AZ），又將資料存放在不同的 Region（增加跨 Region 延遲），兩者都會增加通訊 overhead，與目標相反。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Keeping data in the same Region is good, but placing it in a different Availability Zone from the instances introduces cross-AZ network hops between the nodes and the data storage, increasing latency. The AWS docs explicitly say data storage should be in the same Region AND the same AZ as the instances.","why_zh":"將資料保留在相同 Region 是正確的，但放在與 instances 不同的 Availability Zone，會在節點與資料儲存體之間引入跨 AZ 的網路跳轉而增加延遲。AWS 文件明確指出資料儲存體應與 instances 位於相同 Region 且相同 AZ。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/distributed-training-get-started.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-parallel.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/placement-groups.html"]}},{"id":73,"question_en":"A company is running ML models on premises by using custom Python scripts and proprietary datasets. The company is using PyTorch. The model building requires unique domain knowledge. The company needs to move the models to AWS. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST effort?","question_zh":"该公司正在本地使用自定义的 Python 脚本和专有数据集运行机器学习模型，使用的框架是 PyTorch。模 型构建需要独特的领域知识。该公司需要将模型迁移到 AWS 上。 哪种解决方案能以最少的努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use SageMaker built-in algorithms to train the proprietary datasets.","B":"Use SageMaker script mode and premade images for ML frameworks.","C":"Build a container on AWS that includes custom packages and a choice of ML frameworks.","D":"Purchase similar production models through AWS Marketplace."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 SageMaker 内置算法对专有数据集进行训练。","B":"使用 SageMaker 脚本模式和预构建的机器学习框架镜像。","C":"在 AWS 上构建一个包含自定义软件包和可选机器学习框架的容器。","D":"通过 AWS 市场购买类似的生产模型。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The company already has working PyTorch training code (custom Python scripts) and proprietary datasets and wants to move to AWS with the LEAST effort. SageMaker script mode lets you supply your existing PyTorch entry-point script and run it inside an AWS-managed prebuilt PyTorch Deep Learning Container via the SageMaker Python SDK PyTorch estimator. AWS's container-scenarios decision tree states that for a 'Custom model with pre-built SageMaker AI container' using a framework that has a prebuilt image such as TensorFlow and PyTorch, you should 'Use the pre-built Docker image associated with your framework,' optionally adding a requirements.txt for extra packages. The PyTorch resources page reinforces this: you 'train and deploy a model using custom PyTorch code' with the SageMaker Python SDK PyTorch estimators and the prebuilt PyTorch container, which 'make writing a PyTorch script and running it in SageMaker AI easier.' This preserves the unique domain logic and proprietary data while requiring only minor adaptation of existing scripts and no container engineering or model rewriting, making B the least-effort solution.","explanation_zh":"公司已經有可運作的 PyTorch 訓練程式碼（自訂 Python 腳本）與專有資料集，並希望以最少工作量遷移到 AWS。SageMaker script mode 讓你直接提供既有的 PyTorch 進入點腳本，透過 SageMaker Python SDK 的 PyTorch estimator 在 AWS 託管的 prebuilt PyTorch Deep Learning Container 中執行。AWS 官方的容器情境決策樹明確指出：對於『使用具備 prebuilt container 之框架（如 TensorFlow 與 PyTorch）的自訂模型』，應『使用與你框架對應的 prebuilt Docker image』，必要時再加上 requirements.txt 安裝額外套件。PyTorch 資源頁也佐證此點：你可『使用自訂 PyTorch 程式碼來訓練與部署模型』，SageMaker Python SDK 的 PyTorch estimators 與 prebuilt PyTorch container 讓撰寫 PyTorch 腳本並在 SageMaker AI 執行更容易。如此可保留獨特的領域邏輯與專有資料，只需對既有腳本做少量調整，無需自行打造容器或重寫模型，因此 B 是工作量最少的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Built-in algorithms replace your model with AWS's prebuilt algorithm implementations. The company has custom PyTorch code embodying unique domain knowledge, so rewriting and retraining onto a built-in algorithm is high effort and would discard their existing model logic.","why_zh":"Built-in algorithms 會以 AWS 預建演算法取代你的模型。公司擁有蘊含獨特領域知識的自訂 PyTorch 程式碼，改用 built-in algorithm 等於重寫並丟棄既有模型邏輯，工作量很大。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Per the AWS decision tree, building your own container is the use case reserved for a custom framework that has no prebuilt image. PyTorch already has a prebuilt SageMaker container (and supports requirements.txt for extra packages), so building a custom container adds unnecessary Docker engineering and maintenance effort.","why_zh":"依 AWS 決策樹，自建容器是保留給『沒有 prebuilt image 的自訂框架』的情境。PyTorch 已有 SageMaker prebuilt container（且支援 requirements.txt 安裝額外套件），因此自建含自訂套件的容器會增加不必要的 Docker 工程與維運工作量。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Purchasing 'similar' models from AWS Marketplace abandons the company's proprietary datasets and unique domain knowledge; a marketplace model is not their model and would not meet their requirement to move their own models to AWS.","why_zh":"從 AWS Marketplace 購買『類似』模型等於放棄公司的專有資料集與獨特領域知識；Marketplace 模型並非他們自己的模型，無法滿足將自有模型遷移到 AWS 的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/docker-containers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/pre-built-containers-frameworks-deep-learning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/pytorch.html"]}},{"id":74,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon SageMaker and millions of files to train an ML model. Each file is several megabytes in size. The files are stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company needs to improve training performance. Which solution will meet these requirements in the LEAST amount of time?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用亚马逊 SageMaker 和数百万个文件来训练一个机器学习模型。每个文件的大小为数兆字 节。这些文件存储在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中。该公司需要提高训练性能。 哪种解决方案能在最短的时间内满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Transfer the data to a new S3 bucket that provides S3 Express One Zone storage. Adjust the training job to use the new S3 bucket.","B":"Create an Amazon FSx for Lustre file system. Link the file system to the existing S3 bucket. Adjust the training job to read from the file system.","C":"Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Transfer the existing data to the file system. Adjust the training job to read from the file system.","D":"Create an Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) cluster. Link the Redis OSS cluster to the existing S3 bucket. Stream the data from the Redis OSS cluster directly to the training job."},"options_zh":{"A":"将数据转移到提供 S3 Express One Zone 存储的新 S3 存储桶。调整训练作业以使用新的 S3 存储桶。","B":"创建一个 Amazon FSx for Lustre 文件系统。将该文件系统链接到现有的 S3 存储桶。调整训练作业以从该 文件系统读取数据。","C":"创建一个亚马逊弹性文件系统（Amazon EFS）文件系统。将现有数据传输到该文件系统。调整训练作业 以从该文件系统读取数据。","D":"创建一个 Amazon ElastiCache（Redis OSS）集群。将 Redis OSS 集群链接到现有的 S3 存储桶。将 Redis OSS 集群中的数据直接流式传输到训练作业。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario is millions of multi-MB files already sitting in S3, and the goal is to improve SageMaker training performance in the LEAST amount of time. Amazon FSx for Lustre is AWS's purpose-built high-performance file system for ML training: the SageMaker doc 'Choosing an input mode and a storage unit' states that when a dataset is too large for file mode or has many files, FSx for Lustre 'scales to hundreds of gigabytes per second (GB/s) of throughput and millions of IOPS,' which is ideal here. The decisive 'least time' factor is that FSx for Lustre can be LINKED to the existing S3 bucket via a data repository association (DRA): only file/directory metadata is imported and object data is loaded lazily on first access, so you do not have to physically copy the millions of files before starting training. SageMaker natively consumes the file system as a data input channel via FileSystemInput / FileSystemDataSource ('FSxLustre'). This is faster to stand up than option A (which requires copying all data into a new S3 Express One Zone directory bucket) and option C (which explicitly requires transferring the existing data into EFS first), and option D is technically invalid.","explanation_zh":"情境是 S3 中已存放數百萬個各為數 MB 的檔案,目標是以最短時間提升 SageMaker 訓練效能。Amazon FSx for Lustre 是 AWS 專為 ML 訓練打造的高效能檔案系統:SageMaker 文件「Choosing an input mode and a storage unit」指出,當資料集過大不適合 file mode、或含有大量檔案時,FSx for Lustre 可「擴展到每秒數百 GB 的吞吐量與數百萬 IOPS」,正適合此情境。關鍵的「最短時間」因素在於 FSx for Lustre 可透過 data repository association (DRA) 直接「連結」到現有的 S3 bucket:只匯入檔案/目錄的 metadata,物件資料在首次存取時才以 lazy load 方式載入,因此無需在開始訓練前先實際搬移數百萬個檔案。SageMaker 透過 FileSystemInput / FileSystemDataSource(「FSxLustre」)原生將該檔案系統作為 data input channel。相較於選項 A(需先把所有資料複製到新的 S3 Express One Zone directory bucket)與選項 C(明確要求先把現有資料搬移到 EFS),此作法部署更快;選項 D 在技術上不成立。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 Express One Zone improves request latency, but this approach requires physically transferring (copying) millions of files into a new directory bucket before training can use it, which is a significant up-front time cost. S3 Express One Zone is optimized for high-request-rate, latency-sensitive small-object access rather than the high-throughput sequential/random training data-loading that FSx for Lustre delivers, and it is not the AWS-recommended high-throughput training data source for this profile.","why_zh":"S3 Express One Zone 可降低請求延遲,但此方案需先把數百萬個檔案實際搬移(複製)到新的 directory bucket 後訓練才能使用,前置時間成本很高。S3 Express One Zone 針對高請求速率、低延遲的小物件存取最佳化,而非 FSx for Lustre 所提供的高吞吐訓練資料載入,且非 AWS 對此情境建議的高吞吐訓練資料來源。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This option explicitly requires transferring the existing data into the EFS file system first, so it does not save the upfront copy time. Per the SageMaker best-practices doc, Amazon EFS is positioned for cases where the dataset already lives in EFS (e.g., from preprocessing/annotation), not as the optimized high-throughput choice for S3-resident training data; FSx for Lustre is the recommended option for large datasets with many files.","why_zh":"此選項明確要求先把現有資料搬移到 EFS 檔案系統,因此並未省下前置複製時間。依 SageMaker 最佳實務文件,Amazon EFS 適用於資料原本就存在 EFS 的情境(例如前處理/標註產生),並非針對存放於 S3 的訓練資料的高吞吐最佳選擇;FSx for Lustre 才是大型、多檔案資料集的建議選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) is an in-memory key-value cache. It cannot be 'linked' to an S3 bucket, and SageMaker training jobs cannot stream file objects directly from a Redis cluster as a data input channel. This option is technically invalid for loading millions of multi-MB training files.","why_zh":"Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) 是記憶體內的鍵值快取。它無法被「連結」到 S3 bucket,SageMaker 訓練作業也無法把 Redis cluster 當作 data input channel 直接串流檔案物件。對於載入數百萬個數 MB 的訓練檔案,此選項在技術上不成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-access-training-data-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-access-training-data-fsx.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/LustreGuide/create-dra-linked-data-repo.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/LustreGuide/overview-dra-data-repo.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/LustreGuide/fsx-data-repositories.html"]}},{"id":75,"question_en":"A company wants to develop an ML model by using tabular data from its customers. The data contains meaningful ordered features with sensitive information that should not be discarded. An ML engineer must ensure that the sensitive data is masked before another team starts to build the model. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望利用其客户的表格数据开发一个机器学习模型。这些数据包含有意义的有序特征，其中包含 不应丢弃的敏感信息。机器学习工程师必须确保在另一个团队开始构建模型之前，对敏感数据进行屏蔽处 理。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Made to categorize the sensitive data.","B":"Prepare the data by using AWS Glue DataBrew.","C":"Run an AWS Batch job to change the sensitive data to random values.","D":"Run an Amazon EMR job to change the sensitive data to random values."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用亚马逊的 Made to 服务对敏感数据进行分类。","B":"使用 AWS Glue DataBrew 准备数据。","C":"运行一个 AWS Batch 作业将敏感数据更改为随机值。","D":"运行一个 Amazon EMR 作业，将敏感数据更改为随机值。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to MASK sensitive data (not discard it) while preserving the meaningful ordered features, and to do so before another team builds the model. AWS Glue DataBrew is a visual, serverless data-preparation tool with purpose-built PII data-masking recipe steps (substitution, shuffling, deterministic/probabilistic encryption, masking out, hashing, nulling). The DataBrew PII docs explicitly frame this exact scenario: when you build analytic functions or ML models you need safeguards so that data analysts and data scientists who use the dataset cannot see individuals' PII. These transforms obfuscate the sensitive values in place during data prep without removing the columns, and order-preserving techniques such as deterministic encryption (which always produces the same ciphertext for a given value) keep the ordered features consistent and meaningful. This satisfies 'mask the sensitive data before another team builds the model' with the least operational effort. The other options either only detect/categorize sensitive data (Macie) or destroy the meaningful ordering by replacing values with random data (Batch/EMR).","explanation_zh":"需求是要對敏感資料進行遮罩 (mask)，而非丟棄，同時保留具意義的有序特徵 (meaningful ordered features)，並在另一團隊建立模型之前完成。AWS Glue DataBrew 是視覺化、無伺服器的資料準備工具，內建專門的 PII 資料遮罩 recipe 步驟 (替換 substitution、洗牌 shuffling、確定性/機率性加密 deterministic/probabilistic encryption、遮蔽 masking out、雜湊 hashing、置空 nulling)。DataBrew 的 PII 官方文件明確描述了此情境：當你建立分析函式或 ML 模型時，需要安全防護，讓使用該資料集的資料分析師與資料科學家無法看到個人的 PII。這些轉換會在資料準備過程中就地混淆敏感值而不刪除欄位，而確定性加密 (對同一值永遠產生相同密文) 等保留順序的方法可讓有序特徵維持一致且有意義。這最直接且操作負擔最低地滿足了「在另一團隊建立模型前遮罩敏感資料」的要求。其他選項要嘛只是偵測/分類敏感資料 (Macie)，要嘛用隨機值取代而破壞有意義的順序 (Batch/EMR)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Macie (the option's 'Amazon Made' is a typo) only discovers and classifies/categorizes sensitive data in Amazon S3 and produces findings; it does not mask, redact, or transform the data, so the masking requirement is unmet.","why_zh":"Amazon Macie (選項拼為 'Amazon Made') 只能在 Amazon S3 中發現並分類敏感資料並產生 findings，無法遮罩、修訂或轉換資料，因此無法滿足遮罩需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Changing sensitive data to random values via an AWS Batch job destroys the meaningful order of the ordered features and adds significant custom-code operational overhead; the ordered relationship is effectively discarded/unusable, violating the 'meaningful ordered features should not be discarded' constraint.","why_zh":"用 AWS Batch 作業把敏感資料改為隨機值會破壞有序特徵的意義，並需大量自訂程式碼帶來高操作負擔；有序關係等同被丟棄而不可用，違反「有意義的有序特徵不應丟棄」的限制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same flaw as C: replacing values with random data in an Amazon EMR job breaks the meaningful ordering and is high-effort/custom; it does not 'mask' while preserving the features that must not be discarded.","why_zh":"與 C 相同的缺陷：在 Amazon EMR 作業中以隨機值取代會破壞有意義的順序，且需高度自訂、負擔大；它不是在保留不可丟棄特徵的前提下進行遮罩。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/databrew/latest/dg/personal-information-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/databrew/latest/dg/recipe-actions.pii.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/databrew/latest/dg/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html"]}},{"id":76,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to deploy ML models to get inferences from large datasets in an asynchronous manner. The ML engineer also needs to implement scheduled monitoring of the data quality of the models. The ML engineer must receive alerts when changes in data quality occur. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"机器学习工程师需要以异步方式部署机器学习模型，以便从大型数据集中获取推断结果。该工程师还需 要实现对模型数据质量的定期监控，并在数据质量发生变化时收到警报。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the models by using scheduled AWS Glue jobs. Use Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor the data quality and to send alerts.","B":"Deploy the models by using scheduled AWS Batch jobs. Use AWS CloudTrail to monitor the data quality and to send alerts.","C":"Deploy the models by using Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) on AWS Fargate. Use Amazon EventBridge to monitor the data quality and to send alerts.","D":"Deploy the models by using Amazon SageMaker batch transform. Use SageMaker Model Monitor to monitor the data quality and to send alerts."},"options_zh":{"A":"通过使用计划的 AWS Glue 作业部署模型。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 警报来监控数据质量并发送 警报。","B":"通过使用计划的 AWS Batch 作业部署模型。使用 AWS CloudTrail 监控数据质量并发送警报。","C":"使用 AWS Fargate 上的 Amazon Elastic Container Service （Amazon ECS） 部署模型。使用 Amazon EventBridge 监控数据质量并发送警报。","D":"使用 Amazon SageMaker 批量转换部署模型。利用 SageMaker 模型监控器监控数据质量并发送警报。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are (1) asynchronous inference on large datasets, (2) scheduled data quality monitoring, and (3) alerts when data quality changes. Amazon SageMaker batch transform is the purpose-built feature for getting inferences from large datasets without a persistent endpoint; it automatically distributes the workload across compute instances and processes data in batches asynchronously. SageMaker Model Monitor supports scheduled (cron-based) data quality monitoring via CreateMonitoringSchedule, and the docs explicitly state you can create a monitoring schedule for a real-time endpoint or a batch transform job. Each scheduled processing job compares the current dataset to your baseline statistics and constraints, generates a violations report, and emits CloudWatch metrics per feature (enable_cloudwatch_metrics=True), which you can wire to CloudWatch alarms/SNS to alert on data-quality drift. Only option D natively delivers all three requirements as a managed, integrated SageMaker solution.","explanation_zh":"需求為 (1) 對大型資料集進行非同步推論、(2) 排程式的資料品質監控、(3) 在資料品質改變時發出警示。Amazon SageMaker batch transform 正是專為從大型資料集取得推論而設計的功能，不需要常駐 endpoint，會自動將工作負載分散到多個運算執行個體，以批次方式非同步處理資料。SageMaker Model Monitor 透過 CreateMonitoringSchedule 支援排程式（cron）的資料品質監控，官方文件明確說明可為 real-time endpoint 或 batch transform job 建立 monitoring schedule。每個排程的 processing job 會將目前資料集與 baseline 統計與 constraints 比較、產生 violations 報告，並針對每個 feature 發出 CloudWatch metrics（enable_cloudwatch_metrics=True），可串接 CloudWatch alarms/SNS 在資料品質 drift 時發出警示。只有選項 D 以受管、整合的 SageMaker 方案原生滿足全部三項需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Glue is a serverless ETL service for data integration, not an ML model inference/deployment service; CloudWatch alarms alone only threshold on emitted metrics and cannot perform statistical data-quality monitoring against a trained baseline the way Model Monitor does.","why_zh":"AWS Glue 是用於資料整合的無伺服器 ETL 服務，並非 ML 模型推論/部署服務；單靠 CloudWatch 警報只能對既有指標設定門檻，無法像 Model Monitor 那樣對訓練 baseline 進行統計式資料品質監控。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Batch can run containerized compute jobs but is not a managed ML inference service; AWS CloudTrail records API/management-event audit logs and cannot monitor data quality or detect data drift, so this option fails the monitoring requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Batch 可執行容器化的運算工作但非受管 ML 推論服務；AWS CloudTrail 記錄的是 API/管理事件的稽核日誌，無法監控資料品質或偵測資料漂移，因此無法滿足監控需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon ECS on Fargate would require building custom inference serving and monitoring logic; Amazon EventBridge is an event-routing/scheduling service with no built-in data-quality drift detection, so it cannot natively monitor model data quality or alert on data-quality changes.","why_zh":"Amazon ECS on Fargate 需自行建置推論服務與監控邏輯；Amazon EventBridge 是事件路由/排程服務，沒有內建的資料品質漂移偵測，無法原生監控模型資料品質或在資料品質改變時發出警示。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/batch-transform.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-scheduling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-data-quality.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor.html"]}},{"id":77,"question_en":"An ML engineer normalized training data by using min-max normalization in AWS Glue DataBrew. The ML engineer must normalize the production inference data in the same way as the training data before passing the production inference data to the model for predictions. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"","options_en":{"A":"Apply statistics from a well-known dataset to normalize the production samples.","B":"Keep the min-max normalization statistics from the training set. Use these values to normalize the production samples.","C":"Calculate a new set of min-max normalization statistics from a batch of production samples. Use these values to normalize all the production samples.","D":"Calculate a new set of min-max normalization statistics from each production sample. Use these values to normalize all the production samples."},"options_zh":{},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Min-max normalization rescales a feature with x' = (x - min) / (max - min), where min and max are statistics fit on the training data. To guarantee that production inference data lands on exactly the same scale the model was trained on, you must apply the identical transformation, which means persisting and reusing the same min and max values computed from the training set. Recomputing statistics from production data (whether per-batch or per-sample) shifts the scale of features and produces a different mapping than the model saw during training, causing training-serving skew and degraded, inconsistent predictions. The AWS Well-Architected Machine Learning Lens (MLREL03-BP02 'Verify feature consistency across training and inference') explicitly lists 'recreating feature transformations separately for training and inference pipelines' as a common anti-pattern, states the objective is 'reducing the training-serving skew by keeping feature consistency between training and inference,' and requires that both training and inference paths use the same feature definitions and transformations. Therefore, keeping the training-set min-max statistics and using them to normalize production samples (option B) is the only correct approach.","explanation_zh":"Min-max normalization 使用公式 x' = (x - min) / (max - min) 重新縮放特徵，其中 min 和 max 是在訓練資料上擬合出的統計值。為了確保生產推論資料落在模型訓練時所用的相同尺度上，必須套用完全相同的轉換，也就是保存並重複使用從訓練集計算出的同一組 min 與 max 值。若從生產資料重新計算統計值（不論是每批次或每個樣本），都會改變特徵的縮放方式，產生與模型訓練時不同的映射，導致 training-serving skew（訓練與服務偏移），使預測結果不一致且品質下降。AWS Well-Architected Machine Learning Lens（MLREL03-BP02「Verify feature consistency across training and inference」）明確將「在訓練與推論管線中各自重建特徵轉換」列為常見反模式，並指出目標是「透過維持訓練與推論之間的特徵一致性來降低 training-serving skew」，同時要求訓練與推論兩條路徑都使用相同的特徵定義與轉換。因此，保留訓練集的 min-max 統計值並用其正規化生產樣本（選項 B）是唯一正確的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Statistics from an unrelated well-known dataset have no relationship to the model's training distribution, so applying them produces a scale the model never learned and yields meaningless predictions.","why_zh":"來自無關的知名資料集的統計值與模型的訓練分佈毫無關係，套用後會產生模型從未學過的尺度，導致預測無意義。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Recomputing min-max from a production batch creates new min/max values that differ from the training set, so the same raw value maps to a different normalized value, introducing training-serving skew and inconsistent predictions.","why_zh":"從生產批次重新計算 min-max 會產生與訓練集不同的 min/max 值，使同一原始值映射到不同的正規化值，造成 training-serving skew 與預測不一致。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Computing min-max from each single sample is mathematically degenerate (a single value has min=max, giving division by zero or a constant) and bears no relation to the training scale, so it cannot reproduce the training-time transformation.","why_zh":"從每個單一樣本計算 min-max 在數學上是退化的（單一值的 min=max，會導致除以零或常數），且與訓練尺度無關，無法重現訓練時的轉換。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/machine-learning-lens/mlrel03-bp02.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/machine-learning-lens/mlops06-bp01.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/feature-store.html"]}},{"id":78,"question_en":"A company is planning to use Amazon SageMaker to make classification ratings that are based on images. The company has 6 TB of training data that is stored on an Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP system virtual machine (SVM). The SVM is in the same VPC as SageMaker. An ML engineer must make the training data accessible for ML models that are in the SageMaker environment. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司计划使用亚马逊 SageMaker 基于图像进行分类评级。该公司有 6TB 的训练数据存储在亚马逊 FSx for NetApp ONTAP 系统虚拟机（SVM）上。该 SVM 与 SageMaker 处于同一虚拟私有云（VPC） 中。 机器学习工程师必须让训练数据能够被 SageMaker 环境中的机器学习模型访问。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Mount the FSx for ONTAP file system as a volume to the SageMaker Instance.","B":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Use Mountpoint for Amazon S3 to link the S3 bucket to the FSx for ONTAP file system.","C":"Create a catalog connection from SageMaker Data Wrangler to the FSx for ONTAP file system.","D":"Create a direct connection from SageMaker Data Wrangler to the FSx for ONTAP file system."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 FSx for ONTAP 文件系统挂载为卷到 SageMaker 实例上。","B":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。使用 Amazon S3 的挂载点将 S3 存储桶链接到 FSx for ONTAP 文 件系统。","C":"从 SageMaker Data Wrangler 到 FSx for ONTAP 文件系统创建目录连接。","D":"从 SageMaker Data Wrangler 直接连接到 FSx for ONTAP 文件系统。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP exposes its data through a storage virtual machine (SVM) over standard NFS, SMB, iSCSI, and NVMe protocols, and AWS documents mounting ONTAP volumes on Linux compute clients that sit in the same VPC as the file system. Because the SVM is already in the same VPC as the SageMaker environment, a SageMaker (Linux) instance can directly mount the ONTAP volume as a file system volume via the SVM's NFS endpoint (for example, sudo mount -t nfs svm-dns-name:/volume-junction-path /fsx), making the 6 TB of image training data immediately accessible to the ML models with the least operational overhead. This native file-mount pattern is the canonical access method documented for FSx for ONTAP. The other options describe features that do not exist or do not apply: Mountpoint for Amazon S3 mounts an S3 bucket as a local file system and provides no way to 'link' an S3 bucket to an ONTAP file system, and SageMaker Data Wrangler has no FSx for ONTAP connector (its sources are S3, Athena, Redshift, EMR, Databricks, Salesforce Data Cloud, Snowflake, and other SaaS platforms) and is built for tabular data preparation rather than serving bulk image training data.","explanation_zh":"Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP 透過 storage virtual machine (SVM) 以標準 NFS、SMB、iSCSI 與 NVMe 通訊協定提供資料存取，且 AWS 文件記載可在與檔案系統位於同一 VPC 的 Linux 運算用戶端上掛載 ONTAP volume。由於 SVM 與 SageMaker 環境已位於同一個 VPC，SageMaker(Linux)執行個體可以直接透過 SVM 的 NFS 端點將 ONTAP volume 掛載為檔案系統 volume(例如 sudo mount -t nfs svm-dns-name:/volume-junction-path /fsx)，讓 6 TB 的影像訓練資料立即可供 ML 模型使用，且作業負擔最低。此原生檔案掛載方式正是 FSx for ONTAP 文件所記載的標準存取方法。其他選項所述功能皆不存在或不適用:Mountpoint for Amazon S3 是將 S3 儲存貯體掛載為本機檔案系統，並無法把 S3 儲存貯體「連結」到 ONTAP 檔案系統;SageMaker Data Wrangler 並沒有連到 FSx for ONTAP 的連接器(其來源為 S3、Athena、Redshift、EMR、Databricks、Salesforce Data Cloud、Snowflake 及其他 SaaS 平台)，且其設計用於表格資料準備，而非為訓練提供大量影像資料。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Mountpoint for Amazon S3 mounts an S3 bucket as a local file system on a client; it provides no mechanism to 'link' an S3 bucket to an FSx for ONTAP file system. The 6 TB of training data already lives on ONTAP, not S3, so creating a bucket and using Mountpoint is a fabricated, non-functional pairing that adds steps without making the ONTAP data accessible.","why_zh":"Mountpoint for Amazon S3 是在用戶端把 S3 儲存貯體掛載為本機檔案系統，並沒有將 S3 儲存貯體「連結」到 FSx for ONTAP 檔案系統的機制。6 TB 的訓練資料原本就在 ONTAP 上而非 S3，因此建立貯體再用 Mountpoint 是虛構且無法運作的組合，只會增加步驟卻無法讓 ONTAP 資料可被存取。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SageMaker Data Wrangler does not offer a 'catalog connection' to FSx for ONTAP. Per the AWS import documentation its sources are S3, Athena, Redshift, EMR, Databricks (JDBC), Salesforce Data Cloud, Snowflake, and other SaaS platforms. Data Wrangler also targets tabular data preparation, not 6 TB of image training data, so it does not fit the requirement of making files accessible to ML models.","why_zh":"SageMaker Data Wrangler 並未提供連到 FSx for ONTAP 的 'catalog connection'。依 AWS 匯入文件，其來源為 S3、Athena、Redshift、EMR、Databricks (JDBC)、Salesforce Data Cloud、Snowflake 及其他 SaaS 平台。Data Wrangler 也是用於表格資料準備，而非 6 TB 的影像訓練資料，因此不符合讓檔案可供 ML 模型存取的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Like option C, there is no native 'direct connection' from Data Wrangler to FSx for ONTAP; this connector is not in Data Wrangler's documented source list. Data Wrangler is designed for tabular feature engineering rather than serving image data to training jobs, so it cannot mount or directly expose the ONTAP volume to the ML models.","why_zh":"與選項 C 相同，Data Wrangler 並沒有連到 FSx for ONTAP 的原生 'direct connection';此連接器不在 Data Wrangler 文件所列的來源中。Data Wrangler 是為表格特徵工程設計，而非為訓練工作提供影像資料，因此無法掛載或直接把 ONTAP volume 提供給 ML 模型。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/attach-linux-client.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/how-it-works-fsx-ontap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/supported-fsx-clients.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler-import.html"]}},{"id":79,"question_en":"A company regularly receives new training data from the vendor of an ML model. The vendor delivers cleaned and prepared data to the company's Amazon S3 bucket every 3-4 days. The company has an Amazon SageMaker pipeline to retrain the model. An ML engineer needs to implement a solution to run the pipeline when new data is uploaded to the S3 bucket. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司定期从其机器学习模型的供应商处接收新的训练数据。供应商每 3 至 4 天就会将清理和 准备好的数据交付到该公司的亚马逊 S3 存储桶中。 该公司有一个用于重新训练模型的 Amazon SageMaker 管道。一位机器学习工程师需要实现一 个解决方案，以便在新数据上传到 S3 存储桶时运行该管道。 哪种解决方案能以最少的操作努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 Lifecycle rule to transfer the data to the SageMaker training instance and to initiate training.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function that scans the S3 bucket. Program the Lambda function to initiate the pipeline when new data is uploaded.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that has an event pattern that matches the S3 upload. Configure the pipeline as the target of the rule.","D":"Use Amazon Managed Workflows for Apache Airflow (Amazon MWAA) to orchestrate the pipeline when new data is uploaded."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 S3 生命周期规则，将数据传输到 SageMaker 训练实例并启动训练。","B":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来扫描 S3 存储桶。编写该 Lambda 函数，使其在有新数据上传时启动管 道。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则的事件模式与 S3 上传相匹配。将管道配置为该规则的 目标。","D":"当有新数据上传时，使用亚马逊托管的 Apache Airflow 工作流（Amazon MWAA）来编排管道。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is LEAST operational effort. Amazon S3 can send 'Object Created' events directly to Amazon EventBridge (no polling or Lambda needed once EventBridge is enabled on the bucket), and Amazon SageMaker Pipelines is natively supported as an EventBridge target. The SageMaker documentation explicitly states that pipeline executions can be initiated by events including 'a new file being uploaded to your Amazon S3 bucket', and that the StartPipelineExecution action is the one automatically initiated. So you create a single EventBridge rule whose event pattern matches the S3 upload and set the pipeline as the target. This is a fully managed, serverless, event-driven integration with no custom code, no polling, and no infrastructure to operate, which is the least operational effort.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定條件是「最少維運工作量」(LEAST operational effort)。Amazon S3 可以將 'Object Created' 事件直接傳送到 Amazon EventBridge（在 bucket 上啟用 EventBridge 後，無需輪詢或 Lambda），而 Amazon SageMaker Pipelines 原生支援作為 EventBridge 的 target。SageMaker 官方文件明確指出 pipeline 執行可由多種事件觸發，其中包含「新檔案上傳到您的 Amazon S3 bucket」，且自動啟動的動作為 StartPipelineExecution。因此只需建立一條 EventBridge rule，使其 event pattern 符合 S3 上傳事件，並將 pipeline 設為 target 即可。這是完全託管、無伺服器、事件驅動的整合，無需自訂程式碼、無需輪詢、也無需維運基礎設施，是維運工作量最少的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An S3 Lifecycle rule only transitions objects between storage classes (e.g., to S3 Glacier) or expires/deletes them. It cannot transfer data to a training instance or initiate SageMaker training. This option misuses the feature entirely.","why_zh":"S3 Lifecycle rule 只能在儲存類別之間轉換物件（例如轉到 S3 Glacier）或讓物件到期/刪除，它無法把資料傳到訓練執行個體，也無法啟動 SageMaker 訓練。此選項完全誤用了該功能。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A Lambda function that scans (polls) the bucket requires writing, deploying, and maintaining custom code plus a scheduling mechanism, and polling is wasteful and laggy. Even an event-triggered Lambda would add an unnecessary intermediary, because EventBridge can target the pipeline directly, so the Lambda is more operational overhead.","why_zh":"用 Lambda 去掃描（輪詢）bucket 需要撰寫、部署並維護自訂程式碼，還要加上排程機制，輪詢既浪費又有延遲。即使是事件觸發的 Lambda 也只是多了一個不必要的中介，因為 EventBridge 可以直接以 pipeline 為 target，因此 Lambda 反而增加維運負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon MWAA (managed Airflow) is a full orchestration environment requiring you to provision, size, and maintain an Airflow environment and author DAGs. That is far more operational effort than a single EventBridge rule for a simple 'run pipeline on upload' trigger.","why_zh":"Amazon MWAA（託管 Airflow）是完整的編排環境，需要佈建、調整大小並維護 Airflow 環境並撰寫 DAG。對於單純的「上傳即執行 pipeline」觸發來說，這比單一條 EventBridge rule 的維運工作量大得多。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/pipeline-eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventBridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventNotifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-events-rule-sagemakerpipelineparameters.html"]}},{"id":80,"question_en":"An ML engineer is developing a fraud detection model by using the Amazon SageMaker XGBoost algorithm. The model classifies transactions as either fraudulent or legitimate. During testing, the model excels at identifying fraud in the training dataset. However, the model is inefficient at identifying fraud in new and unseen transactions. What should the ML engineer do to improve the fraud detection for new transactions?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师正在使用亚马逊 SageMaker 的 XGBoost 算法开发一个欺诈检测模型。该模型 将交易分类为欺诈交易或合法交易。 在测试过程中，该模型在识别训练数据集中的欺诈行为方面表现出色。然而，该模型在识别新的、 未曾见过的交易中的欺诈行为方面效率低下。 机器学习工程师应该采取什么措施来提高对新交易的欺诈检测能力？","options_en":{"A":"Increase the learning rate.","B":"Remove some irrelevant features from the training dataset.","C":"Increase the value of the max_depth hyperparameter.","D":"Decrease the value of the max_depth hyperparameter."},"options_zh":{"A":"提高学习率。","B":"从训练数据集中移除一些不相关的特征。","C":"增大 max_depth 超参数的值。","D":"减小 max_depth 超参数的值。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This scenario is a textbook description of overfitting: the SageMaker XGBoost model performs excellently on the training dataset but generalizes poorly to new, unseen transactions. The AWS Model Fit documentation defines overfitting as when a model 'performs well on the training data but does not perform well on the evaluation data' because it is 'memorizing the data it has seen and is unable to generalize to unseen examples,' and prescribes reducing model flexibility/complexity as the remedy. The SageMaker XGBoost hyperparameters reference states that max_depth is the 'Maximum depth of a tree. Increasing this value makes the model more complex and likely to be overfit.' Therefore DECREASING max_depth lowers tree complexity, makes the model more conservative, and is the most direct, XGBoost-specific, documentation-backed fix to improve generalization to new transactions.","explanation_zh":"此情境是典型的過度擬合 (overfitting) 描述：SageMaker XGBoost 模型在訓練資料集上表現極佳，但對新的、未見過的交易泛化能力差。AWS Model Fit 文件將 overfitting 定義為模型「在訓練資料上表現良好，但在評估資料上表現不佳」，原因是模型「記憶了已看過的資料，無法泛化到未見過的範例」，並指出補救方法是降低模型彈性/複雜度。SageMaker XGBoost 超參數參考文件指出 max_depth 是「樹的最大深度。增加此值會使模型更複雜且更容易過度擬合」。因此「降低」max_depth 可減少樹的複雜度、使模型更保守，是最直接、針對 XGBoost、且有官方文件依據的修正方法，能改善對新交易的泛化能力。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Increasing the learning rate (eta) makes the boosting process LESS conservative. The SageMaker XGBoost doc says eta is the 'Step size shrinkage used in updates to prevent overfitting' and 'shrinks the feature weights to make the boosting process more conservative.' Raising eta moves in the wrong direction and tends to worsen, not fix, overfitting.","why_zh":"提高學習率 (eta) 會使提升 (boosting) 過程更不保守。SageMaker XGBoost 文件指出 eta 是「用於更新以防止過度擬合的步長收縮」並「縮小特徵權重以使 boosting 過程更保守」。提高 eta 方向相反，反而會加劇而非修正過度擬合。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Feature selection is a valid overfitting remedy in the AWS Model Fit doc, but this option specifically says removing IRRELEVANT features. Tree-based XGBoost already largely ignores irrelevant features via split gain, so removing them mainly reduces noise/dimensionality and is an indirect, weaker fix. It does not directly target the documented driver of XGBoost overfitting (excessive tree depth/complexity) the way decreasing max_depth does, and the question explicitly frames the choice around max_depth.","why_zh":"特徵選擇在 AWS Model Fit 文件中是有效的過度擬合補救方法，但此選項特指移除「不相關 (irrelevant)」的特徵。基於樹的 XGBoost 在分裂增益時已大致忽略不相關特徵，移除它們主要是降低雜訊/維度，屬於間接且較弱的修正。它不像降低 max_depth 那樣直接針對 XGBoost 過度擬合的文件記載成因（樹深度/複雜度過高），且題目明確將選擇聚焦於 max_depth。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the exact opposite of the correct fix. The SageMaker XGBoost doc explicitly states that increasing max_depth 'makes the model more complex and likely to be overfit,' which would make generalization to new transactions even worse.","why_zh":"這與正確修正完全相反。SageMaker XGBoost 文件明確指出增加 max_depth「使模型更複雜且更容易過度擬合」，這會使對新交易的泛化能力更差。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/xgboost_hyperparameters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/latest/dg/model-fit-underfitting-vs-overfitting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/xgboost-tuning.html"]}},{"id":81,"question_en":"A company has a binary classification model in production. An ML engineer needs to develop a new version of the model. The new model version must maximize correct predictions of positive labels and negative labels. The ML engineer must use a metric to recalibrate the model to meet these requirements. Which metric should the ML engineer use for the model recalibration?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用一个二分类模型。一位机器学习工程师需要开发该模型的新版本。 新模型版本必须最大限度地提高对正标签和负标签的正确预测。机器学习工程师必须使用一种度量标准来 重新校准模型以满足这些要求。 机器学习工程师应该使用哪种指标来重新校准模型？","options_en":{"A":"Accuracy","B":"Precision","C":"Recall","D":"Specificity"},"options_zh":{"A":"准确性","B":"精度","C":"回忆","D":"特异性"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to maximize correct predictions of BOTH positive labels (true positives) AND negative labels (true negatives). Per AWS documentation, Accuracy (ACC) measures the fraction of correct predictions overall, computed as (TP + TN) / (TP + TN + FP + FN). It is the only listed metric that simultaneously rewards correctly classifying both the positive and negative classes. The same AWS docs define Precision as the fraction of actual positives among examples predicted positive (TP / (TP + FP)) and Recall as the fraction of actual positives predicted positive (TP / (TP + FN)); both focus exclusively on the positive class and ignore true negatives. Specificity (TN / (TN + FP)) focuses only on the negative class. Therefore Accuracy is the correct metric to recalibrate the model so it maximizes correct predictions for both positive and negative labels.","explanation_zh":"需求是要同時最大化正確預測 positive labels(true positives)與 negative labels(true negatives)。根據 AWS 文件,Accuracy(ACC)衡量整體正確預測的比例,計算為 (TP + TN) / (TP + TN + FP + FN),是所列選項中唯一同時獎勵正確分類 positive 與 negative 兩個類別的指標。同一份 AWS 文件將 Precision 定義為在被預測為 positive 的樣本中實際為 positive 的比例(TP / (TP + FP)),將 Recall 定義為實際 positive 中被預測為 positive 的比例(TP / (TP + FN));兩者都只聚焦於 positive 類別並忽略 true negatives。Specificity(TN / (TN + FP))則只聚焦於 negative 類別。因此 Accuracy 是用來重新校準模型、同時最大化 positive 與 negative labels 正確預測的正確指標。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Precision = TP / (TP + FP) measures only how many of the predicted-positive examples are actually positive. It evaluates the positive class only and ignores true negatives, so it does not maximize correct negative-label predictions and fails the both-classes requirement.","why_zh":"Precision = TP / (TP + FP) 只衡量被預測為 positive 的樣本中實際為 positive 的比例。它只評估 positive 類別,忽略 true negatives,因此無法最大化 negative labels 的正確預測,不符合同時涵蓋兩個類別的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Recall (sensitivity) = TP / (TP + FN) measures only the fraction of actual positives that are correctly predicted. It concerns the positive class only and disregards negative-label correctness (true negatives) entirely.","why_zh":"Recall(sensitivity)= TP / (TP + FN) 只衡量實際 positive 中被正確預測的比例。它只關注 positive 類別,完全不考慮 negative labels 的正確性(true negatives)。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Specificity = TN / (TN + FP) is the true negative rate. It captures only correct negative predictions and ignores positive-label correctness (true positives), so it optimizes only the negative class, not both.","why_zh":"Specificity = TN / (TN + FP) 是 true negative rate,只反映 negative 預測的正確性,忽略 positive labels 的正確性(true positives),因此只最佳化 negative 類別而非兩者。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/latest/dg/binary-model-insights.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/latest/dg/binary-classification.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-accuracy-evaluation.html"]}},{"id":82,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon SageMaker to create ML models. The company's data scientists need fine- grained control of the ML workflows that they orchestrate. The data scientists also need the ability to visualize SageMaker jobs and workflows as a directed acyclic graph (DAG). The data scientists must keep a running history of model discovery experiments and must establish model governance for auditing and compliance verifications. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用亚马逊 SageMaker 来创建机器学习模型。该公司的数据科学家需要对其编排的机器学 习工作流进行精细控制。数据科学家还需要具备以下能力： 将 SageMaker 作业和工作流可视化为有向无环图（DAG）。数据科学家必须保留模型发现实验的运行 历史记录，并且必须建立模型治理机制以进行审计和合规性验证。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CodePipeline and its integration with SageMaker Studio to manage the entire ML workflows. Use SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking for the running history of experiments and for auditing and compliance verifications.","B":"Use AWS CodePipeline and its integration with SageMaker Experiments to manage the entire ML workflows. Use SageMaker Experiments for the running history of experiments and for auditing and compliance verifications.","C":"Use SageMaker Pipelines and its integration with SageMaker Studio to manage the entire ML workflows. Use SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking for the running history of experiments and for auditing and compliance verifications.","D":"Use SageMaker Pipelines and its integration with SageMaker Experiments to manage the entire ML workflows. Use SageMaker Experiments for the running history of experiments and for auditing and compliance verifications."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 及其与 SageMaker Studio 的集成来管理整个机器学习工作流。使用 SageMaker ML 血统跟踪来记录实验的运行历史，并用于审计和合规性验证。","B":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 及其与 SageMaker Experiments 的集成来管理整个机器学习工作流。使用 SageMaker Experiments 来记录实验的运行历史，并用于审计和合规性验证。","C":"使用 SageMaker Pipelines 及其与 SageMaker Studio 的集成来管理整个机器学习工作流。使用 SageMaker ML 血统跟踪来记录实验的运行历史，并用于审计和合规性验证。","D":"使用 SageMaker Pipelines 及其与 SageMaker Experiments 的集成来管理整个机器学习工作流。使用 SageMaker Experiments 来记录实验运行历史，并用于审计和合规性验证。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"SageMaker Pipelines is the SageMaker-native ML workflow orchestrator that gives data scientists fine-grained control and represents each pipeline as a directed acyclic graph (DAG); the Pipelines overview docs state 'An Amazon SageMaker AI pipeline is a series of interconnected steps in directed acyclic graph (DAG)', and the DAG is visualized and monitored through the SageMaker Studio integration. The second requirement is decided by exact wording: the ML Lineage Tracking docs explicitly list that data scientists can 'Keep a running history of model discovery experiments' and 'Establish model governance by tracking model lineage artifacts for auditing and compliance verification' - verbatim the phrases used in the question. By contrast, SageMaker Experiments only tracks training iterations, metrics, and parameters for repeatability/comparison, and AWS CodePipeline is a generic software CI/CD service, not the SageMaker ML DAG orchestrator. Therefore Pipelines + Studio for orchestration/visualization, plus ML Lineage Tracking for running history and governance/audit/compliance, satisfies every requirement, making C correct.","explanation_zh":"SageMaker Pipelines 是 SageMaker 原生的 ML 工作流程編排器，讓資料科學家擁有細粒度控制，並將每條 pipeline 表示為 directed acyclic graph (DAG)；Pipelines overview 文件明確指出『An Amazon SageMaker AI pipeline is a series of interconnected steps in directed acyclic graph (DAG)』，且該 DAG 透過 SageMaker Studio 整合進行視覺化與監控。第二項需求由用語完全比對決定：ML Lineage Tracking 文件明確列出資料科學家可以『Keep a running history of model discovery experiments』以及『Establish model governance by tracking model lineage artifacts for auditing and compliance verification』，與題目用字一字不差。相對地，SageMaker Experiments 僅追蹤訓練迭代、指標與參數以利重現/比較，而 AWS CodePipeline 是一般軟體 CI/CD 服務，並非 SageMaker 的 ML DAG 編排器。因此 Pipelines + Studio 負責編排與視覺化，加上 ML Lineage Tracking 提供實驗歷史紀錄與治理/稽核/合規，完全符合所有需求，故 C 為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS CodePipeline is a generic CI/CD service for software delivery; it is not the SageMaker-native ML workflow orchestrator and does not render SageMaker jobs/workflows as a DAG inside Studio. ML Lineage Tracking is the correct governance half, but the orchestration half is wrong, so the option fails.","why_zh":"AWS CodePipeline 是一般軟體交付的 CI/CD 服務，並非 SageMaker 原生的 ML 工作流程編排器，也不會在 Studio 中將 SageMaker 工作/流程呈現為 DAG。雖然 ML Lineage Tracking 是正確的治理選項，但編排部分錯誤，故此選項不成立。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Wrong on both halves: CodePipeline is not the SageMaker ML DAG orchestrator, and SageMaker Experiments tracks training iterations/metrics/parameters for repeatability and comparison rather than establishing model governance for auditing and compliance, which is the role of ML Lineage Tracking.","why_zh":"兩半皆錯：CodePipeline 並非 SageMaker 的 ML DAG 編排器；而 SageMaker Experiments 是用來追蹤訓練迭代/指標/參數以利重現與比較，並非用於建立稽核與合規的模型治理，後者才是 ML Lineage Tracking 的職責。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The orchestration half (Pipelines + Studio) is right, but SageMaker Experiments is for tracking and comparing training trials, not for model governance, auditing, and compliance verification. AWS docs assign the exact phrases 'running history of model discovery experiments' and 'model governance ... for auditing and compliance verification' specifically to ML Lineage Tracking, so Experiments is the wrong governance choice.","why_zh":"編排部分（Pipelines + Studio）正確，但 SageMaker Experiments 是用於追蹤與比較訓練試驗，並非用於模型治理、稽核與合規驗證。AWS 文件將『running history of model discovery experiments』與『model governance ... for auditing and compliance verification』這些用語明確歸屬於 ML Lineage Tracking，因此以 Experiments 作為治理選項是錯誤的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/lineage-tracking.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/pipelines-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/pipelines-build.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/experiments-mlops.html"]}},{"id":83,"question_en":"A company wants to reduce the cost of its containerized ML applications. The applications use ML models that run on Amazon EC2 instances, AWS Lambda functions, and an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. The EC2 workloads and ECS workloads use Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes to save predictions and artifacts. An ML engineer must identify resources that are being used inefficiently. The ML engineer also must generate recommendations to reduce the cost of these resources. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development effort?","question_zh":"一家公司希望降低其容器化机器学习应用程序的成本。这些应用程序使用在亚马逊 EC2 实例、AWS Lambda 函数以及亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）集群上运行的机器学习模型。EC2 工作负载和 ECS 工作负载使用亚马逊弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）卷来保存预测结果和工件。 机器学习工程师必须识别出使用效率低下的资源，并且还必须提出降低这些资源成本的建议。 哪种解决方案能以最少的开发工作量满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create code to evaluate each instance's memory and compute usage.","B":"Add cost allocation tags to the resources. Activate the tags in AWS Billing and Cost Management.","C":"Check AWS CloudTrail event history for the creation of the resources.","D":"Run AWS Compute Optimizer."},"options_zh":{"A":"编写代码来评估每个实例的内存和计算使用情况。","B":"为资源添加成本分配标签。在 AWS 账单和成本管理中激活这些标签。","C":"检查 AWS CloudTrail 事件历史记录，查看资源创建情况。","D":"运行 AWS 计算优化器。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS Compute Optimizer is a managed service that analyzes resource configuration and Amazon CloudWatch utilization metrics to identify inefficiently used (over-provisioned, under-provisioned, or idle) resources and automatically generates rightsizing recommendations to reduce cost and improve performance. Its supported-resources list explicitly includes Amazon EC2 instances, Amazon EBS volumes, AWS Lambda functions, and Amazon ECS services on AWS Fargate, covering every resource type named in the scenario. The engineer only needs to opt in (no code), so it meets both requirements (identify inefficient resources and recommend cost reductions) with the LEAST development effort. The other options fall short: writing custom code (A) is the opposite of least effort; cost allocation tags (B) only attribute spend by resource in Billing and Cost Management and do not analyze utilization or produce rightsizing recommendations; and CloudTrail event history (C) only logs who created resources, not how efficiently they are used.","explanation_zh":"AWS Compute Optimizer 是一項受管服務，會分析資源的組態與 Amazon CloudWatch 使用率指標，找出使用效率不佳（過度配置、配置不足或閒置）的資源，並自動產生 rightsizing 建議以降低成本、提升效能。其支援資源清單明確包含 Amazon EC2 instances、Amazon EBS volumes、AWS Lambda functions 以及 Amazon ECS services on AWS Fargate，涵蓋情境中提到的所有資源類型。工程師只需 opt in（不需撰寫程式碼），即可同時滿足「找出低效資源」與「提出降低成本建議」兩項需求，且開發工作量最少。其他選項皆不符合：自行撰寫程式碼（A）與「最少開發工作量」相反；cost allocation tags（B）只在 Billing and Cost Management 中依資源歸屬成本，並不分析使用率或產生 rightsizing 建議；CloudTrail 事件歷史（C）只記錄誰建立了資源，無法評估使用效率。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating custom code to evaluate each instance's memory and compute usage requires significant development and maintenance effort, directly conflicting with the LEAST development effort requirement, and it only addresses EC2 rather than Lambda, ECS, and EBS.","why_zh":"撰寫自訂程式碼評估每個執行個體的記憶體與運算使用率需要大量開發與維護工作，直接違反「最少開發工作量」的要求，且只處理 EC2，未涵蓋 Lambda、ECS 或 EBS。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Cost allocation tags only let you group and attribute costs to resources in AWS Billing and Cost Management; they do not analyze utilization metrics or generate rightsizing/efficiency recommendations, so they cannot identify inefficiently used resources.","why_zh":"cost allocation tags 只能在 AWS Billing and Cost Management 中將成本分組並歸屬到資源，不會分析使用率指標或產生 rightsizing／效率建議，因此無法找出使用效率不佳的資源。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS CloudTrail event history records API activity such as who created a resource and when; it provides an audit trail, not utilization analysis or cost-reduction recommendations, so it cannot identify inefficient resources.","why_zh":"AWS CloudTrail 事件歷史記錄 API 活動，例如誰在何時建立了資源，提供的是稽核軌跡，而非使用率分析或降低成本的建議，因此無法找出低效資源。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/compute-optimizer/latest/ug/what-is-compute-optimizer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/compute-optimizer/latest/ug/requirements.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/compute-optimizer/latest/ug/supported-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/compute-optimizer/latest/ug/viewing-recommendations.html"]}},{"id":84,"question_en":"A company needs to create a central catalog for all the company's ML models. The models are in AWS accounts where the company developed the models initially. The models are hosted in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repositories. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要为其所有的机器学习模型创建一个中央目录。这些模型最初是在公司的 AWS 账户中开发 的，并托管在亚马逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）的存储库中。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure ECR cross-account replication for each existing ECR repository. Ensure that each model is visible in each AWS account.","B":"Create a new AWS account with a new ECR repository as the central catalog. Configure ECR cross- account replication between the initial ECR repositories and the central catalog.","C":"Use the Amazon SageMaker Model Registry to create a model group for models hosted in Amazon ECR. Create a new AWS account. In the new account, use the SageMaker Model Registry as the central catalog. Attach a cross-account resource policy to each model group in the initial AWS accounts.","D":"Use an AWS Glue Data Catalog to store the models. Run an AWS Glue crawler to migrate the models from the ECR repositories to the Data Catalog. Configure cross-account access to the Data Catalog."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个现有的 ECR 代码库配置跨账户复制。确保每个模型在每个 AWS 账户中都可见。","B":"创建一个新的 AWS 账户，并在其中创建一个新的 ECR 仓库作为中央目录。在初始的 ECR 仓库与中央 目录之间配置 ECR 跨账户复制。","C":"使用 Amazon SageMaker 模型注册表为托管在 Amazon ECR 中的模型创建模型组。创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在新账户中，将 SageMaker 模型注册表用作中央目录。在初始 AWS 账户中的每个模型 组上附加跨账户资源策略。","D":"使用 AWS Glue 数据目录存储模型。运行 AWS Glue 爬虫程序将模型从 ECR 存储库迁移到数据目录。配 置跨账户访问数据目录。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Analytics","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement is a single central catalog for ML models that are packaged as container images stored in Amazon ECR across the accounts where they were developed. Amazon SageMaker Model Registry is the purpose-built service for cataloging, versioning, and managing ML models: you organize models into Model (Package) Groups, and each model package's container definition references the inference image in Amazon ECR, so the models stay in ECR while the Registry catalogs them with metadata, versions, lineage, and approval status. The Model Registry supports cross-account discoverability: each model owner account attaches a resource policy to its model package group via the put-model-package-group-policy API (surfaced through AWS RAM), letting a designated consumer account discover and access all the shared model groups. Creating a new account that acts as the resource consumer therefore gives the company one central catalog without copying or duplicating any model artifacts, exactly as option C describes.","explanation_zh":"需求是為跨多個開發帳戶、以容器映像形式封裝在 Amazon ECR 中的 ML 模型建立一個單一中央目錄。Amazon SageMaker Model Registry 正是專為編目、版本控管與管理 ML 模型而設計的服務：你將模型組織成 Model (Package) Groups，而每個 model package 的 container definition 會參照 Amazon ECR 中的推論映像，因此模型本身仍保留在 ECR，由 Registry 以 metadata、版本、lineage 與核准狀態進行編目。Model Registry 支援 cross-account discoverability：每個模型擁有者帳戶透過 put-model-package-group-policy API（透過 AWS RAM 呈現）對其 model package group 附加 resource policy，讓指定的消費者帳戶可探索並存取所有共享的 model group。因此建立一個作為 resource consumer 的新帳戶，即可讓公司擁有單一中央目錄，且無須複製或重複任何模型成品，正符合選項 C 的描述。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"ECR cross-account replication only copies container image bits between repositories; it does not create a model catalog with model metadata, versions, lineage, or approval status. Replicating every repository into every account also produces massive duplication and yields no single central catalog, failing the core requirement.","why_zh":"ECR 跨帳戶 replication 只是在 repository 之間複製容器映像，並未建立帶有模型 metadata、版本、lineage 或核准狀態的模型目錄。把每個 repository 複製到每個帳戶還會造成大量重複，且沒有單一的中央目錄，無法滿足核心需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Using a new ECR repository as the 'catalog' with replication still only stores raw container images, not model catalog metadata or versions. ECR is an image registry, not a model registry; it provides no model-group cataloging, lineage, or approval workflow, so it does not meet the requirement for an ML model catalog.","why_zh":"把新的 ECR repository 當作『目錄』並做 replication，仍然只儲存原始容器映像，而非模型目錄的 metadata 或版本。ECR 是映像登錄，而非模型登錄；它不提供 model-group 編目、lineage 或核准流程，因此無法滿足 ML 模型目錄的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Glue Data Catalog is a metadata catalog for data tables and schemas used by analytics services, and Glue crawlers crawl data stores such as Amazon S3 or JDBC sources, not ECR container images. It cannot crawl ECR or store or catalog ML model artifacts, so this option is technically invalid.","why_zh":"AWS Glue Data Catalog 是供分析服務使用的資料表與結構描述 metadata 目錄，而 Glue crawler 爬取的是 Amazon S3 或 JDBC 等資料存放區，而非 ECR 容器映像。它無法爬取 ECR，也無法儲存或編目 ML 模型成品，因此此選項技術上不成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry-ram.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry-ram-discover.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/sagemaker/put-model-package-group-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/replication.html"]}},{"id":85,"question_en":"A company has developed a new ML model. The company requires online model validation on 10% of the traffic before the company fully releases the model in production. The company uses an Amazon SageMaker endpoint behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) to serve the model. Which solution will set up the required online validation with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司开发了一种新的机器学习模型。该公司要求在全面将模型投入生产之前，在 10% 的流量上进行在 线模型验证。该公司使用位于应用负载均衡器（ALB）后面的 Amazon SageMaker 端点来提供模型服务。 哪种解决方案能以最低的操作开销建立所需的在线验证？","options_en":{"A":"Use production variants to add the new model to the existing SageMaker endpoint. Set the variant weight to 0.1 for the new model. Monitor the number of invocations by using Amazon CloudWatch.","B":"Use production variants to add the new model to the existing SageMaker endpoint. Set the variant weight to 1 for the new model. Monitor the number of invocations by using Amazon CloudWatch.","C":"Create a new SageMaker endpoint. Use production variants to add the new model to the new endpoint. Monitor the number of invocations by using Amazon CloudWatch.","D":"Configure the ALB to route 10% of the traffic to the new model at the existing SageMaker endpoint. Monitor the number of invocations by using AWS CloudTrail."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用生产变体将新模型添加到现有的 SageMaker 端点。将新模型的变体权重设置为 0.1。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 监控调用次数。","B":"使用生产变体将新模型添加到现有的 SageMaker 端点。将新模型的变体权重设置为 1。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 监控调用次数。","C":"创建一个新的 SageMaker 端点。使用生产变体将新模型添加到新端点。通过 Amazon CloudWatch 监控调 用次数。","D":"将应用负载均衡器（ALB）配置为将现有 SageMaker 端点的 10% 流量路由到新模型。使用 AWS CloudTrail 监控调用次数。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the canonical AWS pattern for online model validation. The SageMaker 'Options for evaluating your machine learning model' page states that for 'Online testing with live data,' SageMaker 'supports A/B testing for models in production by using production variants. Production variants are models that use the same inference code and are deployed on the same SageMaker endpoint. You configure the production variants so that a small portion of the live traffic goes to the model that you want to validate. For example, you might choose to send 10% of the traffic to a model variant for evaluation.' Adding the new model as a second production variant on the EXISTING endpoint and giving it a small relative weight (0.1, versus the existing model's larger weight) routes roughly 10% of live traffic to it without provisioning any new infrastructure, giving the least operational overhead. SageMaker distributes invocation requests across variants by their relative weights, and CloudWatch already publishes per-variant Invocations metrics for monitoring. Option A is correct.","explanation_zh":"這是 AWS 線上模型驗證的標準作法。SageMaker 的 'Options for evaluating your machine learning model' 文件指出，對於「使用即時資料的線上測試」，SageMaker「透過 production variants 支援正式環境模型的 A/B testing。Production variants 是使用相同推論程式碼、部署在同一個 SageMaker endpoint 上的模型。你設定 production variants 讓一小部分即時流量導向你要驗證的模型。例如，你可能選擇將 10% 的流量送往某個 model variant 進行評估。」將新模型以第二個 production variant 加到既有 endpoint，並給予較小的相對 weight（0.1，相對於既有模型較大的權重），即可將約 10% 的即時流量導向它，且不需建立任何新基礎架構，操作負擔最低。SageMaker 會依各 variant 的相對權重分配 invocation 請求，且 CloudWatch 已提供各 variant 的 Invocations 指標可供監控。選項 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Variant weights are RELATIVE, not absolute percentages. The AWS A/B test example shows weight 1 on each of two variants yields a 50/50 split (each receives 1/2 of total weight). Setting the new model's weight to 1 does not produce the required 10% validation split.","why_zh":"Variant weight 是相對值而非絕對百分比。AWS 的 A/B test 範例顯示兩個 variant 各設 weight 1 會得到 50/50 分流（各佔總權重的 1/2）。把新模型 weight 設為 1 無法產生題目要求的 10% 驗證分流。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating a brand-new endpoint adds infrastructure and does not, by itself, split live traffic 90/10 between the old and new models; you would need an additional external routing layer to send only 10%. That is more operational overhead, not less.","why_zh":"建立全新的 endpoint 會增加基礎架構，且本身無法在新舊模型間以 90/10 分流即時流量；還需額外的外部路由層才能只送 10%。這是更高而非更低的操作負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Routing 10% via the ALB requires two separate endpoints/target groups and manual ALB weighted-target configuration, which is more operational overhead than native production-variant weights on one endpoint. Also, CloudTrail records API/management events, not per-model inference invocation counts; CloudWatch is the correct tool to monitor invocations.","why_zh":"透過 ALB 分流 10% 需要兩個獨立 endpoint/target group 並手動設定 ALB 加權目標，操作負擔高於在單一 endpoint 上使用原生 production-variant 權重。此外 CloudTrail 記錄的是 API/管理事件，而非各模型的推論 invocation 計數；正確的監控工具是 CloudWatch。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/how-it-works-model-validation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-ab-testing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/APIReference/API_CreateEndpointConfig.html"]}},{"id":86,"question_en":"A company needs to develop an ML model. The model must identify an item in an image and must provide the location of the item. Which Amazon SageMaker algorithm will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要开发一个机器学习模型。该模型必须能够识别图像中的物品，并提供该物品的位置。 哪种亚马逊 SageMaker 算法能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Image classification","B":"XGBoost","C":"Object detection","D":"K-nearest neighbors (k-NN)"},"options_zh":{"A":"图像分类","B":"XGBoost（梯度提升决策树）","C":"目标检测","D":"K 近邻（k-NN）"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: identify (classify) an item in an image AND provide its location. The Amazon SageMaker built-in Object Detection algorithm does exactly this. Per AWS docs, it 'detects and classifies objects in images using a single deep neural network,' identifies all instances of objects within the image scene, categorizes each into a class with a confidence score, and indicates each object's 'location and scale in the image ... by a rectangular bounding box' (using the Single Shot multibox Detector, SSD, framework). The bounding-box output is what distinguishes it from Image classification, which per AWS docs only 'outputs one or more labels assigned to that image' with no location information. XGBoost and k-NN are tabular/numeric algorithms and cannot localize items in images.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩個部分：在影像中辨識（分類）物件，並且提供該物件的位置。Amazon SageMaker 內建的 Object Detection 演算法正好滿足這兩點。根據 AWS 文件，它使用單一深度神經網路偵測並分類影像中的物件，辨識影像中所有物件實例，將每個物件歸類到某個類別並給出信賴分數，並以矩形邊界框（rectangular bounding box）標示每個物件在影像中的「位置與大小」（採用 Single Shot multibox Detector，SSD 框架）。這個邊界框輸出正是它與 Image classification 的差別所在——後者根據 AWS 文件僅「輸出指派給整張影像的一個或多個標籤」，不提供位置資訊。XGBoost 與 k-NN 屬於表格／數值型演算法，無法定位影像中的物件。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Image classification only assigns one or more category labels to an entire image; per AWS docs it 'outputs one or more labels assigned to that image' and produces no bounding box or location, so it fails the localization requirement.","why_zh":"Image classification 只會對整張影像指派一個或多個類別標籤；根據 AWS 文件它「輸出指派給整張影像的一個或多個標籤」，不產生邊界框或位置，因此無法滿足定位需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"XGBoost is a gradient-boosted tree algorithm for tabular regression/classification and ranking; it is not an image/computer-vision algorithm and cannot detect or localize items in images.","why_zh":"XGBoost 是用於表格資料迴歸／分類與排序的梯度提升樹演算法，並非影像／電腦視覺演算法，無法偵測或定位影像中的物件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"K-nearest neighbors (k-NN) is an index-based classification/regression algorithm for tabular numeric feature vectors; it performs no object localization and does not produce bounding boxes.","why_zh":"K-nearest neighbors (k-NN) 是針對表格數值特徵向量的索引式分類／迴歸演算法，不執行物件定位，也不產生邊界框。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/object-detection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/algo-object-detection-tech-notes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/image-classification.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/algos.html"]}},{"id":87,"question_en":"A company has an Amazon S3 bucket that contains 1 TB of files from different sources. The S3 bucket contains the following file types in the same S3 folder: CSV, JSON, XLSX, and Apache Parquet. An ML engineer must implement a solution that uses AWS Glue DataBrew to process the data. The ML engineer also must store the final output in Amazon S3 so that AWS Glue can consume the output in the future. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个亚马逊 S3 存储桶，其中包含来自不同来源的 1TB 文件。该 S3 存储桶中的同一 S3 文件 夹内有以下文件类型：CSV、JSON、XLSX 和 Apache Parquet。 机器学习工程师必须实现一个解决方案，该方案使用 AWS Glue DataBrew 来处理数据。此外，机器学习 工程师还必须将最终输出存储在 Amazon S3 中，以便 AWS Glue 在未来能够使用该输出。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use DataBrew to process the existing S3 folder. Store the output in Apache Parquet format.","B":"Use DataBrew to process the existing S3 folder. Store the output in AWS Glue Parquet format.","C":"Separate the data into a different folder for each file type. Use DataBrew to process each folder individually. Store the output in Apache Parquet format.","D":"Separate the data into a different folder for each file type. Use DataBrew to process each folder individually. Store the output in AWS Glue Parquet format."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 DataBrew 处理现有的 S3 文件夹。将输出以 Apache Parquet 格式存储。","B":"使用 DataBrew 处理现有的 S3 文件夹。将输出以 AWS Glue Parquet 格式存储。","C":"将数据按文件类型分别存入不同的文件夹。使用 DataBrew 分别处理每个文件夹。将输出存储为 Apache Parquet 格式。","D":"按文件类型将数据分别存入不同的文件夹。使用 DataBrew 分别处理每个文件夹。将输出存储为 AWS Glue Parquet 格式。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two AWS-documented facts decide this. First, the AWS Glue DataBrew 'Supported file types for data sources' page states: 'If you are importing a folder, all files in the folder must be of the same file type.' The bucket mixes CSV, JSON, XLSX (Excel), and Parquet in one folder, so DataBrew cannot ingest that folder as a single dataset. This eliminates A and B, both of which 'process the existing S3 folder.' All four types are individually supported DataBrew inputs, so the data must first be separated into one folder per file type. Second, DataBrew job output supports both PARQUET (Apache Parquet) and GLUEPARQUET as Format values. The requirement is a generic, future-proof output that 'AWS Glue can consume in the future,' so standard Apache Parquet is correct: it is the portable, columnar open format that any downstream AWS Glue job, crawler, or Athena reads natively. GlueParquet is merely a specialized performance writer (the AWS Glue docs explicitly say its 'glueparquet' access pattern 'is no longer advocated' and it has limitations such as supporting only schema evolution, not column-type changes). So the answer is C: separate into per-type folders, process each, and store output as Apache Parquet.","explanation_zh":"兩個 AWS 官方文件事實決定答案。第一，AWS Glue DataBrew 的「Supported file types for data sources」頁面明確指出：『If you are importing a folder, all files in the folder must be of the same file type.』本題的 S3 資料夾把 CSV、JSON、XLSX（Excel）、Parquet 混在同一個資料夾，因此 DataBrew 無法把該資料夾當成單一 dataset 匯入。這就排除了 A 和 B（兩者都直接『process the existing S3 folder』）。這四種類型 DataBrew 都個別支援為輸入，所以必須先依檔案類型分到各自的資料夾。第二，DataBrew job 的輸出 Format 同時支援 PARQUET（Apache Parquet）與 GLUEPARQUET。需求是『未來讓 AWS Glue 能消費此輸出』的通用、面向未來格式，因此標準 Apache Parquet 才正確：它是可攜的欄式開放格式，任何下游的 AWS Glue job、crawler 或 Athena 都能原生讀取。GlueParquet 只是專用的效能 writer（AWS Glue 文件明確表示其 'glueparquet' 存取模式『no longer advocated』，且有限制，例如只支援 schema 演進、不支援欄位型別變更）。因此正確答案為 C：依類型分資料夾、各自處理、輸出為 Apache Parquet。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DataBrew cannot process a folder containing mixed file types as one dataset. AWS docs require that all files in an imported folder be the same file type, so processing the existing mixed CSV/JSON/XLSX/Parquet folder fails before any output format matters.","why_zh":"DataBrew 無法把含多種檔案類型的資料夾當成單一 dataset 處理。AWS 文件要求匯入資料夾內所有檔案必須是同一類型，因此直接處理混合的 CSV/JSON/XLSX/Parquet 資料夾在輸出格式之前就會失敗。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as A: processing the existing mixed-type folder violates DataBrew's same-file-type rule. It also picks GlueParquet, a specialized writer whose 'glueparquet' access pattern AWS no longer advocates, instead of the standard Apache Parquet open format for general Glue consumption.","why_zh":"與 A 同樣的致命缺陷：處理現有混合類型資料夾違反 DataBrew 同一檔案類型規則。且選用 GlueParquet（其 'glueparquet' 存取模式 AWS 已不再建議）的專用 writer，而非供 Glue 通用消費的標準 Apache Parquet 開放格式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The folder-separation step is correct, but the output should be standard Apache Parquet. GlueParquet is a performance-optimized Glue DynamicFrame writer (only schema evolution, not column-type changes; cannot write empty DataFrames), and AWS docs state the 'glueparquet' access pattern is no longer advocated, so it is not the general portable columnar format intended for broad future Glue/Athena consumption.","why_zh":"依類型分資料夾的步驟正確，但輸出應為標準 Apache Parquet。GlueParquet 是針對效能最佳化的 Glue DynamicFrame writer（只支援 schema 演進、不支援欄位型別變更、無法寫入空 DataFrame），且 AWS 文件指出 'glueparquet' 存取模式已不再建議，因此並非供未來 Glue/Athena 廣泛消費的通用可攜欄式格式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/databrew/latest/dg/supported-data-file-sources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-databrew-job-output.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/aws-glue-programming-etl-format-parquet-home.html"]}},{"id":88,"question_en":"A manufacturing company uses an ML model to determine whether products meet a standard for quality. The model produces an output of \"Passed\" or \"Failed.\" Robots separate the products into the two categories by using the model to analyze photos on the assembly line. Which metrics should the company use to evaluate the model's performance? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"","options_en":{"A":"Precision and recall","B":"Root mean square error (RMSE) and mean absolute percentage error (MAPE)","C":"Accuracy and F1 score","D":"Bilingual Evaluation Understudy (BLEU) score","E":"Perplexity"},"options_zh":{},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The model outputs 'Passed' or 'Failed' to sort products into two buckets, which is a binary (2-category) classification problem, so the company must use classification evaluation metrics. The Amazon ML Binary Classification guide states that typical binary classification accuracy metrics are accuracy (ACC), precision, recall, false positive rate, and F1-measure (the harmonic mean of precision and recall). The SageMaker Canvas metrics reference confirms the same by listing Accuracy, AUC, BalancedAccuracy, F1, precision, and recall under 'Metrics for categorical prediction' (including 2-category prediction). Therefore both A (precision and recall) and C (accuracy and F1 score) are valid pairs of binary classification metrics. The remaining options apply to other problem types: B (RMSE and MAPE) are numeric/regression error metrics, D (BLEU) is for machine translation/text generation, and E (perplexity) is for language model evaluation, none of which fit a Pass/Fail classifier.","explanation_zh":"模型輸出「Passed」或「Failed」將產品分成兩類，屬於二元（2 類別）分類問題，因此公司必須使用分類評估指標。Amazon ML 的 Binary Classification 文件指出，典型的二元分類指標為 accuracy (ACC)、precision、recall、false positive rate 與 F1-measure（precision 與 recall 的調和平均數）。SageMaker Canvas 的 metrics 參考文件同樣在「Metrics for categorical prediction」（含 2 類別預測）下列出 Accuracy、AUC、BalancedAccuracy、F1、precision 與 recall。因此 A（precision 與 recall）與 C（accuracy 與 F1 score）皆為有效的二元分類指標組合。其餘選項適用於其他問題類型：B（RMSE 與 MAPE）為數值/迴歸誤差指標，D（BLEU）用於機器翻譯/文字生成，E（perplexity）用於語言模型評估，皆不適用於 Pass/Fail 分類器。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"RMSE and MAPE are numeric (regression) error metrics that measure the distance between continuous predicted and actual values. The SageMaker Canvas metrics reference lists both under 'Metrics for numeric prediction', not categorical prediction. A Pass/Fail classifier produces discrete classes, not continuous numbers, so these metrics do not apply.","why_zh":"RMSE 與 MAPE 是數值（迴歸）誤差指標，衡量連續預測值與實際值之間的差距。SageMaker Canvas metrics 文件將兩者列於「Metrics for numeric prediction」而非分類預測。Pass/Fail 分類器產生離散類別而非連續數值，因此這些指標不適用。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"BLEU (Bilingual Evaluation Understudy) score evaluates the quality of machine-translated or generated text by comparing it to reference text. It is a natural language generation metric and has no relevance to a binary Pass/Fail image-classification model.","why_zh":"BLEU（Bilingual Evaluation Understudy）分數用於評估機器翻譯或生成文字的品質，透過與參考文本比較。它是自然語言生成指標，與二元 Pass/Fail 影像分類模型無關。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Perplexity measures how well a probabilistic language model predicts a sample of text. It is used to evaluate language models, not classification models, so it does not fit a Pass/Fail quality-inspection use case.","why_zh":"Perplexity 衡量機率語言模型對文本樣本的預測能力，用於評估語言模型而非分類模型，因此不適用於 Pass/Fail 品質檢測情境。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/latest/dg/binary-classification.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-metrics.html"]}},{"id":89,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to encrypt all data in transit when an ML training job runs. The ML engineer must ensure that encryption in transit is applied to processes that Amazon SageMaker uses during the training job. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"当机器学习训练任务运行时，机器学习工程师需要对所有传输中的数据进行加密。机器学习工程师必须确 保在训练任务期间，亚马逊 SageMaker 使用的所有流程都应用了传输加密。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Encrypt communication between nodes for batch processing.","B":"Encrypt communication between nodes in a training cluster.","C":"Specify an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key during creation of the training job request.","D":"Specify an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key during creation of the SageMaker domain."},"options_zh":{"A":"对节点间用于批处理的通信进行加密。","B":"对训练集群中节点之间的通信进行加密。","C":"在创建训练作业请求时指定一个 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥。","D":"在创建 SageMaker 域时指定一个 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"To apply encryption in transit to the processes SageMaker uses during a training job, you enable inter-container traffic encryption, which encrypts communication between the nodes in a distributed training cluster. The SageMaker 'Protecting Data in Transit with Encryption' page states that some intranetwork traffic (including communications between nodes in distributed training jobs) is unencrypted by default, and that 'You can choose to encrypt communication between nodes in a training job cluster and processing job cluster.' The companion 'Protect Communications Between ML Compute Instances in a Distributed Training Job' page explains this is done by setting EnableInterContainerTrafficEncryption=True on the CreateTrainingJob (or CreateHyperParameterTuningJob) API, or via the console checkbox. Option B precisely describes this mechanism. Option A is wrong because the same documentation explicitly states 'There are no inter-node communications for batch processing,' so there is nothing to encrypt. AWS KMS keys (C and D) provide encryption at rest for storage volumes, output artifacts, and domain storage, not encryption in transit between training nodes.","explanation_zh":"若要為 SageMaker 在訓練作業執行期間使用的處理程序套用傳輸中加密 (encryption in transit)，您需啟用 inter-container traffic encryption，藉此加密分散式訓練叢集中各節點之間的通訊。SageMaker 的「Protecting Data in Transit with Encryption」文件指出，部分內部網路流量 (包含分散式訓練作業中節點之間的通訊) 預設為未加密，並表示「You can choose to encrypt communication between nodes in a training job cluster and processing job cluster.」搭配的「Protect Communications Between ML Compute Instances in a Distributed Training Job」頁面說明，這是透過在 CreateTrainingJob (或 CreateHyperParameterTuningJob) API 上設定 EnableInterContainerTrafficEncryption=True，或透過主控台核取方塊來完成。選項 B 正是描述此機制。選項 A 不正確，因為相同文件明確指出「There are no inter-node communications for batch processing」，因此沒有可加密的對象。AWS KMS 金鑰 (C 與 D) 提供的是儲存磁碟區、輸出成品及 domain 儲存的靜態加密 (at rest)，而非訓練節點之間的傳輸中加密。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The 'Protecting Data in Transit with Encryption' page explicitly states 'There are no inter-node communications for batch processing,' so there is no batch-processing inter-node traffic to encrypt. This is a distractor that swaps 'training cluster' for 'batch processing.'","why_zh":"「Protecting Data in Transit with Encryption」頁面明確指出「There are no inter-node communications for batch processing」，因此批次處理沒有可加密的節點間流量。此選項是把「訓練叢集」偷換成「批次處理」的誘答。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Specifying an AWS KMS key on the CreateTrainingJob request (VolumeKmsKeyId / OutputDataConfig.KmsKeyId) provides encryption at rest for the storage volumes and output artifacts, not encryption in transit between training nodes.","why_zh":"在 CreateTrainingJob 請求上指定 AWS KMS 金鑰 (VolumeKmsKeyId / OutputDataConfig.KmsKeyId) 提供的是儲存磁碟區與輸出成品的靜態加密，而非訓練節點之間的傳輸中加密。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Specifying an AWS KMS key when creating the SageMaker domain encrypts the domain's storage (e.g., the associated EFS volume) at rest. It does not encrypt in-transit traffic between nodes during a training job.","why_zh":"在建立 SageMaker domain 時指定 AWS KMS 金鑰，加密的是 domain 儲存 (例如關聯的 EFS 磁碟區) 的靜態資料，並不會加密訓練作業期間節點之間的傳輸中流量。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/encryption-in-transit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/train-encrypt.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/APIReference/API_CreateTrainingJob.html"]}},{"id":90,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to use metrics to assess the quality of a time-series forecasting model. Which metrics apply to this model? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一名机器学习工程师需要使用指标来评估时间序列预测模型的质量。 哪些指标适用于此模型？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Recall","B":"LogLoss","C":"Root mean square error (RMSE)","D":"InferenceLatency","E":"Average weighted quantile loss (wQL)"},"options_zh":{"A":"召回","B":"对数损失函数","C":"均方根误差（RMSE）","D":"推理延迟","E":"加权平均分位数损失（wQL）"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Time-series forecasting in AWS (Amazon Forecast and SageMaker Autopilot/Canvas) is evaluated with metrics tailored to point forecasts and probabilistic (quantile) forecasts. The Amazon Forecast 'Evaluating Predictor Accuracy' page states Forecast evaluates predictors using RMSE, Weighted Quantile Loss (wQL), Average wQL, MAPE, MASE, and WAPE. The SageMaker Autopilot 'Objective metrics' page for time-series forecasting lists the same set and explicitly defines RMSE (square root of the averaged squared error between predicted and actual values; flags large errors/outliers) and Average Weighted Quantile Loss (the default; averages forecast accuracy across the P10/P50/P90 quantiles). Therefore RMSE (C) and Average weighted quantile loss (wQL) (E) are the two metrics that apply. The other options belong to different problem types: Recall and LogLoss are classification metrics, and InferenceLatency is an operational/serving metric, not a forecast-quality metric.","explanation_zh":"AWS 的時間序列預測（Amazon Forecast 與 SageMaker Autopilot/Canvas）使用針對點預測與機率（分位數）預測量身打造的指標來評估。Amazon Forecast 的「Evaluating Predictor Accuracy」頁面說明 Forecast 使用 RMSE、Weighted Quantile Loss (wQL)、Average wQL、MAPE、MASE 與 WAPE 來評估 predictor。SageMaker Autopilot 的「Objective metrics」頁面（時間序列預測）列出相同的指標集，並明確定義 RMSE（預測值與實際值平方差平均之平方根，可凸顯大誤差與離群值）以及 Average Weighted Quantile Loss（預設值，對 P10/P50/P90 分位數的預測準確度取平均）。因此 RMSE (C) 與 Average weighted quantile loss (wQL) (E) 是適用的兩個指標。其他選項屬於不同的問題類型：Recall 與 LogLoss 是分類指標，InferenceLatency 是營運/服務層面的指標，而非預測品質指標。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Recall is a classification metric (true positives / actual positives) used for categorization problems, not for continuous time-series forecasting accuracy.","why_zh":"Recall 是分類指標（真陽性 / 實際陽性），用於分類問題，不適用於連續型時間序列預測的準確度評估。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"LogLoss (cross-entropy) is a probabilistic classification metric measuring the quality of predicted class probabilities; it is not a metric AWS uses to evaluate time-series forecasts.","why_zh":"LogLoss（交叉熵）是衡量預測類別機率品質的分類指標，並非 AWS 用來評估時間序列預測的指標。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"InferenceLatency is an operational/serving performance metric (how fast an endpoint responds), unrelated to the statistical accuracy of a forecast.","why_zh":"InferenceLatency 是營運/服務效能指標（端點回應速度），與預測的統計準確度無關。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/forecast/latest/dg/metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/timeseries-objective-metric.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-metrics.html"]}},{"id":91,"question_en":"A company runs Amazon SageMaker ML models that use accelerated instances. The models require real- time responses. Each model has different scaling requirements. The company must not allow a cold start for the models. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司运行使用加速实例的亚马逊 SageMaker 机器学习模型。这些模型需要实时响应。每个模型 的扩展需求各不相同。该公司决不允许这些模型出现冷启动的情况。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a SageMaker Serverless Inference endpoint for each model. Use provisioned concurrency for the endpoints.","B":"Create a SageMaker Asynchronous Inference endpoint for each model. Create an auto scaling policy for each endpoint.","C":"Create a SageMaker endpoint. Create an inference component for each model. In the inference component settings, specify the newly created endpoint. Create an auto scaling policy for each inference component. Set the parameter for the minimum number of copies to at least 1.","D":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Store all the model artifacts in the S3 bucket. Create a SageMaker multi- model endpoint. Point the endpoint to the S3 bucket. Create an auto scaling policy for the endpoint. Set the parameter for the minimum number of copies to at least 1."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个模型创建一个 SageMaker 无服务器推理端点。为这些端点使用预配置的并发设置。","B":"为每个模型创建一个 SageMaker 异步推理端点。为每个端点创建一个自动扩展策略。","C":"创建一个 SageMaker 端点。为每个模型创建一个推理组件。在推理组件设置中，指定新创 建的端点。为每个推理组件创建一个自动缩放策略。将副本的最小数量参数设置为至少 1。","D":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。将所有模型构件存储在该 S3 存储桶中。创建一个 SageMaker 多模型 端点。将端点指向 S3 存储桶。为端点创建一个自动扩展策略。将最小副本数参数设置为至少 1。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The hard requirements are: accelerated (GPU) instances, real-time responses, per-model (different) scaling, and no cold start. Option C deploys a SageMaker real-time endpoint with one inference component per model. The real-time inference docs state that in inference component settings you can 'optimize resource utilization by tailoring how the required CPU cores, accelerators, and memory are allocated to the model,' so accelerated instances are supported, and each model gets its own resource and scaling profile (satisfying the different scaling requirements). The same docs state you 'can set a minimum number of copies to ensure that the model loads in the quantity that you require to serve requests'; setting the minimum number of copies to at least 1 keeps every model loaded and warm, eliminating cold starts. This is the only option that meets all four requirements simultaneously.","explanation_zh":"硬性需求為：accelerated (GPU) 執行個體、real-time 回應、每個模型有不同的擴展需求、且不允許 cold start。選項 C 部署一個 SageMaker real-time endpoint，並為每個模型建立一個 inference component。官方 real-time inference 文件指出，在 inference component 設定中可『透過調整模型所需的 CPU cores、accelerators 與記憶體配置來最佳化資源利用率』，因此支援 accelerated instances，且每個模型擁有各自的資源與擴展設定（滿足不同的擴展需求）。同一份文件也指出可『設定最小 copy 數量，以確保模型以服務請求所需的數量載入』；將 minimum number of copies 設為至少 1 可讓每個模型保持載入且 warm，消除 cold start。這是唯一能同時滿足全部四項需求的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SageMaker Serverless Inference does not use accelerated/GPU instances (it is configured by memory size and integrates with AWS Lambda), so it cannot meet the accelerated-instance requirement. The serverless docs also explicitly state it is for workloads that 'can tolerate cold starts' and that it 'scales your endpoint down to 0.' Provisioned Concurrency only warms a fixed concurrency level on the same serverless (non-accelerated) substrate, so the accelerated-instance requirement still fails.","why_zh":"SageMaker Serverless Inference 不使用 accelerated/GPU 執行個體（以記憶體大小配置並整合 AWS Lambda），無法滿足 accelerated-instance 需求。官方文件也明確說明它適用於『可以容忍 cold start』的工作負載，且會『將 endpoint 縮減到 0』。即使加上 Provisioned Concurrency，也只是在相同的 serverless（非 accelerated）基礎上保溫固定的並行數，仍無法滿足 accelerated-instance 需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Asynchronous Inference queues requests for large payloads and long-running jobs and returns results to Amazon S3; it is not a real-time response mechanism. The async docs also note it 'autoscales instances [to] zero' when idle, which produces cold starts. It fails both the real-time and the no-cold-start requirements.","why_zh":"Asynchronous Inference 透過佇列處理大型 payload 與長時間作業並將結果寫回 Amazon S3，並非 real-time 回應機制。官方文件也指出閒置時它會『將執行個體自動縮減到零』，因而產生 cold start。它同時違反 real-time 與 no-cold-start 需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Multi-model endpoints dynamically download and cache models from Amazon S3 on demand; the MME docs explicitly warn the application must be 'tolerant of occasional cold start-related latency penalties' for infrequently used models, so it violates the no-cold-start requirement. MME also auto scales the whole fleet with one shared policy rather than per-model, and the 'minimum number of copies' parameter belongs to inference components, not to multi-model endpoints, making the option technically invalid.","why_zh":"Multi-model endpoint 會依需求從 Amazon S3 動態下載並快取模型；MME 文件明確警告應用程式必須『容忍偶發的 cold start 相關延遲』，因此違反 no-cold-start 需求。MME 也以單一共用政策對整個 fleet 進行 auto scaling（非每個模型獨立），且『minimum number of copies』是 inference component 的參數而非 multi-model endpoint 的參數，使此選項在技術上不成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/realtime-endpoints-deploy-models.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/serverless-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/multi-model-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/async-inference.html"]}},{"id":92,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon SageMaker for its ML process. A compliance audit discovers that an Amazon S3 bucket for training data uses server-side encryption with S3 managed keys (SSE-S3). The company requires customer managed keys. An ML engineer changes the S3 bucket to use server- side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS). The ML engineer makes no other configuration changes. After the change to the encryption settings, SageMaker training jobs start to fail with AccessDenied errors. What should the ML engineer do to resolve this problem?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 SageMaker 进行其机器学习流程。合规审计发现，用于训练数据的亚马逊 S3 存 储桶使用了服务器端加密且采用 S3 管理的密钥（SSE-S3）。 该公司要求客户管理密钥。一位机器学习工程师将 S3 存储桶更改为使用 AWS KMS 密钥的服务器端 加密（SSE-KMS）。该机器学习工程师未进行其他配置更改。 更改加密设置后，SageMaker 训练作业开始因访问被拒绝错误而失败。 机器学习工程师应该怎么做才能解决这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Update the IAM policy that is attached to the execution role for the training jobs. Include the s3:ListBucket and s3:GetObject permissions.","B":"Update the S3 bucket policy that is attached to the S3 bucket. Set the value of the aws:SecureTransport condition key to True.","C":"Update the IAM policy that is attached to the execution role for the training jobs. Include the kms:Encrypt and kms:Decrypt permissions.","D":"Update the IAM policy that is attached to the user that created the training jobs. Include the kms:CreateGrant permission."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新附加到训练作业执行角色的 IAM 策略。包含 s3:ListBucket 和 s3:GetObject 权限。","B":"更新附加到 S3 存储桶的 S3 存储桶策略。将 aws:SecureTransport 条件键的值设 置为 True。","C":"更新附加到训练作业执行角色的 IAM 策略。包含 kms:Encrypt 和 kms:Decrypt 权限。","D":"更新与创建训练作业的用户关联的 IAM 策略。包含 kms:CreateGrant 权限。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The training jobs succeeded under SSE-S3, which requires no AWS KMS permissions, and the only change was switching the bucket's default encryption to SSE-KMS with a customer managed key. Therefore the SageMaker execution role already had the needed S3 permissions (s3:ListBucket, s3:GetObject), and the new AccessDenied is purely a KMS authorization failure: the role has no permission on the customer managed key. The Amazon S3 documentation states the requirement explicitly: 'To download an object encrypted with an AWS KMS key, you need kms:Decrypt permissions for the key,' and PutObject under SSE-KMS needs kms:GenerateDataKey. Option C is the only choice that adds KMS permissions (including kms:Decrypt) to the execution role that actually runs the jobs, so it directly resolves the failure to read the SSE-KMS-encrypted training data. The strictly precise write action would be kms:GenerateDataKey rather than kms:Encrypt because S3 uses envelope encryption, but a training job's blocking need is decrypt, and C is the only option that grants KMS access to the correct principal, making it the best and correct answer.","explanation_zh":"訓練工作在 SSE-S3 下原本成功,而 SSE-S3 不需要任何 AWS KMS 權限;唯一的變更是把 bucket 的預設加密改為使用 customer managed key 的 SSE-KMS。因此 SageMaker execution role 早已具備所需的 S3 權限(s3:ListBucket、s3:GetObject),新出現的 AccessDenied 純粹是 KMS 授權失敗:該 role 對 customer managed key 沒有權限。Amazon S3 文件明確指出此需求:『要下載以 AWS KMS key 加密的物件,需要該 key 的 kms:Decrypt 權限』,而在 SSE-KMS 下執行 PutObject 則需要 kms:GenerateDataKey。選項 C 是唯一為實際執行工作的 execution role 新增 KMS 權限(含 kms:Decrypt)的選項,直接解決無法讀取 SSE-KMS 加密訓練資料的問題。嚴格來說寫入應使用 kms:GenerateDataKey 而非 kms:Encrypt(因 S3 採用 envelope encryption),但訓練工作的關鍵阻礙是解密能力,且 C 是唯一將 KMS 存取權授予正確 principal 的選項,故為最佳且正確的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"s3:ListBucket and s3:GetObject were already granted because the jobs succeeded under SSE-S3 (which needs no KMS permission); the encryption change did not remove any S3 permission, so re-adding S3 actions does not address the KMS-based AccessDenied.","why_zh":"s3:ListBucket 與 s3:GetObject 早已具備,因為在 SSE-S3 下工作原本就成功(SSE-S3 不需 KMS 權限);更改加密並未移除任何 S3 權限,因此再加一次 S3 動作無法解決源自 KMS 的 AccessDenied。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"aws:SecureTransport only enforces HTTPS/TLS in transit and grants no KMS access; setting it to True as a bucket-policy condition cannot provide decrypt rights and would only further restrict access, so it cannot fix a KMS AccessDenied.","why_zh":"aws:SecureTransport 僅強制傳輸使用 HTTPS/TLS,完全不授予任何 KMS 存取權;在 bucket policy 中將其設為 True 無法提供解密權限,只會進一步限制存取,因此無法修復 KMS 的 AccessDenied。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The principal that runs the training jobs and reads the data is the SageMaker execution role, not the IAM user who launched them; and kms:CreateGrant alone does not grant kms:Decrypt of the existing encrypted objects, so it does not resolve the read failure.","why_zh":"執行訓練工作並讀取資料的 principal 是 SageMaker execution role,而非啟動工作的 IAM 使用者;且僅有 kms:CreateGrant 並不會授予對既有加密物件的 kms:Decrypt 權限,因此無法解決讀取失敗。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingKMSEncryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/specifying-kms-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/sagemaker-roles-start-eoj-perms.html","https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/s3-bucket-access-default-encryption"]}},{"id":93,"question_en":"A company runs training jobs on Amazon SageMaker by using a compute optimized instance. Demand for training runs will remain constant for the next 55 weeks. The instance needs to run for 35 hours each week. The company needs to reduce its model training costs. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊 SageMaker 上使用计算优化型实例运行训练任务。未来 55 周内，训练任务的需求 将保持不变。该实例每周需要运行 35 小时。该公司需要降低其模型训练成本。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use a serverless endpoint with a provisioned concurrency of 35 hours for each week. Run the training on the endpoint.","B":"Use SageMaker Edge Manager for the training. Specify the instance requirement in the edge device configuration. Run the training.","C":"Use the heterogeneous cluster feature of SageMaker Training. Configure the instance_type, instance_count, and instance_groups arguments to run training jobs.","D":"Opt in to a SageMaker Savings Plan with a 1-year term and an All Upfront payment. Run a SageMaker Training job on the instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"每周使用一个具有 35 小时预配置并发量的无服务器端点。在该端点上运行训练。","B":"使用 SageMaker Edge Manager 进行训练。在边缘设备配置中指定实例需求。运行训练。","C":"使用 SageMaker Training 的异构集群功能。配置 instance_type、instance_count 和 instance_ groups 参数以运行训练任务。","D":"选择订阅为期 1 年且采用全额预付的 SageMaker 节省计划。在该实例上运行 SageMaker 训练作业。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The workload is predictable and sustained: constant demand for 55 weeks, 35 hours each week on a single compute-optimized instance. That steady, committable usage pattern is the textbook case for a committed-use discount. AWS documents four Savings Plans types, and SageMaker AI Savings Plans provide up to 64% savings off On-Demand rates and apply automatically to SageMaker AI instance usage regardless of instance family, size, or Region, and across components 'for example, Notebook, Training, etc.' so the discount covers SageMaker Training jobs. Opting in to a 1-year term with All Upfront payment maximizes the discount and matches the ~55-week (roughly 1-year) horizon while you keep running normal SageMaker Training jobs on the same instance, directly reducing training cost. The other options do not lower the compute rate: heterogeneous clusters (C) only improve price-performance by mixing CPU/GPU instance types to fix a resource bottleneck (which is not described here and can add instances/cost), serverless endpoints (A) serve inference rather than training and provisioned concurrency is not measured in hours, and SageMaker Edge Manager (B) deploys and manages models on edge devices for inference and cannot run training.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載可預測且持續：55 週需求固定、每週執行 35 小時於單一 compute-optimized 執行個體。如此穩定且可承諾的使用型態，正是承諾使用折扣的典型案例。AWS 提供四種 Savings Plans，其中 SageMaker AI Savings Plans 相較 On-Demand 可省下最高 64%，並自動套用於 SageMaker AI 的執行個體使用量（不論 instance family、size、Region），且涵蓋各 component（文件明列「例如 Notebook、Training 等」），因此折扣適用於 SageMaker Training job。選擇 1-year term 搭配 All Upfront 付款可最大化折扣，且與約 55 週（約一年）的時程相符，同時仍在同一執行個體上照常執行 SageMaker Training job，直接降低訓練成本。其他選項都無法降低運算費率：heterogeneous cluster（C）僅透過混合 CPU/GPU 執行個體類型解決資源瓶頸以改善性價比（題目並未描述此瓶頸，且可能因增加執行個體而提高成本）；serverless endpoint（A）用於推論而非訓練，且 provisioned concurrency 並非以小時計；SageMaker Edge Manager（B）用於在邊緣裝置部署與管理模型做推論，無法執行訓練。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Serverless inference endpoints serve inference, not training; you cannot run a training job on an endpoint, and provisioned concurrency is configured as concurrent capacity, not in hours per week.","why_zh":"Serverless 推論端點用於推論而非訓練；無法在端點上執行訓練 job，且 provisioned concurrency 是以並行容量設定，並非以每週小時數計。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"SageMaker Edge Manager deploys and manages models on edge devices for inference; it does not perform model training, so it cannot reduce training costs.","why_zh":"SageMaker Edge Manager 用於在邊緣裝置部署與管理模型做推論，並不執行模型訓練，因此無法降低訓練成本。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Heterogeneous clusters improve price-performance by mixing CPU and GPU instance types to resolve a resource bottleneck (e.g., CPU bottleneck causing low GPU utilization). No such bottleneck is described, this does not provide a committed-use discount, and adding instance groups can increase total cost.","why_zh":"Heterogeneous cluster 透過混合 CPU 與 GPU 執行個體類型解決資源瓶頸（例如 CPU 瓶頸導致 GPU 使用率低）以改善性價比。題目並未描述此類瓶頸，且它不提供承諾使用折扣，新增 instance group 反而可能提高總成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/savingsplans/latest/userguide/plan-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/savingsplans/latest/userguide/what-is-savings-plans.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/train-heterogeneous-cluster.html"]}},{"id":94,"question_en":"HOTSPOT A company needs to train an ML model that will use historical transaction data to predict customer behavior. Select the correct AWS service from the following list to perform each task on the data. Each service should be selected one time or not at all. Amazon Athena AWS Glue Amazon Kinesis Data Streams Amazon S3 Hot Area: Correct Answer: Section: (none) Explanation/Reference: Explanation: Query the data: Amazon Athena Amazon Athena is an interactive query service that allows you to analyze structured data stored in Amazon S3 using SQL. It is ideal for querying historical transaction data. Store the data: Amazon S3 Amazon S3 is a scalable and durable storage service used to store large amounts of historical transaction data, making it the best choice for data storage in this scenario. Transform the data: AWS Glue AWS Glue is a fully managed extract, transform, and load (ETL) service that helps clean, normalize, and prepare data for ML model training.","question_zh":"热点 一家公司需要训练一个机器学习模型，该模型将利用历史交易数据来预测客户行为。 从以下列表中选择正确的 AWS 服务来对数据执行每项任务。每个服务只能选择一次或根本不 选。 Amazon Athena AWS Glue 亚马逊 Kinesis 数据流 亚马逊 S3 热点区域： 正确答案： 部分：（无） 解释/参考： 解释： 查询数据：Amazon Athena Amazon Athena 是一项交互式查询服务，可让您使用 SQL 分析存储在 Amazon S3 中的结构化数据。它非常 适合查询历史交易数据。 存储数据：亚马逊 S3 服务 亚马逊 S3 是一种可扩展且持久的存储服务，用于存储大量历史交易数据，因此在这种情况下是数据存储的 最佳选择。 转换数据：AWS Glue AWS Glue 是一项完全托管的提取、转换和加载（ETL）服务，有助于清理、规范化和准备数据以用于机 器学习模型训练。","options_en":{},"options_zh":{},"answer":[],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":95,"question_en":"A company deployed an ML model that uses the XGBoost algorithm to predict product failures. The model is hosted on an Amazon SageMaker endpoint and is trained on normal operating data. An AWS Lambda function provides the predictions to the company's application. An ML engineer must implement a solution that uses incoming live data to detect decreased model accuracy over time. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司部署了一个使用 XGBoost 算法的机器学习模型，用于预测产品故障。该模型托管在亚马逊 SageMaker 端点上，并基于正常运行数据进行训练。一个 AWS Lambda 函数将预测结果提供给该公司的应 用程序。 一位机器学习工程师必须实现一种解决方案，利用实时传入的数据来检测模型准确率随时间的下降 情况。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon CloudWatch to create a dashboard that monitors real-time inference data and model predictions. Use the dashboard to detect drift.","B":"Modify the Lambda function to calculate model drift by using real-time inference data and model predictions. Program the Lambda function to send alerts.","C":"Schedule a monitoring job in SageMaker Model Monitor. Use the job to detect drift by analyzing the live data against a baseline of the training data statistics and constraints.","D":"Schedule a monitoring job in SageMaker Debugger. Use the job to detect drift by analyzing the live data against a baseline of the training data statistics and constraints."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 创建一个仪表板，用于监控实时推理数据和模型预测。利用该仪表板检测 漂移。","B":"修改 Lambda 函数，通过使用实时推理数据和模型预测来计算模型漂移。编写 Lambda 函数以发送 警报。","C":"在 SageMaker 模型监控器中安排一个监控任务。使用该任务通过将实时数据与训练数据的统计信息和约 束条件的基线进行对比来检测数据漂移。","D":"在 SageMaker Debugger 中安排一个监控任务。使用该任务通过将实时数据与训练数据的统计信息和 约束条件的基线进行对比来检测数据漂移。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to use incoming live inference data to detect decreased model accuracy over time relative to the data the model was trained on. Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor is purpose-built for exactly this. The Data quality monitoring doc states verbatim: 'If the statistical nature of the data that your model receives while in production drifts away from the nature of the baseline data it was trained on, the model begins to lose accuracy in its predictions. Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor uses rules to detect data drift and alerts you when it happens.' The Model Monitor workflow is to capture live inference inputs and outputs from the endpoint, create a baseline from the training dataset that computes schema constraints and statistics, and run scheduled monitoring jobs that compare live predictions against those constraints, reporting violations and integrating with CloudWatch for alerts. This matches option C precisely. Option D names SageMaker Debugger, which debugs training jobs in real time (overfitting, vanishing gradients, non-converging issues) and does not analyze live production inference data against a training baseline.","explanation_zh":"需求是利用傳入的即時推論資料,偵測模型相對於訓練資料而言隨時間下降的準確度。Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor 正是為此設計。Data quality 監控文件明確指出:當生產環境中模型接收到的資料其統計特性,偏離模型訓練時所依據的 baseline 資料時,模型的預測準確度就會開始下降;SageMaker Model Monitor 會使用 rules 偵測 data drift 並在發生時發出警示。Model Monitor 的流程是:擷取 endpoint 的即時推論輸入與輸出、由訓練資料集建立 baseline(計算 schema constraints 與 statistics),並排程 monitoring job,將即時預測與這些 constraints 比對,回報 violations 並整合 CloudWatch 發送警示。這完全對應選項 C。選項 D 提到 SageMaker Debugger,它是即時除錯訓練作業(overfitting、vanishing gradients、不收斂等問題),並不會將即時生產推論資料與訓練 baseline 進行比對。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CloudWatch dashboard only visualizes metrics; it does not compute a baseline from training data or run statistical drift detection comparing live data to that baseline. Detecting drift would require manual interpretation rather than an automated rules-based comparison.","why_zh":"CloudWatch dashboard 僅將指標視覺化,無法從訓練資料計算 baseline,也不會執行將即時資料與該 baseline 比較的統計式 drift 偵測。偵測 drift 需要人工判讀,而非自動化的規則比較。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Hand-coding drift calculation and alerting inside the Lambda function requires building and maintaining custom statistical baselining and drift logic, which is exactly the undifferentiated tooling that SageMaker Model Monitor provides out of the box. It is high operational overhead and error-prone compared to the managed service.","why_zh":"在 Lambda function 中自行撰寫 drift 計算與警示,需要自行建置與維護自訂的統計 baseline 與 drift 邏輯,而這正是 SageMaker Model Monitor 已內建提供的功能。相較於受管服務,此方式營運負擔高且容易出錯。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SageMaker Debugger operates on training jobs in real time to catch issues like overfitting, vanishing gradients, and non-converging tensors. It does not consume live production inference data from an endpoint nor compare it to a training-data baseline, so it cannot detect production model drift over time.","why_zh":"SageMaker Debugger 是在訓練作業執行期間即時運作,用以捕捉 overfitting、vanishing gradients、tensor 不收斂等問題。它不會取用 endpoint 的即時生產推論資料,也不會與訓練資料 baseline 比較,因此無法偵測生產模型隨時間產生的 drift。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-data-quality.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-create-baseline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/train-debugger.html"]}},{"id":96,"question_en":"A company has an ML model that uses historical transaction data to predict customer behavior. An ML engineer is optimizing the model in Amazon SageMaker to enhance the model's predictive accuracy. The ML engineer must examine the input data and the resulting predictions to identify trends that could skew the model's performance across different demographics. Which solution will provide this level of analysis?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个机器学习模型，该模型利用历史交易数据来预测客户行为。一位机器学习工程师正在亚 马逊 SageMaker 中优化该模型，以提高其预测准确性。这位机器学习工程师必须检查输入数据和生成的预 测结果，以识别可能使模型在不同人口群体中的表现产生偏差的趋势。 哪种解决方案能提供这种程度的分析？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor network metrics and CPU metrics for resource optimization during model training.","B":"Create AWS Glue DataBrew recipes to correct the data based on statistics from the model output.","C":"Use SageMaker Clarify to evaluate the model and training data for underlying patterns that might affect accuracy.","D":"Create AWS Lambda functions to automate data pre-processing and to ensure consistent quality of input data for the model."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用亚马逊 CloudWatch 监控网络指标和 CPU 指标，以在模型训练期间优化资源。","B":"创建 AWS Glue DataBrew 配方，根据模型输出的统计信息来校正数据。","C":"使用 SageMaker Clarify 对模型和训练数据进行评估，以查找可能影响准确性的潜在模式。","D":"创建 AWS Lambda 函数以实现数据预处理的自动化，并确保数据质量的一致性。 模型的输入数据。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement is to examine BOTH the input/training data AND the resulting predictions to surface trends (bias) that could skew model performance across demographics. Amazon SageMaker Clarify is purpose-built for this: the official docs state it 'helps you identify various types of bias in pre-training data and in post-training that can emerge during model training or when the model is in production,' and it provides model explainability via SHAP feature attributions. Clarify lets you define demographic attributes as 'facets' and computes pre-training bias metrics on observed labels (input data) and post-training bias metrics on predicted labels (model output), revealing how outcomes differ across groups. This is exactly the data-plus-predictions, cross-demographic analysis the question asks for. The other options do not analyze data and predictions for demographic skew: CloudWatch (A) tracks resource/infrastructure metrics; Glue DataBrew (B) transforms/cleans data; Lambda (D) automates preprocessing for consistent input quality.","explanation_zh":"題目要求同時檢視輸入/訓練資料與模型預測結果，找出可能造成模型在不同人口族群間表現偏差（bias）的趨勢。Amazon SageMaker Clarify 正是為此設計：官方文件指出它可協助識別訓練前（pre-training）資料中的偏差，以及訓練後（post-training）在模型訓練或上線後出現的偏差，並透過 SHAP 特徵歸因提供模型可解釋性（model explainability）。Clarify 可將人口屬性定義為 facets，對觀測標籤（輸入資料）計算 pre-training bias metrics、對預測標籤（模型輸出）計算 post-training bias metrics，揭示不同族群間結果的差異，完全符合題目要求的「資料加預測、跨族群」分析。其他選項皆無法分析資料與預測以找出族群偏差：CloudWatch（A）監控資源/基礎設施指標；Glue DataBrew（B）用於轉換/清理資料；Lambda（D）自動化前處理以確保輸入品質一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon CloudWatch monitors network and CPU/infrastructure metrics for resource optimization during training. It does not analyze input data or predictions for bias or demographic skew, so it cannot fulfill the requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon CloudWatch 監控訓練期間的網路與 CPU/基礎設施指標以最佳化資源，無法分析輸入資料或預測中的偏差或族群差異，因此無法滿足需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Glue DataBrew recipes transform and clean data. They do not evaluate model predictions for bias or measure how outcomes differ across demographic groups; correcting data based on output statistics is remediation/transformation, not bias analysis.","why_zh":"AWS Glue DataBrew recipes 用於轉換與清理資料，無法評估模型預測的偏差，也無法衡量不同族群間結果的差異；依輸出統計修正資料屬於修正/轉換，並非偏差分析。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Lambda functions can automate data pre-processing to ensure consistent input quality, but they do not examine predictions or compute bias metrics across demographic facets, so they do not provide the required analytical examination.","why_zh":"AWS Lambda 函式可自動化資料前處理以確保輸入品質一致，但無法檢視預測結果或對族群 facets 計算偏差指標，因此無法提供題目要求的分析性檢視。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-explainability.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-configure-processing-jobs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-measure-data-bias.html"]}},{"id":97,"question_en":"A company uses 10 Reserved Instances of accelerated instance types to serve the current version of an ML model. An ML engineer needs to deploy a new version of the model to an Amazon SageMaker real- time inference endpoint. The solution must use the original 10 instances to serve both versions of the model. The solution also must include one additional Reserved Instance that is available to use in the deployment process. The transition between versions must occur with no downtime or service interruptions. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 10 个加速实例类型的预留实例来运行当前版本的机器学习模型。一位机器学习工程师 需要将该模型的新版本部署到 Amazon SageMaker 实时推理端点。 该解决方案必须使用原有的 10 个预留实例来支持两个版本的模型。该解决方案还必须包含一个额外的 预留实例，以便在部署过程中使用。两个版本之间的切换必须在不造成停机或服务中断的情况下进行。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a blue/green deployment with all-at-once traffic shifting.","B":"Configure a blue/green deployment with canary traffic shifting and a size of 10%.","C":"Configure a shadow test with a traffic sampling percentage of 10%.","D":"Configure a rolling deployment with a rolling batch size of 1."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个蓝绿部署，并一次性完成流量切换。","B":"配置蓝绿部署，启用金丝雀流量切换，并将流量切换比例设为 10%。","C":"配置一个影子测试，流量采样百分比为 10%。","D":"配置一个滚动部署，滚动批次大小为 1。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The binding constraint is capacity. Only ONE additional Reserved Instance is available, both model versions must serve traffic during the transition, and there can be no downtime. A SageMaker rolling deployment incrementally provisions capacity in batches and cleans up old instances after each traffic shift, so it 'reduces the amount of additional instances needed' and is 'useful especially for accelerated instances that are in high demand' (the exact scenario here). The docs state rolling deployments have 'reduced capacity requirements' versus blue/green because 'fewer instances are active at a time,' and the endpoint requires extra capacity 'roughly the batch size overhead.' A rolling batch size of 1 instance equals 10% of a 10-instance fleet, which is within the allowed 5-50% range. SageMaker provisions 1 new instance (the single spare), shifts a portion of traffic, bakes, cleans up 1 old instance, and repeats - so both versions run on the original 10 instances plus only 1 extra, with no downtime. Blue/green (A and B) instead 'provisions the green fleet' (a full 10-instance green fleet) alongside the blue fleet, needing ~10 extra instances; the canary size in B only controls the traffic percentage routed, not the instances provisioned. Shadow testing (C) deploys a separate shadow variant and returns 'only the responses of the production variant' to clients, so it validates rather than serving both versions to users, and it adds a separate fleet rather than fitting the 1-instance budget.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限制是容量。只有一個額外的 Reserved Instance 可用,兩個模型版本必須在轉換期間同時提供服務,且不能有停機。SageMaker rolling deployment 以批次方式逐步佈建容量,並在每次流量轉移後清除舊 instance,因此能'減少更新端點所需的額外 instance 數量',且'特別適用於需求量高的 accelerated instance'(正是本題情境)。官方文件指出相較於 blue/green,rolling deployment '降低容量需求',因為'同一時間活躍的 instance 較少',端點所需的額外容量'大約等於批次大小的額外負擔'。rolling batch size 設為 1 個 instance 等於 10 個 instance fleet 的 10%,落在允許的 5-50% 範圍內。SageMaker 佈建 1 個新 instance(那唯一備用的 instance),轉移部分流量,經過 baking 期,清除 1 個舊 instance,如此重複,因此兩個版本在原本 10 個 instance 加上僅 1 個額外 instance 上運行,且無停機。Blue/green(A 與 B)則會在 blue fleet 旁'佈建完整的 green fleet'(整組 10 個 green instance),需約 10 個額外 instance;B 的 canary size 僅控制路由的流量百分比,不影響佈建的 instance 數量。Shadow test(C)會部署獨立的 shadow variant,且'只將 production variant 的回應'傳回客戶端,因此是驗證工具而非對使用者同時提供兩個版本服務,且會新增獨立 fleet 而非符合 1 個 instance 的預算。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Blue/green all-at-once provisions a full green fleet of 10 instances alongside the blue fleet, requiring ~10 additional instances - far more than the single spare. It also shifts all traffic at once with no gradual safety guardrail.","why_zh":"Blue/green all-at-once 會在 blue fleet 旁佈建完整的 10 個 green instance,需約 10 個額外 instance,遠超過唯一備用 instance。且一次性轉移全部流量,缺乏漸進式安全機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Blue/green canary still 'provisions the green fleet' (a full 10 instances) next to the blue fleet; the 10% canary controls only the traffic percentage routed, not the number of instances provisioned. It needs ~10 extra instances, exceeding the single available spare.","why_zh":"Blue/green canary 仍會在 blue fleet 旁'佈建 green fleet'(整組 10 個 instance);10% canary 僅控制路由的流量百分比,不影響佈建的 instance 數量。需約 10 個額外 instance,超過唯一可用備用 instance。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Shadow testing deploys a separate shadow variant that receives a copy of sampled traffic, but 'only the responses of the production variant are returned to the calling application.' It is a validation tool, not a zero-downtime production transition, and it adds a separate fleet rather than serving both production versions on the original 10 instances within the 1-instance budget.","why_zh":"Shadow test 會部署獨立的 shadow variant 接收採樣流量的副本,但'只將 production variant 的回應傳回呼叫的應用程式'。它是驗證工具,而非零停機的正式版本轉換,且會新增獨立 fleet,而非在原本 10 個 instance 上於 1 個 instance 預算內同時提供兩個正式版本服務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/deployment-guardrails-rolling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/deployment-guardrails.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/deployment-guardrails-blue-green-canary.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/shadow-tests.html"]}},{"id":98,"question_en":"An IoT company uses Amazon SageMaker to train and test an XGBoost model for object detection. ML engineers need to monitor performance metrics when they train the model with variants in hyperparameters. The ML engineers also need to send Short Message Service (SMS) text messages after training is complete. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家物联网公司使用亚马逊 SageMaker 来训练和测试用于对象检测的 XGBoost 模型。机器学习工程师 在使用不同超参数变体训练模型时需要监控性能指标。训练完成后，机器学习工程师还需要发送短信。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor performance metrics. Use Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) for message delivery.","B":"Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor performance metrics. Use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) for message delivery.","C":"Use AWS CloudTrail to monitor performance metrics. Use Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) for message delivery.","D":"Use AWS CloudTrail to monitor performance metrics. Use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) for message delivery."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 监控性能指标。使用 Amazon 简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）进行消 息传递。","B":"使用亚马逊 CloudWatch 监控性能指标。使用亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）进行消息传递。","C":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 监控性能指标。使用亚马逊简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）进行消息传递。","D":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 监控性能指标。使用亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）进行消息传 递。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements drive the answer: monitoring training performance metrics across hyperparameter variants, and sending SMS messages when training completes. Amazon SageMaker writes training metrics (such as training error and accuracy) to logs and sends them to Amazon CloudWatch in real time, where you can view and graph them to compare runs that use different hyperparameters. AWS CloudTrail only records API and management events for audit and governance, so it cannot monitor algorithm performance metrics, ruling out options C and D. For notifications, Amazon SNS natively publishes SMS text messages directly to mobile phone numbers (or via a topic), whereas Amazon SQS is a point-to-point queue for decoupling application components and cannot deliver SMS, ruling out options A and C. Only option B pairs CloudWatch (metrics) with SNS (SMS), so it is correct.","explanation_zh":"兩個需求決定了答案:在不同 hyperparameter 變體下監控訓練效能指標,以及在訓練完成後發送 SMS 簡訊。Amazon SageMaker 會將訓練指標(例如訓練誤差與準確度)寫入日誌並即時送往 Amazon CloudWatch,你可在其中檢視並繪製圖表,以比較使用不同 hyperparameter 的訓練執行。AWS CloudTrail 只記錄 API 與管理事件以供稽核與治理,無法監控演算法效能指標,因此排除選項 C 與 D。在通知方面,Amazon SNS 原生支援直接(或透過 topic)向行動電話號碼發布 SMS 簡訊,而 Amazon SQS 是用於解耦應用程式元件的點對點佇列,無法傳遞 SMS,因此排除選項 A 與 C。只有選項 B 將 CloudWatch(指標)與 SNS(SMS)搭配,因此為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudWatch correctly handles performance metrics, but Amazon SQS is a point-to-point message queue for decoupling application components and cannot deliver SMS text messages to phones. SMS delivery requires Amazon SNS.","why_zh":"CloudWatch 正確處理效能指標,但 Amazon SQS 是用於解耦應用程式元件的點對點訊息佇列,無法向手機發送 SMS 簡訊。SMS 傳遞需要 Amazon SNS。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Both halves are wrong: AWS CloudTrail records API/management events for audit, not SageMaker training performance metrics, and Amazon SQS cannot send SMS messages.","why_zh":"兩個部分都錯誤:AWS CloudTrail 記錄用於稽核的 API/管理事件,而非 SageMaker 訓練效能指標,且 Amazon SQS 無法發送 SMS 簡訊。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon SNS is correct for SMS, but AWS CloudTrail only logs API and management events for governance and audit; it does not capture or graph algorithm training performance metrics. SageMaker emits those metrics to CloudWatch.","why_zh":"Amazon SNS 適合發送 SMS,但 AWS CloudTrail 只記錄用於治理與稽核的 API 與管理事件,無法擷取或繪製演算法訓練效能指標。SageMaker 將這些指標送往 CloudWatch。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/training-metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/view-train-metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sms_sending-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-mobile-phone-number-as-subscriber.html"]}},{"id":99,"question_en":"A company is working on an ML project that will include Amazon SageMaker notebook instances. An ML engineer must ensure that the SageMaker notebook instances do not allow root access. Which solution will prevent the deployment of notebook instances that allow root access?","question_zh":"","options_en":{"A":"Use IAM condition keys to stop deployments of SageMaker notebook instances that allow root access.","B":"Use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) keys to stop deployments of SageMaker notebook instances that allow root access.","C":"Monitor resource creation by using Amazon EventBridge events. Create an AWS Lambda function that deletes all deployed SageMaker notebook instances that allow root access.","D":"Monitor resource creation by using AWS CloudFormation events. Create an AWS Lambda function that deletes all deployed SageMaker notebook instances that allow root access."},"options_zh":{},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon SageMaker exposes the IAM condition key sagemaker:RootAccess, which the Service Authorization Reference defines as 'Filters access by the root access associated with the resource in the request' (type String). Because RootAccess is a request field on the CreateNotebookInstance and UpdateNotebookInstance APIs, an ML engineer can attach an IAM identity-based policy or SCP that denies sagemaker:CreateNotebookInstance/UpdateNotebookInstance whenever sagemaker:RootAccess equals Enabled (or is not Disabled). This is a true preventive control: the API call to create a notebook instance with root access is rejected before any resource is provisioned, so the instance is never deployed. The SageMaker doc 'Control root access to a SageMaker notebook instance' confirms RootAccess is set on Create/Update, and the Service Authorization Reference confirms sagemaker:RootAccess is a supported condition key. The question's qualifier 'prevent the deployment' requires a proactive guardrail rather than a detect-and-remediate workflow, making A the only correct choice.","explanation_zh":"Amazon SageMaker 提供 IAM 條件金鑰 sagemaker:RootAccess，Service Authorization Reference 將其定義為「Filters access by the root access associated with the resource in the request」（型別 String）。由於 RootAccess 是 CreateNotebookInstance 與 UpdateNotebookInstance API 的請求欄位，ML engineer 可附加 IAM identity-based policy 或 SCP，當 sagemaker:RootAccess 等於 Enabled（或非 Disabled）時就 Deny sagemaker:CreateNotebookInstance/UpdateNotebookInstance。這是真正的預防性控制：含 root access 的 notebook instance 建立呼叫會在資源佈建前就被拒絕，因此該執行個體根本不會被部署。SageMaker 文件「Control root access to a SageMaker notebook instance」說明 RootAccess 在 Create/Update 時設定，而 Service Authorization Reference 也明列 sagemaker:RootAccess 為支援的條件金鑰。題目限定詞「prevent the deployment」需要主動式護欄，而非偵測後再補救的流程，因此 A 為唯一正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS KMS keys control encryption of data at rest (e.g., the notebook's EBS volume) and are referenced via separate condition keys such as sagemaker:VolumeKmsKeyArn. They have no relationship to OS-level root access on the notebook instance and cannot block creation of an instance with RootAccess enabled.","why_zh":"AWS KMS 金鑰用於控制靜態資料加密（例如 notebook 的 EBS 磁碟區），對應的是 sagemaker:VolumeKmsKeyArn 等其他條件金鑰，與 notebook instance 的 OS 層級 root access 無關，無法阻擋以 RootAccess=Enabled 建立執行個體。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An EventBridge-plus-Lambda workflow that deletes offending instances is detective/reactive, not preventive: the notebook instance is still created (and briefly allows root access) before deletion, so it does not 'prevent the deployment.' It also adds operational overhead versus a single IAM condition key.","why_zh":"用 EventBridge 加 Lambda 刪除違規執行個體屬於偵測/反應式，而非預防式：notebook instance 仍會被建立（並短暫允許 root access）後才被刪除，無法真正『阻止部署』，且相較單一 IAM 條件金鑰增加營運負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same reactive flaw as C, and it relies on CloudFormation events, so it only catches instances created via CloudFormation and only after they exist. It deletes rather than prevents, failing the 'prevent the deployment' requirement.","why_zh":"與 C 同樣是反應式缺陷，且依賴 CloudFormation 事件，僅能在透過 CloudFormation 建立後才偵測到。它是事後刪除而非預防，不符合『阻止部署』的要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/service-authorization/latest/reference/list_amazonsagemaker.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/nbi-root-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/APIReference/API_CreateNotebookInstance.html"]}},{"id":100,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon SageMaker to develop ML models. The company stores sensitive training data in an Amazon S3 bucket. The model training must have network isolation from the internet. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"","options_en":{"A":"Run the SageMaker training jobs in private subnets. Create a NAT gateway. Route traffic for training through the NAT gateway.","B":"Run the SageMaker training jobs in private subnets. Create an S3 gateway VPC endpoint. Route traffic for training through the S3 gateway VPC endpoint.","C":"Run the SageMaker training jobs in public subnets that have an attached security group. In the security group, use inbound rules to limit traffic from the internet. Encrypt SageMaker instance storage by using server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS).","D":"Encrypt traffic to Amazon S3 by using a bucket policy that includes a value of True for the aws:SecureTransport condition key. Use default at-rest encryption for Amazon S3. Encrypt SageMaker instance storage by using server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS)."},"options_zh":{},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"To isolate SageMaker training jobs from the internet while still reaching the sensitive training data in Amazon S3, AWS recommends running the training jobs in an Amazon VPC with private subnets that have no internet access, and then creating an Amazon S3 gateway VPC endpoint so the training containers reach the S3 bucket over the AWS private network. The SageMaker doc 'Give SageMaker AI Training Jobs Access to Resources in Your Amazon VPC' states: 'To control access to your training jobs, run them in an Amazon VPC with private subnets that don't have internet access' and 'If you configure your VPC so that training containers don't have access to the internet, they can't connect to the Amazon S3 buckets that contain your training data unless you create a VPC endpoint that allows access.' This exactly matches option B and meets the network-isolation-from-the-internet requirement. The other options fail: a NAT gateway grants outbound internet access (the opposite of isolation), public subnets route to an internet gateway, and a bucket policy with aws:SecureTransport plus encryption only enforce TLS in transit and at-rest confidentiality, not network isolation.","explanation_zh":"若要讓 SageMaker 訓練作業與網際網路隔離，同時仍能存取存放於 Amazon S3 的敏感訓練資料，AWS 建議將訓練作業執行於沒有網際網路存取的私有子網路 (private subnet) 的 Amazon VPC 中，並建立 Amazon S3 gateway VPC endpoint，讓訓練容器透過 AWS 私有網路存取 S3 儲存貯體。SageMaker 官方文件「Give SageMaker AI Training Jobs Access to Resources in Your Amazon VPC」指出：應在沒有網際網路存取的私有子網路執行訓練作業以控管存取；若 VPC 設定使訓練容器無法存取網際網路，則除非建立 VPC endpoint，否則無法連線到存放訓練資料的 S3 儲存貯體。這正好符合選項 B 並滿足與網際網路隔離的需求。其他選項皆不符合：NAT gateway 反而提供對外網際網路存取（與隔離相反）；public subnet 會路由至 internet gateway；而使用 aws:SecureTransport 的 bucket policy 加上加密只能強制傳輸中 TLS 與靜態加密的機密性，並非網路隔離。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A NAT gateway exists specifically to GIVE private-subnet instances outbound internet access. Routing training traffic through a NAT gateway therefore connects the training job to the internet, which is the opposite of network isolation from the internet.","why_zh":"NAT gateway 的用途正是讓私有子網路中的執行個體取得對外網際網路存取。將訓練流量導向 NAT gateway 反而會讓訓練作業連上網際網路，與「與網際網路隔離」的需求完全相反。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Public subnets have a route to an internet gateway, so by definition they are not isolated from the internet. Security group inbound rules and SSE-KMS storage encryption address access control and at-rest encryption, not network isolation, so they do not meet the requirement.","why_zh":"Public subnet 具有通往 internet gateway 的路由，依定義並未與網際網路隔離。安全群組的入站規則與 SSE-KMS 儲存加密處理的是存取控制與靜態加密，而非網路隔離，因此無法滿足需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An aws:SecureTransport bucket policy only forces requests to use TLS/HTTPS, and default at-rest plus SSE-KMS encryption only protect data confidentiality. None of these isolate the workload from the internet; traffic to S3 would still traverse the public S3 endpoint over the internet, failing the network-isolation requirement.","why_zh":"aws:SecureTransport bucket policy 僅強制請求使用 TLS/HTTPS，預設靜態加密與 SSE-KMS 只保護資料機密性。這些都無法讓工作負載與網際網路隔離；前往 S3 的流量仍會經由公開的 S3 端點透過網際網路傳輸，無法滿足網路隔離的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/train-vpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonVPC/latest/UserGuide/vpc-endpoints-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonVPC/latest/UserGuide/vpce-gateway.html"]}},{"id":101,"question_en":"A company needs an AWS solution that will automatically create versions of ML models as the models are created. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司需要一个 AWS 解决方案，能够在创建机器学习模型时自动为这些模型创建版本。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR)","B":"Model packages from Amazon SageMaker Marketplace","C":"Amazon SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking","D":"Amazon SageMaker Model Registry"},"options_zh":{"A":"亚马逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）","B":"来自亚马逊 SageMaker 市场的模型包","C":"亚马逊 SageMaker 机器学习血统追踪","D":"亚马逊 SageMaker 模型注册表"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon SageMaker Model Registry is purpose-built to catalog and automatically version ML models as they are created. Per the AWS docs, the registry is structured as Model (Package) Groups: 'The version of each model package is a numerical value that starts at 1 and is incremented with each new model package added to a Model Group... The Model Registry receives every new model that you retrain, gives it a version, and assigns it to a Model Group.' This precisely matches the requirement of automatically creating versions of models as they are created. ML Lineage Tracking (C) only creates and stores metadata about workflow steps (training jobs, datasets, pipelines, endpoints) for reproducibility, governance, and audit; it does not version models. ECR (A) is a container image registry, not an ML model-versioning service. The same Model Registry doc explicitly states that AWS Marketplace model packages (B) 'are not versionable entities and are not associated with Model Groups,' so they cannot auto-version models.","explanation_zh":"Amazon SageMaker Model Registry 專為在模型建立時自動建立版本而設計。根據 AWS 文件，Model Registry 以 Model (Package) Groups 結構組織：每個 model package 的版本是從 1 開始的數值，每當有新的 model package 加入 Model Group 時就會遞增；Model Registry 會接收你每次重新訓練的新模型，賦予版本並指派到對應的 Model Group。這正好符合「在模型建立時自動建立版本」的需求。ML Lineage Tracking (C) 只建立並儲存工作流程步驟（training jobs、datasets、pipelines、endpoints）的中繼資料，用於可重現性、治理與稽核，並不會替模型建立版本。ECR (A) 是容器映像登錄檔，並非 ML 模型版本控管服務。同一份 Model Registry 文件明確指出 AWS Marketplace 的 model packages (B) 不是可版本化的實體，也不與 Model Groups 關聯，因此無法自動為模型建立版本。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon ECR is a container image registry for Docker/OCI images. It versions container images via tags/digests, not ML models, and has no concept of automatically incrementing model versions within a Model Group.","why_zh":"Amazon ECR 是用於 Docker/OCI 映像的容器映像登錄檔。它以標籤/摘要為容器映像建立版本，而非 ML 模型，且沒有在 Model Group 內自動遞增模型版本的概念。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Model packages from AWS Marketplace are explicitly stated in the AWS docs to be 'not versionable entities and are not associated with Model Groups in the Model Registry,' so they cannot automatically version models as they are created.","why_zh":"AWS 文件明確指出來自 AWS Marketplace 的 model packages「不是可版本化的實體，且不與 Model Registry 中的 Model Groups 關聯」，因此無法在模型建立時自動為其建立版本。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking creates and stores metadata about workflow steps (training jobs, datasets, pipelines, endpoints) for reproducibility, governance, and audit. It tracks lineage/relationships but does not assign or increment model versions.","why_zh":"SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking 建立並儲存工作流程步驟（training jobs、datasets、pipelines、endpoints）的中繼資料，用於可重現性、治理與稽核。它追蹤譜系/關聯，但不會指派或遞增模型版本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry-models.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/lineage-tracking.html"]}},{"id":102,"question_en":"A company needs to use Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) to supplement an open source large language model (LLM) that runs on Amazon Bedrock. The company's data for RAG is a set of documents in an Amazon S3 bucket. The documents consist of .csv files and .docx files. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司需要使用检索增强生成（RAG）来补充在亚马逊 Bedrock 上运行的开源大型语言模型（LLM）。 该公司用于 RAG 的数据是一组存储在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中的文档，这些文档包括.csv 文件和.docx 文件。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a pipeline in Amazon SageMaker Pipelines to generate a new model. Call the new model from Amazon Bedrock to perform RAG queries.","B":"Convert the data into vectors. Store the data in an Amazon Neptune database. Connect the database to Amazon Bedrock. Call the Amazon Bedrock API to perform RAG queries.","C":"Fine-tune an existing LLM by using an AutoML job in Amazon SageMaker. Configure the S3 bucket as a data source for the AutoML job. Deploy the LLM to a SageMaker endpoint. Use the endpoint to perform RAG queries.","D":"Create a knowledge base for Amazon Bedrock. Configure a data source that references the S3 bucket. Use the Amazon Bedrock API to perform RAG queries."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon SageMaker Pipelines 中创建一个管道以生成新模型。从 Amazon Bedrock 调用新模型来执行 RAG 查询。","B":"将数据转换为向量。将数据存储在 Amazon Neptune 数据库中。将数据库连接到 Amazon Bedrock。调用 Amazon Bedrock API 来执行 RAG 查询。","C":"使用 Amazon SageMaker 中的 AutoML 作业对现有的语言模型进行微调。将 S3 存储桶配置为 AutoML 作 业的数据源。将语言模型部署到 SageMaker 端点。使用该端点执行 RAG 查询。","D":"为 Amazon Bedrock 创建知识库。配置一个引用 S3 存储桶的数据源。使用 Amazon Bedrock API 执行 RAG 查询。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases is a fully managed Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) capability that implements the entire workflow: it ingests documents from a data source, chunks them, generates embeddings, stores the vectors, keeps them in sync, and serves retrieval and prompt augmentation through the Retrieve and RetrieveAndGenerate APIs. You simply create a knowledge base and configure a data source that points at the S3 bucket. The AWS docs explicitly list both Comma-separated values (.csv) and Microsoft Word document (.doc/.docx) as supported source document formats for an S3 data source, so no custom preprocessing is needed. This is the LEAST operational overhead because Bedrock manages the embedding model, vector store, and ingestion pipeline for you. Every other option requires building and running custom infrastructure: Option A builds a SageMaker pipeline to train a new model, Option B requires manually vectorizing data and standing up/connecting a Neptune database, and Option C fine-tunes and hosts a model on a self-managed SageMaker endpoint. Options A and C also conceptually misframe RAG as a model-training/fine-tuning problem, when RAG augments an existing LLM with retrieved context rather than retraining it.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases 是一個全託管的 Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) 功能，能夠實作整個流程：從 data source 攝取文件、切塊 (chunking)、產生 embeddings、儲存向量、保持同步，並透過 Retrieve 和 RetrieveAndGenerate API 提供檢索與提示增強。你只需建立 knowledge base 並設定一個指向該 S3 bucket 的 data source 即可。AWS 文件明確列出 Comma-separated values (.csv) 與 Microsoft Word document (.doc/.docx) 都是 S3 data source 支援的來源文件格式，因此不需任何自訂前處理。這是營運負擔最低的方案，因為 Bedrock 替你管理 embedding model、向量儲存與攝取管線。其他每個選項都需要自行建置並維運自訂基礎設施：選項 A 用 SageMaker Pipelines 訓練新模型；選項 B 需手動將資料向量化並建立/連接 Neptune 資料庫；選項 C 則需在自管的 SageMaker endpoint 上微調並託管模型。此外，選項 A 與 C 在概念上誤把 RAG 當成模型訓練/微調問題，但 RAG 是用檢索到的內容增強既有 LLM，而非重新訓練它。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Building a SageMaker Pipelines workflow to 'generate a new model' is high operational overhead and conceptually wrong: RAG does not generate or train a new model, it retrieves external context to augment prompts at query time. There is also no native flow to simply call an arbitrary SageMaker-built model from Bedrock for RAG.","why_zh":"建立 SageMaker Pipelines 來『產生新模型』營運負擔高且概念錯誤：RAG 不是訓練或產生新模型，而是在查詢時檢索外部內容來增強提示。也沒有原生流程能直接從 Bedrock 呼叫任意 SageMaker 建出的模型來做 RAG。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Manually converting documents into vectors and standing up/connecting an Amazon Neptune database is the self-managed RAG path with significantly more operational overhead. You would own the embedding generation, vector ingestion, and database management instead of letting Bedrock Knowledge Bases handle it. Although Neptune can serve as a vector store option, doing this manually is not the least-overhead solution.","why_zh":"手動將文件轉成向量並建立/連接 Amazon Neptune 資料庫屬於自管 RAG 路徑，營運負擔明顯更高。你必須自行負責 embedding 產生、向量攝取與資料庫管理，而非交由 Bedrock Knowledge Bases 處理。雖然 Neptune 可作為向量儲存選項，手動建置並非負擔最低的方案。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Fine-tuning an LLM via a SageMaker AutoML job and hosting it on a SageMaker endpoint is both high overhead and the wrong technique. Fine-tuning bakes knowledge into model weights, whereas RAG retrieves external documents at inference time; the question explicitly asks for RAG. Managing AutoML jobs and a self-managed endpoint also far exceeds the overhead of a managed knowledge base.","why_zh":"透過 SageMaker AutoML job 微調 LLM 並託管在 SageMaker endpoint 上，不僅負擔高，技術方向也錯誤。微調是把知識寫入模型權重，而 RAG 是在推論時檢索外部文件；題目明確要求 RAG。管理 AutoML job 與自管 endpoint 的負擔也遠高於使用託管的 knowledge base。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/knowledge-base.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/knowledge-base-ds.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-data-source-sync-ingest.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-managed-create.html"]}},{"id":103,"question_en":"A company plans to deploy an ML model for production inference on an Amazon SageMaker endpoint. The average inference payload size will vary from 100 MB to 300 MB. Inference requests must be processed in 60 minutes or less. Which SageMaker inference option will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司计划在亚马逊 SageMaker 端点上部署一个用于生产推理的机器学习模型。平均推理负载大小 将在 100MB 到 300MB 之间变化。推理请求必须在 60 分钟或更短时间内处理完毕。 哪种 SageMaker 推理选项能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Serverless inference","B":"Asynchronous inference","C":"Real-time inference","D":"Batch transform"},"options_zh":{"A":"无服务器推理","B":"异步推理","C":"实时推理","D":"批量转换"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The official SageMaker inference-options matrix states that Asynchronous Inference 'can support payloads up to 1 GB and long processing times up to one hour,' and it runs on a managed SageMaker endpoint: the client places the payload in Amazon S3, calls InvokeEndpointAsync with a pointer to it, SageMaker queues and processes the request, then writes the result back to S3. This fits the requirements exactly: 100-300 MB payloads (well under the 1 GB limit) and processing within 60 minutes (matching the one-hour ceiling) on a deployed endpoint. Real-time inference supports only up to 25 MB payloads and 60-second processing (8 min for streaming), and serverless inference only up to 4 MB and 60 seconds, so both fail the size and time constraints. Batch transform handles GB-scale datasets and multi-day runs, but it is an offline job with no persistent endpoint, so it does not satisfy the requirement to deploy the model on a SageMaker endpoint for production inference.","explanation_zh":"官方 SageMaker inference options 對照表載明 Asynchronous Inference「可支援最大 1 GB 的 payload 以及長達 1 小時的處理時間」，且是部署在受管的 SageMaker endpoint 上執行：用戶端先把 payload 放到 Amazon S3，透過 InvokeEndpointAsync 傳入指向該檔案的指標，SageMaker 將請求排隊並處理後，再把結果寫回 S3。這完全符合本題需求：100-300 MB payload（遠低於 1 GB 上限）且需在 60 分鐘內完成（正好對應 1 小時上限），並部署於 endpoint 上。Real-time inference 僅支援最大 25 MB payload 與 60 秒處理時間（串流 8 分鐘）；serverless inference 僅支援最大 4 MB 與 60 秒，兩者皆無法滿足大小與時間限制。Batch transform 雖能處理 GB 級資料集與長達數天的作業，但屬離線批次工作、沒有持久化 endpoint，因此不符合題目要求「部署於 SageMaker endpoint」進行生產推論的條件。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Serverless inference supports payloads only up to 4 MB and processing times up to 60 seconds, far below the 100-300 MB payload and 60-minute requirements.","why_zh":"Serverless inference 僅支援最大 4 MB payload 與 60 秒處理時間，遠低於 100-300 MB payload 與 60 分鐘的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Real-time inference caps payloads at 25 MB and processing at 60 seconds (8 min for streaming responses), so it cannot handle 100-300 MB payloads or 60-minute processing.","why_zh":"Real-time inference payload 上限 25 MB、處理時間 60 秒（串流回應 8 分鐘），無法處理 100-300 MB payload 或 60 分鐘的處理時間。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Batch transform can handle GB-scale data and multi-day runs, but it is an offline batch job with no persistent endpoint; the question requires deploying the model on a SageMaker endpoint for production inference, which batch transform does not provide.","why_zh":"Batch transform 可處理 GB 級資料與長時間作業，但屬離線批次作業、沒有持久化 endpoint；題目要求將模型部署於 SageMaker endpoint 進行生產推論，batch transform 並不提供 endpoint。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/deploy-model-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/async-inference.html"]}},{"id":104,"question_en":"An ML engineer notices class imbalance in an image classification training job. What should the ML engineer do to resolve this issue?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师注意到图像分类训练任务中存在类别不平衡的情况。 机器学习工程师应该采取什么措施来解决这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Reduce the size of the dataset.","B":"Transform some of the images in the dataset.","C":"Apply random oversampling on the dataset.","D":"Apply random data splitting on the dataset."},"options_zh":{"A":"减小数据集的规模。","B":"对数据集中的部分图像进行转换。","C":"对数据集应用随机过采样。","D":"对数据集进行随机数据划分。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Random oversampling is the canonical, AWS-documented technique for directly resolving class imbalance. SageMaker Data Wrangler's 'Balance Data' transform explicitly lists Random oversampling as an operator that 'randomly duplicates samples in the minority category' so that classes reach an equal proportion (alongside Random undersampling and SMOTE). This is the only listed option that actually changes the class distribution, so the model sees a balanced number of examples per class. The other choices do not rebalance classes: reducing the dataset and random data splitting leave class proportions unchanged, and generically 'transforming some of the images' (data augmentation, e.g., the Image Classification crop/crop_color augmentation_type) is primarily a generalization/regularization technique that does not, as phrased, target the minority class or change class proportions. Therefore C is the precise answer for resolving class imbalance.","explanation_zh":"Random oversampling 是 AWS 官方文件中用來直接解決 class imbalance 的標準技術。SageMaker Data Wrangler 的「Balance Data」轉換明確將 Random oversampling 列為一個運算子，會「隨機複製少數類別中的樣本」，使各類別達到相等比例（同時還有 Random undersampling 與 SMOTE）。它是唯一真正改變類別分布的選項，使模型在每個類別看到平衡的樣本數量。其他選項都無法重新平衡類別：縮小資料集與隨機資料切分都不會改變類別比例；而泛泛地「轉換部分影像」（data augmentation，例如 Image Classification 的 crop/crop_color augmentation_type）主要是泛化/正則化技術，按其措辭並未針對少數類別也不會改變類別比例。因此 C 是解決 class imbalance 的精確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Reducing the dataset size does not change the relative proportions of classes and discards useful training data, worsening model quality rather than fixing imbalance.","why_zh":"縮小資料集大小不會改變各類別的相對比例，還會丟棄有用的訓練資料，反而降低模型品質，並未解決不平衡。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Transforming/augmenting some images (e.g., the SageMaker Image Classification augmentation_type crop/crop_color/crop_color_transform) is primarily a generalization technique. As phrased ('some of the images'), it does not target the minority class or rebalance class proportions, so it does not directly resolve class imbalance the way oversampling does.","why_zh":"轉換/擴增部分影像（例如 SageMaker Image Classification 的 augmentation_type crop/crop_color/crop_color_transform）主要是泛化技術。如其措辭（『部分影像』）並未針對少數類別或重新平衡類別比例，因此不像 oversampling 那樣直接解決 class imbalance。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Random data splitting partitions data into train/validation/test sets; it has nothing to do with the class distribution within those sets and does not address imbalance.","why_zh":"隨機資料切分是把資料分成 train/validation/test 集，與這些集合內的類別分布無關，無法解決不平衡。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/canvas-transform.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler-transform.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/IC-Hyperparameter.html"]}},{"id":105,"question_en":"A company receives daily .csv files about customer interactions with its ML model. The company stores the files in Amazon S3 and uses the files to retrain the model. An ML engineer needs to implement a solution to mask credit card numbers in the files before the model is retrained. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST development effort?","question_zh":"一家公司每天都会收到有关客户与其机器学习模型互动情况的.csv 文件。该公司将这些文件存储在亚马逊 S3 中，并使用这些文件对模型进行再训练。一位机器学习工程师需要实现一个解决方案，在对模型进行 再训练之前对文件中的信用卡号码进行屏蔽处理。 哪种解决方案能以最少的开发工作量满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a discovery job in Amazon Macie. Configure the job to find and mask sensitive data.","B":"Create Apache Spark code to run on an AWS Glue job. Use the Sensitive Data Detection functionality in AWS Glue to find and mask sensitive data.","C":"Create Apache Spark code to run on an AWS Glue job. Program the code to perform a regex operation to find and mask sensitive data.","D":"Create Apache Spark code to run on an Amazon EC2 instance. Program the code to perform an operation to find and mask sensitive data."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon Macie 中创建一个发现任务。配置该任务以查找并屏蔽敏感数据。","B":"编写可在 AWS Glue 作业上运行的 Apache Spark 代码。使用 AWS Glue 中的敏感数据检测功能查找并屏 蔽敏感数据。","C":"编写可在 AWS Glue 作业上运行的 Apache Spark 代码。编写代码以执行正则表达式操作来查找并屏蔽敏 感数据。","D":"编写可在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行的 Apache Spark 代码。编写程序代码以执行查找并屏蔽敏感数据 的操作。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Glue includes a built-in Sensitive Data Detection feature (the Detect PII transform) that lets you detect, mask, or remove PII. It ships with managed/pre-defined entity types including CREDIT_CARD (in the Universal category) and built-in masking actions: Redact detected text, Partially redact detected text, and Apply cryptographic hash (SHA-256). The docs state that 'if a masking action is selected, the DataFrame will return data with sensitive data masked.' Because credit-card detection AND masking are provided out of the box, the engineer only configures the transform on a Glue job rather than writing custom matching logic, giving the LEAST development effort. Option C also uses a Glue Spark job but forces the engineer to hand-write and maintain custom regex to find and mask the data, which is more development effort. Option A (Amazon Macie) does not satisfy the requirement at all: Macie only discovers, classifies, and reports sensitive data via findings; it does not modify or mask objects in S3. Option D additionally requires provisioning and managing an EC2 instance plus writing custom masking code, the highest effort. Therefore B meets the requirement with the least development effort.","explanation_zh":"AWS Glue 內建 Sensitive Data Detection 功能（Detect PII transform），可偵測、遮罩或移除 PII。它提供受管/預先定義的實體類型，包含 CREDIT_CARD（屬於 Universal 類別），並內建遮罩動作：Redact detected text、Partially redact detected text 以及 Apply cryptographic hash（SHA-256）。官方文件指出『若選擇了遮罩動作，DataFrame 會回傳已遮罩敏感資料的結果』。由於信用卡偵測與遮罩都是開箱即用，工程師只需在 Glue job 上設定該 transform，而不需自行撰寫比對邏輯，因此開發工作量最少。選項 C 同樣使用 Glue Spark job，但強迫工程師親手撰寫並維護 regex 來尋找與遮罩資料，開發工作量較高。選項 A（Amazon Macie）完全無法滿足需求：Macie 只能透過 findings 發現、分類並報告敏感資料，並不會修改或遮罩 S3 中的物件。選項 D 還需額外佈建與管理 EC2 執行個體並撰寫自訂遮罩程式碼，工作量最高。因此 B 以最少的開發工作量滿足需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Macie only discovers, classifies, and reports sensitive data by generating findings/reports; it cannot mask or modify the data inside the .csv files in S3. It does not meet the in-place masking requirement at all.","why_zh":"Amazon Macie 僅透過產生 findings/報告來發現、分類與報告敏感資料；它無法遮罩或修改 S3 中 .csv 檔案內的資料，根本無法滿足就地遮罩的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Although it runs on a Glue job, it requires the engineer to write and maintain custom regex to both find and mask credit card numbers, which is more development effort than configuring Glue's built-in Sensitive Data Detection / Detect PII transform (option B).","why_zh":"雖然在 Glue job 上執行，但需要工程師自行撰寫並維護 regex 來尋找與遮罩信用卡號碼，開發工作量比設定 Glue 內建的 Sensitive Data Detection / Detect PII transform（選項 B）更高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Running Spark on a self-managed EC2 instance adds infrastructure provisioning, patching, and management on top of writing custom masking code, making it the highest development and operational effort.","why_zh":"在自管的 EC2 執行個體上執行 Spark，除了要撰寫自訂遮罩程式碼外還要佈建、修補與管理基礎設施，開發與運維工作量最高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/detect-PII.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/sensitive-data-managed-data-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/aws-glue-api-sensitive-data-example.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html"]}},{"id":106,"question_en":"A medical company is using AWS to build a tool to recommend treatments for patients. The company has obtained health records and self-reported textual information in English from patients. The company needs to use this information to gain insight about the patients. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST development effort?","question_zh":"一家医疗公司正在利用亚马逊网络服务（AWS）开发一款工具，为患者推荐治疗方案。该公司已获取了患 者用英语提供的健康记录和自我报告的文本信息。公司需要利用这些信息来深入了解患者的情况。 哪种解决方案能以最少的开发工作量满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon SageMaker to build a recurrent neural network (RNN) to summarize the data.","B":"Use Amazon Comprehend Medical to summarize the data.","C":"Use Amazon Kendra to create a quick-search tool to query the data.","D":"Use the Amazon SageMaker Sequence-to-Sequence (seq2seq) algorithm to create a text summary from the data."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用亚马逊 SageMaker 构建一个循环神经网络（RNN）来总结数据。","B":"使用 Amazon Comprehend Medical 对数据进行总结。","C":"使用 Amazon Kendra 创建一个快速搜索工具来查询数据。","D":"使用亚马逊 SageMaker 序列到序列（seq2seq）算法从数据中生成文本摘要。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Comprehend Medical is a fully managed, pre-trained NLP service that detects and returns useful information from unstructured clinical text such as physician's notes, discharge summaries, test results, and case notes, and links detected entities to standardized medical ontologies (ICD-10-CM, RxNorm, SNOMED CT) for English (US-EN) text. The AWS docs explicitly list a 'Patient case management and outcome' use case where patients report health concerns in a narrative and providers analyze case notes to gain insight - matching this scenario almost verbatim. Because it is a pay-per-use API with no model to design, train, or tune, it meets the 'LEAST development effort' requirement. Options A (RNN) and D (seq2seq) require building and training custom deep-learning models in SageMaker, which is the opposite of least effort and not medically specialized. Option C (Kendra) builds an enterprise search/Q&A index rather than extracting medical insight from clinical text, so it does not satisfy the requirement.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Comprehend Medical 是一項全託管、預先訓練好的 NLP 服務，能從非結構化的臨床文字（例如醫師筆記、出院摘要、檢驗結果與病例註記）中偵測並回傳有用資訊，並可將偵測到的實體連結到標準化醫療本體（ICD-10-CM、RxNorm、SNOMED CT），支援英文（US-EN）文字。AWS 文件明確列出「Patient case management and outcome（病患個案管理與結果）」使用案例：病患以敘述方式自述健康狀況，醫療提供者分析病例註記以取得洞察，這幾乎與題目情境一字不差地吻合。由於它是按用量計費的 API，無需設計、訓練或調校任何模型，因此符合「開發工作量最少」的要求。選項 A（RNN）與 D（seq2seq）都需要在 SageMaker 中建構並訓練自訂深度學習模型，與最少工作量背道而馳，且非醫療專用。選項 C（Kendra）建立的是企業搜尋／問答索引，而非從臨床文字中萃取醫療洞察，因此不符合需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Building an RNN to summarize the data in Amazon SageMaker requires designing, training, and tuning a custom deep-learning model. This is far more development effort than a pre-trained managed API and is not specialized for medical/clinical text.","why_zh":"在 Amazon SageMaker 中建構 RNN 來摘要資料需要設計、訓練與調校自訂深度學習模型，開發工作量遠高於使用預先訓練好的託管 API，且並非針對醫療/臨床文字做最佳化。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Kendra is an intelligent enterprise search service that creates a search/Q&A index over documents. It does not extract medical entities (conditions, medications, PHI) or link them to clinical ontologies, so it does not provide the medical insight the company needs.","why_zh":"Amazon Kendra 是智慧型企業搜尋服務，可在文件上建立搜尋/問答索引，但它不會萃取醫療實體（病況、藥物、PHI）或將其連結到臨床本體，因此無法提供公司所需的醫療洞察。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The Amazon SageMaker seq2seq algorithm still requires you to build, train, and tune a custom text-summarization model with labeled data. This is significant development effort, and the generic algorithm is not specialized for clinical/medical text like Comprehend Medical.","why_zh":"Amazon SageMaker seq2seq 演算法仍需使用標註資料建構、訓練並調校自訂的文字摘要模型，屬於相當大的開發工作量，且此通用演算法不像 Comprehend Medical 針對臨床/醫療文字做專門最佳化。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend-medical/latest/dev/comprehendmedical-welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend-medical/latest/dev/textanalysis-entitiesv2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/generative-ai-nlp-healthcare/comprehend-medical.html"]}},{"id":107,"question_en":"A company needs to extract entities from a PDF document to build a classifier model. Which solution will extract and store the entities in the LEAST amount of time?","question_zh":"一家公司需要从 PDF 文档中提取实体以构建分类器模型。 哪种解决方案能在最短的时间内提取并存储实体？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Comprehend to extract the entities. Store the output in Amazon S3.","B":"Use an open source AI optical character recognition (OCR) tool on Amazon SageMaker to extract the entities. Store the output in Amazon S3.","C":"Use Amazon Textract to extract the entities. Use Amazon Comprehend to convert the entities to text. Store the output in Amazon S3.","D":"Use Amazon Textract integrated with Amazon Augmented AI (Amazon A2I) to extract the entities. Store the output in Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Comprehend 提取实体。将输出存储在 Amazon S3 中。","B":"在亚马逊 SageMaker 上使用开源的人工智能光学字符识别（OCR）工具提取实体。将输出存储在亚马逊 S3 中。","C":"使用 Amazon Textract 提取实体。使用 Amazon Comprehend 将实体转换为文本。将输出存储在 Amazon S3 中。","D":"使用与亚马逊增强型人工智能（亚马逊 A2I）集成的亚马逊 Textract 提取实体。 将输出存储在亚马逊 S3 中。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The qualifier is the LEAST amount of time to extract AND store entities. Amazon Comprehend is the purpose-built NLP service for entity detection (DetectEntities / BatchDetectEntities / StartEntitiesDetectionJob, plus custom entity recognition). AWS docs confirm Comprehend supports one-step document processing: you can input PDF documents directly to a custom analysis job and 'Amazon Comprehend automatically performs the text extraction before running the analysis' (an internal parser for native PDFs, and Amazon Textract APIs internally for images and scanned PDFs), and a custom entity recognizer works on PDF files 'with no pre-processing or doc flattening required.' The asynchronous StartEntitiesDetectionJob 'produces a file containing a list of Entity objects' that is written to the configured Amazon S3 output location. Option A is therefore the single managed service, fewest-steps path, giving the least time. Option C (the dump's suggested answer) is technically reversed and nonsensical: Textract extracts text/structure (not NLP entities), and Comprehend produces entities FROM text rather than 'converting entities to text'; even the legitimate Textract->Comprehend chaining adds an extra service and orchestration step. Option B requires building/deploying open-source OCR infrastructure on SageMaker (high setup overhead, and OCR yields only raw text), and Option D adds an Amazon A2I human-in-the-loop review that inherently increases latency. So A wins on the least-time criterion.","explanation_zh":"題目的限定條件是「以最少的時間」抽取並儲存實體。Amazon Comprehend 是專門做 NLP 實體偵測的服務(DetectEntities / BatchDetectEntities / StartEntitiesDetectionJob,以及 custom entity recognition)。AWS 文件確認 Comprehend 支援一步式 document processing:可直接把 PDF 文件輸入到 custom analysis job,且「Amazon Comprehend 會在分析前自動完成文字抽取」(原生 PDF 用內建 parser,影像/掃描 PDF 則內部呼叫 Amazon Textract API),而 custom entity recognizer 可直接處理 PDF 檔案「無須前處理或文件扁平化(no pre-processing or doc flattening required)」。非同步的 StartEntitiesDetectionJob 會「產出一個包含 Entity 物件清單的檔案」,並寫入所設定的 Amazon S3 輸出位置。因此 Option A 是單一受管服務、步驟最少的路徑,時間最短。Option C(題庫建議答案)在技術上是顛倒且不合理的:Textract 抽取的是文字/結構(非 NLP 實體),而 Comprehend 是從文字產生實體,而非『把實體轉成文字』;即使是正當的 Textract->Comprehend 串接也多了一個服務與編排步驟。Option B 需要在 SageMaker 上建置/部署開源 OCR 基礎設施(高設定成本,且 OCR 只產出原始文字),Option D 加入 Amazon A2I 人工審查,本質上會增加延遲。因此以最少時間為準,A 勝出。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Deploying an open-source OCR tool on SageMaker requires provisioning, configuring, and running custom infrastructure, which is far slower to set up than a managed entity-extraction service. OCR also only yields raw text, not extracted entities, so additional NLP work is still needed.","why_zh":"在 SageMaker 上部署開源 OCR 工具需要佈建、設定並執行自訂基礎設施,設定速度遠慢於受管的實體抽取服務。而且 OCR 只產出原始文字而非實體,還需額外的 NLP 處理。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Roles are reversed and the wording is nonsensical: Textract extracts text/structure (not NLP entities), and Comprehend extracts entities FROM text rather than 'converting entities to text.' Even the correct Textract->Comprehend pattern adds an extra service and orchestration step versus Comprehend alone (which already calls Textract internally when needed), so it is not the least-time option. This is the dump's suggested answer and it is wrong.","why_zh":"角色被顛倒且語意不通:Textract 抽取的是文字/結構(非 NLP 實體),而 Comprehend 是從文字抽取實體,而非『把實體轉成文字』。即使是正確的 Textract->Comprehend 流程,也比單用 Comprehend(在需要時已會內部呼叫 Textract)多一個服務與編排步驟,並非最省時。這是題庫建議答案,但它是錯的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Adding Amazon Augmented AI (A2I) introduces a human-in-the-loop review workflow, which inherently increases latency and time-to-result; it is optimized for accuracy/oversight, not speed. It is the slowest option.","why_zh":"加入 Amazon Augmented AI (A2I) 會引入人工審查流程,本質上會增加延遲與取得結果的時間;它是為了準確度/監督而設計,而非速度。是最慢的選項。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/idp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/idp-inputs-async.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/how-entities.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/custom-entity-recognition.html"]}},{"id":108,"question_en":"A company shares Amazon SageMaker Studio notebooks that are accessible through a VPN. The company must enforce access controls to prevent malicious actors from exploiting presigned URLs to access the notebooks. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司通过虚拟专用网络（VPN）共享亚马逊 SageMaker Studio 笔记本。该公司必须实施访问控制 措施，以防止恶意人员利用预签名的 URL 来访问这些笔记本。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up Studio client IP validation by using the aws:sourceIp IAM policy condition.","B":"Set up Studio client VPC validation by using the aws:sourceVpc IAM policy condition.","C":"Set up Studio client role endpoint validation by using the aws:PrimaryTag IAM policy condition.","D":"Set up Studio client user endpoint validation by using the aws:PrincipalTag IAM policy condition."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 aws:sourceIp IAM 策略条件设置 Studio 客户端 IP 验证。","B":"使用 aws:sourceVpc IAM 策略条件设置 Studio 客户端 VPC 验证。","C":"使用 aws:PrimaryTag IAM 策略条件设置 Studio 客户端角色端点验证。","D":"通过使用 aws:PrincipalTag IAM 策略条件来设置 Studio 客户端用户端点验证。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"SageMaker Studio access uses presigned URLs (CreatePresignedDomainUrl), and the threat is a stolen URL being replayed by an attacker. AWS's documented guardrail is to attach an IAM network-restriction Condition to the CreatePresignedDomainUrl action: SageMaker applies that condition both when the URL is generated AND when the generated URL is used, so a URL created from a valid network but used from a non-valid network is rejected (AWS Prescriptive Guidance, Appendix A: 'If a URL is generated from a valid network and then sent by a non-valid network ... the request that sends the URL fails'). The deciding factor between the network condition keys is the topology: users reach SageMaker over a VPN, so traffic egresses the corporate network and hits the PUBLIC SageMaker/S3 endpoint from a known corporate IP range. The key that restricts requests by source IP range against the public endpoint is aws:sourceIp (used with the IpAddress operator), so option A is correct. The VPC-oriented keys (aws:sourceVpc, aws:VpcSourceIp, aws:sourceVpce) only evaluate when the request flows through a VPC interface endpoint (PrivateLink), which is not the VPN-to-public-endpoint scenario described.","explanation_zh":"SageMaker Studio 透過 presigned URL（CreatePresignedDomainUrl）存取，威脅是被竊取的 URL 遭攻擊者重放使用。AWS 文件記載的防護是在 CreatePresignedDomainUrl 動作上加入 IAM 網路限制 Condition：SageMaker 在「產生 URL」與「使用該 URL」兩個時點都會套用此條件，因此從合法網路產生卻從非合法網路使用的 URL 會被拒絕（AWS Prescriptive Guidance, Appendix A：『若 URL 從合法網路產生卻由非合法網路送出 … 送出該 URL 的請求會失敗』）。在各網路條件鍵之間做選擇的關鍵在於網路拓撲：使用者透過 VPN 連到 SageMaker，流量從公司網路出口送出、以已知的公司 IP 範圍打到「公開的」SageMaker/S3 端點。能以來源 IP 範圍限制對公開端點存取的條件鍵是 aws:sourceIp（搭配 IpAddress 運算子），因此選項 A 正確。VPC 導向的條件鍵（aws:sourceVpc、aws:VpcSourceIp、aws:sourceVpce）只有在請求經由 VPC interface endpoint（PrivateLink）時才會被評估，並不符合題目描述的 VPN 連到公開端點情境。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"aws:sourceVpc (and related aws:VpcSourceIp/aws:sourceVpce keys) are only present and evaluable when the request reaches SageMaker through a VPC interface endpoint (PrivateLink). VPN users hitting the public SageMaker/S3 endpoint arrive from a corporate egress IP range, not from inside a VPC, so this key would not match and the guardrail would fail (or block everyone). It fits a PrivateLink/VPC-only design, not the VPN-to-public-endpoint pattern in the question.","why_zh":"aws:sourceVpc（以及相關的 aws:VpcSourceIp/aws:sourceVpce）只有當請求透過 VPC interface endpoint（PrivateLink）到達 SageMaker 時才會存在並可被評估。透過 VPN 連到公開 SageMaker/S3 端點的使用者來自公司出口 IP 範圍而非 VPC 內部，因此此條件鍵無法比對成功，防護會失效（或把所有人都擋掉）。它適用於 PrivateLink／VPC-only 設計，而非題目中的 VPN 連到公開端點模式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"aws:PrimaryTag is not a valid AWS global condition key (the real tag keys are aws:PrincipalTag and aws:ResourceTag), and 'role endpoint validation' is not a real mechanism. Even treated as ABAC, a tag-based condition controls identity/resource attributes, not the network from which a presigned URL is used, so it cannot block a URL replayed from a different network.","why_zh":"aws:PrimaryTag 並非有效的 AWS 全域條件鍵（真實的標籤鍵是 aws:PrincipalTag 與 aws:ResourceTag），且「role endpoint validation」並非真實機制。即便當作 ABAC，標籤型條件控制的是身分或資源屬性而非 presigned URL 被使用的網路來源，因此無法阻擋從不同網路重放的 URL。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"aws:PrincipalTag is a real key but it is an identity/ABAC control based on tags attached to the calling principal, not a network-based control. It does not restrict which network a presigned URL can be used from, so it cannot stop an attacker who replays a stolen URL from a different IP.","why_zh":"aws:PrincipalTag 是真實存在的條件鍵，但它是依呼叫主體標籤運作的身分／ABAC 控制，並非以網路為基礎的控制。它無法限制 presigned URL 可從哪個網路使用，因此無法阻止攻擊者從不同 IP 重放遭竊取的 URL。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/presigned-url-best-practices/appendix-a.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/mlflow-private-link-restrict.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/APIReference/API_CreatePresignedDomainUrl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/howitworks-access-ws.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/APIReference/API_IamPolicyConstraints.html"]}},{"id":109,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to merge and transform data from two sources to retrain an existing ML model. One data source consists of .csv files that are stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. Each .csv file consists of millions of records. The other data source is an Amazon Aurora DB cluster. The result of the merge process must be written to a second S3 bucket. The ML engineer needs to perform this merge-and-transform task every week. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师需要合并并转换来自两个来源的数据，以重新训练现有的机器学习模型。其中一个数据 源由存储在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中的 .csv 文件组成，每个 .csv 文件包含数百万条记录。另一个数据源是亚马逊 Aurora 数据库集群。 合并过程的结果必须写入第二个 S3 存储桶。机器学习工程师每周都需要执行此合并和转换任务。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a transient Amazon EMR cluster every week. Use the cluster to run an Apache Spark job to merge and transform the data.","B":"Create a weekly AWS Glue job that uses the Apache Spark engine. Use DynamicFrame native operations to merge and transform the data.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that runs Apache Spark code every week to merge and transform the data. Configure the Lambda function to connect to the initial S3 bucket and the DB cluster.","D":"Create an AWS Batch job that runs Apache Spark code on Amazon EC2 instances every week. Configure the Spark code to save the data from the EC2 instances to the second S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"每周创建一个临时的 Amazon EMR 集群。使用该集群运行一个 Apache Spark 作业来合并和转换数据。","B":"创建一个每周运行的 AWS Glue 作业，使用 Apache Spark 引擎。利用 DynamicFrame 原生操作来 合并和转换数据。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，每周运行一次 Apache Spark 代码以合并和转换数据。配置该 Lambda 函数 以连接到初始的 S3 存储桶和数据库集群。","D":"创建一个 AWS Batch 作业，每周在 Amazon EC2 实例上运行 Apache Spark 代码。配置 Spark 代码， 将 EC2 实例中的数据保存到第二个 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The qualifier is LEAST operational overhead for a recurring weekly merge-and-transform of S3 .csv files plus an Aurora DB cluster, writing the result to a second S3 bucket. AWS Glue is a fully serverless data integration service with no infrastructure to manage; it connects to 70+ data sources (including Aurora via JDBC and S3), runs on a managed Apache Spark engine, and jobs can be scheduled (e.g., weekly via a schedule trigger). The Glue DynamicFrame class provides native operations such as join and mergeDynamicFrame to merge and transform records, then write to S3. Because there are no clusters, instances, or runtimes to provision, patch, or tear down, option B has the lowest operational overhead. The other options all require provisioning and/or managing compute (EMR, EC2/Batch) or are technically unsuitable (Lambda cannot run a full Spark cluster).","explanation_zh":"本題的限定條件是「LEAST operational overhead（最少維運負擔）」，需求是每週一次合併並轉換 S3 中的 .csv 檔案與 Amazon Aurora DB cluster 的資料，並將結果寫入第二個 S3 bucket。AWS Glue 是完全 serverless 的資料整合服務，沒有基礎設施需要管理；它可連接 70 多種資料來源（包含透過 JDBC 連接的 Aurora 及 S3），執行於受管的 Apache Spark 引擎，且 job 可排程（例如以 schedule trigger 設定每週執行）。Glue 的 DynamicFrame class 提供 join、mergeDynamicFrame 等原生操作來合併與轉換資料，再寫回 S3。因為不需佈建、修補或拆除任何 cluster、instance 或 runtime，選項 B 的維運負擔最低。其他選項皆需佈建/管理運算資源（EMR、EC2/Batch），或在技術上不可行（Lambda 無法執行完整的 Spark cluster）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A transient EMR cluster still requires you to define, configure, launch, and tear down the cluster each week, plus manage the Spark application and EMR versions. That is significantly more operational overhead than serverless Glue.","why_zh":"transient EMR cluster 仍需每週定義、設定、啟動並拆除 cluster，並管理 Spark 應用與 EMR 版本，維運負擔明顯高於 serverless 的 Glue。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Lambda cannot run a distributed Apache Spark cluster; it has a 15-minute max runtime and limited memory/ephemeral storage, which cannot process millions of records across two large sources with a Spark merge. Technically unsuitable.","why_zh":"AWS Lambda 無法執行分散式 Apache Spark cluster，最長執行時間僅 15 分鐘，且記憶體/暫存空間有限，無法以 Spark 合併處理兩個大型來源中數百萬筆記錄。技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Batch on EC2 requires you to manage the EC2 compute environment, container/job definitions, and the Spark setup yourself. This is far more operational overhead than the fully managed, serverless Glue Spark engine.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上執行 AWS Batch 需自行管理 EC2 運算環境、容器/job 定義及 Spark 安裝設定，維運負擔遠高於全受管、serverless 的 Glue Spark 引擎。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/what-is-glue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/aws-glue-api-crawler-pyspark-extensions-dynamic-frame.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/aws-glue-programming-etl-connect-jdbc-home.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/aws-glue-programming-etl-connect.html"]}},{"id":110,"question_en":"An ML engineer has deployed an Amazon SageMaker model to a serverless endpoint in production. The model is invoked by the InvokeEndpoint API operation. The model's latency in production is higher than the baseline latency in the test environment. The ML engineer thinks that the increase in latency is because of model startup time. What should the ML engineer do to confirm or deny this hypothesis?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师已将一个 Amazon SageMaker 模型部署到生产环境中的无服务器端点。该模型通过 InvokeEndpoint API 操作被调用。 该模型在生产环境中的延迟高于测试环境中的基准延迟。机器学习工程师认为延迟增加是因为模型 启动时间所致。 机器学习工程师应该怎么做才能证实或否定这一假设？","options_en":{"A":"Schedule a SageMaker Model Monitor job. Observe metrics about model quality.","B":"Schedule a SageMaker Model Monitor job with Amazon CloudWatch metrics enabled.","C":"Enable Amazon CloudWatch metrics. Observe the ModelSetupTime metric in the SageMaker namespace.","D":"Enable Amazon CloudWatch metrics. Observe the ModelLoadingWaitTime metric in the SageMaker namespace."},"options_zh":{"A":"安排一个 SageMaker 模型监控任务。观察有关模型质量的指标。","B":"安排一个启用 Amazon CloudWatch 指标的 SageMaker 模型监控作业。","C":"启用 Amazon CloudWatch 指标。在 SageMaker 命名空间中观察 ModelSetupTime 指标。","D":"启用 Amazon CloudWatch 指标。在 SageMaker 命名空间中观察 ModelLoadingWaitTime 指标。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The endpoint is a SageMaker Serverless Inference endpoint, and the suspected cause is model startup (cold-start) time. The official SageMaker CloudWatch invocation-metrics documentation defines ModelSetupTime as 'the time it takes to launch new compute resources for a serverless endpoint. The time can vary depending on the model size, how long it takes to download the model, and the start-up time of the container.' This is precisely the serverless cold-start cost the engineer suspects, and it is published in the AWS/SageMaker namespace from InvokeEndpoint calls. So the engineer should enable CloudWatch metrics and observe ModelSetupTime to confirm or deny the hypothesis (answer C). Note that ModelLoadingWaitTime (answer D) IS a real SageMaker metric, but it belongs to the multi-model endpoint (MME) model-loading metrics group ('the interval of time that an invocation request has waited for the target model to be downloaded, loaded, or both'), not to serverless endpoints - so it does not apply to this serverless scenario. The dump's suggested answer D is therefore wrong: it names a metric that exists only for multi-model endpoints, while serverless startup time is exposed via ModelSetupTime.","explanation_zh":"此端點是 SageMaker Serverless Inference 端點,工程師懷疑的原因是模型啟動(冷啟動)時間。官方 SageMaker CloudWatch 呼叫指標文件將 ModelSetupTime 定義為「為 serverless 端點啟動新運算資源所需的時間,該時間會依模型大小、下載模型所需時間以及容器啟動時間而異」。這正是工程師懷疑的 serverless 冷啟動成本,並由 InvokeEndpoint 呼叫發佈於 AWS/SageMaker 命名空間。因此工程師應啟用 CloudWatch 指標並觀察 ModelSetupTime,以驗證或否定該假設(答案 C)。請注意 ModelLoadingWaitTime(答案 D)確實是真實存在的 SageMaker 指標,但它屬於 multi-model endpoint (MME) 的模型載入指標群組(「呼叫請求為了讓目標模型被下載、載入或兩者以執行推論而等待的時間間隔」),並不屬於 serverless 端點,故不適用於此 serverless 情境。題庫建議答案 D 因此錯誤:它指的是僅存在於 multi-model endpoint 的指標,而 serverless 啟動時間是透過 ModelSetupTime 呈現。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SageMaker Model Monitor observes model/data quality (drift, accuracy, bias, data quality), not invocation latency or startup time. It cannot confirm or deny a cold-start latency hypothesis.","why_zh":"SageMaker Model Monitor 觀察的是模型/資料品質(漂移、準確度、偏差、資料品質),而非呼叫延遲或啟動時間,無法用來驗證冷啟動延遲假設。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Model Monitor (even with CloudWatch metrics enabled) emits model-quality/data-quality metrics, not the ModelSetupTime startup metric needed here. It is the wrong tool for measuring serverless cold-start latency.","why_zh":"Model Monitor(即使啟用 CloudWatch 指標)發出的是模型品質/資料品質指標,而非此處所需的 ModelSetupTime 啟動指標;用錯工具來量測 serverless 冷啟動延遲。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"ModelLoadingWaitTime is a published SageMaker metric, but it is a multi-model endpoint (MME) model-loading metric (time an invocation waited for the target model to download/load), not a serverless endpoint metric. The scenario is a serverless endpoint, where startup time is captured by ModelSetupTime instead.","why_zh":"ModelLoadingWaitTime 確實是已發佈的 SageMaker 指標,但它是 multi-model endpoint (MME) 的模型載入指標(呼叫等待目標模型下載/載入的時間),而非 serverless 端點指標。本情境是 serverless 端點,其啟動時間改由 ModelSetupTime 量測。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/monitoring-cloudwatch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/serverless-endpoints.html"]}},{"id":111,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to ensure that a dataset complies with regulations for personally identifiable information (PII). The ML engineer will use the data to train an ML model on Amazon SageMaker instances. SageMaker must not use any of the PII. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way?","question_zh":"","options_en":{"A":"Use the Amazon Comprehend DetectPiiEntities API call to redact the PII from the data. Store the data in an Amazon S3 bucket. Access the S3 bucket from the SageMaker instances for model training.","B":"Use the Amazon Comprehend DetectPiiEntities API call to redact the PII from the data. Store the data in an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Mount the EFS file system to the SageMaker instances for model training.","C":"Use AWS Glue DataBrew to cleanse the dataset of PII. Store the data in an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Mount the EFS file system to the SageMaker instances for model training.","D":"Use Amazon Macie for automatic discovery of PII in the data. Remove the PII. Store the data in an Amazon S3 bucket. Mount the S3 bucket to the SageMaker instances for model training."},"options_zh":{},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The goal is to strip all PII from a dataset before SageMaker training with the least operational effort. Amazon Comprehend offers a purpose-built, fully managed PII redaction capability: its asynchronous PII batch job returns a copy of the input with each PII entity masked (per the 'Redact PII entities' section of the Comprehend docs), satisfying 'SageMaker must not use any of the PII' in a single managed run with no custom code. Storing the redacted output in Amazon S3 is the most operationally efficient destination because S3 is the native, default input/output data source for SageMaker training jobs and needs no extra provisioning. Option A combines managed redaction with the native S3 data path, giving the lowest overhead. Option B is identical except it stores data in Amazon EFS, which must be created, mounted, and run inside a VPC, adding overhead with no benefit. Macie (D) only discovers and reports sensitive data as findings (it does not remove or redact PII, and S3 is accessed, not 'mounted'), and Glue DataBrew (C) requires building recipes/projects plus EFS mounting, both of which add setup compared with a single managed Comprehend redaction job writing to S3.","explanation_zh":"目標是在 SageMaker 訓練前以最少營運工作量移除資料集中所有 PII。Amazon Comprehend 提供專門且全託管的 PII 遮蔽 (redaction) 功能：其非同步 PII 批次工作會回傳一份已將每個 PII 實體遮蔽的輸入副本（見 Comprehend 文件「Redact PII entities」一節），單一託管執行即可滿足「SageMaker 不得使用任何 PII」的要求，且無需自訂程式碼。將遮蔽後的輸出存放在 Amazon S3 是最具營運效率的目的地，因為 S3 是 SageMaker 訓練工作原生的預設輸入/輸出資料來源，無需額外佈建。選項 A 結合了託管遮蔽與原生 S3 資料路徑，營運負擔最低。選項 B 除了改存於 Amazon EFS 外與 A 相同，而 EFS 需建立、掛載並在 VPC 內執行，增加負擔卻無好處。Macie（D）僅以 findings 形式探索並報告敏感資料（並不會移除或遮蔽 PII，且 S3 是被存取而非「掛載」），而 Glue DataBrew（C）需建立 recipe/project 並掛載 EFS；相較於單一託管的 Comprehend 遮蔽工作寫入 S3，兩者皆增加設定成本。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses the same managed Comprehend redaction as A but stores the data in Amazon EFS, which must be provisioned, mounted, and run within a VPC for SageMaker access — more operational overhead than S3 with no added benefit.","why_zh":"與 A 一樣使用託管的 Comprehend 遮蔽，但改存於 Amazon EFS；EFS 需佈建、掛載並在 VPC 內供 SageMaker 存取，比 S3 營運負擔更高且無額外好處。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Glue DataBrew can mask/cleanse PII, but it requires building projects and recipe steps and runs as a separate data-prep workflow; storing the result in EFS adds mounting and VPC overhead, making it less operationally efficient than a single managed Comprehend redaction job writing to S3.","why_zh":"AWS Glue DataBrew 可遮蔽/清理 PII，但需建立 project 與 recipe 步驟，並以獨立的資料準備流程執行；將結果存於 EFS 又增加掛載與 VPC 負擔，較單一託管的 Comprehend 遮蔽工作寫入 S3 效率更低。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Macie only discovers and reports sensitive data via findings — it does not remove or redact PII, so 'Remove the PII' is an unspecified manual/extra step. The wording 'Mount the S3 bucket to the SageMaker instances' is also technically wrong because S3 is accessed via API, not mounted as a file system.","why_zh":"Amazon Macie 僅透過 findings 探索並報告敏感資料——它不會移除或遮蔽 PII，因此「移除 PII」是未定義的手動/額外步驟。此外「將 S3 bucket 掛載到 SageMaker 執行個體」在技術上也不正確，因為 S3 是透過 API 存取，而非像檔案系統般掛載。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/how-pii.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/automatic-model-tuning-ex-bucket.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/detect-PII.html"]}},{"id":112,"question_en":"A company must install a custom script on any newly created Amazon SageMaker notebook instances. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"公司必须在任何新创建的亚马逊 SageMaker 笔记本实例上安装自定义脚本。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a lifecycle configuration script to install the custom script when a new SageMaker notebook is created. Attach the lifecycle configuration to every new SageMaker notebook as part of the creation steps.","B":"Create a custom Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) image that contains the custom script. Push the ECR image to a Docker registry. Attach the Docker image to a SageMaker Studio domain. Select the kernel to run as part of the SageMaker notebook.","C":"Create a custom package index repository. Use AWS CodeArtifact to manage the installation of the custom script. Set up AWS PrivateLink endpoints to connect CodeArtifact to the SageMaker instance. Install the script.","D":"Store the custom script in Amazon S3. Create an AWS Lambda function to install the custom script on new SageMaker notebooks. Configure Amazon EventBridge to invoke the Lambda function when a new SageMaker notebook is initialized."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个生命周期配置脚本，在创建新的 SageMaker 笔记本时安装自定义脚本。在创建新 SageMaker 笔记本的过程中，将生命周期配置附加到每个新创建的 SageMaker 笔记本上。","B":"创建一个自定义的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 镜像，其中包含自定义脚本。将 ECR 镜像推送到 Docker 注册表。将 Docker 镜像附加到 SageMaker Studio 域。选择要在 SageMaker 笔记本中运行的内核。","C":"创建自定义软件包索引存储库。使用 AWS CodeArtifact 来管理自定义脚本的安装。设置 AWS PrivateLink 端点以将 CodeArtifact 连接到 SageMaker 实例。安装该脚本。","D":"将自定义脚本存储在 Amazon S3 中。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于在新的 SageMaker 笔记本上安 装自定义脚本。配置 Amazon EventBridge，在新的 SageMaker 笔记本初始化时调用该 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A SageMaker notebook instance lifecycle configuration (LCC) is the native, fully managed mechanism for this exact requirement. AWS documentation states an LCC 'provides shell scripts that run only when you create the notebook instance or whenever you start one' and explicitly lists 'Installing packages or sample notebooks on a notebook instance' and 'Using a shell script to customize a notebook instance' as core use cases. You author the script once and attach the LCC during notebook creation, so every newly created notebook instance runs the custom script automatically with no additional infrastructure to build, secure, or operate. That makes A the least-operational-overhead solution. The other options introduce extra services (Lambda, EventBridge, ECR, CodeArtifact, PrivateLink) that must be built and maintained, or they target SageMaker Studio rather than notebook instances.","explanation_zh":"SageMaker notebook instance 的 lifecycle configuration (LCC) 正是滿足此需求的原生、全託管機制。AWS 文件指出 LCC「提供僅在建立 notebook instance 或每次啟動時才執行的 shell scripts」，並明確將「在 notebook instance 上安裝套件或範例 notebook」與「使用 shell script 自訂 notebook instance」列為核心使用案例。你只需撰寫一次 script 並在建立 notebook 時附加該 LCC，之後每個新建立的 notebook instance 都會自動執行該自訂 script，不需另外建置、保護或維運任何基礎設施，因此營運負擔最低。其他選項都引入需要自行建置與維護的額外服務 (Lambda、EventBridge、ECR、CodeArtifact、PrivateLink)，或是針對 SageMaker Studio 而非 notebook instances。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A custom ECR image attached as a Studio kernel applies to SageMaker Studio, not to classic SageMaker notebook instances, and it customizes the container/kernel rather than running an install script on every newly created notebook instance. Building, pushing, and maintaining a custom Docker image is far more operational overhead than a managed LCC.","why_zh":"把自訂 ECR 映像作為 Studio kernel 附加是用於 SageMaker Studio，而非傳統的 SageMaker notebook instances，且它是自訂容器/kernel 而非在每個新建立的 notebook instance 上執行安裝 script。建置、推送並維護自訂 Docker 映像的營運負擔遠高於託管的 LCC。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Building a custom package index repository with CodeArtifact plus PrivateLink endpoints is heavy, indirect infrastructure that does not automatically run a script when a notebook is created. It introduces significant setup and networking maintenance, far more operational overhead than an LCC.","why_zh":"以 CodeArtifact 建立自訂套件索引儲存庫並加上 PrivateLink endpoints 是繁重且間接的基礎設施，無法在 notebook 建立時自動執行 script，需要大量設定與網路維護，營運負擔遠高於 LCC。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An S3 + Lambda + EventBridge pipeline is a custom event-driven solution requiring code, IAM roles, and ongoing maintenance, and reliably injecting an install onto a freshly created notebook instance from outside is complex. The purpose-built LCC achieves the same result running natively at creation with no custom code or eventing to operate.","why_zh":"S3 + Lambda + EventBridge 的管線是需要程式碼、IAM 角色與持續維護的自訂事件驅動方案，而且從外部可靠地對新建立的 notebook instance 注入安裝相當複雜。專為此用途設計的 LCC 在建立時原生執行即可達成相同結果，不需任何自訂程式碼或事件機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/notebook-lifecycle-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/notebook-lifecycle-config-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/howitworks-create-ws.html"]}},{"id":113,"question_en":"A company is building a real-time data processing pipeline for an ecommerce application. The application generates a high volume of clickstream data that must be ingested, processed, and visualized in near real time. The company needs a solution that supports SQL for data processing and Jupyter notebooks for interactive analysis. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在为一款电子商务应用构建实时数据处理管道。该应用会产生大量的点击流数据，这些数据必 须近乎实时地被采集、处理和可视化。该公司需要一个支持 SQL 用于数据处理以及 Jupyter 笔记本用于交 互式分析的解决方案。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Data Firehose to ingest the data. Create an AWS Lambda function to process the data. Store the processed data in Amazon S3. Use Amazon QuickSight to visualize the data.","B":"Use Amazon Kinesis Data Streams to ingest the data. Use Amazon Data Firehose to transform the data. Use Amazon Athena to process the data. Use Amazon QuickSight to visualize the data.","C":"Use Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK) to ingest the data. Use AWS Glue with PySpark to process the data. Store the processed data in Amazon S3. Use Amazon QuickSight to visualize the data.","D":"Use Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK) to ingest the data. Use Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink to process the data. Use the built-in Flink dashboard to visualize the data."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Data Firehose 接收数据。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来处理数据。将处理后的数据存储 在 Amazon S3 中。使用 Amazon QuickSight 来可视化数据。","B":"使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 接收数据。使用 Amazon Data Firehose 转换数据。使用 Amazon Athena 处理数据。使用 Amazon QuickSight 可视化数据。","C":"使用亚马逊托管的 Apache Kafka 流处理服务（Amazon MSK）来摄取数据。使用 AWS Glue 和 PySpark 来处理数据。将处理后的数据存储在亚马逊 S3 中。使用亚马逊 QuickSight 来可视化数据。","D":"使用亚马逊托管的 Apache Kafka 服务（Amazon MSK）来摄取数据。使用亚马逊托管的 Apache Flink 服务 来处理数据。使用内置的 Flink 控制面板来可视化数据。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The two decisive requirements are SQL for processing the near-real-time clickstream AND a notebook environment for interactive analysis. Only option D's stack of Amazon MSK plus Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink satisfies both: MSK ingests the high-volume clickstream as a real-time stream, and Managed Service for Apache Flink Studio notebooks let you 'interactively query data streams in real time, using standard SQL, Python, and Scala' via the %flink.ssql stream-SQL interpreter in a web-based (Apache Zeppelin) notebook, which also provides built-in data visualization. None of the other options pair real-time stream processing with an interactive SQL notebook. The one imprecise clause in D is 'use the built-in Flink dashboard to visualize the data' — per the docs the Apache Flink Dashboard is read-only and only shows operational health (Task Managers, Task Slots, and Job status), not business/clickstream data; however the Studio notebook itself can visualize results, and D remains the only architecture meeting the core SQL + interactive-notebook + real-time requirements, so it is the best answer.","explanation_zh":"兩個決定性需求是「用 SQL 處理近即時點擊流資料」以及「用 notebook 環境進行互動式分析」。只有選項 D 的 Amazon MSK 加上 Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink 同時滿足兩者：MSK 以即時串流方式擷取大量點擊流，而 Managed Service for Apache Flink 的 Studio notebooks 可透過 %flink.ssql 串流 SQL 直譯器，在 web 介面（Apache Zeppelin）notebook 中『以標準 SQL、Python、Scala 即時互動查詢資料串流』，且 Zeppelin 本身內建 Data Visualization。其他選項都無法同時提供即時串流處理與互動式 SQL notebook。D 中唯一不精確的措辭是『使用內建 Flink dashboard 來視覺化資料』——根據文件，Apache Flink Dashboard 是唯讀的，只顯示運維健康狀態（Task Managers、Task Slots、Job 狀態），並非業務／點擊流資料的視覺化工具；但 Studio notebook 本身即可視覺化查詢結果，且 D 仍是唯一同時滿足核心 SQL + 互動 notebook + 即時這三項需求的架構，因此為最佳答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Data Firehose plus a Lambda function processes data with custom code, not SQL, and the stack provides no interactive notebook for analysis. It writes to S3 (micro-batch to data-at-rest), so both the SQL-processing and notebook requirements are unmet.","why_zh":"Amazon Data Firehose 加 Lambda 以自訂程式碼處理資料，並非 SQL，且整個架構沒有可供互動分析的 notebook；又寫入 S3（微批次落地），SQL 處理與 notebook 需求皆未滿足。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Athena queries data already landed in S3, which is an ad-hoc/batch model rather than near-real-time stream processing, and the stack provides no interactive notebook for analysis. The notebook requirement is not met.","why_zh":"Athena 查詢的是已落地到 S3 的資料，屬於臨時／批次查詢模式，而非近即時串流處理，且整個架構沒有可供互動分析的 notebook，無法滿足 notebook 需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Glue with PySpark writing to S3 is a batch/micro-batch ETL pattern, not near-real-time interactive streaming, and it is code-centric (PySpark) rather than the SQL-plus-interactive-notebook combination the question requires.","why_zh":"AWS Glue 搭配 PySpark 寫入 S3 屬於批次／微批次 ETL 模式，並非近即時的互動式串流，且以程式碼（PySpark）為主，而非題目要求的『SQL + 互動 notebook』組合。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managed-flink/latest/java/how-notebook.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managed-flink/latest/java/how-zeppelin-interactive.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managed-flink/latest/java/how-zeppelin-sql-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managed-flink/latest/java/how-dashboard.html"]}},{"id":114,"question_en":"A medical company needs to store clinical data. The data includes personally identifiable information (PII) and protected health information (PHI). An ML engineer needs to implement a solution to ensure that the PII and PHI are not used to train ML models. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家医疗公司需要存储临床数据。这些数据包含个人身份信息（PII）和受保护的健康信息（PHI）。 一位机器学习工程师需要实施解决方案，以确保个人身份信息（PII）和受保护的健康信息（PHI）不被 用于训练机器学习模型。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Store the clinical data in Amazon S3 buckets. Use AWS Glue DataBrew to mask the PII and PHI before the data is used for model training.","B":"Upload the clinical data to an Amazon Redshift database. Use built-in SQL stored procedures to automatically classify and mask the PII and PHI before the data is used for model training.","C":"Use Amazon Comprehend to detect and mask the PII before the data is used for model training. Use Amazon Comprehend Medical to detect and mask the PHI before the data is used for model training.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function to encrypt the PII and PHI. Program the Lambda function to save the encrypted data to an Amazon S3 bucket for model training."},"options_zh":{"A":"将临床数据存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。在使用数据进行模型训练之前，使用 AWS Glue DataBrew 对个 人身份信息（PII）和受保护的健康信息（PHI）进行脱敏处理。","B":"将临床数据上传至亚马逊 Redshift 数据库。在使用数据进行模型训练之前，利用内置的 SQL 存储 过程自动对个人身份信息（PII）和受保护的健康信息（PHI）进行分类和屏蔽。","C":"在使用数据进行模型训练之前，使用 Amazon Comprehend 检测并屏蔽 PII（个人身份信息）。在使用数 据进行模型训练之前，使用 Amazon Comprehend Medical 检测并屏蔽 PHI（个人健康信息）。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来加密个人身份信息（PII）和受保护的健康信息（PHI）。编写 Lambda 函 数，将加密后的数据保存到 Amazon S3 存储桶中用于模型训练。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to ensure both PII and protected health information (PHI) in clinical data are not used to train ML models, which means de-identifying/redacting that sensitive data before training. Amazon Comprehend provides a purpose-built PII detection and redaction capability: its PII redaction job returns a copy of the input text with each PII entity (NAME, ADDRESS, CREDIT_DEBIT_NUMBER, etc.) replaced by masking characters. Amazon Comprehend Medical provides the DetectPHI operation, which is purpose-built to detect the HIPAA Protected Health Information entities (mapped to the 18-identifier categories such as NAME, DATE, ID, ADDRESS) in unstructured clinical text. Using Comprehend for PII and Comprehend Medical for PHI is the AWS NLP-based de-identification approach for clinical/medical free text, so option C removes both classes of sensitive data before training. The other options either lack the described capability (Redshift has no built-in stored procedures that auto-classify and mask PII/PHI), do not actually remove sensitive content (Lambda encryption preserves the underlying PII/PHI values), or are not purpose-built for PHI in unstructured clinical text (Glue DataBrew uses column/pattern-based masking rather than medical NLP).","explanation_zh":"需求是確保臨床資料中的 PII 與受保護健康資訊（PHI）不被用於訓練 ML 模型，亦即必須在訓練前對這些敏感資料進行去識別化/遮蔽。Amazon Comprehend 具備專門的 PII 偵測與遮蔽能力：其 PII redaction 工作會回傳一份將每個 PII 實體（NAME、ADDRESS、CREDIT_DEBIT_NUMBER 等）以遮蔽字元取代的輸入文字副本。Amazon Comprehend Medical 提供 DetectPHI 操作，專門用於偵測非結構化臨床文字中的 HIPAA PHI 實體（對應到 18 類識別碼，如 NAME、DATE、ID、ADDRESS）。以 Comprehend 處理 PII、以 Comprehend Medical 處理 PHI，正是 AWS 用於臨床/醫療自由文字的 NLP 去識別化做法，因此選項 C 能在訓練前移除這兩類敏感資料。其他選項要麼缺乏所述能力（Redshift 並無可自動分類與遮蔽 PII/PHI 的內建預存程序），要麼並未真正移除敏感內容（Lambda 加密仍保留底層 PII/PHI 值），要麼並非針對非結構化臨床文字中的 PHI 而設計（Glue DataBrew 採用以欄位/模式為基礎的遮蔽，而非醫療 NLP）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Glue DataBrew is a visual, column-based data-prep tool that can mask PII via pattern/column transforms, but it is not purpose-built for detecting PHI in unstructured clinical free text and lacks medical NLP, so it would not reliably de-identify HIPAA PHI for model training.","why_zh":"AWS Glue DataBrew 是以欄位為基礎的視覺化資料準備工具，可透過模式/欄位轉換遮蔽 PII，但並非為偵測非結構化臨床自由文字中的 PHI 而設計，且缺乏醫療 NLP，因此無法可靠地將 HIPAA PHI 去識別化以供模型訓練。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Redshift has no built-in SQL stored procedures that automatically classify and mask PII and PHI; this capability as described does not exist, so the option is technically fabricated.","why_zh":"Amazon Redshift 並無可自動分類與遮蔽 PII 及 PHI 的內建 SQL 預存程序；所述功能並不存在，因此此選項在技術上屬虛構。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Encrypting the PII and PHI with a Lambda function protects data at rest but does not remove or de-identify it; the sensitive values (decrypted for training, or even as ciphertext) still represent the same PII/PHI, so models could still be trained on it.","why_zh":"以 Lambda 函式加密 PII 與 PHI 僅保護靜態資料，並未移除或去識別化；敏感值（在訓練時解密後，甚至作為密文）仍代表相同的 PII/PHI，模型仍可能據此訓練。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/how-pii.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend-medical/latest/dev/textanalysis-phi.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend-medical/latest/dev/comprehendmedical-welcome.html"]}},{"id":115,"question_en":"An ML engineer is developing a classification model. The ML engineer needs to use custom libraries in processing jobs, training jobs, and pipelines in Amazon SageMaker. Which solution will provide this functionality with the LEAST implementation effort?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师正在开发一个分类模型。该工程师需要在 Amazon SageMaker 中的处理作业、训练 作业和管道中使用自定义库。 哪种解决方案能以最少的实施工作量提供此功能？","options_en":{"A":"Manually install the libraries in the SageMaker containers.","B":"Build a custom Docker container that includes the required libraries. Host the container in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Use the ECR image in the SageMaker jobs and pipelines.","C":"Create a SageMaker notebook instance to host the jobs. Create an AWS Lambda function to install the libraries on the notebook instance when the notebook instance starts. Configure the SageMaker jobs and pipelines to run on the notebook instance.","D":"Run code for the libraries externally on Amazon EC2 instances. Store the results in Amazon S3. Import the results into the SageMaker jobs and pipelines."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 SageMaker 容器中手动安装库。","B":"构建一个包含所需库的自定义 Docker 容器。将该容器托管在亚马逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中。 在 SageMaker 作业和管道中使用 ECR 镜像。","C":"创建一个 SageMaker 笔记本实例来承载作业。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，在笔记本实例启动时为其安 装库。配置 SageMaker 作业和管道在笔记本实例上运行。","D":"在亚马逊 EC2 实例上外部运行库代码。将结果存储在亚马逊 S3 中。导入 将结果输入到 SageMaker 作业和管道中。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon SageMaker always runs scripts, processing jobs, training algorithms, and pipeline steps inside Docker containers, and each of those job types natively accepts a custom container image referenced by an Amazon ECR URI. The AWS container decision-tree documentation states that when a pre-built image does not include the custom packages you need, you should extend it or build your own container, host it in ECR, and reference that image in your jobs. Building one custom Docker image with all required libraries baked in and pointing every processing job, training job, and pipeline step at that same ECR image yields a single, reusable, repeatable artifact - the least implementation effort for consistent custom libraries across all three workloads. The other options either do not persist (ad-hoc installs on ephemeral containers), misrepresent how managed jobs run (they do not run on a notebook instance), or move the work outside SageMaker entirely.","explanation_zh":"Amazon SageMaker 在執行 script、processing job、training 演算法與 pipeline step 時一律使用 Docker container，而這些 job 類型都原生支援透過 Amazon ECR 的 image URI 指定自訂 container image。AWS 的 container 決策樹文件指出：當 pre-built image 不含你所需的自訂套件時，應該擴充（extend）它或自行建置（build）container，將其放在 ECR，然後在 job 中參照該 image。只要建置一個內含所有所需函式庫的自訂 Docker image，並讓每個 processing job、training job 與 pipeline step 都指向同一個 ECR image，就能取得單一、可重複使用、可重現的 artifact，是讓三種工作負載一致使用自訂函式庫所需實作工作量最少的方案。其他選項不是無法持久化（在短暫的 container 上臨時安裝），就是誤解 managed job 的執行方式（它們並非在 notebook instance 上執行），或乾脆把工作搬到 SageMaker 之外。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SageMaker job containers are ephemeral and recreated for every job run, so manually installed libraries do not persist; you would have to reinstall them on each invocation, which is unreliable and high effort, not the least, and is not a single reusable artifact across processing, training, and pipelines.","why_zh":"SageMaker job container 是短暫的，每次執行 job 都會重新建立，手動安裝的函式庫無法保存；每次叫用都得重裝，既不可靠又費工，並非工作量最少，也不是可在 processing、training 與 pipeline 之間重用的單一 artifact。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Managed SageMaker processing jobs, training jobs, and pipeline steps run on managed job clusters, not on a notebook instance, so you cannot configure them to run on the notebook; adding a Lambda to install libraries on notebook startup is architecturally invalid and adds effort.","why_zh":"受管的 SageMaker processing job、training job 與 pipeline step 在受管的 job 叢集上執行，而非在 notebook instance 上，因此無法將它們設定為在 notebook 上執行；再加上用 Lambda 在 notebook 啟動時安裝函式庫，架構上不成立且增加工作量。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Running library code externally on EC2 and importing results via S3 moves compute out of SageMaker, requires custom orchestration glue, and never actually makes the custom libraries available inside the SageMaker jobs and pipelines - maximum effort and does not meet the requirement.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上於外部執行函式庫程式碼並透過 S3 匯入結果，會把運算移出 SageMaker，需要自訂協調黏合，且實際上並未讓自訂函式庫在 SageMaker job 與 pipeline 內可用 - 工作量最大且不符合需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/docker-containers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/docker-containers-adapt-your-own.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/prebuilt-containers-extend.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/use-your-own-processing-code.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/build-your-own-processing-container.html"]}},{"id":116,"question_en":"An ML engineer is deploying a trained model to an Amazon SageMaker endpoint. The ML engineer needs to receive alerts when data quality issues occur in production. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师正在将一个训练好的模型部署到亚马逊 SageMaker 端点。该机器学习工程师需要在生 产环境中出现数据质量问题时收到警报。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an Amazon CloudWatch metric alarm and a corresponding action to send an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) notification.","B":"Integrate the SageMaker endpoint with a SageMaker Clarify processing job. Configure an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to provide alerts.","C":"Configure a monitoring job in SageMaker Model Monitor. Integrate Model Monitor with Amazon CloudWatch to provide alerts.","D":"Configure a data flow in SageMaker Data Wrangler. Integrate Data Wrangler with Amazon CloudWatch to provide alerts."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个 Amazon CloudWatch 指标警报以及相应的操作，以发送 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）通知。","B":"将 SageMaker 端点与 SageMaker Clarify 处理作业集成。配置 Amazon CloudWatch 警报以提供提醒。","C":"在 SageMaker 模型监控器中配置监控任务。将模型监控器与 Amazon CloudWatch 集成以提供警报。","D":"在 SageMaker Data Wrangler 中配置数据流。将 Data Wrangler 与 Amazon CloudWatch 集成以提供警报。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Detecting data quality issues for a deployed SageMaker endpoint in production is the exact purpose of SageMaker Model Monitor's data quality monitoring. The AWS docs state that data quality monitoring 'automatically monitors machine learning (ML) models in production and notifies you when data quality issues arise.' The documented workflow is: enable data capture on the endpoint, create a baseline (constraints and statistics computed with Deequ), schedule data quality monitoring jobs, and 'Integrate data quality monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch.' Model Monitor emits CloudWatch metrics such as feature_baseline_drift_{feature_name}; you then create a CloudWatch alarm on those metrics (with an SNS action) to receive alerts. Option C matches this end-to-end pattern exactly.","explanation_zh":"偵測已部署 SageMaker endpoint 在生產環境中的資料品質問題，正是 SageMaker Model Monitor 的 data quality monitoring 的用途。AWS 文件指出 data quality monitoring 會「自動監控生產環境中的 ML 模型，並在出現資料品質問題時通知你」。文件化的流程為：在 endpoint 上啟用 data capture、建立 baseline（以 Deequ 計算 constraints 與 statistics）、排程 data quality monitoring jobs，並「將 data quality monitoring 與 Amazon CloudWatch 整合」。Model Monitor 會發出如 feature_baseline_drift_{feature_name} 等 CloudWatch 指標；接著你針對這些指標建立 CloudWatch alarm（搭配 SNS 動作）即可收到告警。選項 C 完全符合此端到端模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A plain CloudWatch metric alarm + SNS can alert on endpoint operational/infrastructure metrics (latency, invocations, errors), but CloudWatch does not natively compute data quality / data drift metrics. Without Model Monitor first analyzing captured inference data against a baseline, there is no data-quality metric for an alarm to watch, so this alone cannot detect data quality issues.","why_zh":"單純的 CloudWatch metric alarm + SNS 可針對 endpoint 的運算/基礎設施指標（延遲、調用次數、錯誤）發出告警，但 CloudWatch 本身不會計算資料品質／資料漂移指標。若沒有先用 Model Monitor 將擷取的推論資料與 baseline 比對，就沒有資料品質指標可供 alarm 監看，因此單靠此選項無法偵測資料品質問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"SageMaker Clarify monitoring targets bias drift and feature attribution drift, not general data quality (schema/statistics) drift. The docs list Clarify-based monitoring as distinct from data quality monitoring, so Clarify is the wrong tool for this requirement; the dedicated capability is Model Monitor's data quality monitor.","why_zh":"SageMaker Clarify 監控的是 bias drift 與 feature attribution drift，而非一般的資料品質（schema/統計）漂移。文件將以 Clarify 為基礎的監控與 data quality monitoring 分列為不同類型，因此 Clarify 不是此需求的正確工具；專責的功能是 Model Monitor 的 data quality monitor。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SageMaker Data Wrangler is a data preparation / feature engineering tool used before training to clean and transform datasets. It is not a production monitoring service for deployed endpoints and does not detect data-quality drift on a live endpoint or emit ongoing alerts via CloudWatch.","why_zh":"SageMaker Data Wrangler 是訓練前用於清理與轉換資料集的資料準備／特徵工程工具，並非針對已部署 endpoint 的生產監控服務，無法偵測線上 endpoint 的資料品質漂移，也不會透過 CloudWatch 發出持續告警。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-data-quality.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-interpreting-cloudwatch.html"]}},{"id":117,"question_en":"A company needs to use Amazon SageMaker to train a model on more than 300 GB of data. The training data is composed of files that are 200 MB in size. The data is stored in Amazon S3 Standard storage and feeds a dashboard tool. Which SageMaker training ingestion mechanism is the MOST cost-effective solution for this scenario?","question_zh":"一家公司需要使用亚马逊 SageMaker 对超过 300GB 的数据进行模型训练。训练数据由大小为 200MB 的文 件组成。这些数据存储在亚马逊 S3 标准存储中，并为一个仪表板工具提供数据。 对于此场景，哪种 SageMaker 训练数据摄取机制是最具成本效益的解决方案？","options_en":{"A":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system","B":"Amazon FSx for Lustre file system","C":"Amazon S3 in fast file mode while using S3 Express One Zone","D":"Amazon S3 in fast file mode without using S3 Express One Zone"},"options_zh":{"A":"亚马逊弹性文件系统（Amazon EFS）文件系统","B":"亚马逊 FSx for Lustre 文件系统","C":"在使用 S3 Express One Zone 时，Amazon S3 快速文件模式","D":"快速文件模式下的 Amazon S3（未使用 S3 Express One Zone）"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The dataset is 300+ GB made of 200 MB files already stored in S3 Standard, where it also feeds a dashboard tool, so it must stay accessible in regular S3. AWS guidance ('Choosing an input mode and a storage unit') says that for larger datasets with larger files (more than 50 MB per file, ideal for containers more than 150 MB) the first option is fast file mode, because it streams S3 objects on demand via a POSIX interface and, unlike FSx for Lustre or EFS, requires no file system creation or VPC connection. That eliminates EFS (A) and FSx for Lustre (B), which both require copying the data into a provisioned file system and add VPC/operational overhead. The deciding factor between C and D is cost: S3 Express One Zone is a separate, higher-per-GB single-AZ storage class that AWS recommends only when the workload is performance sensitive and benefits from single-digit-millisecond PUT/GET latencies, and it requires a directory bucket - so adopting it would mean copying 300+ GB into a more expensive store, not 'most cost-effective.' Reading directly from the existing S3 Standard data with fast file mode (D) incurs no additional storage-class cost or data duplication, making it the cheapest viable option.","explanation_zh":"資料集為 300+ GB、由 200 MB 檔案組成，且已存放在 S3 Standard，同時供 dashboard 工具使用，因此必須保持在一般 S3 中可存取。AWS 官方指南（Choosing an input mode and a storage unit）指出，對於檔案較大（每個檔案 >50 MB，最適合 >150 MB 容器）的大型資料集，第一選擇是 fast file mode，因為它透過 POSIX 介面依需求串流 S3 物件，且不像 FSx for Lustre 或 EFS 需要建立檔案系統或連接 VPC。這排除了 EFS（A）與 FSx for Lustre（B），兩者皆須把資料複製到預配的檔案系統並增加 VPC/營運負擔。C 與 D 的關鍵差異在成本：S3 Express One Zone 是每 GB 較貴、單一 AZ 的獨立儲存類別，AWS 僅在工作負載對效能敏感、需要單位數毫秒 PUT/GET 延遲時才建議使用，並需要 directory bucket，採用它等於把 300+ GB 複製到更昂貴的儲存，並非最具成本效益。直接以 fast file mode 讀取既有 S3 Standard 資料（D）不需額外儲存類別費用或資料複製，是最便宜可行的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"EFS requires the data to already reside in an EFS file system and the training job to connect to a VPC. The data is in S3 Standard, so you would have to copy it into a provisioned EFS file system - extra cost and operational overhead, not cost-effective.","why_zh":"EFS 要求資料事先已存放於 EFS 檔案系統，且訓練工作需連接 VPC。資料目前在 S3 Standard，採用 EFS 須先把資料複製到預配的 EFS 檔案系統，增加成本與營運負擔，並不符合成本效益。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"FSx for Lustre delivers the highest throughput but requires creating/maintaining a file system, connecting to a VPC, and has cold-start lazy-loading overhead. AWS recommends it mainly for datasets too large for file mode, with many small files, or random-read patterns - overkill and more costly for 200 MB sequential-read files already in S3.","why_zh":"FSx for Lustre 提供最高吞吐量，但需建立並維護檔案系統、連接 VPC，且有 lazy-loading 冷啟動開銷。AWS 主要建議用於對 file mode 而言過大、含大量小檔或隨機讀取模式的資料集；對已在 S3 的 200 MB 循序讀取檔案而言過度且更昂貴。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"S3 Express One Zone is a higher-cost, single-AZ storage class that AWS recommends only when the application is performance sensitive and benefits from single-digit-millisecond PUT/GET latencies; it requires a directory bucket. The data already lives in S3 Standard, so using Express One Zone would mean copying it into a more expensive store - the opposite of 'most cost-effective.' The scenario emphasizes cost, not lowest latency.","why_zh":"S3 Express One Zone 是成本較高、單一 AZ 的儲存類別，AWS 僅在應用程式對效能敏感、需要單位數毫秒 PUT/GET 延遲時才建議使用，並需要 directory bucket。資料已存於 S3 Standard，使用 Express One Zone 須複製到更昂貴的儲存，與「最具成本效益」背道而馳。本題強調成本而非最低延遲。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-access-training-data-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-access-training-data.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/directory-bucket-use-cases.html"]}},{"id":118,"question_en":"A company has an ML model that is deployed to an Amazon SageMaker endpoint for real-time inference. The company needs to deploy a new model. The company must compare the new model’s performance to the currently deployed model’s performance before shifting all traffic to the new model. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个部署在亚马逊 SageMaker 端点上用于实时推理的机器学习模型。该公司需要部署一个新的模 型。该公司必须将新模型的性能与 在将所有流量切换到新模型之前，当前部署模型的性能。 哪种解决方案能以最少的操作努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the new model to a separate endpoint. Manually split traffic between the two endpoints.","B":"Deploy the new model to a separate endpoint. Use Amazon CloudFront to distribute traffic between the two endpoints.","C":"Deploy the new model as a shadow variant on the same endpoint as the current model. Route a portion of live traffic to the shadow model for evaluation.","D":"Use AWS Lambda functions with custom logic to route traffic between the current model and the new model."},"options_zh":{"A":"将新模型部署到单独的端点。手动在两个端点之间分配流量。","B":"将新模型部署到单独的端点。使用 Amazon CloudFront 在两个端点之间分配流量。","C":"在与当前模型相同的端点上部署新模型作为影子变体。将一部分实时流量路由到影子模型以进 行评估。","D":"使用具有自定义逻辑的 AWS Lambda 函数在当前模型和新模型之间路由流量。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon SageMaker shadow testing is purpose-built for this scenario. The AWS docs state you can 'evaluate any changes to your model serving infrastructure by comparing its performance against the currently deployed infrastructure,' and explicitly list the use case of promoting 'a new model that has been validated offline to production' while you 'evaluate operational performance metrics such as latency and error rate before making this decision.' When you add a shadow variant, SageMaker 'automatically deploys the new variant in shadow mode and routes a copy of the inference requests to it in real time within the same endpoint,' returning only the production variant's responses to callers. AWS manages the shadow infrastructure, request mirroring, a guided console workflow, and a live comparison dashboard, so 'you don't need to invest in building your shadow testing infrastructure' - the least operational effort. The other options require you to build and maintain custom traffic-splitting and metric-comparison logic.","explanation_zh":"Amazon SageMaker shadow testing 正是為此情境設計。AWS 文件指出你可以「將模型服務基礎設施的任何變更與目前部署的基礎設施進行效能比較」，並明確列出此使用案例：在將「已離線驗證的新模型」推上 production 之前，先「評估 latency、error rate 等操作效能指標再做決定」。當你新增 shadow variant 時，SageMaker 會「自動以 shadow 模式部署新 variant，並在同一個 endpoint 內即時將推論請求的副本路由到它」，且只把 production variant 的回應回傳給呼叫端。AWS 代為管理 shadow 基礎設施、請求鏡像、引導式 console 工作流程與即時比較儀表板，所以「你不需要投入建置自己的 shadow testing 基礎設施」，操作負擔最少。其他選項都需要自行建置與維護流量分配與指標比較邏輯。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Deploying to a separate endpoint and manually splitting traffic forces you to build, operate, and maintain the routing and a custom comparison mechanism yourself, which is far more operational effort than the managed shadow-test workflow that mirrors traffic automatically.","why_zh":"部署到另一個 endpoint 並手動分配流量，需自行建置、運作與維護路由與自訂比較機制，操作負擔遠高於會自動鏡像流量的託管 shadow test 工作流程。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudFront is a content delivery network, not an inference-evaluation tool; using it to split model traffic is an unnatural, custom setup that adds complexity and provides no built-in model-performance comparison.","why_zh":"CloudFront 是內容傳遞網路 (CDN)，並非推論評估工具；用它分配模型流量是不自然的自建方案，增加複雜度且無內建的模型效能比較。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Custom Lambda routing logic means you must develop, deploy, and maintain code plus your own metric-comparison process, giving the highest operational overhead rather than the least.","why_zh":"自訂 Lambda 路由邏輯意味著必須開發、部署並維護程式碼，外加自己的指標比較流程，操作負擔最高而非最少。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/shadow-tests.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/shadow-tests-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-deploy-mlops.html"]}},{"id":119,"question_en":"A company runs an ML model on Amazon SageMaker. The company uses an automatic process that makes API calls to create training jobs for the model. The company has new compliance rules that prohibit the collection of aggregated metadata from training jobs. Which solution will prevent SageMaker from collecting metadata from the training jobs?","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊 SageMaker 上运行机器学习模型。该公司使用自动流程通过调用 API 来为模型创建训 练任务。该公司有新的合规规定，禁止从训练任务中收集聚合的元数据。 哪种解决方案可以防止 SageMaker 从训练作业中收集元数据？","options_en":{"A":"Opt out of metadata tracking for any training job that is submitted.","B":"Ensure that training jobs are running in a private subnet in a custom VPC.","C":"Encrypt the training data with an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key.","D":"Reconfigure the training jobs to use only AWS Nitro instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"对于提交的任何训练任务，选择退出元数据跟踪。","B":"确保训练任务在自定义 VPC 的私有子网中运行。","C":"使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）客户管理密钥对训练数据进行加密。","D":"重新配置训练任务，使其仅使用 AWS Nitro 实例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon SageMaker AI collects aggregate metadata about training jobs (usage information from AWS-owned and open-source libraries used during training, plus errors) to improve its services. The official 'Data Privacy in Amazon SageMaker AI' page documents the exact mechanism to stop this: opt out of metadata collection by setting the OPT_OUT_TRACKING environment variable to 1 in the CreateTrainingJob API call. The docs explicitly state 'You must choose to opt out of metadata collection for each training job that you submit' and that the opt-out must be done in the API call (it cannot be done inside a training script). Because the company uses an automated process that issues CreateTrainingJob API calls, opting out per submitted training job (or account-wide via SageMaker Python SDK defaults) is the correct and intended mechanism to satisfy the compliance rule. None of the other options (VPC placement, encryption, or instance type) affect this telemetry collection.","explanation_zh":"Amazon SageMaker AI 會收集 training jobs 的彙整 metadata（來自訓練期間使用的 AWS 自有與開源程式庫之使用資訊，以及錯誤），用於改善服務。官方「Data Privacy in Amazon SageMaker AI」文件記載了停止此行為的確切機制：在 CreateTrainingJob API 呼叫中將環境變數 OPT_OUT_TRACKING 設為 1，即可退出 metadata 收集。文件明確指出「您必須為每個提交的 training job 選擇退出 metadata 收集」，且退出動作必須在 API 呼叫中完成（無法在 training script 內完成）。由於公司使用自動化流程呼叫 CreateTrainingJob API，針對每個提交的 training job 進行退出（或透過 SageMaker Python SDK 預設值在帳戶層級退出）正是滿足合規規則的正確且設計上的機制。其他選項（VPC 配置、加密或執行個體類型）都不會影響此遙測收集。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Running training jobs in a private subnet of a custom VPC provides network isolation and controls inbound/outbound traffic, but it does not stop SageMaker from collecting aggregate metadata about library usage and errors. Metadata collection is a service-level feature governed by the OPT_OUT_TRACKING setting, not by VPC placement.","why_zh":"在自訂 VPC 的私有子網路中執行 training jobs 可提供網路隔離並控制進出流量，但無法阻止 SageMaker 收集關於程式庫使用與錯誤的彙整 metadata。Metadata 收集是由 OPT_OUT_TRACKING 設定控制的服務層級功能，與 VPC 配置無關。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Encrypting training data with an AWS KMS customer managed key protects data at rest. It has no effect on the aggregate metadata (library usage and errors) that SageMaker collects to improve services.","why_zh":"使用 AWS KMS 客戶受管金鑰加密 training data 可保護靜態資料，但對 SageMaker 為改善服務而收集的彙整 metadata（程式庫使用與錯誤）沒有任何影響。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Nitro instances provide hardware-level isolation and confidential computing, but switching instance types does not disable SageMaker's training-job metadata collection. The opt-out is controlled by the OPT_OUT_TRACKING environment variable in the API call, not by instance type.","why_zh":"AWS Nitro 執行個體提供硬體層級的隔離與機密運算，但更換執行個體類型並不會停用 SageMaker 的 training job metadata 收集。退出由 API 呼叫中的 OPT_OUT_TRACKING 環境變數控制，而非執行個體類型。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-privacy.html"]}},{"id":120,"question_en":"A company is exploring generative AI and wants to add a new product feature. An ML engineer is making API calls from existing Amazon EC2 instances to Amazon Bedrock. The EC2 instances are in a private subnet and must remain private during the implementation. The EC2 instances have an assigned security group that allows access to all IP addresses in the private subnet. What should the ML engineer do to establish a connection between the EC2 instances and Amazon Bedrock?","question_zh":"一家公司正在探索生成式人工智能，并希望添加一项新的产品功能。一位机器学习工程师正在从现有的 亚马逊 EC2 实例向亚马逊 Bedrock 发起 API 调用。这些 EC2 实例位于一个私有子网中，在实施过程中 必须保持私有状态。这些 EC2 实例被分配了一个安全组，该安全组允许与私有子网中的所有 IP 地址进 行访问。 机器学习工程师应如何在 EC2 实例与亚马逊 Bedrock 之间建立连接？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the security group to allow inbound and outbound traffic to and from Amazon Bedrock.","B":"Use AWS PrivateLink to access Amazon Bedrock through an interface VPC endpoint.","C":"Configure Amazon Bedrock to use the private subnet where the EC2 instances are deployed.","D":"Link the existing VPC to Amazon Bedrock by using an AWS Direct Connect connection."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改安全组设置，允许与 Amazon Bedrock 之间的入站和出站流量。","B":"使用 AWS PrivateLink 通过接口 VPC 终端节点访问 Amazon Bedrock。","C":"将 Amazon Bedrock 配置为使用部署了 EC2 实例的私有子网。","D":"使用 AWS Direct Connect 连接将现有的 VPC 与 Amazon Bedrock 相连。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Bedrock supports AWS PrivateLink interface VPC endpoints. The Bedrock User Guide states verbatim that you can use AWS PrivateLink to create a private connection between your VPC and Amazon Bedrock, accessing Bedrock as if it were in your VPC, without an internet gateway, NAT device, VPN connection, or Direct Connect connection, and instances in your VPC do not need public IP addresses. This exactly satisfies the requirement that the EC2 instances stay in a private subnet and remain private. The ML engineer creates an interface endpoint (for example, com.amazonaws.region.bedrock-runtime), and AWS provisions an endpoint network interface in the subnet so API calls from the private-subnet EC2 instances route privately over the AWS network. The endpoint's security group and the EC2 security group control traffic, and no public path is introduced.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Bedrock 支援 AWS PrivateLink 的 interface VPC endpoint。Bedrock User Guide 原文指出，你可以使用 AWS PrivateLink 在你的 VPC 與 Amazon Bedrock 之間建立私有連線，像 Bedrock 位於你的 VPC 中一樣存取它，不需要 internet gateway、NAT device、VPN connection 或 Direct Connect connection，而且 VPC 中的執行個體不需要公有 IP。這正好符合題目要求：EC2 instances 位於 private subnet 且必須保持私有。ML engineer 建立 interface endpoint（例如 com.amazonaws.region.bedrock-runtime），AWS 會在該 subnet 中佈建 endpoint network interface，讓 private subnet 中 EC2 instances 的 API 呼叫透過 AWS 內部網路私有地路由。Endpoint 的 security group 與 EC2 的 security group 控管流量，不會引入任何公有路徑。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Bedrock is a public AWS service endpoint, not a discrete set of IP addresses you can target in a security group rule, so modifying the security group alone provides no private network path. Reaching the public Bedrock endpoint from a private subnet would require a NAT gateway or internet egress, which conflicts with keeping the instances private.","why_zh":"Bedrock 是公有的 AWS 服務端點，不是可在 security group 規則中指定的一組固定 IP，光修改 security group 無法提供私有網路路徑。從 private subnet 連到公有 Bedrock 端點會需要 NAT gateway 或對外上網，這與保持執行個體私有相互矛盾。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Bedrock is a fully managed AWS service; you cannot deploy or configure it into your own subnet. Connectivity is achieved by bringing the service into your VPC via a PrivateLink interface endpoint, not by placing Bedrock inside your subnet.","why_zh":"Amazon Bedrock 是全託管的 AWS 服務，你無法把它部署或設定到自己的 subnet 中。連線方式是透過 PrivateLink interface endpoint 把服務帶進你的 VPC，而非把 Bedrock 放進你的 subnet。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Direct Connect provides a dedicated link between on-premises networks and AWS; it does not link a VPC to a managed service like Bedrock. The Bedrock docs explicitly note that PrivateLink avoids needing a Direct Connect connection, and Direct Connect is irrelevant for EC2-to-Bedrock traffic that is already inside AWS.","why_zh":"AWS Direct Connect 提供地端網路與 AWS 之間的專線，並不是用來把 VPC 連接到 Bedrock 這類託管服務。Bedrock 文件明確指出使用 PrivateLink 即可避免需要 Direct Connect，而對於本就位於 AWS 內部的 EC2-to-Bedrock 流量，Direct Connect 並不相關。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/vpc-interface-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/usingVPC.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/create-interface-endpoint.html"]}},{"id":121,"question_en":"HOTSPOT An ecommerce company is using Amazon SageMaker Clarify Foundation Model Evaluations (FMEval) to evaluate ML models. Select the correct model evaluation task from the following list for each ecommerce use case. Each model evaluation task should be selected one time. Classification evaluation Open-ended generation Question answering Text summarization Hot Area: Correct Answer: Section: (none) Explanation/Reference: Explanation: Categorize customer reviews as positive, neutral, or negative sentiment → Classification evaluation Sentiment categorization is a classification task. Create concise product descriptions from complete manufacturer details → Text summarization Condensing manufacturer details into product descriptions is a summarization task. Recommend products based on a user's browsing history → Open-ended generation Generating recommendations requires open-ended generative modeling. Respond to specific customer queries about product features → Question answering Handling direct customer queries about features aligns with question answering.","question_zh":"热点 一家电子商务公司正在使用亚马逊 SageMaker Clarify 基础模型评估（FMEval）来评估机器学习模型。 从以下列表中为每个电商用例选择正确的模型评估任务。每个模型评估任务只能选择一次。 分类评估 开放式生成 问答 文本摘要 热点区域： 正确答案： 部分：（无） 解释/参考： 解释： 将客户评论分类为积极、中立或消极情绪 → 分类评估 情绪分类是一项分类任务。 从完整的制造商详情中提炼出简洁的产品描述 → 文本摘要 将制造商详情浓缩为产品描述是一项 摘要任务。 根据用户的浏览历史推荐产品 → 开放式生成 生成推荐需要开放式生成建模。 回应客户关于产品特性的具体询问 → 问答处理 直接处理客户关于产品特性的询问与 问答处理相符。","options_en":{},"options_zh":{},"answer":[],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":122,"question_en":"A company wants to launch a new internal generative AI interface to answer user questions. The interface will be based on a popular open source large language model (LLM). Which combination of steps will deploy the interface with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon SageMaker JumpStart to deploy the LLM.","B":"Download the LLM as a .zip file. Deploy the LLM on a GPU-based Amazon EC2 instance.","C":"Create a frontend HTML interface that uses an Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API with AWS Lambda functions to handle the user interaction.","D":"Use Amazon QuickSight to create a UI to handle the user interaction.","E":"Use Amazon Lex to create a UI to handle the user interaction."},"options_zh":{},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The task needs two building blocks with the LEAST operational overhead: a way to host the open-source LLM and a way to build the user interface. Amazon SageMaker JumpStart (A) onboards and maintains publicly available open-source foundation models (LLaMa-3, BLOOM, FLAN-T5, Mistral, etc.) and deploys them to a fully managed SageMaker AI endpoint with a single SDK/CLI command, so AWS handles infrastructure, GPU serving, scaling, and model maintenance. For the interface, a frontend HTML page backed by an Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API and AWS Lambda (C) is a fully serverless pattern with no servers to manage; AWS documents this exact WebSocket-API-plus-Lambda design as the way to build a real-time chat application, and its bidirectional behavior fits streaming two-way chat with the LLM endpoint. Together, A + C give a managed model endpoint plus a serverless UI, which is the lowest-overhead combination. The other options are either the highest overhead (B, self-managed GPU EC2) or the wrong type of service for a generative-AI chat UI (D QuickSight is BI; E Lex is an intent/slot NLU bot builder that adds modeling work and does not naturally pass free-form prompts to a self-hosted JumpStart LLM endpoint).","explanation_zh":"本題需要兩個維運負擔最低的組件：一個用於託管開源 LLM，一個用於建立使用者介面。Amazon SageMaker JumpStart (A) 會為你引入並維護公開可用的開源基礎模型（LLaMa-3、BLOOM、FLAN-T5、Mistral 等），只需單一 SDK/CLI 指令即可部署到完全託管的 SageMaker AI endpoint，AWS 負責基礎設施、GPU 推論服務、擴展與模型維護。介面方面，以 Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API 搭配 AWS Lambda 為後端的前端 HTML 頁面 (C) 是完全 serverless 的架構，無伺服器需管理；AWS 官方文件正是以此 WebSocket API 加 Lambda 的設計來建立即時聊天應用，且其雙向特性適合與 LLM endpoint 進行串流式雙向聊天。A + C 結合提供託管模型 endpoint 加上 serverless UI，是維運負擔最低的組合。其餘選項要不是維運負擔最高（B 自管 GPU EC2），就是服務類型不適合生成式 AI 聊天 UI（D QuickSight 是 BI 工具；E Lex 是基於 intent/slot 的 NLU 機器人建構工具，會增加建模工作，且無法自然地將自由形式提示傳遞給自行託管的 JumpStart LLM endpoint）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Downloading the model as a .zip and running it on a GPU-based EC2 instance forces you to provision the instance, install GPU drivers/CUDA, set up a model-serving framework, patch the OS, and manage scaling yourself. That is the HIGHEST operational overhead, the opposite of what is asked, and it is strictly worse than the managed JumpStart endpoint in option A.","why_zh":"將模型下載為 .zip 並在 GPU EC2 instance 上執行，需自行佈建執行個體、安裝 GPU 驅動/CUDA、建立模型服務框架、修補作業系統並自行管理擴展，是最高的維運負擔，與題意相反，且明顯不如選項 A 的託管 JumpStart endpoint。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon QuickSight is a business intelligence and dashboarding service for visualizing data. It is not designed to build an interactive chat UI that sends prompts to and renders responses from an LLM endpoint, so it cannot serve as the generative AI interface.","why_zh":"Amazon QuickSight 是用於資料視覺化的商業智慧與儀表板服務，並非設計來建立可向 LLM endpoint 傳送提示並呈現回應的互動式聊天 UI，因此無法作為生成式 AI 介面。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Amazon Lex builds intent- and slot-based conversational bots driven by NLU. The scenario hosts a generic open-source LLM on SageMaker and wants a free-form 'ask any question' interface; Lex's intent-modeling and bot-design work add overhead and it does not naturally pass arbitrary prompts straight through to a self-hosted JumpStart LLM endpoint, making the serverless API Gateway + Lambda + HTML option (C) the lower-overhead UI choice.","why_zh":"Amazon Lex 用於建立以 NLU 驅動、基於 intent 與 slot 的對話機器人。本情境是在 SageMaker 上託管通用開源 LLM 並希望提供自由形式的「任意提問」介面；Lex 的 intent 建模與機器人設計工作會增加負擔，且無法自然地將任意提示直接傳遞給自行託管的 JumpStart LLM endpoint，因此 serverless 的 API Gateway + Lambda + HTML 選項 (C) 才是維運負擔較低的 UI 選擇。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/jumpstart-foundation-models.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/deploy-jumpstart-model.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/jumpstart-foundation-models-use-python-sdk-model-class.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-websocket-api.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/websocket-api-chat-app.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-apigateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lexv2/latest/dg/what-is.html"]}},{"id":123,"question_en":"A company wants to build a real-time analytics application that uses streaming data from social media. An ML engineer must implement a solution that ingests and transforms 5 GB of data each minute. The solution also must load the data into a data store that supports fast queries for the real-time analytics. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司想要构建一个实时分析应用程序，该程序使用来自社交媒体的流数据。一位机器学习工程师必须实现一个解决方案，每分 钟能够摄取并转换 5GB 的数据。该解决方案还必须将数据加载到支持快速查询以进行实时分析的数据存储中。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon EventBridge to ingest the social media data. Use AWS Glue to transform the data. Store the transformed data in Amazon ElastiCache (Memcached).","B":"Use Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) to ingest the social media data. Use AWS Lambda to transform the data. Store the transformed data in Amazon S3.","C":"Use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to ingest the social media data. Use Amazon EMR to transform the data. Store the transformed data in Amazon RDS.","D":"Use Amazon Kinesis Data Streams to ingest the social media data. Use Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink to transform the data. Store the transformed data in Amazon DynamoDB."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 来摄取社交媒体数据。使用 AWS Glue 来转换数据。将转换后的数据存储在 Amazon ElastiCache （Memcached）中。","B":"使用亚马逊简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）来获取社交媒体数据。使用 AWS Lambda 来转换数据。将转换后的数据存储在亚马逊 S3 中。","C":"使用亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）来获取社交媒体数据。使用亚马逊弹性 MapReduce（Amazon EMR）来转换数据。将 转换后的数据存储在亚马逊关系数据库服务（Amazon RDS）中。","D":"使用亚马逊 Kinesis 数据流来摄取社交媒体数据。使用亚马逊托管的 Apache Flink 服务来转换数据。将转换后的数据存储在亚马 逊 DynamoDB 中。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a real-time analytics pipeline that ingests high-throughput streaming social media data (5 GB/min), transforms it, and lands it in a store supporting fast queries. Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is purpose-built for 'rapid and continuous data intake and aggregation' of large streams in real time, and AWS documentation explicitly lists social media as a typical data source. Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink (formerly Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink) is the fully managed service for processing and transforming streaming data in real time with stateful computations, and it provides sink connectors (including DynamoDB) to write transformed records continuously. Amazon DynamoDB delivers consistent single-digit millisecond read/write performance, making it the ideal fast-query data store for the real-time analytics application. This end-to-end combination is the canonical AWS streaming-analytics architecture, so D is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是建立即時分析管線，要能擷取高吞吐量的串流社群媒體資料（每分鐘 5 GB）、進行轉換，並寫入支援快速查詢的資料儲存。Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 專為即時「快速且持續地擷取與彙整」大量串流資料而設計，AWS 文件明確將社群媒體列為典型資料來源。Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink（前身為 Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink）是全受管服務，可即時處理與轉換串流資料並支援具狀態運算，並提供 sink 連接器（含 DynamoDB）持續寫入轉換後的記錄。Amazon DynamoDB 提供穩定的個位數毫秒讀寫效能，是即時分析應用快速查詢資料儲存的理想選擇。此端到端組合是 AWS 標準的串流分析架構，因此 D 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon EventBridge is an event bus for application/SaaS event routing, not a high-throughput streaming ingestion service for 5 GB/min of continuous data. AWS Glue is batch/micro-batch ETL, not real-time stream transformation. ElastiCache (Memcached) is a volatile cache without persistence or rich query capabilities, unsuitable as the analytics data store.","why_zh":"Amazon EventBridge 是用於應用程式/SaaS 事件路由的事件匯流排，並非可承載每分鐘 5 GB 連續資料的高吞吐串流擷取服務。AWS Glue 是批次/微批次 ETL，並非即時串流轉換。ElastiCache (Memcached) 是無持久化且查詢能力有限的揮發性快取，不適合作為分析資料儲存。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon SQS is a message queue for decoupling, not an ordered high-throughput streaming ingestion service for real-time analytics, and it lacks replay/fan-out for stream processing. Lambda plus SQS is not designed for sustained 5 GB/min stream transformation, and Amazon S3 is object storage optimized for batch analytics, not fast low-latency queries for a real-time application.","why_zh":"Amazon SQS 是用於解耦的訊息佇列，並非為即時分析設計的有序高吞吐串流擷取服務，且缺乏串流處理所需的重播/扇出能力。Lambda 搭配 SQS 不適合持續每分鐘 5 GB 的串流轉換，而 Amazon S3 是針對批次分析最佳化的物件儲存，無法提供即時應用所需的低延遲快速查詢。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon SNS is a pub/sub notification service, not a streaming ingestion service with buffering/replay for 5 GB/min. Amazon EMR is a batch/cluster processing framework, not the most appropriate real-time stream transformer here. Amazon RDS is a relational OLTP database that does not scale to ingest this streaming volume for real-time analytics as well as DynamoDB's single-digit millisecond performance.","why_zh":"Amazon SNS 是發布/訂閱通知服務，並非具緩衝/重播、可承載每分鐘 5 GB 的串流擷取服務。Amazon EMR 是批次/叢集處理框架，並非此情境下最適合的即時串流轉換器。Amazon RDS 是關聯式 OLTP 資料庫，在此串流量的即時分析擷取上的擴展性不如 DynamoDB 的個位數毫秒效能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managed-flink/latest/java/how-sinks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managed-flink/latest/java/how-flink-connectors.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/bp-relational-modeling.html"]}},{"id":124,"question_en":"A company stores training data as a .csv file in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company must encrypt the data and must control which applications have access to the encryption key. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司将培训数据以.csv 文件的形式存储在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中。该公司必须对数据进行加密，并且必须控制哪些应用程序可以访 问加密密钥。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new SSH access key. Use the AWS Encryption CLI with a reference to the new access key to encrypt the file.","B":"Create a new API key by using the Amazon API Gateway CreateApiKey API operation. Use the AWS CLI with a reference to the new API key to encrypt the file.","C":"Create a new IAM role. Attach a policy that allows the AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) GenerateDataKey action. Use the role to encrypt the file.","D":"Create a new AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key. Use the AWS Encryption CLI with a reference to the new KMS key to encrypt the file."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 SSH 访问密钥。使用 AWS 加密 CLI 并引用新访问密钥来加密文件。","B":"使用 Amazon API Gateway 的 CreateApiKey API 操作创建一个新的 API 密钥。使用 AWS CLI 并引用新创建的 API 密钥来加密 文件。","C":"创建一个新的 IAM 角色。附加一个允许执行 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）GenerateDataKey 操作的策略。使用该角色 对文件进行加密。","D":"创建一个新的 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥。使用 AWS 加密命令行界面（CLI）并引用新创建的 KMS 密钥来加密 文件。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements must both be met: encrypt the .csv file, and control which applications can use the encryption key. A customer-managed AWS KMS key satisfies the access-control requirement because, per AWS docs, key policies are the primary way to control access to a KMS key and 'no AWS principal has any permissions to a KMS key unless they are explicitly allowed... in a key policy, IAM policy, or grant' — so you control exactly which principals/applications may use the key. The AWS Encryption CLI is the command-line interface of the AWS Encryption SDK, a client-side encryption library that protects data keys with wrapping keys; it accepts a KMS key (by key ARN/ID) as the wrapping key and performs envelope encryption of the file. Option D both creates the controllable KMS key and names a real tool that actually encrypts the file with that key, so it fully meets the requirements. The other options reference mechanisms unrelated to data encryption (SSH access key, API Gateway API key) or are incomplete because they never create a KMS key whose access can be controlled.","explanation_zh":"需同時滿足兩項需求：加密該 .csv 檔案，並控制哪些應用程式可使用加密金鑰。建立 customer-managed 的 AWS KMS key 可滿足存取控制需求，因為依 AWS 文件，key policy 是控制 KMS key 存取的主要機制，且「除非在 key policy、IAM policy 或 grant 中明確被允許，否則任何 AWS principal 對 KMS key 都沒有任何權限」，因此可精確控制哪些 principals／應用程式能使用該金鑰。AWS Encryption CLI 是 AWS Encryption SDK（一個用戶端加密函式庫，以 wrapping key 保護 data key）的命令列介面，可透過 key ARN/ID 使用 KMS key 作為 wrapping key，對檔案執行 envelope encryption。選項 D 同時建立了可受控的 KMS key，並指明真正能以該金鑰加密檔案的工具，完整滿足需求。其他選項所引用的機制（SSH access key、API Gateway API key）與資料加密無關，或因從未建立可受控存取的 KMS key 而不完整。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SSH access keys are for SSH authentication (e.g., EC2 access), not for data encryption. The AWS Encryption CLI does not accept an SSH access key to encrypt a file, and SSH keys provide no application-level access control over an encryption key.","why_zh":"SSH access key 用於 SSH 驗證（例如存取 EC2），與資料加密無關。AWS Encryption CLI 不會以 SSH access key 來加密檔案，且 SSH key 無法對加密金鑰提供應用程式層級的存取控制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon API Gateway API keys identify API callers for throttling/usage plans; they are not encryption keys and cannot encrypt data. The AWS CLI cannot encrypt a file with an API Gateway API key, and this provides no key access control.","why_zh":"Amazon API Gateway 的 API key 用於識別 API 呼叫者以進行節流／使用方案，並非加密金鑰，無法加密資料。AWS CLI 無法用 API Gateway API key 加密檔案，也無法提供金鑰存取控制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This never creates a KMS key, so there is no key whose access can be controlled — yet the requirement is to control access to the encryption key. kms:GenerateDataKey requires an existing KMS key to act on, and 'use the role to encrypt the file' is incomplete/vague: an IAM role does not itself encrypt a file and no encryption tool is named. Option D both creates the controllable key and names a working encryption tool.","why_zh":"此選項從未建立 KMS key，因此沒有可受控存取的金鑰，但需求正是要控制加密金鑰的存取。kms:GenerateDataKey 需要既有的 KMS key 才能運作；「使用該角色加密檔案」也不完整且含糊：IAM role 本身無法加密檔案，且未指明加密工具。選項 D 既建立了可受控金鑰，又指明了可運作的加密工具。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policy-default.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/encryption-sdk/latest/developer-guide/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/encryption-sdk/latest/developer-guide/crypto-cli-install.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/encryption-sdk/latest/developer-guide/concepts.html"]}},{"id":125,"question_en":"A company needs to perform feature engineering, aggregation, and data preparation. After the features are produced, the company must implement a solution on AWS to process and store the features. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要进行特征工程、聚合和数据准备。在生成特征之后，该公司必须在 AWS 上实施解决方案来处理和存储这些特征。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon SageMaker Feature Processing to process and ingest the data. Use SageMaker Feature Store to manage and store the features.","B":"Use Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor to automatically ingest and transform the data. Create an Amazon S3 bucket to store the features in JSON format.","C":"Use Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink to transform the data and to ingest the data directly into Amazon SageMaker Feature Store. Use Feature Store to manage and store the features.","D":"Use an Amazon SageMaker batch transform job to analyze, transform, and ingest the data. Create an Amazon DynamoDB table to store the features."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon SageMaker 特征处理来处理和摄取数据。使用 SageMaker 特征处理 用于管理和存储特征的存储库。","B":"使用 Amazon SageMaker 模型监控器自动摄取和转换数据。创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶以 JSON 格 式存储特征。","C":"使用亚马逊托管的 Apache Flink 服务来转换数据，并将数据直接摄取到亚马逊 SageMaker 特征存储中。 使用特征存储来管理和存储特征。","D":"使用 Amazon SageMaker 批量转换作业来分析、转换和摄取数据。创建一个 Amazon DynamoDB 表来存 储特征。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon SageMaker Feature Store Feature Processing is purpose-built for this workflow. AWS docs state it 'is a capability with which you can transform raw data into machine learning (ML) features' via a Feature Processor SDK that lets you 'transform and ingest data from batch data sources into your feature groups,' while Feature Store provisions the underlying compute and Pipelines. The Feature Processing examples explicitly cover aggregation and data preparation (joining multiple data sources, sliding-window and tumbling-window aggregates, Pandas transforms). SageMaker Feature Store then manages and stores the produced features in its online and offline stores. This makes option A a direct, native fit for both processing the features and storing them; the other options misuse services not designed for feature engineering plus managed feature storage.","explanation_zh":"Amazon SageMaker Feature Store Feature Processing 正是為此工作流程量身打造。AWS 文件指出它是「可將原始資料轉換為 machine learning (ML) 特徵」的能力，透過 Feature Processor SDK 可「從批次資料來源轉換並 ingest 資料到你的 feature groups」，並由 Feature Store 自動佈建底層運算與 Pipelines。其 Feature Processing 範例明確涵蓋聚合與資料準備（join 多個資料來源、sliding-window 與 tumbling-window 聚合、Pandas 轉換）。接著由 SageMaker Feature Store 在其 online 與 offline store 中管理並儲存所產生的特徵。因此選項 A 在處理與儲存特徵兩方面都是原生且最契合的解法；其他選項皆誤用了非為特徵工程與受管特徵儲存而設計的服務。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"SageMaker Model Monitor watches deployed models/endpoints for data quality, model quality, bias, and feature-attribution drift; it does not ingest or transform raw data for feature engineering. Storing features as plain JSON in S3 also provides no feature-group management, online lookup, or point-in-time/offline store capabilities.","why_zh":"SageMaker Model Monitor 用於監控已部署模型/端點的資料品質、模型品質、偏差與特徵歸因漂移，並非用來 ingest 或轉換原始資料做特徵工程。把特徵以純 JSON 存入 S3 也無 feature group 管理、線上查詢或 offline store 等能力。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink has no native sink/connector to ingest directly into SageMaker Feature Store; there is no documented Flink-to-Feature Store integration. Feature Store ingestion uses the Feature Processor SDK, the PutRecord API, or custom code calling PutRecord, not a direct Flink sink.","why_zh":"Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink 沒有可直接 ingest 進 SageMaker Feature Store 的原生 sink/connector，也沒有官方記載的 Flink 到 Feature Store 整合。Feature Store 的 ingest 透過 Feature Processor SDK、PutRecord API 或自訂程式呼叫 PutRecord 達成，而非直接的 Flink sink。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A SageMaker batch transform job runs inference on data using an existing trained model; it is not a general-purpose tool to analyze, transform, and ingest raw data for feature engineering. A self-managed DynamoDB table is also not the AWS-managed feature storage service and lacks the feature-group, lineage, and offline-store functionality that Feature Store provides.","why_zh":"SageMaker batch transform job 是用既有已訓練模型對資料進行推論，並非用來分析、轉換並 ingest 原始資料做特徵工程的通用工具。自行管理的 DynamoDB 表也不是 AWS 受管的特徵儲存服務，缺乏 Feature Store 提供的 feature group、lineage 與 offline store 功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/feature-store-feature-processing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/feature-store-feature-processor-sdk.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/feature-store-feature-processor-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/feature-store-offline.html"]}},{"id":126,"question_en":"A company is developing a new online application to gather information from customers. An ML engineer has developed a new ML model that will determine a score for each customer. The model will use the score to determine which product to display to the customer. The ML engineer needs to minimize response-time latency for the model. How should the ML engineer deploy the application in Amazon SageMaker to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一款新的在线应用程序，用于收集客户信息。一位机器学习工程师开发了一个新的机器 学习模型，该模型将为每位客户确定一个分数。模型将根据分数来决定向客户展示哪种产品。这位机器学 习工程师需要尽量减少模型的响应时间延迟。 机器学习工程师应如何在亚马逊 SageMaker 中部署应用程序以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure batch transform.","B":"Configure a real-time inference endpoint.","C":"Configure a serverless inference endpoint.","D":"Configure an asynchronous inference endpoint."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置批处理转换。","B":"配置实时推理端点。","C":"配置无服务器推理端点。","D":"配置异步推理端点。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The application is an online, interactive customer-scoring service that must return a product recommendation synchronously with minimal response-time latency. AWS documentation states that real-time inference is 'ideal for online inferences that have low latency or high throughput requirements,' providing a persistent, fully managed REST API endpoint backed by always-on instances of your choice. Because the instances are always provisioned, there are no cold starts (unlike serverless inference) and no request queuing (unlike asynchronous inference), giving the lowest and most consistent synchronous latency. This directly satisfies the requirement to minimize response-time latency, so option B is correct.","explanation_zh":"此應用程式是一個線上、互動式的客戶評分服務，必須以最低的回應延遲同步回傳產品推薦。AWS 文件指出 real-time inference「適用於有低延遲或高吞吐量需求的線上推論」，提供持久、完全託管的 REST API 端點，並由你選擇的常駐 (always-on) 執行個體支援。由於執行個體一直處於佈建狀態，沒有冷啟動 (cold start)（不像 serverless inference），也沒有請求排隊 (queuing)（不像 asynchronous inference），因此能提供最低且最一致的同步延遲。這正好滿足最小化回應延遲的需求，所以選項 B 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Batch transform is for offline processing of large datasets available upfront with no persistent endpoint and processing times up to days; it cannot return a synchronous, low-latency score for an online application.","why_zh":"Batch transform 用於離線批次處理已事先備齊的大型資料集，無持續端點且處理時間可達數天，無法為線上應用提供同步、低延遲的評分。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Serverless inference suits intermittent or unpredictable traffic and scales from zero, so it can incur cold-start latency; this conflicts with the goal of minimizing response-time latency that an always-on real-time endpoint meets better.","why_zh":"Serverless inference 適合間歇性或不可預測的流量並可縮放至零，因此會產生冷啟動延遲；這與最小化回應延遲的目標相衝突，而常駐的 real-time 端點能更好地達成。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Asynchronous inference queues requests for large payloads with long processing times (up to 1 GB, up to one hour) and returns results via S3/SNS rather than synchronously; the queuing model is the opposite of a low-latency interactive response.","why_zh":"Asynchronous inference 將大型負載、長處理時間（最高 1 GB、最長一小時）的請求排入佇列，並透過 S3/SNS 回傳結果而非同步回應；這種排隊模式與低延遲互動回應的需求相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/deploy-model-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/realtime-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/serverless-endpoints.html"]}},{"id":127,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon EMR. The company has a large dataset in Amazon S3 that needs to be ingested into Amazon SageMaker Feature Store. The dataset contains historical data and real-time streaming data. The company must ensure that the Feature Store online store is updated with the most recent data as soon as the data becomes available. The company also must maintain a complete Feature Store offline store for batch processing. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用亚马逊 EMR。该公司在亚马逊 S3 中有一个大型数据集，需要将其导入到亚马逊 SageMaker 特征存储中。该数据集包含历史数据和实时流数据。 公司必须确保在数据一可用时，就将最新数据更新到 Feature Store 在线商店中。公司还必须维护一个完 整的 Feature Store 离线商店，用于批处理。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use the PutRecord API in Feature Store Runtime to ingest all the data into the online store.","B":"Use the PutRecord API in Feature Store Runtime to ingest all the data into the offline store.","C":"Use the Feature Store Spark connector to ingest the data as Spark DataFrames with the online store and offline store enabled.","D":"Use the Feature Store Spark connector to ingest the data as Spark DataFrames with only the online store enabled."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Feature Store Runtime 中的 PutRecord API 将所有数据摄取到在线存储中。","B":"使用 Feature Store Runtime 中的 PutRecord API 将所有数据摄取到离线存储中。","C":"使用 Feature Store Spark 连接器将数据作为 Spark 数据框摄取，同时启用在线存储和离线存储。","D":"使用功能存储 Spark 连接器将数据作为仅启用在线存储的 Spark 数据框进行摄取。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The Feature Store Spark connector is the purpose-built mechanism for batch-ingesting large datasets from a Spark/EMR ETL pipeline into SageMaker Feature Store. Per the official docs (batch-ingestion-spark-connector-setup), under default ingestion (both stores enabled and ingest_data() called without target_stores), the connector first writes each DataFrame record to the online store via the PutRecord API, so the online store reflects the most recent data, keeping only the record with the largest event time. If the offline store is enabled, within 15 minutes Feature Store then ingests the data into the offline store. This simultaneously keeps the online store current as soon as data arrives and maintains a complete offline store for batch processing, satisfying every requirement. The dataset is large and lives in S3 on EMR, so Spark DataFrame batch ingestion is the natural fit, and the same connector path handles both historical and incrementally-arriving streaming data.","explanation_zh":"Feature Store Spark connector 是專為從 Spark/EMR ETL 管線將大型資料集批次匯入 SageMaker Feature Store 而設計的機制。根據官方文件（batch-ingestion-spark-connector-setup），在預設匯入模式下（同時啟用 online store 與 offline store，且呼叫 ingest_data() 時未指定 target_stores），connector 會先透過 PutRecord API 將每筆 DataFrame 記錄寫入 online store，因此 online store 反映最新資料，只保留 event time 最大的記錄。若同時啟用 offline store，Feature Store 會在 15 分鐘內將資料匯入 offline store。這同時讓 online store 在資料到達時即保持最新，並維護一份完整的 offline store 供批次處理，滿足所有需求。資料集很大且存放在 EMR 上的 S3，因此以 Spark DataFrame 批次匯入最為合適，且同一條 connector 路徑可同時處理歷史資料與陸續到達的串流資料。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"PutRecord is a per-record (synchronous) Feature Store Runtime API meant for low-volume real-time writes, not for ingesting a large S3 dataset from an EMR/Spark pipeline. It also frames ingestion as online-only; while PutRecord replicates to the offline store when offline is enabled, the option does not establish a complete offline store and is poorly suited to the large batch workload from EMR.","why_zh":"PutRecord 是逐筆（同步）的 Feature Store Runtime API，用於低量即時寫入，不適合從 EMR/Spark 管線匯入大型 S3 資料集。它也將匯入描述為僅針對 online store；雖然在啟用 offline 時 PutRecord 會複寫到 offline store，但此選項並未建立完整的 offline store，且不適合來自 EMR 的大型批次工作負載。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"You cannot ingest directly into the offline store with PutRecord. PutRecord writes to the online store (and is then replicated to the offline store only if offline is enabled); there is no way to target the offline store with it. It also would not keep the online store updated in the way required for a large batch from EMR, so it fails the requirements.","why_zh":"無法以 PutRecord 直接匯入 offline store。PutRecord 寫入 online store（且僅在啟用 offline 時才會複寫到 offline store），無法以它指定寫入 offline store。它也無法以滿足需求的方式處理來自 EMR 的大型批次並更新 online store，因此無法符合需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"With only the online store enabled, the docs state that ingesting directly into the online store does not update the offline store, so no complete offline store exists for batch processing. This directly violates the requirement to maintain a complete offline store.","why_zh":"若僅啟用 online store，文件明確指出直接匯入 online store 不會更新 offline store，因此不存在供批次處理的完整 offline store，直接違反維護完整 offline store 的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/batch-ingestion-spark-connector-setup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/feature-store-storage-configurations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/feature-store-concepts.html"]}},{"id":128,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to deploy four ML models in an Amazon SageMaker inference pipeline. The models were built with different frameworks. The ML engineer also needs to give clients the ability to use the invoke_endpoint call to perform inference for each model. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师需要在亚马逊 SageMaker 推理管道中部署四个机器学习模型。这些模型是使用不同 的框架构建的。该机器学习工程师还需要让客户能够使用 invoke_endpoint 调用为每个模型执行推理操作。 哪种解决方案能以最经济高效的方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a SageMaker multi-model endpoint.","B":"Create a SageMaker multi-container endpoint.","C":"Create multiple SageMaker single-model endpoints.","D":"Run a SparkML job to generate multiple endpoints."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 SageMaker 多模型端点。","B":"创建一个 SageMaker 多容器端点。","C":"创建多个 SageMaker 单模型端点。","D":"运行一个 SparkML 作业以生成多个端点。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A SageMaker multi-container endpoint lets you deploy up to 15 containers that use different models or frameworks on a single endpoint, which directly satisfies the 'four models built with different frameworks' requirement. Because all containers share one endpoint and instance fleet, it is more cost-effective than running separate endpoints. The containers can be run in sequence as an inference pipeline (matching the question's 'inference pipeline' wording) and also support direct invocation: clients call invoke_endpoint and specify the TargetContainerHostname parameter to run inference against an individual container/model. A multi-model endpoint (A) is the wrong fit because the AWS docs state it is ideal for hosting many models that use the SAME ML framework on a shared serving container, so it cannot host four models built with different frameworks.","explanation_zh":"SageMaker multi-container endpoint 可在單一 endpoint 上部署最多 15 個使用不同模型或不同框架的容器，正好滿足「四個以不同框架建立的模型」這個需求。由於所有容器共用同一個 endpoint 與 instance fleet，比起為每個模型各自建立 endpoint 更具成本效益。這些容器可以依序串接成一條 inference pipeline（呼應題目的「inference pipeline」用語），同時也支援 direct invocation：用戶端呼叫 invoke_endpoint 並指定 TargetContainerHostname 參數，即可對個別容器/模型執行推論。multi-model endpoint (A) 並不適用，因為 AWS 文件明確指出它適合在共用 serving container 上託管大量使用「相同 ML 框架」的模型，無法承載四個以不同框架建立的模型。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A multi-model endpoint is designed for a large number of models that use the SAME ML framework on a shared serving container; it cannot host four models built with different frameworks, so it fails the core requirement.","why_zh":"multi-model endpoint 是為大量使用「相同 ML 框架」、共用同一 serving container 的模型而設計，無法承載四個不同框架的模型，因此不符合核心需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Multiple single-model endpoints work functionally but each model needs its own dedicated endpoint and instances; the AWS docs note shared-fleet approaches reduce hosting cost compared with single-model endpoints, so this is not the MOST cost-effective option.","why_zh":"多個 single-model endpoint 在功能上可行，但每個模型都需要各自專屬的 endpoint 與 instances；AWS 文件指出共用 fleet 的做法比 single-model endpoint 更省成本，因此這不是「最具成本效益」的選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SparkML is used for feature/data transformation (and can serve as a container inside an inference pipeline), not for generating multiple model-serving endpoints; it does not satisfy the requirement and is not the cost-effective serving solution.","why_zh":"SparkML 用於特徵/資料轉換（可作為 inference pipeline 中的一個容器），而非用來產生多個模型服務 endpoint；它無法滿足需求，也不是具成本效益的服務方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/multi-container-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/multi-container-direct.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/multi-model-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/inference-pipelines.html"]}},{"id":129,"question_en":"An ML engineer wants an Amazon SageMaker notebook to automatically stop running after 1 hour of idle time. How can the ML engineer accomplish this goal?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师希望其 Amazon SageMaker 笔记本在闲置 1 小时后自动停止运行。 机器学习工程师如何才能实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Create a lifecycle configuration in SageMaker. Copy the auto-stop-idle script from GitHub to the Start Notebook section.","B":"Create a lifecycle configuration in SageMaker. Copy the auto-stop-idle script from GitHub to the Create Notebook section.","C":"Track the notebook's CPU metric by using Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Invoke an AWS Lambda function from CloudWatch Logs to shut down the notebook instance if CPU utilization becomes zero.","D":"Track the notebook's memory metric by using Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Invoke an AWS Lambda function from CloudWatch Logs to shut down the notebook instance if memory utilization becomes zero."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 SageMaker 中创建一个生命周期配置。将 GitHub 上的 auto-stop-idle 脚本复制到“启动笔记本” 部分。","B":"在 SageMaker 中创建一个生命周期配置。将 GitHub 上的 auto-stop-idle 脚本复制到“创建笔记本”部 分。","C":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 跟踪笔记本的 CPU 指标。如果 CPU 利用率变为零，则从 CloudWatch Logs 调用 AWS Lambda 函数来关闭笔记本实例。","D":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 跟踪笔记本的内存指标。如果内存利用率变为零，则从 CloudWatch Logs 调用 AWS Lambda 函数来关闭笔记本实例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A SageMaker notebook instance lifecycle configuration (LCC) has two script hooks. In the SageMaker console, the 'Start notebook' editor holds a script that 'runs when you create the notebook and every time you start it' (the OnStart hook), while the 'Create notebook' editor holds a script that 'runs only once, when you create the notebook' (the OnCreate hook). The well-known auto-stop-idle script from the AWS samples GitHub repo (amazon-sagemaker-notebook-instance-lifecycle-config-samples) installs a cron job that polls the Jupyter API for idle time and calls StopNotebookInstance after the configured threshold (e.g., 1 hour). Because a notebook instance can be stopped and restarted repeatedly, the cron job must be re-established on every start, so the script must go in the 'Start notebook' (OnStart) section, making A correct. Placing it only in 'Create notebook' (B) would arm the watcher just once and would not re-arm after subsequent stops/starts. The CloudWatch options confuse CloudWatch Logs with CloudWatch metrics and rely on CPU/memory reaching exactly zero, which is unreliable for an idle-but-running Jupyter kernel; the AWS-documented approach is the LCC auto-stop-idle script.","explanation_zh":"SageMaker notebook instance 的 lifecycle configuration (LCC) 有兩個腳本掛鉤。在 SageMaker console 中，'Start notebook' 編輯器存放的腳本「會在你建立 notebook 時以及每次啟動 notebook 時執行」（即 OnStart 掛鉤）；而 'Create notebook' 編輯器存放的腳本「只在你建立 notebook 時執行一次」（即 OnCreate 掛鉤）。AWS samples GitHub repo（amazon-sagemaker-notebook-instance-lifecycle-config-samples）中著名的 auto-stop-idle 腳本會安裝一個 cron job，定期輪詢 Jupyter API 的閒置時間，並在達到設定門檻（例如 1 小時）後呼叫 StopNotebookInstance。由於 notebook instance 可被反覆停止與重新啟動，該 cron job 必須在每次啟動時重新建立，因此腳本必須放在 'Start notebook' (OnStart) 區段，故 A 正確。若只放在 'Create notebook' (B)，監看程式只會在建立時設定一次，之後停止/啟動後不會重新啟用。C 與 D 兩個 CloudWatch 選項混淆了 CloudWatch Logs 與 CloudWatch metrics，且依賴 CPU/memory 達到「正好為零」，但閒置但仍在執行的 Jupyter kernel 不一定會讓使用率歸零，並不可靠；AWS 官方文件記載的做法正是 LCC 的 auto-stop-idle 腳本。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The 'Create notebook' (OnCreate) hook runs only once at instance creation, per the AWS console procedure. The auto-stop-idle cron job is not re-armed across stop/start, so placing the script here would fail to re-establish the idle watcher after the instance is restarted; it must go in 'Start notebook' (OnStart) instead.","why_zh":"依 AWS console 程序，'Create notebook' (OnCreate) 掛鉤只在建立 instance 時執行一次。auto-stop-idle 的 cron job 在停止/啟動之間不會重新啟用，放在此處會導致 instance 重新啟動後無法重新建立閒置監看；應改放在 'Start notebook' (OnStart)。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs does not track CPU metrics (metrics live in CloudWatch metrics, not Logs), and you cannot 'invoke a Lambda from CloudWatch Logs' on a metric this way. CPU utilization of an idle-but-running Jupyter kernel rarely hits exactly zero, so this trigger is unreliable; the documented solution is the LCC auto-stop-idle script.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs 不會追蹤 CPU 指標（指標位於 CloudWatch metrics，而非 Logs），也無法以此方式「從 CloudWatch Logs 觸發 Lambda」。閒置但仍在執行的 Jupyter kernel 其 CPU 使用率幾乎不會正好歸零，故此觸發不可靠；文件記載的解法是 LCC 的 auto-stop-idle 腳本。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same flaws as C but with memory: CloudWatch Logs does not hold memory metrics, and a notebook with a loaded kernel/processes keeps non-zero memory even while idle, so 'memory utilization becomes zero' is essentially never true and would never stop the instance.","why_zh":"與 C 同樣的缺陷，只是換成記憶體：CloudWatch Logs 不存放記憶體指標，而且載入 kernel/程序的 notebook 即使閒置仍會占用非零記憶體，因此「記憶體使用率歸零」幾乎永遠不會成立，根本不會停止 instance。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/notebook-lifecycle-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/notebook-lifecycle-config-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/APIReference/API_CreateNotebookInstanceLifecycleConfig.html"]}},{"id":130,"question_en":"A company wants to provide services to help other businesses label images. The company wants its labeling specialists to complete human labeling tasks on AWS. How should the company register the labeling specialists to receive tasks on AWS?","question_zh":"一家公司希望提供服务来帮助其他企业标注图像。该公司希望其标注专家能够在亚马逊网络服务 （AWS）上完成人工标注任务。 公司应如何在 AWS 上注册标注专家以接收任务？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Data Exchange.","B":"Create and use an internal workforce in Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth.","C":"Create and use Amazon Mechanical Turk entities in an Amazon SageMaker human loop.","D":"Use the Amazon Mechanical Turk website."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 数据交换。","B":"在 Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth 中创建并使用内部员工队伍。","C":"在 Amazon SageMaker 人工循环中创建和使用 Amazon Mechanical Turk 实体。","D":"使用亚马逊的 Mechanical Turk 网站。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The company wants to register its OWN labeling specialists (people it employs or controls) so they can receive human labeling tasks on AWS. In Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth this is exactly a private (internal) workforce. AWS docs state: 'A private workforce is a group of workers that you choose. These can be employees of your company or a group of subject matter experts from your industry.' You create and manage these workers using Amazon Cognito or your own OIDC Identity Provider, then organize them into private work teams that receive labeling jobs. By contrast, the Amazon Mechanical Turk workforce is described as 'a world-wide resource' — an anonymous public crowd you do not register named specialists into, and Ground Truth even requires that input data be free of PII when using it. AWS Data Exchange is for licensing third-party data sets, not for registering human labelers. Therefore creating and using an internal (private) workforce in SageMaker Ground Truth is the correct way to register the company's labeling specialists.","explanation_zh":"公司想要註冊「自己的」標註專員（其僱用或管理的人員），讓他們在 AWS 上接收人工標註任務。在 Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth 中，這正是 private（內部）workforce 的定義。AWS 文件指出：「A private workforce is a group of workers that you choose. These can be employees of your company or a group of subject matter experts from your industry.」你可以透過 Amazon Cognito 或自有的 OIDC Identity Provider 來建立與管理這些工作者，再將他們組織成 private work teams 以接收標註任務。相對地，Amazon Mechanical Turk workforce 被描述為「a world-wide resource」——一個匿名的公開群眾資源，你無法在其中註冊具名的專員，而且使用它時 Ground Truth 會要求輸入資料不得含有 PII。AWS Data Exchange 用於授權第三方資料集，並非用來註冊人工標註人員。因此，在 SageMaker Ground Truth 中建立並使用 internal（private）workforce 才是註冊公司標註專員的正確做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Data Exchange is a marketplace for finding, subscribing to, and licensing third-party data products (data sets, APIs, models). It has nothing to do with registering human workers or distributing human labeling tasks, so it does not meet the requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Data Exchange 是用於尋找、訂閱及授權第三方資料產品（資料集、API、模型）的市場，與註冊人工工作者或分派人工標註任務無關，無法滿足需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Mechanical Turk used within an Amazon A2I / SageMaker human loop draws on the public anonymous crowd marketplace, not the company's own named specialists. You cannot register specific employees as 'Mechanical Turk entities,' and PII data is prohibited, so this does not register the company's labeling specialists.","why_zh":"在 Amazon A2I / SageMaker human loop 中使用 Mechanical Turk，依賴的是公共匿名群眾市場，而非公司自己的具名專員。你無法將特定員工註冊為「Mechanical Turk 實體」，且禁止使用 PII 資料，因此無法註冊公司的標註專員。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The Amazon Mechanical Turk website publishes HITs to an anonymous, world-wide public crowd; it is not a mechanism to onboard or register a company's own specific labeling specialists. AWS docs describe Mechanical Turk as 'a world-wide resource' and require PII-free input, which conflicts with using controlled, named workers.","why_zh":"Amazon Mechanical Turk 網站向匿名、全球的公開群眾發布 HITs，並非用來讓公司自己的特定標註專員加入或註冊的機制。AWS 文件將 Mechanical Turk 描述為「a world-wide resource」並要求輸入資料不含 PII，這與使用受控、具名的工作者相衝突。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/sms-workforce-private.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/sms-workforce-management-private.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/sms-workforce-management-public.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/sms.html"]}},{"id":131,"question_en":"A company wants to use Amazon SageMaker to host an ML model that runs on CPU for real-time predictions. The model will have intermittent traffic during business hours and will have periods of no traffic after business hours. The company needs a solution that will serve inference requests in the most cost- effective manner. Which hosting option will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望使用亚马逊 SageMaker 来托管一个在 CPU 上运行的机器学习模型，以进行实时预测。该 模型在工作时间会有间歇性的流量，在工作时间之后则会有流量中断的时段。该公司需要一个能以最具 成本效益的方式处理推理请求的解决方案。 哪种托管方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the model to a SageMaker real-time endpoint. Add a schedule-based auto scaling policy to handle traffic surges during business hours.","B":"Deploy the model to a SageMaker Serverless Inference endpoint. Configure increased provisioned concurrency during business hours.","C":"Deploy the model to a SageMaker Asynchronous Inference endpoint. Configure an auto scaling policy that scales in to zero outside business hours.","D":"Deploy the model to a SageMaker real-time endpoint. Create a scheduled AWS Lambda function that activates the endpoint during business hours only."},"options_zh":{"A":"将模型部署到 SageMaker 实时终端节点。添加基于计划的自动扩展策略，以应对业务时段的流量 激增。","B":"将模型部署到 SageMaker 无服务器推理端点。在营业时间配置更高的预置并发量。","C":"将模型部署到 SageMaker 异步推理端点。配置一个自动缩放策略，在非营业时间缩放至零。","D":"将模型部署到 SageMaker 实时端点。创建一个按计划执行的 AWS Lambda 函数，仅在工作时间激活 该端点。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The workload needs real-time, CPU-based inference with intermittent traffic during business hours and zero traffic afterward, at the lowest cost. SageMaker Serverless Inference is purpose-built for this: the AWS docs state it is 'ideal for workloads which have idle periods between traffic spurts,' uses a pay-per-use model, and 'during times when there are no requests, Serverless Inference scales your endpoint down to 0, helping you to minimize your costs.' Adding increased Provisioned Concurrency during business hours addresses the 'predictable bursts' pattern (the docs call Serverless Inference with Provisioned Concurrency 'a cost-effective option when you have predictable bursts in your traffic'), and Application Auto Scaling can adjust Provisioned Concurrency on a schedule while the endpoint still scales to 0 after hours. Real-time endpoints (A, D) run on always-on instances that bill hourly even with no traffic, and Asynchronous Inference (C) is for large payloads / long-running queued requests and serves only asynchronous invocations, not the required real-time predictions. Therefore B is the most cost-effective real-time option.","explanation_zh":"此工作負載需要以最低成本提供即時 (real-time)、CPU 型推論，流量在上班時間間歇性出現、下班後則完全沒有流量。SageMaker Serverless Inference 正是為此設計：AWS 文件指出它『非常適合在流量爆發之間有閒置期的工作負載』，採用按使用量計費模式，且『在沒有任何請求時，Serverless Inference 會將端點縮減至 0，協助您將成本降到最低』。在上班時間提高 Provisioned Concurrency 可應對『可預測的爆發』流量（文件稱搭配 Provisioned Concurrency 的 Serverless Inference 是『流量爆發可預測時的具成本效益選項』），並可透過 Application Auto Scaling 依排程調整 Provisioned Concurrency，而端點在下班後仍會縮減至 0。Real-time 端點 (A、D) 使用持續開啟的執行個體，即使沒有流量也按小時計費；Asynchronous Inference (C) 用於大型負載／長時間執行的佇列式請求，且僅接受非同步呼叫，無法提供題目要求的即時預測。因此 B 是最具成本效益的即時選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A real-time endpoint runs on always-on instances that bill hourly. Schedule-based auto scaling can add capacity for surges but still keeps at least the minimum instance(s) running and billing during the no-traffic period after business hours, so it is not the most cost-effective choice.","why_zh":"Real-time 端點使用持續開啟的執行個體並按小時計費。排程式 auto scaling 可在尖峰時增加容量，但下班後無流量期間仍至少保留最低數量的執行個體持續計費，因此並非最具成本效益的選項。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Asynchronous Inference is designed for large payloads (up to 1GB) and long processing times (up to one hour) with queued requests; the AsyncInferenceConfig means the endpoint only receives asynchronous invocations. The question explicitly requires real-time predictions, so async does not fit even though it can scale to zero.","why_zh":"Asynchronous Inference 專為大型負載（最高 1GB）與長處理時間（最長一小時）的佇列式請求設計；AsyncInferenceConfig 表示端點只接受非同步呼叫。題目明確要求即時預測，因此即使它能縮減至零也不符合需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A provisioned real-time endpoint bills hourly while it exists, and a Lambda cannot simply 'activate/deactivate' an endpoint on a schedule. Toggling availability requires deleting and recreating (or scaling) the endpoint, which adds operational complexity and cold-start downtime, and is less cost-effective and clean than Serverless Inference scaling to zero automatically.","why_zh":"已佈建的 real-time 端點只要存在就按小時計費，且 Lambda 無法單純依排程『啟用／停用』端點。要切換可用性需刪除並重新建立（或調整）端點，會增加營運複雜度與冷啟動停機時間，相較於 Serverless Inference 自動縮減至零，既不夠乾淨也不夠具成本效益。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/serverless-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/serverless-endpoints-autoscale.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/async-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/deploy-model.html"]}},{"id":132,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to train a supervised deep learning model. The available dataset is a large number of unlabeled images that only employees should access. The ML engineer needs to implement a solution that labels the dataset with the highest possible accuracy. Which combination of steps should the ML engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师需要训练一个有监督的深度学习模型。可用的数据集包含大量未标注的图像，只 有员工可以访问这些图像。该机器学习工程师需要实现一个解决方案，以尽可能高的准确度对数据集 进行标注。 机器学习工程师应采取哪两种步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Rekognition to automatically label the dataset.","B":"Train the deep learning model directly on the raw data. Let the model infer the labels by itself.","C":"Use Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth to create an annotation job that specifies the labeling task and requirements.","D":"Set up workforce teams to access a private workforce to run and review the annotation job created by Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth.","E":"Use Amazon Mechanical Turk to complete the annotation job created by Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用亚马逊 Rekognition 自动为数据集添加标签。","B":"直接在原始数据上训练深度学习模型。让模型自行推断标签。","C":"使用 Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth 创建一个标注任务，明确标注任务及要求。","D":"组建工作团队，以获取私有劳动力来运行和审查由亚马逊 SageMaker Ground Truth 创建的标注任务。","E":"使用亚马逊 Mechanical Turk 完成由亚马逊 SageMaker Ground Truth 创建的标注任务。"},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements drive the answer: only employees may access the images, and the labels must have the highest possible accuracy for a supervised deep learning model. Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth is the AWS managed service that 'helps you build high-quality training datasets,' so creating an annotation/labeling job that specifies the task type and requirements is the foundational step (C). To keep the images inside the organization you must use a private workforce, which AWS defines as 'a group of workers that you choose. These can be employees of your company,' created 'from your employees or contractors for handling data within your organization'; you then build private work teams to run and review the job (D). Mechanical Turk (E) is explicitly disallowed because it is a 'world-wide resource' of 500,000+ independent contractors, AWS warns 'You should not share confidential information, personal information... with this workforce,' and Ground Truth 'require[s] that your input data is free of PII' when using it. Automated labeling with Amazon Rekognition (A) does not deliver the highest possible accuracy compared to a trusted internal expert team, and training directly on raw unlabeled data (B) is impossible for a supervised model, which by definition needs labels.","explanation_zh":"兩項要求決定答案：只有員工可存取影像，且監督式深度學習模型的標籤必須具備最高可能準確度。Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth 是 AWS 用來「建立高品質訓練資料集」的受管服務，因此建立指定任務類型與需求的 annotation/labeling job 是基礎步驟（C）。為將影像保留在組織內部，必須使用 private workforce，AWS 定義其為「由你選擇的一群工作者，可以是貴公司的員工」，且「由你的員工或承包商建立以處理組織內部資料」；接著建立 private work teams 來執行與審核此 job（D）。Mechanical Turk（E）被明確排除，因為它是超過 50 萬名全球獨立承包商的「world-wide resource」，AWS 警告「不應與此 workforce 分享機密資訊、個人資訊」，且使用時 Ground Truth「要求輸入資料不含 PII」。使用 Amazon Rekognition 自動標註（A）相較於可信賴的內部專家團隊無法提供最高準確度；直接在未標註原始資料上訓練（B）對監督式模型不可行，因為其本質上需要標籤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Rekognition provides pre-trained automatic labels for general objects/scenes, but it cannot guarantee the highest possible accuracy for a custom supervised dataset and does not address the employee-only access constraint; auto-labeling alone is lower accuracy than trusted human annotation by an internal expert team.","why_zh":"Amazon Rekognition 提供通用物件/場景的預訓練自動標記，但無法為自訂監督式資料集保證最高準確度，也未滿足僅限員工存取的限制；純自動標記的準確度低於可信賴內部專家團隊的人工標註。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Supervised deep learning requires labeled data by definition; a model cannot 'infer its own labels' from raw unlabeled images for supervised training, so this fails the core requirement of producing an accurately labeled dataset.","why_zh":"監督式深度學習依定義需要已標記資料；模型無法從原始未標記影像「自行推斷標籤」來進行監督式訓練，因此不符合產生準確標記資料集的核心需求。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Amazon Mechanical Turk is a public, 'world-wide resource' of 500,000+ independent contractors, not employees. AWS docs explicitly state 'You should not share confidential information, personal information... with this workforce' and Ground Truth 'require[s] that your input data is free of PII' when using Mechanical Turk, violating the 'only employees should access' requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon Mechanical Turk 是公開的全球「world-wide resource」（超過 50 萬名獨立承包者），並非員工。AWS 文件明確指出「不應與此 workforce 分享機密資訊、個人資訊」，且使用 Mechanical Turk 時 Ground Truth「要求輸入資料不含 PII」，違反「只有員工可存取」的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/sms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/sms-workforce-private.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/sms-workforce-management-public.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/sms-workforce-management.html"]}},{"id":133,"question_en":"A company is using an Amazon S3 bucket to collect data that will be used for ML workflows. The company needs to use AWS Glue DataBrew to clean and normalize the data. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"","options_en":{"A":"Create a DataBrew dataset by using the S3 path. Clean and normalize the data by using a DataBrew profile job.","B":"Create a DataBrew dataset by using the S3 path. Clean and normalize the data by using a DataBrew recipe job.","C":"Create a DataBrew dataset by using a Java Database Connectivity (JDBC) driver to connect to the S3 bucket. Clean and normalize the data by using a DataBrew profile job.","D":"Create a DataBrew dataset by using a Java Database Connectivity (JDBC) driver to connect to the S3 bucket. Clean and normalize the data by using a DataBrew recipe job."},"options_zh":{},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Database","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Glue DataBrew connects to Amazon S3 natively: when you create a dataset you simply point it at the S3 path, so no JDBC driver is needed (JDBC is a separate connection type used for relational/database sources, not S3). That eliminates options C and D. For the actual cleaning and normalizing, you author a recipe (an ordered set of transformation steps) and run it at scale as a recipe job. The AWS docs state verbatim: 'Use a DataBrew recipe job to clean and normalize the data in a DataBrew dataset and write the result to an output location of your choice.' A profile job, by contrast, only runs evaluations/statistics to help you understand data quality and does NOT transform or clean the data, which rules out option A. Therefore the correct solution is to create the dataset from the S3 path and clean/normalize with a recipe job (option B).","explanation_zh":"AWS Glue DataBrew 原生支援連接 Amazon S3：建立 dataset 時只需指定 S3 path 即可，不需要 JDBC driver（JDBC 是另一種連接類型，用於關聯式/資料庫來源，而非 S3），因此可排除選項 C 與 D。實際的清理與正規化是透過撰寫 recipe（一組有序的轉換步驟）並以 recipe job 大規模執行。AWS 文件原文寫道：'Use a DataBrew recipe job to clean and normalize the data in a DataBrew dataset and write the result to an output location of your choice.'。相對地，profile job 只會對 dataset 執行評估/統計，協助你了解資料品質，並不會轉換或清理資料，因此排除選項 A。所以正確解法是用 S3 path 建立 dataset，並用 recipe job 清理/正規化（選項 B）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses the correct S3-path dataset, but a profile job only runs evaluations and gathers statistics (data quality, data understanding); it does not transform, clean, or normalize the data. Cleaning/normalizing requires a recipe job.","why_zh":"雖然用正確的 S3 path 建立 dataset，但 profile job 只會執行評估並收集統計資訊（資料品質、了解資料），並不會轉換、清理或正規化資料。清理/正規化需要 recipe job。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Wrong on both counts: S3 is a native DataBrew connection type (no JDBC driver needed; JDBC is for relational databases), and a profile job only analyzes rather than cleans/normalizes the data.","why_zh":"兩處皆錯：S3 是 DataBrew 原生連接類型（不需 JDBC driver；JDBC 用於關聯式資料庫），且 profile job 只分析而非清理/正規化資料。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses the correct recipe job for cleaning/normalizing, but incorrectly proposes a JDBC driver to connect to S3. DataBrew connects to S3 directly via the S3 path; JDBC is for database sources, not S3.","why_zh":"雖然用正確的 recipe job 來清理/正規化，但錯誤地提出用 JDBC driver 連接 S3。DataBrew 是透過 S3 path 直接連接 S3；JDBC 用於資料庫來源，而非 S3。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/databrew/latest/dg/jobs.recipe.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/databrew/latest/dg/jobs.profile.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/databrew/latest/dg/datasets.html"]}},{"id":134,"question_en":"A company is developing a new ML model that uses the XGBoost algorithm. The company will train the model on data that is stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. The data is in a nested JSON format. An ML engineer needs to convert the JSON files into a tabular format. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一种新的机器学习模型，该模型使用 XGBoost 算法。公司将使用存储在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中的数据来训练该模型。这些数据采用嵌套的 JSON 格式。 一位机器学习工程师需要将 JSON 文件转换为表格格式。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Glue PySpark job that uses the Relationalize transform to convert the files.","B":"Write custom Scala code to convert the files. Use Amazon EMR Serverless to run the Scala code.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that uses a Python runtime and invokes the reduce() function to convert the files. Invoke the Lambda function.","D":"Create an Amazon Athena database that is based on the JSON files. Use the Athena flatten function to convert the data."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个使用 AWS Glue PySpark 作业，利用 Relationalize 转换来转换文件。","B":"编写自定义的 Scala 代码来转换文件。使用 Amazon EMR Serverless 来运行该 Scala 代码。","C":"创建一个使用 Python 运行时的 AWS Lambda 函数，并调用 reduce（） 函数来转换文件。调用该 Lambda 函数。","D":"创建一个基于 JSON 文件的 Amazon Athena 数据库。使用 Athena 的展平函数来转换数据。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The qualifier is LEAST operational overhead. AWS Glue's Relationalize transform is purpose-built for this task: per the AWS Glue docs it 'flattens a nested schema in a DynamicFrame and pivots out array columns from the flattened frame,' producing relational/tabular CSV output. AWS Glue is serverless (no cluster to provision or manage) and Relationalize is a single built-in transform, so the PySpark job needs almost no custom code. This is the canonical AWS-recommended way to convert nested JSON into a tabular/relational format with minimal effort, which is also ideal for feeding XGBoost (which expects tabular CSV input).","explanation_zh":"限定條件是 LEAST operational overhead（最少維運負擔）。AWS Glue 的 Relationalize transform 正是為此任務量身打造：根據 AWS Glue 文件，它會『扁平化 DynamicFrame 中的巢狀 schema 並將陣列欄位 pivot 出來』，產生關聯式／表格化的 CSV 輸出。AWS Glue 是無伺服器的（不需佈建或管理叢集），而 Relationalize 是單一內建 transform，因此 PySpark job 幾乎不需自訂程式碼。這是 AWS 官方推薦、以最少工作量將巢狀 JSON 轉為表格／關聯式格式的標準做法，也最適合用來餵給需要表格化 CSV 輸入的 XGBoost。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Writing custom Scala code and running it on EMR Serverless requires authoring and maintaining custom transformation logic plus configuring an EMR Serverless application. That is far more operational overhead than a single built-in Glue Relationalize transform.","why_zh":"撰寫自訂 Scala 程式並在 EMR Serverless 上執行，需要編寫與維護自訂轉換邏輯，還要設定 EMR Serverless 應用程式，維運負擔遠高於單一內建的 Glue Relationalize transform。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Python's reduce() is a functional reduction helper, not a JSON-flattening tool, so the premise is technically nonsensical. Lambda also has a 15-minute timeout and memory limits unsuited to arbitrary-sized S3 datasets, and you would still write substantial custom parsing code.","why_zh":"Python 的 reduce() 是函數式的歸納輔助函式，並非 JSON 扁平化工具，此前提技術上不成立。Lambda 也有 15 分鐘逾時與記憶體上限，不適合任意大小的 S3 資料集，且仍需撰寫大量自訂解析程式碼。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Per the Athena docs, the flatten function only flattens a nested array's elements into a single array of values; it does NOT convert nested JSON into a tabular/relational dataset. Truly tabularizing nested JSON in Athena requires defining a SerDe table and writing CROSS JOIN UNNEST SQL plus a CTAS to materialize output, which mischaracterizes what the flatten function does and adds more work than Relationalize.","why_zh":"根據 Athena 文件，flatten 函式只是把巢狀陣列的元素扁平化成單一陣列值，並不會將巢狀 JSON 轉成表格／關聯式資料集。要真正在 Athena 中將巢狀 JSON 表格化，需定義 SerDe 資料表並撰寫 CROSS JOIN UNNEST SQL，再用 CTAS 物化輸出；此選項誤述了 flatten 函式的能力，且工作量多於 Relationalize。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/aws-glue-api-crawler-pyspark-transforms-Relationalize.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/aws-glue-api-crawler-pyspark-extensions-dynamic-frame.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/flattening-arrays.html"]}},{"id":135,"question_en":"A medical company ingests streams of data from devices that monitor patients’ vital signs. The company uses Amazon SageMaker and plans to prepare ML models to predict adverse events for patients. The dataset is large with thousands of features. An ML engineer needs to run several hundred training iterations with different sets of features, different algorithms, and many potential parameters. The ML engineer must implement a solution to log the characteristics and results of each training iteration. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST implementation effort?","question_zh":"一家医疗公司从监测患者生命体征的设备中获取大量数据流。该公司使用亚马逊 SageMaker，并计划准 备机器学习模型来预测患者的不良事件。数据集规模庞大，包含数千个特征。 一位机器学习工程师需要针对不同的特征集、不同的参数组合运行数百次训练迭代。 算法以及许多潜在参数。机器学习工程师必须实现一个解决方案，用于记录每次训练迭代的特征和 结果。 哪种解决方案能以最少的实施工作量满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon CloudWatch to create custom metrics for the characteristics of each iteration.","B":"Write the characteristics of each iteration to logs in Amazon S3. Use AWS Glue and Amazon Athena to search the logs.","C":"Use the SageMaker Model Registry to track the characteristics and results of each iteration.","D":"Use SageMaker Experiments to track the characteristics and results of each iteration."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用亚马逊 CloudWatch 为每次迭代的特性创建自定义指标。","B":"将每次迭代的特征写入 Amazon S3 日志。使用 AWS Glue 和 Amazon Athena 搜索日志。","C":"使用 SageMaker 模型注册表来跟踪每次迭代的特征和结果。","D":"使用 SageMaker Experiments 来跟踪每次迭代的特征和结果。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"SageMaker Experiments is the purpose-built, native SageMaker capability for tracking the inputs and outputs across many training iterations. The AWS documentation states almost verbatim that 'ML model building requires many iterations of training as you tune the algorithm, model architecture, and parameters' and that you can 'track parameters, metrics, datasets, and other artifacts related to your model training jobs' through 'a single interface where you can visualize' and compare runs. This exactly matches the requirement to log the characteristics (feature sets, algorithms, parameters) and results of several hundred iterations. Because it is built into SageMaker and only requires adding lightweight SDK calls (or automatic capture), it achieves this with the least implementation effort. CloudWatch custom metrics (A) and an S3+Glue+Athena log pipeline (B) require building and maintaining custom logging/search infrastructure, and the Model Registry (C) catalogs and versions finished models for deployment, not the experimentation/iteration-tracking stage.","explanation_zh":"SageMaker Experiments 是 SageMaker 原生且專為追蹤多次訓練迭代輸入與輸出而設計的功能。AWS 官方文件幾乎逐字描述此情境：'ML model building requires many iterations of training as you tune the algorithm, model architecture, and parameters'，並可 'track parameters, metrics, datasets, and other artifacts related to your model training jobs'，透過 'a single interface' 視覺化與比較各次 run。這正符合題目要記錄數百次迭代的特徵組合、演算法、參數等特性與結果之需求。由於它內建於 SageMaker，只需加入輕量的 SDK 呼叫（或自動擷取），因此實作工作量最少。CloudWatch custom metrics（A）與 S3+Glue+Athena 的日誌管線（B）都需自行建置並維護自訂的記錄/搜尋基礎設施；而 Model Registry（C）是用於編目與版本化已完成的模型以供部署，屬於部署階段而非實驗/迭代追蹤階段。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudWatch custom metrics require you to manually define, emit, and structure metrics for each iteration, and CloudWatch is not designed to associate feature sets, algorithms, and parameters per training trial or to compare hundreds of trials side by side. This is more implementation effort and a poor fit for experiment tracking.","why_zh":"CloudWatch custom metrics 需手動為每次迭代定義、發送並結構化指標，且不適合將特徵組合、演算法與參數與每次訓練 trial 關聯，或並排比較數百次試驗。實作工作量更大且不適合實驗追蹤。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Writing logs to S3 and querying them with Glue plus Athena means building and maintaining a custom logging schema, crawlers/ETL, and a query layer to reconstruct experiment tracking that SageMaker Experiments provides natively, so it is significantly more implementation effort.","why_zh":"將日誌寫入 S3 再用 Glue 與 Athena 查詢，等於自行建置並維護日誌結構、crawler/ETL 與查詢層來重造 SageMaker Experiments 原生提供的實驗追蹤功能，實作工作量明顯更大。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SageMaker Model Registry catalogs and versions finished models for production, manages approval status, and automates deployment; it serves the model-management/deployment stage, not the logging of characteristics (features, algorithms, parameters) and results of hundreds of in-progress training iterations during experimentation.","why_zh":"SageMaker Model Registry 用於編目與版本化已完成的模型以供生產、管理 approval status 並自動化部署；屬於模型管理/部署階段，而非在實驗期間記錄數百次進行中訓練迭代之特徵（特徵、演算法、參數）與結果。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/experiments-mlops.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/experiments.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry.html"]}},{"id":136,"question_en":"A company is planning to create an internal-only chat interface to help employees handle customer queries. Currently, the employees need to refer to a massive knowledge base of internal documents to address customer issues. The new solution must be serverless. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正计划开发一个仅供内部使用的聊天界面，以帮助员工处理客户咨询。目前，员工需要查阅大 量的内部文档知识库来解决客户问题。新的解决方案必须是无服务器的。 哪种步骤组合能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up Amazon Bedrock with the Anthropic Claude foundation model.","B":"Set up Amazon SageMaker JumpStart with the Llama foundation model.","C":"Use Amazon EC2 instances with Amazon API Gateway to invoke the model API.","D":"Use AWS Lambda functions with Amazon API Gateway to invoke the model API.","E":"Use an Amazon S3 bucket to store vector database dumps and embeddings.","F":"Use Amazon RDS for MySQL to store vector database dumps and embeddings."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Anthropic Claude 基础模型设置 Amazon Bedrock。","B":"使用 Llama 基础模型设置 Amazon SageMaker JumpStart。","C":"使用带有 Amazon API Gateway 的 Amazon EC2 实例来调用模型 API。","D":"使用 AWS Lambda 函数与 Amazon API Gateway 来调用模型 API。","E":"使用 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储向量数据库转储文件和嵌入向量。","F":"使用 Amazon RDS for MySQL 来存储向量数据库转储文件和嵌入式数据。"},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is a serverless internal chat over a large internal-document knowledge base, i.e. a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) use case. Amazon Bedrock (A) is a fully managed, serverless service that exposes foundation models such as Anthropic Claude through a unified API with no infrastructure to provision, making it the natural FM choice. AWS Lambda + Amazon API Gateway (D) provides the serverless compute and API layer that fronts the chat interface and invokes the model / Bedrock RetrieveAndGenerate API. Amazon S3 (E) is serverless object storage, and Amazon S3 Vectors is a purpose-built, cost-optimized vector store that, per AWS docs, lets you store and query embeddings 'without provisioning any infrastructure' and can be selected directly as the vector store for an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base for RAG over enterprise documents. Together A+D+E form a fully serverless RAG architecture, whereas B (SageMaker JumpStart endpoints on provisioned ML instances), C (EC2), and F (RDS MySQL DB instances) all require always-on, provisioned, non-serverless resources.","explanation_zh":"本題要求建立一個無伺服器 (serverless) 的內部聊天介面，讓員工查詢龐大的內部文件知識庫，屬於 Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) 應用情境。Amazon Bedrock (A) 是完全託管的無伺服器服務，透過統一 API 提供 Anthropic Claude 等基礎模型，無需佈建任何基礎設施，是最合適的 FM 選擇。AWS Lambda + Amazon API Gateway (D) 提供無伺服器的運算與 API 層，作為聊天介面前端並呼叫模型 / Bedrock RetrieveAndGenerate API。Amazon S3 (E) 是無伺服器物件儲存，而 Amazon S3 Vectors 是專為向量打造、具成本效益的向量儲存；依 AWS 文件，它可在「不佈建任何基礎設施」的情況下儲存與查詢 embeddings，並可直接被選為 Amazon Bedrock knowledge base 的向量儲存，用於企業文件的 RAG。A+D+E 共同組成完全無伺服器的 RAG 架構；相對地，B（SageMaker JumpStart 端點需佈建 ML 執行個體）、C（EC2）與 F（RDS MySQL 資料庫執行個體）都需要持續運行、需佈建的非無伺服器資源。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon SageMaker JumpStart with the Llama model deploys to a SageMaker real-time endpoint, which AWS docs show requires choosing and configuring instance types (always-on EC2-backed ML instances). That is provisioned, not serverless, so it violates the serverless requirement; Bedrock is the serverless FM option.","why_zh":"Amazon SageMaker JumpStart 部署 Llama 模型會建立 SageMaker 即時推論端點，AWS 文件顯示需選擇並設定 instance type（持續運行的 EC2 型 ML 執行個體），屬於需佈建的資源而非無伺服器，違反 serverless 需求；Bedrock 才是無伺服器的 FM 選項。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon EC2 instances are provisioned, always-on compute that you must manage, patch, and scale. Using EC2 directly is not serverless, so this fails the requirement; AWS Lambda is the serverless compute choice.","why_zh":"Amazon EC2 執行個體是需自行管理、修補與擴展、持續運行的佈建型運算資源，並非無伺服器，因此不符需求；AWS Lambda 才是無伺服器的運算選擇。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Amazon RDS for MySQL runs on provisioned DB instances (not serverless), and MySQL is not a supported Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases vector store (the pgvector option requires Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL, not MySQL). It fails both the serverless requirement and vector-store compatibility.","why_zh":"Amazon RDS for MySQL 執行於佈建型資料庫執行個體（非無伺服器），且 MySQL 並非 Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases 支援的向量儲存（pgvector 選項需要 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 而非 MySQL），同時不符無伺服器與向量儲存相容性兩項要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-vectors.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-vectors-bedrock-kb.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/retrieval-augmented-generation-options/rag-fully-managed-bedrock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-parameters-claude.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/deploy-jumpstart-model.html"]}},{"id":137,"question_en":"An ML engineer needs to deploy a trained model that is based on a genetic algorithm. The algorithm solves a complex problem and can take several minutes to generate predictions. When the model is deployed, the model needs to access large amounts of data to process requests. The requests can involve as much as 100 MB of data. Which deployment solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师需要部署一个基于遗传算法的训练模型。该算法能够解决一个复杂的问题，生成 预测结果可能需要几分钟的时间。 当模型部署后，模型需要访问大量数据来处理请求。这些请求可能涉及多达 100MB 的数据。 哪种部署方案能以最低的操作开销满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the model to Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer.","B":"Deploy the model to an Amazon SageMaker real-time endpoint.","C":"Deploy the model to an Amazon SageMaker Asynchronous Inference endpoint.","D":"Package the model as a container. Deploy the model to Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) on Amazon EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"将模型部署到位于应用负载均衡器后面的自动扩展组中的 Amazon EC2 实例上。","B":"将模型部署到 Amazon SageMaker 实时端点。","C":"将模型部署到 Amazon SageMaker 异步推理端点。","D":"将模型打包为容器。将模型部署到运行于 Amazon EC2 实例上的 Amazon Elastic Container Service （Amazon ECS）中。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon SageMaker Asynchronous Inference is explicitly designed for requests with large payloads (up to 1 GB) and long processing times (up to one hour), and it queues incoming requests and processes them asynchronously. The genetic-algorithm model takes several minutes to generate a prediction and handles up to 100 MB of request data, which exceeds the limits of a SageMaker real-time endpoint (per the AWS inference options page, real-time supports payloads up to 25 MB and a 60-second model processing time; the InvokeEndpoint API also documents a 60-second maximum model processing time). Among the deployment options, Async Inference is the only fully managed choice that satisfies BOTH the 100 MB payload and the multi-minute processing requirement, and it does so with the LEAST operational overhead because SageMaker manages the infrastructure, request queuing, autoscaling (including scaling to zero), and patching. Building the serving stack on EC2 behind an ALB (A) or on ECS on EC2 (D) is technically feasible but forces you to operate and scale the cluster, handle long-running/queued requests, and patch the OS yourself, which is far more operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"Amazon SageMaker Asynchronous Inference 專為大型酬載 (up to 1 GB) 與長處理時間 (up to one hour) 的請求設計，會將進入的請求排隊並以非同步方式處理。此基因演算法模型每次預測需要數分鐘，且請求資料可達 100 MB，已超過 SageMaker real-time endpoint 的限制 (依 AWS inference options 頁面，real-time 支援最大 25 MB 酬載與 60 秒的模型處理時間；InvokeEndpoint API 也記載模型最大處理時間為 60 秒)。在各部署選項中，Async Inference 是唯一同時滿足 100 MB 酬載與數分鐘處理時間的完全託管選項，且維運負擔最少，因為 SageMaker 會管理基礎設施、請求排隊、自動擴展 (包含縮減至零) 與修補。於 ALB 後方的 EC2 (A) 或 ECS on EC2 (D) 自建服務堆疊雖技術上可行，但需自行維運與擴展叢集、處理長時間/排隊請求並修補作業系統，維運負擔遠高於 async endpoint。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Deploying to EC2 in an Auto Scaling group behind an ALB requires you to build and manage the model server, scaling policies, OS patching, and long-running/queued request handling yourself. ALB also has a default 60-second idle/response timeout that conflicts with multi-minute predictions, so this is both higher operational overhead and a poor fit.","why_zh":"部署到 ALB 後方 Auto Scaling group 中的 EC2 需自行建置與管理模型伺服器、擴展策略、作業系統修補與長時間/排隊請求處理。ALB 預設 60 秒閒置/回應逾時也與數分鐘的預測時間衝突，因此維運負擔更高且不適合。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Per the AWS inference options page, a SageMaker real-time endpoint supports payloads up to 25 MB and a 60-second model processing time (the InvokeEndpoint API documents the same 60-second maximum). A 100 MB payload and several-minute processing time exceed both hard limits, so a real-time endpoint cannot satisfy the requirements.","why_zh":"依 AWS inference options 頁面，SageMaker real-time endpoint 支援最大 25 MB 酬載與 60 秒的模型處理時間 (InvokeEndpoint API 同樣記載 60 秒上限)。100 MB 酬載與數分鐘處理時間皆超過這些硬性限制，因此 real-time endpoint 無法滿足需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Packaging the model as a container and running it on ECS on EC2 means you manage the cluster capacity, container orchestration, scaling, patching, and the request/queuing layer for large payloads and long jobs. That is significantly more operational overhead than a fully managed SageMaker Asynchronous Inference endpoint.","why_zh":"將模型封裝為容器並在 ECS on EC2 上執行，意味著需自行管理叢集容量、容器編排、擴展、修補以及處理大型酬載與長任務的請求/排隊層。相較於完全託管的 SageMaker Asynchronous Inference endpoint，維運負擔明顯更高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/async-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/deploy-model-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/APIReference/API_runtime_InvokeEndpoint.html"]}},{"id":138,"question_en":"An ML engineer wants to use a set of survey responses as training data for an ML classifier. All the survey responses are either “yes” or “no.” The ML engineer needs to convert the responses into a feature that will produce better model training results. The ML engineer must not increase the dimensionality of the dataset. Which methods will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师希望将一组调查回复用作机器学习分类器的训练数据。所有的调查回复都是“是”或 “否”。 机器学习工程师需要将这些响应转换为一个特征，以获得更好的模型训练结果。机器学习工程师不得 增加数据集的维度。 哪些方法能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Binary encoding","B":"Label encoding","C":"One-hot encoding","D":"Statistical imputation","E":"Tokenization"},"options_zh":{"A":"二进制编码","B":"标签编码","C":"一热编码","D":"统计插补法","E":"分词"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The yes/no survey responses form a binary categorical variable (N=2 categories) stored as one column. The task is to turn it into a numeric feature while keeping dimensionality unchanged, i.e. the result must stay a single column. Label encoding (B) is what AWS SageMaker Data Wrangler calls 'Ordinal encode': it maps each category to an integer between 0 and the total number of categories, so yes/no becomes one {0,1} column with no added dimensionality. Binary encoding (A) writes each category in base-2 across ceil(log2(N)) columns; for N=2 that is ceil(log2(2)) = 1 column, so it also collapses to a single 0/1 column with no dimensionality increase. One-hot encoding (C) is the explicit trap: the AWS Data Wrangler docs state the Columns output style 'create[s] a column for every category', turning 1 column into 2 and increasing dimensionality, so it is disqualified. Statistical imputation (D) only fills missing values and tokenization (E) is a text/NLP step, so neither produces a clean single-column numeric encoding of a binary variable.","explanation_zh":"問卷的 yes/no 回應是一個二元類別變數（N=2 個類別），以單一欄位儲存。任務是把它轉成數值特徵且維度不變，也就是結果必須維持單一欄位。Label encoding（B）正是 AWS SageMaker Data Wrangler 所稱的 'Ordinal encode'：它把每個類別映射為 0 到類別總數之間的整數，因此 yes/no 變成一個 {0,1} 欄位，不增加維度。Binary encoding（A）以 base-2 形式跨 ceil(log2(N)) 個欄位表示每個類別；當 N=2 時為 ceil(log2(2)) = 1 個欄位，因此同樣只需單一 0/1 欄位，不會增加維度。One-hot encoding（C）是明確的陷阱：AWS Data Wrangler 文件指出 Columns 輸出方式會「為每個類別建立一個欄位」，把 1 欄變成 2 欄而增加維度，故不符合要求。Statistical imputation（D）只用來填補缺失值，Tokenization（E）則是文字/NLP 步驟，兩者都無法對二元變數產生乾淨的單欄位數值編碼。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"One-hot encoding creates a separate column for each category. The AWS Data Wrangler docs state the Columns output style creates 'a column for every category', so for yes/no it yields 2 columns, increasing dimensionality and directly violating the 'must not increase the dimensionality' requirement.","why_zh":"One-hot encoding 會為每個類別建立獨立欄位。AWS Data Wrangler 文件說明 Columns 輸出方式會「為每個類別建立一個欄位」，因此對 yes/no 會產生 2 個欄位，增加維度，直接違反「不得增加維度」的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Statistical imputation fills in missing values; it does not convert categorical strings into a numeric feature. The yes/no data has no missing-value problem, so imputation does not address the encoding task.","why_zh":"Statistical imputation 是用來填補缺失值，並不會把類別字串轉換成數值特徵。yes/no 資料並沒有缺失值問題，因此 imputation 無法解決此編碼任務。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Tokenization is a text/NLP preprocessing step that splits free text into tokens (e.g., n-grams). It is inappropriate for a simple binary categorical variable and would not yield a clean single-column numeric feature.","why_zh":"Tokenization 是文字/NLP 的前處理步驟，將自由文字切分成 token（例如 n-grams）。對於簡單的二元類別變數並不適用，也無法產生乾淨的單欄位數值特徵。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler-transform.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/latest/dg/data-transformations-for-machine-learning.html"]}},{"id":139,"question_en":"HOTSPOT An ML engineer must choose the appropriate Amazon SageMaker algorithm to solve specific AI problems. Select the correct SageMaker built-in algorithm from the following list for each use case. Each algorithm should be selected one time. Random Cut Forest (RCF) algorithm Semantic segmentation algorithm Sequence-to-Sequence (seq2seq) algorithm Hot Area: Correct Answer: Section: (none) Explanation/Reference: Explanation: Summarize the text of a research paper → Sequence-to-Sequence (seq2seq) algorithm Seq2seq is designed for natural language tasks such as summarization. Scan every pixel of an image to help self-driving cars identify objects in their path → Semantic segmentation algorithm Semantic segmentation analyzes every pixel in an image to classify objects for tasks like self-driving. Identify abnormal data points in a dataset → Random Cut Forest (RCF) algorithm RCF is used for anomaly detection, making it suitable for identifying abnormal data points.","question_zh":"热点 机器学习工程师必须选择合适的亚马逊 SageMaker 算法来解决特定的人工智能问题。 从以下列表中为每个用例选择正确的 SageMaker 内置算法。每个算法只能选择一次。 随机切割森林（RCF）算法 语义分割算法 序列到序列（seq2seq）算法 热点区域： 正确答案： 部分：（无） 解释/参考： 解释： 序列到序列（seq2seq）算法 该算法专为诸如摘要生成之类的自然语言任务而设计。 扫描图像中的每一个像素，以帮助自动驾驶汽车识别其行驶路径中的物体 → 语义分割算法 语义分割会对图像中的每个像素进行分析，以对物体进行分类，从而应用于自动驾驶等任务。 在数据集中识别异常数据点 → 随机切割森林（RCF）算法 RCF 用于异常检测，因此适 合识别异常数据点。","options_en":{},"options_zh":{},"answer":[],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":140,"question_en":"A company is planning to use an Amazon SageMaker prebuilt algorithm to create a recommendation model. The algorithm must be able to make predictions on high-dimensional sparse data. Which SageMaker algorithm should the company choose for the recommendation model?","question_zh":"一家公司计划使用亚马逊 SageMaker 的预构建算法来创建一个推荐模型。该算法必须能够对高维稀 疏数据进行预测。 该公司应为推荐模型选择哪种 SageMaker 算法？","options_en":{"A":"K-nearest neighbors (k-NN)","B":"Factorization Machines","C":"Principal component analysis (PCA)","D":"Sequence-to-Sequence (seq2seq)"},"options_zh":{"A":"K 近邻（K-NN）","B":"因子分解机","C":"主成分分析（PCA）","D":"序列到序列（seq2seq）"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Factorization Machines is the correct choice. The AWS documentation explicitly describes it as a supervised learning algorithm 'designed to capture interactions between features within high dimensional sparse datasets economically' and states that 'Factorization machines are a good choice for tasks dealing with high dimensional sparse datasets, such as click prediction and item recommendation.' This precisely matches the question's two requirements: high-dimensional sparse data and recommendation. Factorization Machines extends a linear model to model pairwise feature interactions efficiently even when the data is mostly zeros (sparse), which is the canonical recommender-system scenario (e.g., user-item matrices). The AWS docs even note CSV is a poor fit because the data is predominantly sparse, reinforcing that this algorithm is purpose-built for sparse recommendation data.","explanation_zh":"正確答案是 Factorization Machines。AWS 官方文件明確將其描述為一種監督式學習演算法，'設計用來經濟地捕捉高維稀疏資料集中特徵之間的交互作用'，並指出 'Factorization machines 非常適合處理高維稀疏資料集的任務，例如點擊預測與物品推薦'。這精準符合題目的兩個需求：高維稀疏資料與推薦。Factorization Machines 將線性模型延伸，可在資料大多為零（稀疏）時仍有效地建模成對特徵交互，這正是推薦系統（例如使用者-物品矩陣）的典型情境。AWS 文件甚至指出 CSV 不適用，因為資料以稀疏為主，更加印證此演算法是專為稀疏推薦資料而設計。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"k-NN is an index-based algorithm for classification and regression based on nearest neighbors. Its own AWS docs note that high-dimensional data becomes sparse (the 'curse of dimensionality'), which is why k-NN applies dimension reduction; it is not the algorithm AWS recommends for recommendation on high-dimensional sparse data.","why_zh":"k-NN 是基於最近鄰的索引式分類與迴歸演算法。其 AWS 文件本身指出高維資料會變得稀疏（即「維度詛咒」），因此 k-NN 需做降維處理；它並非 AWS 推薦用於高維稀疏資料推薦的演算法。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"PCA is an unsupervised dimensionality-reduction algorithm (via SVD). Although it has a 'regular' mode for sparse data, it only compresses features into uncorrelated components and does not make recommendations or predictions on its own, so it cannot serve as the recommendation model.","why_zh":"PCA 是非監督式的降維演算法（透過 SVD）。雖然它有針對稀疏資料的 'regular' 模式，但只能將特徵壓縮為不相關的成分，本身不會做推薦或預測，因此無法作為推薦模型。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Seq2Seq is a supervised algorithm for converting an input sequence to an output sequence (e.g., machine translation, text summarization, speech-to-text). It is unrelated to high-dimensional sparse recommendation tasks.","why_zh":"Seq2Seq 是將輸入序列轉換為輸出序列的監督式演算法（例如機器翻譯、文字摘要、語音轉文字），與高維稀疏推薦任務無關。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/fact-machines.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/k-nearest-neighbors.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/pca.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/seq-2-seq.html"]}},{"id":141,"question_en":"A company has several teams that have developed separate prediction models on their own laptops. The teams developed the models by using Python with scikit-learn and TensorFlow frameworks. The company must rebuild the models and must integrate the models into an ML infrastructure that the company manages by using Amazon SageMaker. The company also must incorporate the models into a model registry. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司有多个团队，他们在各自的笔记本电脑上独立开发了预测模型。这些团队使用 Python 语言以及 scikit-learn 和 TensorFlow 框架来开发模型。 该公司必须重建这些模型，并将这些模型整合到由公司使用亚马逊 SageMaker 管理的机器学习基础设施中。 该公司还必须将这些模型纳入模型注册表。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Export the models from the laptops to an Amazon S3 bucket. Use an Amazon API Gateway REST API and AWS Lambda functions with SageMaker endpoints to access the models. Register the models in the SageMaker Model Registry.","B":"Import the models into the SageMaker Model Registry. Use SageMaker to run the imported models.","C":"Use code from the laptops to create containers for the models. Use the bring your own container (BYOC) functionality of SageMaker to import and use the models. Register the models in the SageMaker Model Registry.","D":"Import the Python-based models into SageMaker. Rebuild the scikit-learn and TensorFlow models in SageMaker. Register all the models in the SageMaker Model Registry."},"options_zh":{"A":"将模型从笔记本电脑导出到 Amazon S3 存储桶。使用 Amazon API Gateway REST API 和带有 SageMaker 端点的 AWS Lambda 函数来访问模型。在 SageMaker 模型注册表中注册模型。","B":"将模型导入 SageMaker 模型注册表。使用 SageMaker 运行导入的模型。","C":"使用笔记本电脑中的代码为模型创建容器。利用 SageMaker 的自带容器（BYOC）功能导入并使用 这些模型。在 SageMaker 模型注册表中注册这些模型。","D":"将基于 Python 的模型导入到 SageMaker 中。在 SageMaker 中重新构建 scikit-learn 和 TensorFlow 模型。 将所有模型在 SageMaker 模型注册表中进行注册。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are explicit: the company 'must rebuild the models' and integrate them into SageMaker-managed infrastructure, then register them in the SageMaker Model Registry, with the LEAST operational overhead. SageMaker AI ships pre-built, fully managed first-party framework containers for both scikit-learn and TensorFlow, so rebuilding (retraining) the models in SageMaker using those managed framework estimators (script mode) is the lowest-overhead path that still satisfies the mandatory rebuild step. Each training run produces a versioned model package that is assigned to a Model Group and registered in the Model Registry, exactly as option D states. Per the AWS docs, Model Registry model packages are versioned entities that MUST be associated with a Model Group and each corresponds to a trained model, so you cannot simply 'import' raw laptop model files into the registry (rules out B), and neither A nor B performs the required rebuild. BYOC (C) is explicitly reserved by AWS for a 'custom framework that does not have a pre-built image,' which is not the case for scikit-learn or TensorFlow, making it the highest-overhead and unnecessary option.","explanation_zh":"需求很明確：公司『必須重建模型』並整合到 SageMaker 託管的基礎架構中，再將模型註冊到 SageMaker Model Registry，且要求最少的營運負擔。SageMaker AI 為 scikit-learn 與 TensorFlow 都提供預先建置、完全託管的第一方框架容器，因此使用這些託管框架 estimators（script mode）在 SageMaker 中重建（重新訓練）模型，是在滿足必要重建步驟下負擔最低的方式。每次訓練都會產出一個版本化的 model package，並被指派到 Model Group 並註冊到 Model Registry，正是選項 D 所述。依 AWS 文件，Model Registry 的 model package 是版本化實體，且『必須』與 Model Group 關聯，每個都對應一個已訓練的模型，因此無法直接把筆電上的原始模型檔『匯入』註冊表（排除 B），而 A 與 B 都沒有執行必要的重建。BYOC（C）依 AWS 文件僅適用於『沒有預建映像的自訂框架』，但 scikit-learn 與 TensorFlow 都有預建映像，因此 BYOC 是負擔最高且不必要的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"It never rebuilds the models in SageMaker; it only exports the laptop models to S3 and bolts on API Gateway plus Lambda in front of endpoints, adding extra infrastructure and operational overhead while failing the explicit 'rebuild the models' requirement.","why_zh":"完全沒有在 SageMaker 中重建模型，只是把筆電模型匯出到 S3，並在端點前加上 API Gateway 與 Lambda，增加額外基礎架構與營運負擔，且未滿足明確的『重建模型』要求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The Model Registry stores versioned model packages that must be associated with a Model Group, each corresponding to a trained model; you cannot just 'import' arbitrary laptop model files into the registry and have SageMaker run them, and this option skips the mandatory rebuild step entirely.","why_zh":"Model Registry 儲存的是必須與 Model Group 關聯、且各自對應一個已訓練模型的版本化 model package；無法直接把任意筆電模型檔『匯入』註冊表並讓 SageMaker 執行，且此選項完全省略了必要的重建步驟。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Bring-your-own-container is the highest-overhead path; AWS docs explicitly reserve BYOC for a custom framework that does NOT have a pre-built image, but scikit-learn and TensorFlow both have managed pre-built containers, so building custom containers from laptop code is unnecessary work.","why_zh":"自帶容器 (BYOC) 是負擔最高的方式；AWS 文件明確指出 BYOC 僅適用於『沒有預建映像的自訂框架』，但 scikit-learn 與 TensorFlow 都有託管的預建容器，因此用筆電程式碼自建容器屬於不必要的工作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/docker-containers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/sklearn.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/pre-built-containers-frameworks-deep-learning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry-models.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry.html"]}},{"id":142,"question_en":"A company is training a large language model (LLM) by using on-premises infrastructure. A live conversational engine uses the LLM to help customers find real-time insights in credit card data. An ML engineer must implement a solution to train and deploy the LLM on Amazon SageMaker. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在利用本地基础设施训练一个大型语言模型（LLM）。一个实时对话引擎使用该 LLM 帮助客户在信用卡数据中查找实时洞察信息。 一位机器学习工程师必须在亚马逊 SageMaker 上实现一个解决方案，用于训练和部署大型语言模型。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use SageMaker Training Compiler to train the LLM. Deploy the LLM by using SageMaker real-time inference.","B":"Use SageMaker with deep learning containers for large model inference to train the LLM. Deploy the LLM by using SageMaker real-time inference.","C":"Use SageMaker Notebook Jobs to train the LLM. Deploy the LLM by using SageMaker Asynchronous Inference.","D":"Use SageMaker Studio to train the LLM. Deploy the LLM by using SageMaker batch transform."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 SageMaker 训练编译器训练大型语言模型（LLM）。通过 SageMaker 实时推理部署该 LLM。","B":"使用 SageMaker 和深度学习容器进行大型模型推理来训练 LLM。通过使用 SageMaker 实时推理来部署 LLM。","C":"使用 SageMaker 笔记本作业来训练大型语言模型（LLM）。通过使用 SageMaker 异步推理来部署该 LLM。","D":"使用 SageMaker Studio 训练大型语言模型（LLM）。通过 SageMaker 批量转换部署该 LLM。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The question requires a solution that both TRAINS and DEPLOYS the LLM on SageMaker, and the live conversational engine needs real-time serving. The differentiator is the training half. Option A uses SageMaker Training Compiler, which the AWS docs describe as a capability to 'train deep learning (DL) models faster on scalable GPU instances' for models 'with billions of parameters' (exactly LLMs), and it deploys with real-time inference, which AWS recommends for 'persistent, real-time endpoints that make one prediction at a time' (ideal for a live conversational engine). Both halves of A are technically valid. Option B is the trap: it says to use 'deep learning containers for large model inference to TRAIN the LLM,' but the LMI container docs state these are 'specialized Docker containers for LLM inference' used to 'deploy and optimize large language models' - they do NOT train models. So B's training half is a category error and disqualifies it. The note that Training Compiler has 'no new releases or versions' does not remove it; AWS states 'you can continue to utilize SageMaker Training Compiler through the existing AWS Deep Learning Containers,' so it remains a usable training path. Therefore A is the only option whose train + deploy steps are both correct.","explanation_zh":"題目要求一個既能訓練 (train) 又能部署 (deploy) LLM 於 SageMaker 的方案，且即時對話引擎需要 real-time 服務。關鍵差異在於訓練的那一半。選項 A 使用 SageMaker Training Compiler，AWS 文件描述其為『在可擴展 GPU 執行個體上更快地訓練深度學習 (DL) 模型』的能力，並針對『數十億參數』的模型 (正是 LLM)；再以 real-time inference 部署，AWS 建議用於『持久、一次一個預測的即時端點』(非常適合即時對話引擎)。A 的兩個步驟在技術上皆正確。選項 B 是陷阱：它聲稱使用『deep learning containers for large model inference 來 TRAIN (訓練) LLM』，但 LMI 容器文件明確指出這些是『用於 LLM inference 的特殊 Docker 容器』，用來『部署與最佳化大型語言模型』，並不能訓練模型。因此 B 的訓練那一半屬於類別錯誤，足以將其排除。Training Compiler 標註『不再有新版本』並不代表移除；AWS 表示『你可以繼續透過現有的 AWS Deep Learning Containers 使用 SageMaker Training Compiler』，故它仍是可用的訓練路徑。所以 A 是唯一訓練與部署兩步驟皆正確的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The LMI (large model inference) deep learning containers are inference-only: AWS docs describe them as 'specialized Docker containers for LLM inference' to 'deploy and optimize large language models.' They cannot TRAIN an LLM, so the option's training step is technically impossible. The real-time inference deployment half is fine, but the broken training half disqualifies B on a single-answer question.","why_zh":"LMI (large model inference) deep learning containers 僅用於推論：AWS 文件描述其為『用於 LLM inference 的特殊 Docker 容器』，用來『部署與最佳化大型語言模型』。它們無法訓練 (TRAIN) LLM，因此此選項的訓練步驟在技術上不可行。real-time inference 部署那半沒問題，但訓練那半的錯誤在單選題中使 B 被排除。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SageMaker Asynchronous Inference is a queued mode for large payloads (up to 1GB), long processing times, and only NEAR-real-time latency; it is not the live, immediate, low-latency serving a real-time conversational engine needs. Notebook Jobs is a scheduled-notebook execution feature, not the purpose-built path for training a multi-billion-parameter LLM.","why_zh":"SageMaker Asynchronous Inference 是用於大型 payload (最大 1GB)、長時間處理且僅『接近即時』延遲的排隊模式；不符合即時對話引擎所需的即時、低延遲服務。Notebook Jobs 是排程執行 notebook 的功能，並非訓練數十億參數 LLM 的合適路徑。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SageMaker batch transform produces predictions for an entire dataset offline; AWS lists it 'to get predictions for an entire dataset,' which cannot serve a live, real-time conversational engine at all. SageMaker Studio is an IDE, not a dedicated managed training mechanism for an LLM. Both halves fail.","why_zh":"SageMaker batch transform 是離線對整個資料集產生預測；AWS 描述其用於『取得整個資料集的預測』，完全無法服務即時的對話引擎。SageMaker Studio 是 IDE，並非專為 LLM 設計的受管訓練機制。兩個步驟皆不符合。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/training-compiler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/large-model-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/large-model-inference-container-docs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/how-it-works-deployment.html"]}},{"id":143,"question_en":"A company has an existing Amazon SageMaker model (v1) on a production endpoint. The company develops a new model version (v2) and needs to test v2 in production before substituting v2 for v1. The company needs to implement a solution to minimize the risk of v2 generating incorrect output in production. The solution must prevent any disruption of production traffic during the change to v2. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司现有的亚马逊 SageMaker 模型（v1）已在生产端点上运行。该公司开发了一个新模型版本 （v2），需要在生产环境中测试 v2，然后再用 v2 替换 v1。 该公司需要实施一项解决方案，以将 v2 在生产环境中生成错误输出的风险降至最低。该方案必须确 保在切换到 v2 的过程中不会对生产流量造成任何干扰。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a second production variant for v2. Assign 1% of the traffic to v2 and 99% of the traffic to v1. Collect all the output of v2 in an Amazon S3 bucket. If v2 performs as expected, switch all the traffic to v2.","B":"Create a second production variant for v2. Assign 10% of the traffic to v2 and 90% of the traffic to v1. Collect all the output of v2 in an Amazon S3 bucket. If v2 performs as expected, switch all the traffic to v2.","C":"Deploy v2 to a new endpoint. Turn on data capturing for the production endpoint. Write a script to pass 100% of input data to v2. If v2 performs as expected, deactivate the v1 endpoint and direct the traffic to v2.","D":"Deploy v2 into a shadow variant that samples 100% of the inference requests. Collect all the output in an Amazon S3 bucket. If v2 performs as expected, promote v2 to production."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 v2 创建第二个生产变体。将 1% 的流量分配给 v2，99% 的流量分配给 v1。将 v2 的所有输出收集到一 个 Amazon S3 存储桶中。如果 v2 的表现符合预期，则将所有流量切换到 v2。","B":"为 v2 创建第二个生产变体。将 10% 的流量分配给 v2，90% 的流量分配给 v1。将 v2 的所有输出收集到 一个 Amazon S3 存储桶中。如果 v2 的表现符合预期，则将所有流量切换到 v2。","C":"将 v2 部署到新的端点。开启生产端点的数据捕获功能。编写一个脚本，将 100% 的输入数据传递给 v2。 如果 v2 的表现符合预期，则停用 v1 端点，并将流量导向 v2。","D":"将 v2 部署到一个影子变体中，该变体对 100% 的推理请求进行采样。将所有输出收集到一个 Amazon S3 存储桶中。如果 v2 的表现符合预期，则将其推广到生产环境。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"SageMaker shadow variants (shadow testing) are purpose-built for exactly this scenario. When you deploy v2 as a ShadowProductionVariant on the same endpoint, SageMaker replicates a configurable sample of live inference requests to the shadow variant in real time, but per AWS docs 'the responses of the shadow variant are logged for comparison and not returned to the caller... without exposing the caller to the response produced by the shadow variant.' The production variant (v1) continues to return 100% of the actual responses, so v2's incorrect output can never reach real users and there is zero disruption to production traffic. You can log v2's output (e.g., to S3) for offline comparison, and once v2 performs as expected you promote it to production. Options A and B route real traffic to v2 as a production variant, and per AWS docs the production variant a request is routed to 'provides the response to the caller' — so v2's incorrect output would actually reach 1% or 10% of users, violating the requirement. Option C is a manual reimplementation that ends by deactivating the v1 endpoint and redirecting traffic, a hard cutover with operational overhead instead of the native, managed shadow mechanism.","explanation_zh":"SageMaker 的 shadow variant（shadow testing）正是為此情境而設計。將 v2 部署為同一 endpoint 上的 ShadowProductionVariant 後，SageMaker 會即時將可設定比例的現有推論請求複製一份送到 shadow variant，但依 AWS 文件所述，「shadow variant 的回應只會被記錄供比較，不會回傳給呼叫者……不會讓呼叫者接觸到 shadow variant 產生的回應」。生產 variant（v1）仍然回傳 100% 的實際回應，因此 v2 的錯誤輸出絕不會到達真實使用者，也完全不會中斷生產流量。你可以將 v2 的輸出記錄（例如寫入 S3）以供離線比較，待 v2 表現符合預期後再 promote 到生產。選項 A 和 B 將真實流量路由到作為 production variant 的 v2，依 AWS 文件，請求被路由到的 production variant「會將回應提供給呼叫者」，因此 v2 的錯誤輸出會實際到達 1% 或 10% 的使用者，違反需求。選項 C 是手動重現此機制，最後還要停用 v1 endpoint 並重新導向流量，屬於硬切換且增加運營負擔，而非使用原生托管的 shadow 機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A weighted production variant routes 1% of real production traffic to v2, and per AWS docs the production variant a request is routed to provides the response to the caller. So v2's (possibly incorrect) output reaches 1% of real users, which does not minimize the risk of incorrect output reaching production.","why_zh":"加權 production variant 會將 1% 真實生產流量路由到 v2，依 AWS 文件，請求被路由到的 production variant 會將回應提供給呼叫者，因此 v2（可能錯誤的）輸出會到達 1% 真實使用者，無法降低錯誤輸出進入生產的風險。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same flaw as A but worse: it sends 10% of real traffic to v2 and returns v2's responses to those users, exposing 10% of production to potential v2 errors.","why_zh":"與 A 相同但更嚴重：將 10% 真實流量送到 v2 並將 v2 回應回傳給這些使用者，使 10% 生產暴露於可能的 v2 錯誤。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Deploying v2 to a separate endpoint with a custom script to mirror 100% of input is a manual reimplementation of shadow testing, and it ends by deactivating the v1 endpoint and directing traffic to v2 — a hard cutover with operational overhead, rather than using the native, managed ShadowProductionVariant that does this with no end-user impact and a built-in promote step.","why_zh":"將 v2 部署到獨立 endpoint 並用自訂腳本鏡像 100% 輸入，是手動重現 shadow testing，且最後要停用 v1 endpoint 並把流量導向 v2，屬於硬切換並增加運營負擔，而非使用原生托管、對終端使用者零影響且內建 promote 步驟的 ShadowProductionVariant。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-validation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/shadow-tests.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-shadow-deployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-ab-testing.html"]}},{"id":144,"question_en":"A company is building an ML model by using Amazon SageMaker, AWS owned libraries, and open source libraries. The company must ensure that SageMaker does not collect metadata about usage and errors during training. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"","options_en":{"A":"Associate the SageMaker domain with a custom IAM role. Attach the role to a policy that denies Amazon CloudWatch service usage logs.","B":"Add an IAM role to the SageMaker domain to deny Amazon CloudWatch the permission to report metadata.","C":"Turn off the setting in the SageMaker domain to share metadata for console jobs. Opt out of metadata collection for each training job that is submitted through the AWS CLI or AWS SDKs.","D":"Set a parameter to opt out of metadata collection for each training job that is submitted through the AWS CLI, Boto3, or the SageMaker Python SDK."},"options_zh":{},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"Amazon SageMaker AI collects aggregate metadata about AWS-owned and open source libraries used during training, specifically Usage Information and Errors. Per the SageMaker AI Data Privacy documentation, you opt out by setting the environment variable OPT_OUT_TRACKING=1 for each training job created with the CreateTrainingJob API. The docs show this is done via the AWS CLI (create-training-job --environment OPT_OUT_TRACKING=1), the AWS SDK for Python (Boto3), or the SageMaker Python SDK estimator, and you must opt out per job in the API call (you cannot opt out inside a training script). This matches option D exactly. The dump's suggested answer C is wrong because it invents a SageMaker domain setting to 'turn off sharing metadata for console jobs' that does not exist; the docs state that jobs created in the console already have metadata collection disabled by default, so there is no console/domain toggle to configure. Options A and B are wrong because opting out is a per-job environment variable, not an IAM or CloudWatch permission control.","explanation_zh":"Amazon SageMaker AI 會收集訓練期間使用的 AWS-owned 與 open source 函式庫的彙總 metadata，具體包含 Usage Information 與 Errors。根據 SageMaker AI Data Privacy 文件，您要在以 CreateTrainingJob API 建立的每個 training job 中，將環境變數 OPT_OUT_TRACKING 設為 1 來 opt out。文件示範可透過 AWS CLI（create-training-job --environment OPT_OUT_TRACKING=1）、AWS SDK for Python (Boto3) 或 SageMaker Python SDK 的 estimator 設定，且必須在 API 呼叫中逐一 training job 進行 opt out（不能在訓練腳本內 opt out）。這正好對應選項 D。Dump 建議答案 C 是錯的，因為它虛構了一個 SageMaker domain 中『關閉分享 console job 的 metadata』的設定，而此設定並不存在；文件明確指出在 console 建立的 training job 其 metadata 收集預設即為停用，因此沒有 console/domain 開關可設定。選項 A 與 B 也錯，因為 opt out 是逐 training job 的環境變數，而非 IAM 或 CloudWatch 權限控制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Opting out is not controlled by IAM or by denying CloudWatch usage logs. SageMaker metadata collection is disabled via the OPT_OUT_TRACKING environment variable on each training job, not by an IAM policy denying CloudWatch. There is no IAM action that toggles this aggregate library metadata.","why_zh":"Opt out 並非由 IAM 或拒絕 CloudWatch usage logs 控制。SageMaker 的 metadata 收集是透過每個 training job 的 OPT_OUT_TRACKING 環境變數停用，而非以 IAM 政策拒絕 CloudWatch。沒有任何 IAM action 可切換這項彙總 metadata。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"There is no documented mechanism to add an IAM role to the SageMaker domain to deny CloudWatch the permission to report metadata. The metadata collection is not gated by a CloudWatch permission; opt-out is a per-job environment variable (OPT_OUT_TRACKING=1).","why_zh":"並無在 SageMaker domain 加入 IAM role 以拒絕 CloudWatch 回報 metadata 權限的文件化機制。Metadata 收集不受 CloudWatch 權限控管，opt out 是逐 training job 的環境變數（OPT_OUT_TRACKING=1）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is incorrect. It fabricates a SageMaker domain setting to 'turn off sharing metadata for console jobs'; no such toggle exists. The docs state console-created training jobs already have metadata collection disabled by default, so the first clause is invented. Only the per-job (or account-wide) OPT_OUT_TRACKING parameter described in option D is real.","why_zh":"這是 dump 的建議答案，但並不正確。它虛構了 SageMaker domain 中『關閉分享 console job 的 metadata』的設定，實際上並無此開關。文件指出在 console 建立的 training job metadata 收集預設已停用，因此第一個子句屬於虛構。真正存在的只有選項 D 所述逐 training job（或帳戶層級）的 OPT_OUT_TRACKING 參數。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-privacy.html"]}},{"id":145,"question_en":"An ML engineer is training an ML model to identify people’s health risk based on 20 features and 1 target. The target class has two values: Likely to have health risk (positive class) Unlikely to have health risk (negative class) The age range of people in the dataset is 30 years old to 60 years old. Age is one of the features. The ML engineer analyzes the features. For the positive class, the difference in proportions of labels (DPL) value is (+0.9) for the age range of 40 to 45 compared with all other age ranges. What should the ML engineer do to correct this data imbalance?","question_zh":"一位机器学习工程师正在训练一个机器学习模型，根据 20 个特征和 1 个目标来识别人们的健康风险。目标 类别有两个值： 可能存在健康风险（阳性类别） 不太可能有健康风险（阴性类别） 数据集中的人员年龄范围为 30 岁至 60 岁。年龄是其中一个特征。 机器学习工程师对特征进行了分析。对于正类，年龄在 40 至 45 岁范围内的标签比例差异（DPL）值为（+0. 9），与其他所有年龄范围相比。 机器学习工程师应该采取什么措施来纠正这种数据不平衡？","options_en":{"A":"Oversample the positive class for the age range of 40 to 45.","B":"Undersample the positive class for the age range of 40 to 45.","C":"Undersample the positive class for all age ranges except 40 to 45.","D":"Oversample the negative class for all age ranges except 40 to 45."},"options_zh":{"A":"对年龄在 40 至 45 岁范围内的正类样本进行过采样。","B":"对年龄在 40 至 45 岁范围内的正类样本进行欠采样。","C":"对除 40 至 45 岁年龄段外的所有年龄段的正类样本进行欠采样。","D":"对除 40 至 45 岁年龄段之外的所有年龄段的负类进行过采样。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"SageMaker Clarify defines DPL = qa - qd, where facet a is the group under analysis (age 40-45) and facet d is all other age ranges. qa = na(1)/na is the proportion of facet a with a positive label ('Likely to have health risk'), and qd = nd(1)/nd is the same proportion for facet d. AWS docs state that a positive DPL means facet a has a higher proportion of positive outcomes than facet d, and that demographic parity is achieved when DPL is close to 0. A DPL of +0.9 therefore means the 40-45 group is heavily over-concentrated in the positive class relative to every other age range. To push DPL back toward 0, the engineer must lower qa or raise qd. Undersampling the positive class within the 40-45 range reduces na(1)/na = qa, driving DPL toward 0, so Option B is correct.","explanation_zh":"SageMaker Clarify 將 DPL 定義為 DPL = qa - qd，其中 facet a 是被分析的群組（40-45 歲），facet d 是其他所有年齡範圍。qa = na(1)/na 是 facet a 中正向標籤（'Likely to have health risk'）的比例，qd = nd(1)/nd 則是 facet d 的同一比例。AWS 文件指出正的 DPL 代表 facet a 的正向結果比例高於 facet d，而當 DPL 接近 0 時即達到 demographic parity。因此 DPL 為 +0.9 表示正向類別過度集中在 40-45 歲群組，遠高於其他所有年齡範圍。要讓 DPL 趨近 0，工程師必須降低 qa 或提高 qd。對 40-45 歲範圍的正向類別進行 undersample 會降低 na(1)/na = qa，使 DPL 趨近 0，因此選項 B 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Oversampling the positive class for 40-45 increases na(1)/na = qa, pushing DPL even further above +0.9 and worsening the imbalance instead of correcting it.","why_zh":"對 40-45 歲 oversample 正向類別會提高 na(1)/na = qa，使 DPL 更高於 +0.9，反而加劇不平衡而非修正。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Undersampling the positive class in all other age ranges reduces nd(1)/nd = qd, which makes DPL = qa - qd even more positive, worsening the bias.","why_zh":"對其他所有年齡範圍 undersample 正向類別會降低 nd(1)/nd = qd，使 DPL = qa - qd 變得更正，加劇偏差。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Oversampling the negative class in all other ranges increases nd while nd(1) is unchanged, so qd = nd(1)/nd drops, making DPL more positive and worsening the imbalance.","why_zh":"對其他範圍 oversample 負向類別會增加 nd 但 nd(1) 不變，因此 qd = nd(1)/nd 下降，使 DPL 更正，加劇不平衡。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-data-bias-metric-true-label-imbalance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/machine-learning-lens/mlrel03-bp04.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-configure-processing-jobs.html"]}}];
